/* 地点小段·手写层(地理视角第③层):回答「那个朝代,这个地方是什么样」。
   键 = '城市|文明',两边都必须真实存在且城市落在该文明版图内(audit 规则 38)。
   写法:两三句,只写查证过的硬事实,年代拿不准就用「前后/传为」hedge;
   自动层(定位句+大事记筛选)仍会跟在这段后面,这里不重复年表。 */
const PLACE_LORE = {
'西安|西周': ['西周的都城丰镐就在今天西安西南的沣河两岸,文王作丰、武王作镐。周人从这里出兵灭商,又在这里定下分封与宗法的一套规矩;前 771 年犬戎攻破镐京,平王东迁洛邑,西周结束。',
 'The Western Zhou capital of Feng and Hao stood on both banks of the Feng river southwest of today\'s Xi\'an — King Wen built Feng, King Wu built Hao. From here the Zhou marched out to destroy the Shang, and here they laid down the rules of enfeoffment and lineage. In 771 BC the Quanrong stormed Haojing, King Ping moved east to Luoyi, and the Western Zhou was over.'],
'西安|春秋': ['平王东迁后,关中留给了替周王室断后的秦人。秦从一个替周王养马起家的部族,一步步在渭河流域站稳,到春秋中期已是西方大国;秦穆公「称霸西戎」,把势力推到今天甘肃一带。',
 'When King Ping moved east, Guanzhong was left to the Qin, who had covered the Zhou retreat. From a clan that had begun by raising horses for the Zhou king, the Qin worked their way up the Wei valley, and by the middle Spring and Autumn period they were the great power of the west; Duke Mu was recognised as hegemon over the Rong tribes, pushing Qin reach into today\'s Gansu.'],
'西安|战国': ['商鞅先后两次变法:前 356 年立军功爵、行什伍连坐,前 350 年废井田开阡陌,并把都城从栎阳迁到咸阳——就在今天西安西北。这套改革把整个国家改造成一部战争机器;此后一百三十年,六国一个个被从这里发出的军队吞掉。',
 'Shang Yang reformed the state twice — tying rank to battlefield merit in 356 BC, breaking up the old field system in 350 BC and moving the capital from Yueyang to Xianyang, just northwest of today\'s Xi\'an. The reforms remaking the whole state into a machine for war; over the next hundred and thirty years the other six states were swallowed one by one by armies sent out from here.'],
'西安|秦': ['秦统一后咸阳是天下的中心,六国富豪十二万户被迁来此地。城外骊山下修着始皇陵,规模浩大,陪葬坑里成建制地埋着陶制的军队;而阿房宫据近年勘探只建起了夯土台基,并未完工。前 206 年项羽入关,咸阳宫室被焚。',
 'After unification Xianyang was the centre of the world, and a hundred and twenty thousand wealthy households from the conquered states were moved here. The First Emperor\'s tomb was being built under Mount Li outside the city on an enormous scale, with an army in terracotta drawn up in its outer pits. The Epang palace, recent survey suggests, never got past its rammed-earth platform. In 206 BC Xiang Yu entered the passes and the palaces of Xianyang burned.'],
'西安|东汉': ['东汉定都洛阳,长安改称西京,地位降为陪都。190 年董卓挟献帝西迁长安、焚毁洛阳,长安短暂又成了都城;董卓死后关中军阀混战,人口大量流失,这座城元气大伤。',
 'The Eastern Han ruled from Luoyang and Chang\'an became the western capital, second in rank. In 190 Dong Zhuo carried the emperor west to Chang\'an and burned Luoyang, and the city was briefly a capital again; after Dong Zhuo\'s death the warlords of Guanzhong fought among themselves, the population drained away, and the city was left badly weakened.'],
'西安|三国': ['三国时长安属曹魏,是防备蜀汉的西线重镇。诸葛亮五次北伐,目标之一就是关中;据《魏略》记载,魏延曾建议由子午谷奇袭长安,诸葛亮认为太险没有采纳——这条建议后来被反复讨论了一千多年。',
 'Under the Three Kingdoms, Chang\'an belonged to Wei and anchored the western line against Shu Han. Chang\'an was one aim of Zhuge Liang\'s five northern campaigns; The Weilüe records that Wei Yan proposed a surprise dash on the city through the Ziwu valley and that Zhuge Liang judged it too risky and refused — a proposal argued over for more than a thousand years since.'],
'西安|西晋': ['西晋在长安设雍州。永嘉之乱后,晋愍帝退守长安,316 年被匈奴汉国攻破、出城投降,西晋就此灭亡。此后一百多年,长安在前赵、前秦、后秦等政权手里几度易主。',
 'The Western Jin governed Chang\'an as Yongzhou. After the Yongjia disaster, Emperor Min fell back on the city; in 316 the Xiongnu Han state took it and he surrendered outside the gates, ending the Western Jin. For over a century afterwards Chang\'an changed hands among the Former Zhao, Former Qin, Later Qin and others.'],
'西安|南北朝': ['南北朝时长安是西魏、北周的都城。西魏在这里创立府兵制,北周继承并扩充,又复行周礼、灭北齐统一北方;隋文帝杨坚正是从北周的外戚位置上取得政权的,统一南北的班底就在这座城里。',
 'Through the Northern and Southern Dynasties, Chang\'an was the capital of the Western Wei and the Northern Zhou. The Western Wei created the fubing militia system here and the Northern Zhou took it further, revived Zhou ritual, and destroyed the Northern Qi to unify the north. Yang Jian, the founder of the Sui, took power from the position of an imperial in-law at this court — the men who would reunite north and south were already in this city.'],
'西安|隋': ['隋文帝嫌汉长安城旧且水苦,583 年迁到东南另建新城,名大兴城,由宇文恺规划:整齐的里坊、南北中轴、宫城居北。这就是后来唐长安城的底子,面积约八十四平方公里,是当时世界上规模最大的都城之一。',
 'Finding the old Han city cramped and its water brackish, Emperor Wen of Sui moved southeast in 583 and built a new one, Daxing, laid out by Yuwen Kai: regular walled wards, a north-south axis, the palace at the north. This was the foundation of Tang Chang\'an — some eighty-four square kilometres, among the largest planned capitals in the world at the time.'],
'西安|五代十国': ['907 年唐亡时,长安已经空了三年——904 年朱温挟昭宗迁都洛阳,下令拆毁宫室、把木料顺渭水漂走,居民也被驱赶东迁。五代里它先叫大安府、后唐时才复称京兆府,从一国之都降成一个地方州府;此后再没做过统一王朝的首都。',
 'By the time the Tang fell in 907 the city had already stood empty three years: in 904 Zhu Wen had forced the emperor to Luoyang, pulled down the palaces, floated the timber away down the Wei and driven the inhabitants east. Under the Five Dynasties it was first renamed Daan prefecture and only under the Later Tang got its old name Jingzhao back — from capital of an empire to an ordinary provincial seat. It was never the capital of a unified dynasty again.'],
'西安|北宋': ['北宋在这里设永兴军路,长安是西北的军政重镇,面对西夏的前沿。1087 年,唐代的开成石经与一批碑石被集中迁到城里的孔庙保存——这就是西安碑林的开端,今天它藏碑数千,是中国最大的碑石收藏之一。',
 'The Song governed here as Yongxingjun circuit, and Chang\'an was the military and administrative anchor of the northwest, facing the Xia. In 1087 the Tang Kaicheng stone classics and a group of other steles were gathered into the Confucian temple in the city for safekeeping — the beginning of the Forest of Steles, which today holds thousands of inscribed stones and is among the largest such collections in China.'],
'西安|金': ['金与南宋在关中拉锯多年,长安一带反复易手。1231 年蒙古军攻取长安,金在关中的统治结束;连年战乱之后,这一带的户口比北宋时锐减。',
 'The Jin and the Southern Song fought back and forth across Guanzhong for years and the Chang\'an area changed hands repeatedly. In 1231 a Mongol army took the city and Jin rule in Guanzhong ended; after the years of fighting, the registered households of the region had fallen away sharply.'],
'西安|蒙古帝国': ['蒙古取关中后,忽必烈的三子忙哥剌受封安西王,王府冬天驻这里、夏天驻六盘山,城名也一度改称安西。这一带是蒙古经营西北与向四川用兵的后方基地。',
 'After the Mongols took Guanzhong, Kublai\'s third son Mangala was made Prince of Anxi wintering here and summering at Liupanshan, and the city was for a time renamed Anxi. The region served as the Mongol rear base for holding the northwest and for campaigning into Sichuan.'],
'西安|元': ['元代这里是奉元路治所。城市规模远小于唐长安,只相当于唐长安皇城那一块;元末战乱中又受损,直到明初才重新营建。',
 'Under the Yuan the city was the seat of Fengyuan circuit. It was far smaller than Tang Chang\'an, no bigger than the old imperial city precinct, and was damaged again in the wars at the end of the Yuan, waiting until the early Ming to be rebuilt.'],
'西安|明': ['1369 年明军取此城,改名西安——「西安」这个名字从此叫起。1643 年李自成攻下这里,1644 年正月在此建大顺、改称长安,几个月后才北上取北京;这是西安最后一次做一个政权的都城。明初大规模修城,今天西安的城墙就是那时建的,周长十三公里余、高十二米,是中国现存规模最大、保存最完整的古城墙之一。',
 'Ming armies took the city in 1369 and renamed it Xi\'an, western peace — the name it still carries. Li Zicheng took it in 1643 and proclaimed his Shun state here at the start of 1644, restoring the name Chang\'an, before marching north on Beijing a few months later: the last time Xi\'an was any regime\'s capital. The walls were rebuilt on a large scale in the early Ming, and those are the walls that stand today: over thirteen kilometres round and twelve metres high, among the largest and best preserved city walls in China.'],
'西安|清': ['清代西安是陕西省城,城内另筑满城驻防八旗。1900 年八国联军入北京,慈禧与光绪西逃,在西安住了将近一年,朝廷政务一度在这里运转;新政的许多议题就是在这段「西狩」期间定下的。',
 'Under the Qing, Xi\'an was the provincial capital of Shaanxi, with a separate walled quarter inside for the banner garrison. When the allied armies entered Beijing in 1900, the Empress Dowager Cixi and the Guangxu emperor fled west and stayed in Xi\'an for close to a year, with the business of the court running from here for a time; much of the reform agenda that followed was settled during that stay.'],
'西安|民国': ['1936 年 12 月 12 日,张学良、杨虎城在西安扣押了蒋介石,要求停止内战、一致抗日,史称西安事变。事变以和平解决收场,国共第二次合作由此起步——这是二十世纪中国最关键的转折之一。',
 'On 12 December 1936 Zhang Xueliang and Yang Hucheng seized Chiang Kai-shek at Xi\'an and demanded that the civil war stop and the country unite against Japan — the Xi\'an incident. It ended in a negotiated settlement, and the second united front between the Nationalists and the Communists began from it: one of the pivotal turns of twentieth-century China.'],
'西安|共和国': ['1974 年临潼农民打井时挖到陶片,由此发现兵马俑,三个坑估计埋着陶俑陶马八千多件,至今大部分还留在原地没有发掘;1987 年与秦始皇陵一同列入世界遗产。今天的西安是西北最大的城市,也是国内高校与航天工业的重镇之一。',
 'In 1974 farmers digging a well at Lintong struck pottery fragments, and the terracotta army came to light; the three pits are thought to hold more than eight thousand figures and horses, most of them still in the ground, and were listed with the First Emperor\'s tomb as World Heritage in 1987. Xi\'an today is the largest city in the northwest and a centre of universities and of the space industry.'],
'西安|西汉': ['都城长安在今西安西北,未央宫是当时世上最大的宫殿群之一。张骞两次出使西域都从这里出发——丝绸之路的东端起点就定在这座城。',
 'The capital Chang\'an stood just northwest of today\'s Xi\'an, and Weiyang Palace was among the largest palace complexes then on earth. Zhang Qian set out for the Western Regions from here — the eastern end of the Silk Road.'],
'西安|唐': ['唐长安是当时世界上最大的城市之一,人口可能过百万,棋盘般的街坊,中轴朱雀大街宽逾百米。日本遣唐使、粟特商人、各国僧侣都汇在这座城里。',
 'Tang Chang\'an was among the largest cities in the world: a million people, a chessboard of walled wards, and a central avenue over a hundred meters wide. Japanese envoys, Sogdian merchants and monks from across Asia all converged here.'],
'敦煌|西汉': ['汉武帝夺取河西走廊后设四郡,敦煌是最西的一个;再往西出玉门关、阳关,就是西域。此后一千年,它都是丝路进出中国的大门。',
 'After Emperor Wu took the Hexi Corridor, four commanderies were founded — Dunhuang the westernmost. Beyond it lay the Yumen and Yang passes and the Western Regions: for the next thousand years this was the Silk Road\'s gateway into China.'],
'敦煌|唐': ['唐时敦煌称沙州,莫高窟进入全盛,今存洞窟中有相当一部分开凿于隋唐。安史之乱后此地陷于吐蕃六十余年,848 年张议潮起兵赶走吐蕃、收复敦煌,三年后唐朝在这里设归义军,由他统领。',
 'Under the Tang, Dunhuang (then Shazhou) saw the Mogao Caves at their height — a large share the surviving caves were cut in Sui and Tang times. After the An Lushan rebellion it fell to Tibet for six decades, until Zhang Yichao rose and drove the Tibetans out in 848; three years later the Tang made him governor here of the new Return-to-Allegiance Army.'],
'敦煌|东汉': ['东汉的敦煌是经营西域的后方基地:朝廷的诏令、粮草与译员都从这里转运出关,班超在西域经营三十年,与朝廷往来的文书都要走这条路。城东六十多公里外的悬泉置是一座官方驿站,自西汉设郡后就在用,1990 到 1992 年发掘出两万余枚有字简牍,上面记着接待过往使团的账目——连给客人发了几斗米都写着。',
 'Under the Eastern Han, Dunhuang was the rear base for the Western Regions: edicts, grain and interpreters all passed out through it, and the dispatches passing between Ban Chao and the court during his thirty years in the west all went this way. Sixty-odd kilometres east of town stood the Xuanquan post station, in use since the commanderies were founded under the Western Han and excavated between 1990 and 1992: over twenty thousand inscribed wooden slips record the receptions of passing missions, down to how many pecks of grain each guest was issued.'],
'敦煌|三国': ['曹魏的敦煌一度豪强横行,过往胡商常被压价强买。太守仓慈到任后压住豪强、给商队发过所(通行证)、派人护送他们去洛阳;据《三国志》记载,他死后敦煌的官吏百姓「图画其形」,像失去亲人一样难过;西域各国的商人则聚到一起为他发丧,还给他立了祠遥祭。',
 'Under Cao Wei, powerful local families dominated Dunhuang and traders from the west were routinely fleeced. The governor Cang Ci curbed the clans, issued travel passes to caravans and had them escorted on to Luoyang; the Records of the Three Kingdoms says that when he died the officials and townspeople of Dunhuang had his likeness painted and grieved as for a relative, while merchants from across the Western Regions gathered to hold his funeral and set up a shrine to him.'],
'敦煌|西晋': ['西晋时敦煌出了一位译经大师竺法护。他祖上是月氏人,世代住在敦煌,《高僧传》说他通晓三十六国语言;他一生译出《正法华经》等百余部佛经,当时人称他「敦煌菩萨」。',
 'The Western Jin produced Dunhuang\'s great translator, Dharmaraksa. His family were Yuezhi who had lived at Dunhuang for generations, and the Lives of Eminent Monks credits him with thirty-six languages. He turned more than a hundred Buddhist works into Chinese, among them the Lotus Sutra, and his contemporaries called him the Bodhisattva of Dunhuang.'],
'敦煌|隋': ['隋朝只有三十七年,莫高窟却在这段时间集中开凿了一大批洞窟。朝廷重开西域商路,来往的官员和商人出钱造窟祈平安;波斯风格的连珠纹在这一时期的壁画上大量出现。',
 'The Sui lasted only thirty-seven years, yet a great many new caves were cut at Mogao in that time. The court reopened the roads west, and officials and merchants passing through paid for caves to pray for a safe journey; Persian-style pearl-roundel patterns spread through the murals of these years.'],
'敦煌|吐蕃': ['约 786 年吐蕃攻下沙州(敦煌),具体年份史料有几种说法。唐军守将阎朝困守了十来年才开城,条件是不把一城百姓迁走。吐蕃统治的六十多年里莫高窟没有停工,后来藏经洞出土的写本中有数以千计是用吐蕃文写的。',
 'Around 786 the Tibetan Empire took Shazhou (Dunhuang); the sources give more than one date. The Tang commander Yan Chao had held out for about a decade and opened the gates only on the condition that the townspeople not be deported. Cave-cutting at Mogao never stopped through the sixty-odd years of Tibetan rule, and thousands of the manuscripts later found in the Library Cave are written in Tibetan.'],
'敦煌|西夏': ['张议潮之后,敦煌由归义军自治了将近两百年。李元昊称帝前两年,西夏取得瓜、沙二州,这一带此后归西夏治下也近两百年。莫高窟和附近的榆林窟都留下西夏时期的壁画,其中榆林窟里画着一位僧人和猴形的行者牵马取经——比《西游记》成书早了三百多年。',
 'After Zhang Yichao, Dunhuang governed itself under the Guiyi command for close to two hundred years. Two years before Li Yuanhao declared himself emperor, Western Xia took Guazhou and Shazhou, and the oasis stayed under Western Xia for close to two centuries as well. Both Mogao and the nearby Yulin Caves keep Western Xia murals; the Yulin Caves show a monk and a monkey-shaped attendant leading a horse on a scripture-fetching journey — over three hundred years before Journey to the West was written.'],
'敦煌|蒙古帝国': ['1227 年蒙古灭西夏,敦煌随之易主。蒙古打通了东西两端的驿路,《马可波罗行纪》里就专门写到沙州(敦煌)人的风俗,说明这座城的名字当时已经传到了欧洲。',
 'In 1227 the Mongols destroyed Western Xia and Dunhuang changed hands. With the post roads open from end to end, The Travels of Marco Polo gives a passage to the customs of Shazhou (Dunhuang) — a sign that the city\'s name had by then reached Europe.'],
'敦煌|元': ['元朝在这里设沙州路。莫高窟第 3 窟的千手千眼观音是元代壁画的代表作,线条细得像刻上去的;莫高窟还留下一块 1348 年的碑,用梵、藏、汉、西夏、八思巴、回鹘六种文字刻着同一句真言——这条路上走过多少种人,碑上写得明明白白。',
 'The Yuan administered the oasis as Shazhou Route. The thousand-armed Guanyin in Mogao Cave 3 is the masterpiece of Yuan wall painting, its lines as fine as engraving; and a stele of 1348 survives at Mogao carved with one prayer in six scripts — Sanskrit, Tibetan, Chinese, Tangut, Phags-pa and Uyghur — a plain record of how many kinds of people used this road.'],
'敦煌|清': ['雍正年间从甘肃各地迁来两千多户人家屯垦,1725 年设沙州卫,1760 年改称敦煌县——「敦煌」这个汉唐旧名时隔近千年重新用回来。1900 年道士王圆箓在莫高窟清理积沙时打开了一间封住的小室,里面堆着五万余件写本与绢画,这就是藏经洞。它当初为什么被封起来,到今天也没有定论:有人说是躲战乱藏起来的,有人说是把不用的旧经卷集中封存——这是敦煌留下的谜之一。七年后英国人斯坦因、次年法国人伯希和先后用少量银两换走了其中的精华。',
 'In the Yongzheng reign some two thousand households were resettled here to farm; a garrison was set up in 1725, and in 1760 the place was renamed Dunhuang County, reviving a Han and Tang name after nearly a thousand years. In 1900 the Daoist caretaker Wang Yuanlu, clearing sand at Mogao, opened a sealed chamber packed with over fifty thousand manuscripts and paintings — the Library Cave. Why it was sealed up in the first place is still unsettled: some say the contents were hidden from an invasion, others that worn-out scrolls were simply walled away together. It is one of the things Dunhuang has not told anyone. Seven years later Aurel Stein, and the year after him Paul Pelliot, carried off the best of it for small sums of silver.'],
'敦煌|民国': ['1941 年起张大千在这里临摹壁画两年多,摹本影响很大,但他为看下层而剥去表层壁画的做法至今仍有争议。常书鸿 1936 年从法国回国,1943 年带着一批人住进窟前的破庙,1944 年国立敦煌艺术研究所成立——这是莫高窟第一次有了专职看守和修复的人。',
 'From 1941 Zhang Daqian spent over two years copying the murals here; his copies were widely influential, but his practice of stripping outer layers to reach the paintings beneath is disputed to this day. Chang Shuhong had come home from France in 1936, and in 1943 he moved with a small team into a ruined temple below the cliff; the National Dunhuang Art Research Institute followed in 1944 — the first time Mogao had staff paid to guard and repair it.'],
'敦煌|共和国': ['1961 年莫高窟列入首批全国重点文物保护单位,1987 年成为世界文化遗产。樊锦诗在这里工作了半个多世纪,推动把洞窟逐个拍成高精度数字影像——这项工作还在做,已完成的部分放上了「数字敦煌」,进不去的窟在屏幕上也能走一遍。窟内则严格限制人数与停留时间——人呼出的水汽会让壁画起甲脱落。',
 'Mogao was listed among China\'s first nationally protected sites in 1961 and became a World Heritage Site in 1987. Fan Jinshi has worked here for over half a century and drove the effort to photograph the caves one by one at high resolution — work still under way; what is finished has gone onto Digital Dunhuang, so caves closed to visitors can be walked through on a screen. Inside, visitor numbers and dwell time are tightly capped — moisture from human breath makes the paint blister and flake.'],
'敦煌|南北朝': ['莫高窟现存最早的几个洞窟就开凿在五世纪,北魏时期的第 257 窟画着鹿王本生——一头九色的鹿救了溺水的人,那人转头就为赏金去告发它。这幅壁画后来被改编成动画片,今天很多人认得这个故事,却不一定知道它画在敦煌的墙上,已经一千五百年了。',
 'The earliest surviving caves at Mogao were cut in the fifth century. Cave 257, from the Northern Wei, carries the Deer King jataka — a nine-coloured deer saves a drowning man, who promptly turns him in for the reward. The painting was later made into an animated film, and plenty of people who know the story do not know it has been on a wall at Dunhuang for fifteen hundred years.'],
'敦煌|东察合台·叶尔羌': ['1516 年吐鲁番的满速儿汗亲率骑兵打到嘉峪关下。明朝的反应不是出兵,是一步步往里收:关外的卫所此前已陆续内迁,到 1528 年索性把嘉峪关关上——敦煌从此被留在关外。此后近两百年,这一带在西边来的蒙兀儿诸汗手里,汉文史料几乎不再写到它。一座在汉唐是「大门」的城,变成了门外的地方;要等到清朝雍正年间从甘肃各地迁人回来屯垦,它才重新有户口。',
 'When Mansur Khan of Turfan rode up to the Jiayu Pass in 1516, the Ming answer was not to march out but to draw inward step by step: the garrisons beyond the wall had already been pulled in, and in 1528 the pass itself was shut — leaving Dunhuang outside. For nearly two centuries afterwards this country lay in the hands of the Moghul khans to the west, and Chinese sources almost stop mentioning it. A city that had been the gate under the Han and Tang became a place outside the gate; not until the Yongzheng reign of the Qing, when households were moved back in from across Gansu, did it have a registered population again.'],
'洛阳|二里头·夏': ['二里头遗址就在洛阳盆地东边的偃师,是中原目前所知最早的宫城之一:宫殿中轴对称、有专门的青铜作坊,出土过绿松石拼成的龙形器和最早的一批青铜爵。中国学界多认为它对应文献里的夏,但没有出土文字,这个对应仍在争论中。',
 'The Erlitou site lies at Yanshi, on the east side of the Luoyang basin — among the earliest palace cities yet known on the Central Plains, with axially planned halls, dedicated bronze workshops, a dragon figure pieced together from turquoise, and some of the earliest bronze ritual cups. Chinese scholars generally match it with the Xia of the texts; no writing has been found there, and the match is still argued over.'],
'洛阳|商': ['商朝早期在偃师筑过一座城,城墙、宫殿与仓储都有,规模不小,它是汤都西亳,还是灭夏后设在这一带的军事重镇,学界至今没有定论。同时期郑州一带也有一座更大的商城,商的政治中心此后一直在那一带,最后北移到安阳的殷墟,洛阳盆地退居次要。',
 'The early Shang walled a city at Yanshi — ramparts, halls and granaries, and not a small one — whether it was the capital Xibo or a garrison town planted here after the Shang overthrew the Xia is still unsettled. A larger Shang city stood at Zhengzhou at the same time, and the Shang centre stayed in that area before moving north at last to Yinxu at Anyang, leaving the Luoyang basin in second place.'],
'洛阳|西周': ['周灭商后,周公在这里营建成周,把商的遗民迁来管束,也让周人多一个控制东方的据点。西周青铜器「何尊」的铭文里有「宅兹中国」四个字——目前所知「中国」二字最早的出处,说的正是这座城所在的天下之中。',
 'After the Zhou overthrew the Shang, the Duke of Zhou built Chengzhou here, moving Shang subjects in to be watched over and giving the Zhou a second seat from which to hold the east. The inscription on the Western Zhou He zun vessel contains the phrase "dwell in the central state" — the earliest known written occurrence of the words that became China\'s name for itself, and it refers to this very place, the centre of the world as they saw it.'],
'洛阳|春秋': ['前 770 年平王东迁,周王室搬到洛邑,从此只剩天子的名分、没有天子的实力。诸侯来朝越来越少,王室内部还打过王子朝之乱,连典籍都被带走一批。相传孔子曾到洛邑向老子问礼——据说老子当时正是周的守藏史,管着王室藏书。',
 'In 770 BC King Ping moved east to Luoyi, and from then on the Zhou king had the title but not the strength. Fewer and fewer lords came to court, and a succession war — the revolt of Prince Chao — even carried off part of the royal library. Confucius is said to have come here to ask Laozi about ritual; Laozi is said to have been the Zhou keeper of the archives at the time.'],
'洛阳|战国': ['战国的洛邑只是周天子最后一小块地,还分裂成东周、西周两个小公国。前 256 年秦军攻下这里,周赧王降秦,延续八百年的周朝就此结束——从此天下再没有名义上的共主。',
 'By the Warring States, Luoyi was the last scrap of land the Zhou king held, and even that had split into two tiny principalities. In 256 BC a Qin army took it and King Nan submitted, ending eight centuries of Zhou — and with it the last nominal overlord of all the states.'],
'洛阳|秦': ['秦统一前,吕不韦已被封为文信侯,食邑就在洛阳,据记载有十万户——这是他一生最大的一块封地。他组织门客编的《吕氏春秋》,书成后挂在秦都咸阳的市门上,说改得动一个字就赏千金,「一字千金」由此而来。统一之后,洛阳属三川郡。',
 'Before the unification, Lü Buwei had already been made Marquis Wenxin with Luoyang as his estate — a hundred thousand households, by the record, the largest holding of his life. The Lüshi Chunqiu his retainers compiled was hung at the market gate of the Qin capital Xianyang with a thousand gold pieces offered to anyone who could improve a single character, which is where the phrase "a thousand gold for one word" comes from. After unification Luoyang lay in Sanchuan commandery.'],
'洛阳|西汉': ['刘邦称帝后本想定都洛阳,娄敬劝他说关中有山河之险、洛阳四面受敌,张良附议,于是改都长安。整个西汉洛阳都是关东最大的都会之一,粮食与漕运的枢纽,也是诸侯与商贾往来的中心。',
 'When Liu Bang took the imperial title he meant to make Luoyang his capital, until Lou Jing argued that Guanzhong was ringed by mountains and rivers while Luoyang lay open on all four sides; Zhang Liang agreed, and Chang\'an was chosen instead. Through the Western Han, Luoyang remained among the greatest cities east of the passes, the hinge of the grain transport and the meeting place of nobles and merchants.'],
'洛阳|东汉': ['东汉定都洛阳,城里办起太学,鼎盛时太学生以万计。蔡伦在这里改进造纸术并献给朝廷;张衡在这里造出候风地动仪;175 年起把儒家经典刻成熹平石经立在太学门外,天天有人来抄。白马寺相传是这时建的,通常被称作中国最早的佛寺之一。',
 'The Eastern Han made Luoyang its capital and re-established the Imperial Academy here, whose students at its height were counted in the tens of thousands. Cai Lun improved papermaking here and presented it to the throne; Zhang Heng built his seismoscope here; and from 175 the Confucian classics were cut on stone and set up outside the Academy, where people came daily to copy them. The White Horse Temple is traditionally dated to this period and is usually called one of the first Buddhist temples in China.'],
'洛阳|三国': ['曹丕代汉后仍以洛阳为都。此前董卓挟献帝西迁时一把火烧了洛阳,宫室化为焦土,曹魏是在废墟上重建的;这座重建的洛阳城,后来被西晋、北魏一路沿用。',
 'When Cao Pi took the throne from the Han he kept Luoyang as his capital. Dong Zhuo had burned the city when he carried the last Han emperor west, leaving the palaces in ashes, so the Wei rebuilt on the ruins — and the city they rebuilt was used in turn by the Western Jin and the Northern Wei.'],
'洛阳|西晋': ['西晋都洛阳。左思写成《三都赋》,城里人争相传抄,纸都涨了价——「洛阳纸贵」说的就是这件事。311 年匈奴汉国的军队攻破洛阳,烧宫室、掳晋怀帝,史称永嘉之乱;中原士族大批南渡,北方进入五胡十六国的百余年分裂。',
 'The Western Jin ruled from Luoyang. When Zuo Si finished his Rhapsody on the Three Capitals, so many people copied it out that the price of paper rose — which is the origin of the phrase "paper dear in Luoyang." In 311 the armies of the Xiongnu Han state broke into the city, burned the palaces and carried off the emperor: the Yongjia disaster. The great families fled south in numbers, and the north broke into a century of rival kingdoms.'],
'洛阳|隋': ['隋炀帝 605 年下令营建东都洛阳,据记载每月征调民夫两百万。大运河也以洛阳为中心开凿,南接江淮、北通涿郡,城中东北的含嘉仓是当时最大的粮仓之一,现代发掘出的仓窖里还留着炭化的谷物。',
 'In 605 Emperor Yang of Sui ordered an eastern capital built at Luoyang; the records speak of two million labourers called up each month. The Grand Canal was dug with Luoyang at its centre, reaching south to the Huai and north to Zhuo commandery, and the Hanjia granary in the northeast of the city was among the largest of its day — excavated pits there still held carbonised grain.'],
'洛阳|唐': ['唐初以洛阳为东都。684 年武则天临朝称制,把它改称「神都」;690 年称帝后,朝廷长期驻在这里。龙门石窟的卢舍那大佛是稍早的高宗朝开凿的,675 年完工、高十七米余,武则天当时是皇后,出了一笔脂粉钱相助;相传大佛的面容参照了她。城里的南市有数千家店铺,是当时最大的市场之一。',
 'The early Tang made Luoyang the eastern capital. In 684 Wu Zetian, then regent, renamed it the Divine Capital; after she took the throne in 690 the court sat here for years. The Vairocana Buddha at the Longmen grottoes was carved slightly earlier, under Emperor Gaozong, finished in 675 and over seventeen metres tall — she was empress consort then and gave money towards it, and its face is said to have been modelled on hers. The southern market in the city held thousands of shops, among the largest of the age.'],
'洛阳|五代十国': ['五代里后梁、后唐、后晋都一度以洛阳为都,但换朝太快、战乱太密,城池反复受损。到后周与北宋定都开封之后,洛阳的政治地位就让给了下游那座城。',
 'The Later Liang, Later Tang and Later Jin each held court at Luoyang for a time, but the dynasties changed too fast and the fighting was too constant, and the city was damaged again and again. Once the Later Zhou and then the Song settled on Kaifeng, Luoyang gave up its political place to the city downstream.'],
'洛阳|北宋': ['北宋定都开封,洛阳作西京,成了退居的士大夫聚居之地。司马光在这里住了十五年编《资治通鉴》,邵雍、程颐也在城中讲学;欧阳修记洛阳牡丹「天下第一」,这座城的牡丹名声就是从宋代传开的。',
 'The Song capital was Kaifeng and Luoyang served as the western capital, filling up with officials who had stepped back from court. Sima Guang lived here fifteen years compiling his Comprehensive Mirror; Shao Yong and Cheng Yi taught here too. Ouyang Xiu wrote that Luoyang\'s peonies were the finest under heaven, and the city\'s reputation for them dates from the Song.'],
'洛阳|金': ['北宋的西京繁华在靖康之后终结,城区大为收缩。1217 年金把洛阳升为中京金昌府——那时金已被蒙古逼得迁都汴京,洛阳成了新都西边的屏障,此后连年受兵,再没恢复到唐宋时的规模。',
 'The prosperity of the Song western capital ended with the fall of the Northern Song and the built-up area shrank sharply. In 1217 the Jin raised Luoyang to Central Capital, Jinchang prefecture — by then the Mongols had pushed the Jin court south to Kaifeng, and Luoyang became the shield west of the new capital, fought over year after year, never returning to its Tang and Song scale.'],
'洛阳|蒙古帝国': ['1234 年蒙宋联军灭金,金亡后南宋想趁虚收复三京,出兵进入已成空城的洛阳,粮草跟不上、随即被蒙古军击退——史称端平入洛。这一战成了蒙古全面南下攻宋的由头。',
 'In 1234 Mongol and Song armies together destroyed the Jin. The Song then tried to recover the three old capitals while the north was empty, marching into a deserted Luoyang; supplies failed to follow and the Mongols drove them out — the Duanping expedition. It became the pretext for the full Mongol campaign against the Song.'],
'洛阳|元': ['元代设河南府路,治所就在洛阳,但它不再是任何一级的都城。全国的漕运与政治重心已移到大都与江南一线,这座做过十三个王朝都城的城,从此退出了中心舞台。',
 'Under the Yuan it was the seat of Henan-fu circuit, but no longer a capital of any rank. The empire\'s grain transport and political weight had shifted to the Dadu–Jiangnan axis, and the city that had been capital to a long succession of dynasties left the centre of the stage for good.'],
'洛阳|明': ['明神宗把儿子朱常洵封为福王,就藩洛阳,据记载婚礼与府第耗银极巨,而当地连年灾荒。1641 年李自成攻破洛阳,福王被杀,王府被焚——这件事在当时传得很广,也常被后人拿来说明明末的财政与民生。',
 'The Wanli emperor made his son Zhu Changxun Prince of Fu and sent him to Luoyang; the sums spent on his wedding and residence were, by the record, enormous, in a region suffering years of failed harvests. In 1641 Li Zicheng stormed the city, the prince was killed and the palace burned — news that travelled far at the time, and an episode still cited about the finances and the hunger of the late Ming.'],
'洛阳|清': ['清代洛阳是河南府治所,一座中等府城。真正让它重新被人注意的是清末民初的铁路与考古:汴洛铁路(后来陇海线的一段)从城边通过,而北邙山上历代墓葬密集,大量唐三彩与墓志由此出土流散,「洛阳铲」这种探墓工具的名字也是这时叫开的。',
 'Under the Qing, Luoyang was the seat of Henan prefecture, a middling walled city. What brought it back to notice was the railway and archaeology of the late Qing and early Republic: the Bianluo railway, later part of the Longhai line, ran past the city, and the hills of Beimang to the north were dense with tombs of every dynasty, from which quantities of Tang three-colour ware and epitaph stones came to light and were dispersed. The Luoyang spade, a tomb-prospecting tool, takes its name from these years.'],
'洛阳|民国': ['1932 年一二八事变后,国民政府一度迁到洛阳办公,把这里定为「行都」,前后约十个月。抗战期间洛阳是中原战场的要点,1944 年豫湘桂战役中经历过激烈巷战,城区损毁严重。',
 'After the Shanghai incident of January 1932 the Nationalist government moved to Luoyang for about ten months and declared it the temporary capital. In the war with Japan the city was a key point on the central front, and in the Ichigo offensive of 1944 it saw heavy street fighting that left much of it in ruins.'],
'洛阳|共和国': ['一五计划把洛阳选作重工业基地,苏联援建的项目里有拖拉机厂、轴承厂、矿山机器厂,新城区就是那时在旧城以西整片建起来的。第一台「东方红」拖拉机 1958 年在这里下线。',
 'The first Five-Year Plan chose Luoyang as a heavy-industry base, and the Soviet-aided projects here included a tractor works, a bearing works and a mining-machinery works; the new districts west of the old city were laid out whole in those years. The first Dongfanghong tractor came off the line here in 1958.'],
'洛阳|南北朝': ['494 年,北魏孝文帝把都城从平城迁到洛阳,推行说汉话、改汉姓的全面汉化。城南伊水两岸的龙门石窟,就是在迁都前后开凿起来的。',
 'In 494 Emperor Xiaowen of Northern Wei moved his capital from Pingcheng to Luoyang and pushed sweeping sinicization — Chinese speech, Chinese surnames. The Longmen Grottoes south of the city began to be carved at just this time.'],
'开封|二里头·夏': ['开封一带在二里头时期属于中原东缘的边地,离洛阳盆地的那个王权中心约二百公里。这一带地势低平、黄河从旁边过,聚落多沿高地分布——低洼与水患,是这块土地此后三千年一直要面对的事。',
 'In Erlitou times the Kaifeng area lay on the eastern edge of the Central Plains, some two hundred kilometres from the seat of power in the Luoyang basin. The land here is low and flat with the Yellow River running past it, and settlements kept to the higher ground — low ground and flooding are what this place has had to deal with for the three thousand years since.'],
'开封|商': ['商代这一带有聚落但不是中心,商的都城在西边的偃师、郑州与安阳一线。开封真正的起点通常从春秋算起——那时郑庄公在这儿筑城屯粮,取「启拓封疆」之意叫启封,汉代避景帝刘启的名讳才改成开封。',
 'There were settlements here under the Shang but no centre; the Shang capitals lay west of it, at Yanshi, Zhengzhou and Anyang. Kaifeng\'s own beginning is usually counted from the Spring and Autumn period, when Duke Zhuang of Zheng walled a granary town here and named it Qifeng, "opening the frontier"; under the Han the name was changed to Kaifeng to avoid an emperor\'s given name.'],
'开封|西周': ['西周时这一带属于王畿以东的诸侯地界,离成周洛邑约二百公里。真正把开封放上地图的是东周的郑国与魏国,那要再等几百年。',
 'Under the Western Zhou this was territory of the lords east of the royal domain, about two hundred kilometres from Chengzhou at Luoyang. What actually put Kaifeng on the map was the state of Zheng and then of Wei, in the Eastern Zhou — several centuries later.'],
'开封|春秋': ['郑庄公在今开封城南筑启封城储粮备战,这是开封见于记载的开端。郑国夹在晋楚两个大国之间,是春秋时被反复争夺的中间地带,「郑伯克段于鄢」这类故事就出在这里。',
 'Duke Zhuang of Zheng walled a town called Qifeng south of today\'s Kaifeng to store grain against war — the first Kaifeng that enters the record. Zheng lay squeezed between the great powers of Jin and Chu and was fought over throughout the Spring and Autumn period; the well-known tale of Duke Zhuang and his brother at Yan belongs here.'],
'开封|战国': ['前 361 年魏惠王把都城从安邑迁到大梁——就在今天开封城下。大梁靠鸿沟连起黄河与淮河水系,是当时中原水运的枢纽。前 225 年秦将王贲引黄河水灌大梁,三个月后城墙塌了,魏国就此灭亡。',
 'In 361 BC King Hui of Wei moved his capital from Anyi to Daliang — directly beneath today\'s Kaifeng. Daliang sat on the Honggou canal that joined the Yellow River system to the Huai, the hinge of water transport on the Central Plains. In 225 BC the Qin general Wang Ben turned the Yellow River onto it; after three months the walls collapsed and the state of Wei was finished.'],
'开封|秦': ['秦灭魏后在这里设浚仪县,属砀郡。被水淹过的大梁一时难以恢复,秦代的开封只是一座普通县城——它下一次成为都城,要等到一千一百年后。',
 'After destroying Wei, Qin made this Junyi county in Dang commandery. Flooded Daliang was slow to recover, and under the Qin, Kaifeng was an ordinary county town. It would be eleven hundred years before it was a capital again.'],
'开封|西汉': ['西汉的开封叫浚仪,属陈留郡。这一带是关东的产粮区,漕粮经鸿沟旧道运往关中;陈留在汉代是交通要冲,后来三国故事里常出现的「陈留」就是这里。',
 'Under the Western Han the place was called Junyi, in Chenliu commandery. This was grain country east of the passes, and the tax grain went up to Guanzhong along the old Honggou channel. Chenliu was a road junction in Han times — the same Chenliu that turns up often in the Three Kingdoms stories.'],
'开封|东汉': ['东汉的浚仪仍属陈留。这一带世家大族多,曹操起兵就是在陈留散家财、募兵五千——那是他事业的起点。黄河在东汉经王景治理后安流数百年,这一带因此有过一段较稳的日子。',
 'Junyi remained part of Chenliu under the Eastern Han. The area had many great families, and it was at Chenliu that Cao Cao spent his family fortune to raise five thousand men — the beginning of his career. After Wang Jing\'s works on the Yellow River in the Eastern Han the river ran quietly for centuries, and the district had a comparatively settled spell.'],
'开封|三国': ['三国时这里属曹魏兖州陈留郡,是中原腹地。曹魏在这一带大规模屯田,把流民和士兵编组起来官给牛种、分成交租——粮食问题先稳住,才谈得上打仗。',
 'Under the Three Kingdoms this was Chenliu commandery in Wei\'s Yanzhou, deep in the Central Plains. Wei ran large military-agricultural colonies here, organising refugees and soldiers into units, supplying oxen and seed and taking a share of the crop — feeding the armies first, and only then fighting.'],
'开封|西晋': ['西晋的浚仪属陈留国。八王之乱把中原打得残破,永嘉之后这一带反复易主,人口大量南迁;直到北魏统一北方,这里才慢慢缓过来。',
 'Junyi under the Western Jin belonged to the princedom of Chenliu. The War of the Eight Princes wrecked the Central Plains, and after the Yongjia disaster the district changed hands repeatedly and its people moved south in numbers. Only when the Northern Wei unified the north did it begin to recover.'],
'开封|南北朝': ['南北朝时这里长期是南北对峙的中间地带,黄河与淮河之间的这片平原是拉锯区,城池筑了又毁。北魏统一北方后设梁州、后改汴州——「汴」这个字从此和这座城连在一起。',
 'Through the Northern and Southern Dynasties this was middle ground between the rival courts; the plain between the Yellow River and the Huai was fought over back and forth, and its towns were built and destroyed by turns. After the Northern Wei unified the north it set up Liangzhou here, later renamed Bianzhou — and the character Bian has been attached to the city ever since.'],
'开封|隋': ['隋炀帝开通济渠,把黄河的水引到淮河去,汴州正卡在这条运河上。从此南方的粮食要进中原、进关中,大都得从这座城门口过——开封后来能成为国都,底子就是这条河打下的。',
 'Emperor Yang of Sui cut the Tongji canal, carrying Yellow River water down to the Huai, and Bianzhou sat squarely on it. From then on grain coming north from the south had to pass this city on its way to the Central Plains and the capital region — and the canal is why Kaifeng could later be a capital at all.'],
'开封|唐': ['唐代汴州是运河上的大码头,漕船在这里集散,城市因此比前朝繁盛得多。安史之乱后中央要靠江淮的钱粮续命,这条运河和守着运河的汴州就成了命脉;藩镇割据时期,谁据有汴州谁就掐着朝廷的粮道。',
 'Tang Bianzhou was a great wharf on the canal, where the grain barges gathered and dispersed, and the city grew far busier than before. After the An Lushan rebellion the court lived on the taxes of the Huai and Yangtze country, and the canal — and the city that guarded it — became its lifeline; in the age of the warlords, whoever held Bianzhou had a hand on the court\'s grain.'],
'开封|五代十国': ['五代里后梁、后晋、后汉、后周都定都开封,只有后唐都洛阳。选这里是因为运河:军队与朝廷都要吃饭,而粮食从南方来。后周世宗柴荣在这里扩建外城、疏浚运河,为北宋的都城打好了底子。',
 'Of the Five Dynasties, the Later Liang, Later Jin, Later Han and Later Zhou all had their capital at Kaifeng; only the Later Tang chose Luoyang. The reason was the canal: armies and courts have to eat, and the grain came from the south. Emperor Shizong of the Later Zhou extended the outer walls and dredged the canal here, laying the ground for the Song capital that followed.'],
'开封|金': ['1127 年金军攻破开封,掳走徽钦二帝,北宋灭亡,史称靖康之变。金后来把都城从燕京南迁到这里,称南京开封府。1233 年蒙古围城,城内瘟疫大作,次年金亡。',
 'The Jin took Kaifeng in 1127 and carried off two emperors — the Jingkang catastrophe that ended the Northern Song. The Jin later moved their own capital south from Yanjing to this city, calling it the Southern Capital, Kaifeng prefecture. In 1233 the Mongols besieged it, plague broke out inside the walls, and the Jin fell the next year.'],
'开封|蒙古帝国': ['1233 年蒙古军围开封,城中疫死者极多;次年金亡。1234 年南宋想趁虚北上收复三京,一度进入开封,粮草跟不上随即被蒙古军击退——这就是端平入洛,也成了蒙古全面攻宋的由头。',
 'The Mongols besieged Kaifeng in 1233 and great numbers died of plague inside; the Jin fell the following year. In 1234 the Southern Song marched north to recover the three old capitals and briefly entered Kaifeng, but supplies failed and the Mongols drove them back — the Duanping expedition, which became the pretext for the full Mongol war on the Song.'],
'开封|元': ['元代开封是河南江北行省的治所。黄河在这几百年里改道频繁,开封城几次被淤埋抬高;今天在地下叠着好几座不同年代的开封城,「城摞城」是这座城独有的地下景观。',
 'Under the Yuan, Kaifeng was the seat of Henan-Jiangbei province. The Yellow River shifted course often in these centuries and the city was silted over and raised more than once; several Kaifengs of different ages now lie stacked underground — a "city upon city" found nowhere else.'],
'开封|明': ['明代开封是周王的封地,城市恢复了不少。1642 年李自成围城,守军与围城方在河堤上相持,黄河决口灌城,城内死伤极重、几成废墟——决堤责任在哪一方,史料各执一词,至今没有定论。',
 'Ming Kaifeng was the seat of the Prince of Zhou and recovered a good deal. In 1642, with Li Zicheng besieging it, defenders and besiegers faced each other along the river dykes; the Yellow River broke through and flooded the city, killing enormous numbers and leaving it near ruin. Which side breached the dyke is told differently by different sources and has never been settled.'],
'开封|清': ['清代开封是河南省城。黄河年年要防,城墙外的大堤越修越高,城反而低于河床——「悬河」这个词说的就是这一带。1841 年黄河又一次决口围困省城,林则徐被派来堵口,前后耗时半年。',
 'Under the Qing, Kaifeng was the provincial capital of Henan. The Yellow River had to be guarded every year and the dykes outside the walls were raised higher and higher, until the city lay below the riverbed — the "suspended river" of this stretch. When the river broke again in 1841 and cut the provincial capital off, Lin Zexu was sent to close the breach, which took half a year.'],
'开封|民国': ['民国的开封仍是河南省会,直到 1954 年省会才迁往郑州——郑州占了铁路的便宜,京汉与陇海两条线在那里交会。1938 年黄河花园口决堤,河水改道南下,开封以东大片地区成为黄泛区。',
 'Kaifeng remained the provincial capital of Henan through the Republic, until the seat moved to Zhengzhou in 1954 — Zhengzhou had the railways, where the Beijing–Hankou and Longhai lines crossed. When the Yellow River dykes were cut at Huayuankou in 1938 the river turned south, and a great stretch of country east of Kaifeng became the flooded zone.'],
'开封|共和国': ['今天的开封是一座中等城市,靠宋代的名声和地下的遗址活着。城墙、铁塔、繁塔与相国寺还在;地下的北宋皇城遗址在明清开封城之下数米,只做过局部发掘——大部分仍埋在城市底下没有动。',
 'Kaifeng today is a middling city living on its Song reputation and what lies under it. The walls, the Iron Pagoda, the Fan Pagoda and the Xiangguo temple still stand; the Northern Song palace city lies several metres beneath the Ming and Qing town and has only been dug in patches — most of it is still under the modern streets, untouched.'],
'开封|北宋': ['汴京是《清明上河图》画下的那座城:人口可能过百万,街市通宵不禁,是当时世界上最繁华的城市之一。',
 'Bianjing is the city painted in "Along the River During Qingming": perhaps over a million people, streets open through the night — one of the most prosperous cities then on earth.'],
'杭州|秦': ['前 222 年秦灭楚、降越君后,在这里设钱唐县,属会稽郡。那时的杭州还是钱塘江口的一片滩涂,咸潮倒灌、可耕地少,县城只能设在灵隐山下的高处——今天的西湖那时还是与海相通的一个浅湾。',
 'After Qin destroyed Chu in 222 BC and took the submission of Yue, it made this Qiantang county, under Kuaiji commandery. Hangzhou was then a stretch of tidal flat at the mouth of the Qiantang river, salt water pushing inland and little land worth ploughing, so the county seat had to sit on high ground below Lingyin hill — and what is now the West Lake was still a shallow bay open to the sea.'],
'杭州|西汉': ['西汉的钱唐仍是会稽郡下一个小县。这一带真正的难题是潮水:钱塘江口的喇叭形地形让海潮特别猛,农田常被咸水泡坏——此后一千多年,杭州的历史有一大半是和潮水打交道的历史。',
 'Qiantang was still a small county of Kuaiji under the Western Han. The real problem here was the tide: the funnel shape of the river mouth drives the sea in hard, and fields were regularly ruined by salt water. For the next thousand years and more, much of Hangzhou\'s history is the history of dealing with that tide.'],
'杭州|东汉': ['据记载,东汉时华信在这里主持修筑防海大塘,把咸潮挡在外面,湾内的水逐渐淡化。西湖本是钱塘江泥沙把湾口淤住形成的潟湖,这道塘让它最终与海隔断。有了这道塘,钱塘江北岸才有了成片的农田和一座能长大的城。',
 'The record has it that in the Eastern Han one Hua Xin organised the building of a great sea wall here to keep the salt tide out; the water inside gradually turned fresh. The lake was already a lagoon, closed off by silt from the river; the wall finally cut it from the sea. With the wall in place, the north bank of the Qiantang finally had continuous farmland and a town that could grow.'],
'杭州|三国': ['三国时钱唐属东吴。孙吴经营江南,开垦、筑塘、通水道,长江以南的开发就是从这几十年真正起步的;钱唐这样的沿海小县,也是在这股开发潮里慢慢有了人烟。',
 'Qiantang belonged to Wu under the Three Kingdoms. Wu set about developing the south — clearing land, building embankments, opening waterways — and the real settlement of the country below the Yangtze begins in these decades. Small coastal counties like Qiantang filled up slowly in that same tide of development.'],
'杭州|西晋': ['西晋的钱唐仍属吴郡。永嘉之乱后北方人口大批南迁,江南的人口与耕地在此后两百年间成倍增长;杭州湾一带的开发,也是从这批移民带来的劳力与技术开始的。',
 'Qiantang remained part of Wu commandery under the Western Jin. After the Yongjia disaster people came south from the north in great numbers, and over the next two centuries the population and farmland of the lower Yangtze multiplied. The development of the Hangzhou bay country begins with the labour and the techniques those migrants brought.'],
'杭州|东晋·十六国': ['相传灵隐寺建于东晋咸和元年(326),开山的是印度僧人慧理——他见山峰奇秀,说这是「仙灵所隐」,寺名由此而来。此后一千六百多年,灵隐寺屡毁屡建,始终是江南最有名的寺院之一。',
 'Lingyin temple is traditionally dated to 326, founded by the Indian monk Huili, who is said to have looked at the strange peaks and declared this a place where immortals hid — which is where the name comes from. Destroyed and rebuilt many times over the sixteen centuries since, it has remained among the best known monasteries in the south.'],
'杭州|南北朝': ['南朝时这一带先后属吴郡、钱唐郡。江南在宋齐梁陈治下人口稠密、佛寺极多,杭州湾沿岸的水利与围垦也在这时继续推进——为一百多年后杭州能成为运河终点做好了准备。',
 'Under the Southern Dynasties the district belonged first to Wu and later to Qiantang commandery. The south was populous under the Song, Qi, Liang and Chen and full of Buddhist temples, and the diking and reclamation along Hangzhou bay went on through these centuries — preparing the ground for the city to become a canal terminus a hundred years later.'],
'杭州|隋': ['589 年隋灭陈,在这里设杭州——「杭州」这个名字从此叫起。更要紧的是大运河:江南运河的南端就在杭州,从此江南的粮食与丝绸可以经水路一路运到洛阳、长安,这座小县城因运河而变成了大码头。',
 'When the Sui destroyed the Chen in 589 they set up Hangzhou here — the origin of the name. What mattered more was the Grand Canal: the Jiangnan section ended at Hangzhou, so grain and silk from the south could go by water all the way to Luoyang and Chang\'an, and the small county town became a great wharf because of it.'],
'杭州|唐': ['822 年白居易任杭州刺史,在西湖筑堤蓄水,既防旱又灌田;他离任时写「未能抛得杭州去,一半勾留是此湖」。晚年他在洛阳回忆江南,写下「江南忆,最忆是杭州」——杭州与西湖在中国人心里的位置,大半是这几首诗词定下的。',
 'Bai Juyi became prefect of Hangzhou in 822 and built an embankment on the West Lake to hold water against drought and irrigate the fields; on leaving he wrote that half of what kept him was the lake. In old age, remembering the south from Luoyang, he wrote that of all Jiangnan it was Hangzhou he missed most — and the place the city and its lake hold in Chinese affections was largely fixed by those few lyrics.'],
'杭州|五代十国': ['吴越国以杭州为都,历三代五主七十余年。钱镠修捍海石塘挡住钱塘潮,又疏浚西湖、扩建城池,雷峰塔是这一朝立起来的,保俶塔一般也认为建于此时,不过始建年代仍有争议。978 年末代国王钱俶「纳土归宋」,把两浙十三州交给北宋——江南因此避开了一场战祸,这样的收场在五代十国里极为罕见。',
 'The kingdom of Wuyue had its capital at Hangzhou for over seventy years and five rulers. Qian Liu built a stone sea wall against the Qiantang bore, dredged the West Lake and enlarged the city; the Leifeng pagoda went up in this period, and the Baochu pagoda is usually placed here too, though its date is disputed. In 978 the last king handed his thirteen prefectures over to the Song intact — sparing the region a war, an ending almost without parallel among the Ten Kingdoms.'],
'杭州|北宋': ['苏轼两次在杭州做官。1090 年他主持疏浚西湖,把挖出的葑泥堆成一条长堤,就是今天的苏堤。早在 1073 年第一次任上,他就写过「欲把西湖比西子,淡妆浓抹总相宜」,这个比喻此后再没人超过。宋仁宗称杭州「地有湖山美,东南第一州」;《宋史·地理志》记崇宁年间此地二十万三千余户。',
 'Su Shi served twice at Hangzhou. In 1090 he had the West Lake dredged and the weed and mud piled into a long causeway — the Su causeway that still crosses it. Years earlier, on his first posting in 1073, he had written the comparison of the lake to the legendary beauty Xi Shi, fetching in plain dress or fine, which no one has bettered since. Emperor Renzong called Hangzhou the first prefecture of the southeast, and the Song geographical treatise records over two hundred thousand households here.'],
'杭州|蒙古帝国': ['1276 年伯颜率蒙古军兵临临安,谢太皇太后奉传国玺出降,城池未经攻打便易主。正因为没打这一仗,临安的街市、寺观与藏书大体完整地留了下来——几年后到访的马可·波罗,看到的还是那座南宋的城。',
 'In 1276 Bayan brought the Mongol armies up to Lin\'an and the Grand Empress Dowager Xie came out with the imperial seal and surrendered; the city changed hands without being stormed. Because that battle was never fought, its markets, temples and libraries came through largely intact — and the Marco Polo who arrived a few years later was looking at the Song city still.'],
'杭州|元': ['元代杭州是江浙行省的治所,也是当时中国最大的城市之一。马可·波罗在书里称它「行在」,说它是「世界上最富丽名贵之城」,有一万二千座桥——数字显然夸大,但他惊叹的那种繁华,是南宋一百五十年留下的底子。',
 'Under the Yuan, Hangzhou was the seat of Jiangzhe province and among the largest cities in China. Marco Polo calls it Quinsai and the finest and most splendid city in the world, with twelve thousand bridges — a number plainly inflated, but the prosperity that astonished him was what a century and a half as the Song capital had left behind.'],
'杭州|明': ['明代杭州是浙江布政使司驻地。丝绸仍是这座城的产业支柱,官营的织染局在这里,民间机户也多;西湖在明代几度淤塞又几度疏浚,杨孟瑛的一次大疏浚挖出的泥堆成了杨公堤,与白堤、苏堤并列。',
 'Ming Hangzhou was the seat of the Zhejiang provincial administration. Silk remained the industry of the city, with the state dyeing and weaving office here and many private looms besides. The West Lake silted up and was dredged again more than once; the spoil from Yang Mengying\'s great dredging was piled into the Yang causeway, which ranks with Bai\'s and Su\'s.'],
'杭州|清': ['康熙、乾隆各六次南巡,最南都到杭州。西湖十景的名目南宋就有了,康熙南巡时给十景题字立碑,还改了其中几个名字——从此这些景不只写在书里,湖边真的立着碑。1861 年太平军攻占杭州,城中战乱与随后的收复战使人口锐减;战后重建时,西湖周边的园林与寺庙又修了一轮。',
 'The Kangxi and Qianlong emperors each made six southern tours, and Hangzhou was as far south as either went. The Ten Views of the West Lake had been named since the Southern Song; Kangxi wrote the names out for stone stelae and altered a few, so that the views were no longer only on the page but marked at the shore. The Taiping took the city in 1861, and between the fighting and the reconquest that followed the population fell sharply. In the rebuilding afterwards the gardens and temples around the lake were restored once more.'],
'杭州|民国': ['1929 年杭州办了一场西湖博览会,展馆沿湖铺开,前后四个多月、观众以千万计,是民国办过的最大的一次博览会之一。这场展览也把西湖从一处名胜变成了一个可以经营的城市名片。',
 'In 1929 Hangzhou held a West Lake Exposition, its halls spread around the shore, running more than four months and drawing visitors by the tens of millions — among the largest expositions the Republic ever staged. It also turned the lake from a beauty spot into something the city could run as its own emblem.'],
'杭州|共和国': ['1950 年代起西湖多次疏浚,湖底挖深、水质改善;2011 年西湖以文化景观列入世界遗产,理由正是它一千年来「文人与山水互相塑造」的关系。今天杭州是电商与数字支付的中心之一,这座城的名声从山水又添了一层。',
 'From 1950 the West Lake was dredged repeatedly, the bed deepened and the water cleared; in 2011 it was listed as World Heritage as a cultural landscape, on the grounds of a thousand years in which scholars and scenery shaped each other. Hangzhou today is a centre of online commerce and digital payment, adding a second reputation to the one built on its hills and water.'],
'杭州|南宋': ['1129 年宋高宗驻跸于此,杭州升为临安府;1138 年正式定都,名义上仍称「行在」。到十三世纪,它的人口可能已过百万,被认为是当时世界上最大的城市之一。',
 'Gaozong took refuge here in 1129, when Hangzhou was raised to Lin\'an prefecture; it formally became the capital in 1138, though it was always styled a "temporary residence." By the thirteenth century its population may have passed a million — likely among the largest cities in the world.'],
'南京|春秋': ['这一带是吴楚争夺的边地。前 571 年楚在这一带置棠邑,是南京地区最早的行政建置;前 473 年越灭吴后,范蠡在今中华门外筑越城——这才是南京城区有据可查的建城之始。相传吴王夫差还在今朝天宫一带筑过一座「冶城」铸兵器,那是个作坊性质的小城,只见于后世记载。',
 'This was frontier ground fought over by Wu and Chu. In 571 BC Chu set up Tangyi here, the earliest administrative unit in the Nanjing area; in 473 BC, after Yue destroyed Wu, Fan Li walled a town outside today\'s Zhonghua Gate — the earliest attested founding within the city itself. King Fuchai of Wu is also said to have built a foundry town near today\'s Chaotian Palace, a workshop settlement known only from later accounts.'],
'南京|战国': ['前 333 年楚威王大败越国,在今清凉山一带设金陵邑——「金陵」这个名字从此叫起,至今仍是南京最常用的别称。此后两千三百年,这座城换过几十个名字,金陵是沿用最久的一个。',
 'In 333 BC King Wei of Chu heavily defeated Yue and set up Jinling town near today\'s Qingliang Hill — the origin of the name Jinling, still the commonest of Nanjing\'s alternative names. Over the twenty-three centuries since, the city has borne dozens of names; Jinling is the one that has lasted longest.'],
'南京|秦': ['秦改金陵邑为秣陵县,属会稽郡。后世流传一个说法:秦始皇东巡时望气者说金陵有天子气,于是凿断方山的山脉、引淮水贯城以泄王气——这是六朝以后才见于记载的传说,不是当时的事。',
 'Qin renamed the town Moling county, under Kuaiji commandery. A story later grew up that when the First Emperor toured the east his diviners warned of a "son-of-heaven aura" at Jinling, so he had the ridge at Fangshan cut through and a river led across the site to drain it away — a tale that appears only in sources from the Six Dynasties onward, not a contemporary record.'],
'南京|西汉': ['西汉的秣陵是丹阳郡下一个普通县,人口不多。这一带真正的转折要等到东汉末年:孙氏势力在江东站稳,把眼光投向这块「钟山龙蟠、石头虎踞」的地方。',
 'Under the Western Han, Moling was an ordinary county in Danyang commandery with few people. The real turn came at the end of the Eastern Han, when the Sun family took hold of the lower Yangtze and looked to this place — where, as the phrase went, the hills coiled like a dragon and the rocks crouched like a tiger.'],
'南京|东汉': ['211 年孙权把治所迁到秣陵,次年在楚金陵邑旧址的石头山上筑石头城,并改名建业——「建功立业」的意思。这座城从此有了军事和政治的分量;所谓「虎踞龙蟠」,说的正是石头城与钟山这一段地形。',
 'In 211 Sun Quan moved his seat to Moling; the next year he walled Stone City on the hill where the Chu town had stood and renamed the place Jianye, "founding the enterprise." From then on the city carried military and political weight; the tiger and dragon of the old phrase are Stone City and Zhong Mountain.'],
'南京|三国': ['229 年孙权在武昌称帝,同年秋天把都城迁到建业——南京第一次成为一个王朝的都城。东吴据长江之险与曹魏相持数十年,造船与航海也在这时发展起来——朱应、康泰奉命出使南海诸国,留下了中国最早的一批海外见闻记录。',
 'Sun Quan took the imperial title at Wuchang in 229 and moved his capital to Jianye that autumn — the first time Nanjing was the capital of a dynasty. Wu held the Yangtze against Wei for decades, and shipbuilding and seafaring grew up in these years — the envoys Zhu Ying and Kang Tai were sent to the states of the southern seas and left the earliest Chinese accounts of them.'],
'南京|西晋': ['280 年西晋灭吴,两年后建业改名建邺;后来为避晋愍帝司马邺的名讳,又改成建康——这个名字用了两百七十多年。西晋短暂统一的这三十多年,是这座城少有的安静时期。',
 'The Jin destroyed Wu in 280 and two years later Jianye was rewritten with a different second character; later it was changed again to Jiankang, to avoid the personal name of Emperor Min — and Jiankang it stayed for more than two hundred and seventy years. The thirty-odd years of the brief Jin reunification were a rare quiet spell for the city.'],
'南京|东晋·十六国': ['317 年司马睿在建康即位,东晋开国。中原士族大批南渡,史称衣冠南渡,南方的经济与文化从此起飞;王导辅政,「王与马,共天下」说的就是这个格局。淝水之战后东晋守住了半壁,建康成了汉文化的避难所。',
 'Sima Rui took the throne at Jiankang in 317 and the Eastern Jin began. The great families of the north came south in numbers — the "southward flight of caps and gowns" — and the economy and culture of the south took off from then. Wang Dao guided the court, and the saying went that the Wangs and the Simas held the realm between them. After the victory at Fei River the Jin kept its half of China, and Jiankang became the refuge of Chinese high culture.'],
'南京|南北朝': ['宋、齐、梁、陈四朝都以建康为都。梁武帝在位近五十年,城中据记载有二十八万户,佛寺数百——杜牧后来写「南朝四百八十寺」,说的就是这一段。548 年侯景之乱,台城被围五个月,据《南史》记载城中原有十余万人、城破时只剩两三千,梁朝也就此崩塌。',
 'The Song, Qi, Liang and Chen all had their capital at Jiankang. Emperor Wu of Liang reigned nearly fifty years, and the city is recorded as holding two hundred and eighty thousand households and hundreds of Buddhist temples — the "four hundred and eighty temples of the Southern Dynasties" of Du Mu\'s later poem. In 548 Hou Jing\'s revolt besieged the palace city for five months; the histories record over a hundred thousand people inside at the start and only two or three thousand alive when it fell, and the Liang collapsed with it.'],
'南京|隋': ['589 年隋灭陈,统一南北。隋文帝下令把建康城「平荡耕垦」——宫殿与城垣被夷平改成农田,这是这座城历史上最彻底的一次毁灭。此后三百年,这里只是一个普通州县,唐人来凭吊时看到的已是一片荒草。',
 'The Sui destroyed the Chen in 589 and reunified the country. Emperor Wen ordered Jiankang levelled and put under the plough — palaces and walls flattened into farmland, the most complete destruction in the city\'s history. For the next three centuries it was an ordinary county town, and the Tang poets who came to mourn it found grass growing over everything.'],
'南京|唐': ['唐代这里大多数时候只是润州属下的一个县,只在唐末短暂设过升州;地位不高,却成了诗人怀古的去处。李白在凤凰台上写「吴宫花草埋幽径,晋代衣冠成古丘」,刘禹锡写「旧时王谢堂前燕,飞入寻常百姓家」——南京作为「怀古之城」的形象,是唐诗给定的。',
 'For most of the Tang this was only a county under Runzhou, briefly raised to Shengzhou at the very end of the dynasty; a place of no rank, but where poets went to mourn the past. Li Bai wrote on Phoenix Terrace of palace flowers grown over the paths and Jin nobles turned to grave mounds; Liu Yuxi wrote of the swallows that once nested in the halls of the great families now flying into ordinary homes. Nanjing\'s character as a city of elegy was fixed by Tang poetry.'],
'南京|五代十国': ['南唐定都金陵,称江宁府,是十国里最富庶、文化最盛的几个之一。后主李煜亡国后被掳到汴京,写下「问君能有几多愁,恰似一江春水向东流」——中国文学史上最有名的亡国之音,词由此从歌筵走进了士人的心事。',
 'The Southern Tang made Jinling its capital as Jiangning prefecture, among the richest and most cultivated of the Ten Kingdoms. Its last ruler Li Yu, carried off to Kaifeng after the fall, wrote the lines about sorrow running east like a spring river in flood — the most famous lament of a lost country in Chinese literature, and the point at which the song lyric moved from the banquet into the inner life of the scholar.'],
'南京|北宋': ['北宋以江宁府为江南东路治所。王安石两次罢相后都退居到这里,在城东半山园读书写诗,直到去世;他晚年的诗风与新政时期判若两人,写景多、议论少。',
 'The Song governed here as Jiangning prefecture, seat of the Jiangnan East circuit. Wang Anshi retired to the city after each of his two dismissals, living and writing at Banshan garden east of town until his death; the poems of those years read quite unlike the reformer\'s — more landscape, less argument.'],
'南京|南宋': ['建康是南宋抗金的前线重镇,也是行都之一。1130 年岳飞在牛首山一带设伏,收复被金军占据的建康;此后这里长期驻有重兵,与镇江、扬州一线共同支撑着长江防线。',
 'Jiankang was a front-line stronghold against the Jin and one of the Southern Song\'s temporary seats. In 1130 Yue Fei laid an ambush in the hills south of the city and retook Jiankang from the Jin; a large garrison stayed here afterwards, holding the Yangtze line together with Zhenjiang and Yangzhou.'],
'南京|蒙古帝国': ['1275 年伯颜率蒙古军东下,建康守将不战而降。此后蒙宋在江南的战事迅速结束,次年临安投降。这座城没有经历破城之战,是它历次改朝换代里少有的一次。',
 'In 1275 Bayan brought the Mongol armies down the river and the commander at Jiankang surrendered without a fight. The war in the lower Yangtze ended quickly after that, and Lin\'an surrendered the following year. The city was spared a storming — a rare thing among its many changes of dynasty.'],
'南京|元': ['元代这里是集庆路,江南的行政与漕运中心之一。1356 年朱元璋攻下集庆、改名应天府,把它作为根据地——他后来能从南方起兵统一全国,底子就是在这座城打下的。',
 'Under the Yuan this was Jiqing circuit, one of the administrative and grain-transport centres of the south. In 1356 Zhu Yuanzhang took it and renamed it Yingtian prefecture, making it his base — and it was from this city that he built the strength to reunify the country from the south.'],
'南京|清': ['清代改称江宁,设江宁织造署——曹雪芹的祖上在这里当了几十年织造,《红楼梦》里的富贵气就来自那段家世。1842 年英军兵临城下,《南京条约》在江面的军舰上签订;1853 年太平军攻占此城,定为天京,统治十一年。',
 'The Qing renamed it Jiangning and set up the imperial silk manufactory here — Cao Xueqin\'s family ran it for decades, and the wealth described in Dream of the Red Chamber comes out of that background. In 1842 British warships came up to the city and the Treaty of Nanking was signed aboard ship on the river; in 1853 the Taiping took the city, made it their Heavenly Capital, and held it eleven years.'],
'南京|民国': ['1912 年元旦孙中山在此就任临时大总统,中华民国宣告成立;1927 年国民政府定都南京,此后十年城市大规模改建。1937 年 12 月日军攻占南京,对平民与放下武器的军人进行了大规模屠杀与暴行。战后远东国际军事法庭认定,占领后最初六个星期内被杀害的平民与俘虏在二十万人以上;南京审判军事法庭认定的数字为三十万人以上。',
 'On New Year\'s Day 1912 Sun Yat-sen was sworn in here as provisional president and the Republic of China was proclaimed; in 1927 the Nationalist government made Nanjing its capital and the city was rebuilt on a large scale over the next decade. In December 1937 Japanese forces took the city and carried out mass killing and atrocity against civilians and disarmed soldiers. After the war the Tokyo tribunal found that more than two hundred thousand civilians and prisoners were killed in the first six weeks of the occupation; the Nanjing tribunal put the figure at more than three hundred thousand.'],
'南京|共和国': ['1949 年 4 月解放军渡江进入南京,民国在大陆的统治结束。1968 年南京长江大桥建成通车,是当时中国自行设计施工的最长的公铁两用桥,那一代人把它当作工业能力的象征。今天南京是江苏省会,城墙、明孝陵与中山陵都还在。',
 'In April 1949 the People\'s Liberation Army crossed the Yangtze into Nanjing, ending Nationalist rule on the mainland. The Nanjing Yangtze River Bridge opened in 1968, then the longest road-and-rail bridge China had designed and built itself, and a generation took it as the emblem of what the country could make. Nanjing today is the capital of Jiangsu; the city wall, the tomb of the first Ming emperor and Sun Yat-sen\'s mausoleum all still stand.'],
'南京|明': ['1368 年朱元璋在此称帝建明。他修起的城墙现存 25 公里,至今仍是世界规模第一的砖石城墙。',
 'Zhu Yuanzhang proclaimed the Ming dynasty here in 1368. The wall he built still runs 25 kilometers — to this day the largest brick city wall in the world.'],
'北京|战国': ['燕国的都城蓟就在今北京城西南一带,是战国七雄里最靠北的一个。燕昭王为郭隗筑宫、尊他为师,以此招揽人才(后世传说里的「黄金台」就是从这件事来的);乐毅由此来投,率五国联军攻齐,连下七十余城——燕国最风光的一段就是这几年。荆轲刺秦王,也是从燕国出发的。',
 'The Yan capital of Ji stood in the southwest of today\'s Beijing, the northernmost of the seven Warring States. King Zhao of Yan built a residence for Guo Wei and honoured him as his teacher to draw men of talent — the later legend of a Terrace of Gold grew out of that — and Yue Yi came to him and led a five-state army that took more than seventy Qi cities, the few years when Yan stood highest. It was from Yan that Jing Ke set out to assassinate the king of Qin.'],
'北京|秦': ['秦灭燕后在这里设广阳郡。这一带是农耕区与草原的交界,秦朝把燕、赵旧长城连接起来向东延伸,北京北面的那几道山口,从这时起就一直是防线经过的地方。',
 'After destroying Yan, Qin made this Guangyang commandery. It lies where farmland meets steppe, and Qin joined the old walls of Yan and Zhao and carried them east, and the passes in the hills north of Beijing have lain on that line of defence ever since.'],
'北京|西汉': ['西汉的蓟城是燕国、后为广阳国的治所,也是北方边郡的军事补给点。汉与匈奴在这条线上反复拉锯,蓟城是粮草与兵员往北输送的中转站,商业上则是中原与东北、朝鲜半岛往来的门户。',
 'Under the Western Han, Ji was the seat first of the kingdom of Yan and then of Guangyang, and a supply point for the northern frontier. Han and Xiongnu fought back and forth along this line, and Ji was where grain and men were staged for the march north; in trade it was the gateway between the Central Plains, the northeast and the Korean peninsula.'],
'北京|东汉': ['东汉的蓟是幽州刺史部治所。东汉末年公孙瓒据此与袁绍相争,在幽州筑易京自守,最后兵败自焚;此后这一带归了袁绍,官渡之战后又归曹操。',
 'Ji was the seat of Youzhou province under the Eastern Han. At the end of the dynasty Gongsun Zan held it against Yuan Shao, fortified himself at Yijing, and in the end burned himself in his own tower when he was beaten. The region passed to Yuan Shao, and after the battle of Guandu to Cao Cao.'],
'北京|三国': ['三国时幽州属曹魏,是对乌桓、鲜卑用兵的前进基地。曹操北征乌桓走的就是这条线,回程写下「东临碣石,以观沧海」;此后中原政权对东北的经营,大多以这座城为出发点。',
 'Youzhou belonged to Wei under the Three Kingdoms and was the forward base for campaigns against the Wuhuan and the Xianbei. Cao Cao marched this way against the Wuhuan, and wrote on the way back the lines about climbing the cliff to look out over the sea. Later Chinese states pushing into the northeast almost always set out from this city.'],
'北京|西晋': ['西晋的幽州仍治蓟。八王之乱后北方大乱,鲜卑段部、慕容部先后进入这一带,幽州反复易主;这座城从此有三百年时间处在游牧与农耕两种政权的交替之下,这段经历也让它后来更容易被草原王朝选作都城。',
 'The Western Jin still governed Youzhou from Ji. After the War of the Eight Princes the north fell apart and the Duan and Murong branches of the Xianbei came into the region in turn, the province changing hands repeatedly. For three centuries afterwards the city passed back and forth between pastoral and agrarian rulers — an experience that later made it a natural choice of capital for a steppe dynasty.'],
'北京|南北朝': ['北魏统一北方后在这里设幽州。这一带是北魏防御柔然的东段,六镇之外的另一条防线;北齐又大规模修长城,其中一条从山西一路修到海边、经过北京北面的山地;今天这一带的一些墙体就属于那几次工程。',
 'After the Northern Wei unified the north it governed here as Youzhou. This was the eastern stretch of the Wei defences against the Rouran, a second line behind the six garrisons; under the Northern Qi the walls were rebuilt on a large scale, one line running from Shanxi all the way to the sea and passing through the hills north of Beijing; some of the masonry there belongs to those works.'],
'北京|隋': ['隋在这里设涿郡。大运河的北端永济渠通到涿郡,粮食可以直接从江南运到这里——这条水路是隋炀帝三征高句丽的后勤线,百万大军就在这座城集结出发。三次东征耗尽国力,隋朝的崩溃从这里开始。',
 'The Sui governed here as Zhuo commandery. The northern arm of the Grand Canal, the Yongji channel, ran up to Zhuo, so grain could come straight from the lower Yangtze — the supply line for Emperor Yang\'s three campaigns against Goguryeo, whose armies mustered and set out from this city. The three campaigns drained the empire, and the collapse of the Sui began here.'],
'北京|唐': ['唐代这里是幽州,后设范阳节度使,管着东北方向最强的一支边军。755 年安禄山正是从范阳起兵,一路打进洛阳、长安,唐朝由盛转衰。此后幽州长期是河朔三镇之一,名义上归唐、实际自立了一百五十年。',
 'Under the Tang this was Youzhou, later the seat of the Fanyang military governor, who commanded the strongest frontier army in the northeast. It was from Fanyang that An Lushan rose in 755 and marched on Luoyang and Chang\'an, turning the Tang from its height. Youzhou was afterwards one of the three Hebei commands — nominally Tang, in practice independent, for a hundred and fifty years.'],
'北京|辽': ['936 年石敬瑭把燕云十六州许给契丹、938 年正式交割;辽把幽州升为南京幽都府(1012 年才改称析津府),是辽五京之一。辽在这里用汉制管汉人、用契丹制管本族,是所谓「因俗而治」;北京做一个北方大国的陪都,就是从这时开始的。',
 'Shi Jingtang promised the Sixteen Prefectures to the Khitan in 936 and handed them over in 938; the Liao raised Youzhou to Nanjing, Youdu prefecture — renamed Xijin only in 1012 — one of the five Liao capitals. The Liao governed the Chinese here by Chinese institutions and their own people by Khitan ones, ruling each according to custom. This was the beginning of Beijing as a secondary capital of a northern empire.'],
'北京|金': ['1153 年海陵王把都城从上京会宁府迁到燕京,改称中都,仿北宋汴京规制大建宫室——通常说的「北京建都之始」指的就是这一年——燕国与前燕都曾以蓟为都,但从中都起,这座城才连续做了八百年首都。此后除了明初的几十年与民国的二十来年,它一直是中国的政治中心。',
 'In 1153 the Prince of Hailing moved the Jin capital from Shangjing in the far north to Yanjing and renamed it Zhongdu, the Central Capital, building palaces on the model of Song Kaifeng. This is the year usually taken as the start of Beijing as a capital: Yan and the Former Yan had both ruled from Ji long before, but from Zhongdu onward the city held the seat continuously for eight centuries. Apart from a few decades in the early Ming and some twenty years under the Republic, it has been China\'s political centre ever since.'],
'北京|蒙古帝国': ['1215 年蒙古军攻破金中都,城中宫室被焚。此后这座城长期残破,将近半个世纪没有恢复,直到忽必烈决定在旧城东北另建新城——那就是大都,今天北京城的直接前身。',
 'The Mongols took the Jin Central Capital in 1215 and burned its palaces. The city stayed in ruins for close to half a century, until Kublai decided to build a new one northeast of the ruins — Dadu, the direct ancestor of Beijing today.'],
'北京|清': ['1644 年清军入关,沿用明朝的宫城与城市格局,只把内城旗汉分居。清代在西郊修起三山五园,圆明园是其中最大的一处,1860 年英法联军将其焚毁。1900 年八国联军攻入北京,慈禧西逃西安,次年签订《辛丑条约》。',
 'The Qing came through the passes in 1644 and took over the Ming palace city and street plan whole, changing only the division of the inner city between bannermen and Chinese. In the western suburbs they built the great garden palaces, of which the Yuanmingyuan was the largest, burned by British and French troops in 1860. In 1900 the allied armies entered Beijing, Cixi fled west to Xi\'an, and the Boxer Protocol was signed the following year.'],
'北京|民国': ['1912 至 1928 年北京是北洋政府的首都。1919 年 5 月 4 日,学生在天安门前集会抗议巴黎和会关于山东的决定,五四运动由此发端,新文化运动也在这座城的大学里成形。国民政府 1927 年已定都南京;1928 年北伐完成,北京改称北平。',
 'From 1912 to 1928 Beijing was the capital of the Beiyang government. On 4 May 1919 students gathered before Tiananmen to protest the Paris peace conference\'s decision on Shandong, beginning the May Fourth movement; the New Culture movement took shape in the universities of this city as well. The Nationalists had made Nanjing their capital in 1927, and when the Northern Expedition ended in 1928 Beijing was renamed Beiping.'],
'北京|共和国': ['1949 年 9 月 27 日政协会议定都北平并把它复称北京,10 月 1 日在天安门城楼宣告建国。1950 到 1960 年代拆掉了大部分城墙,先为修路、后为修地铁,梁思成等人主张保留旧城、另建新区,未被采纳——这场争论此后一直被人提起。2008 年奥运会前后,这座城又一次大规模改造。',
 'On 27 September 1949 the political consultative conference fixed the capital and gave Beiping back the name Beijing; on 1 October the People\'s Republic was proclaimed from the Tiananmen gate tower. Through the 1950s and 1960s most of the city wall was pulled down, first for roads and later for the subway; Liang Sicheng and others argued for keeping the old city and building a new district beside it, and were overruled — an argument still brought up today. The city was rebuilt on a large scale again around the 2008 Olympics.'],
'北京|元': ['忽必烈在金中都东北另起新城,是为大都——今天北京城的前身。马可·波罗笔下的「汗八里」就是这里,他说大汗的宫殿是世上从未有过的,没有人能造出更好的。',
 'Kublai Khan built a new city northeast of the Jin capital: Dadu, the ancestor of today\'s Beijing. This is Marco Polo\'s "Khanbaliq"; he called the Great Khan\'s palace the greatest that ever was.'],
'北京|明': ['1420 年紫禁城建成,次年永乐帝正式迁都北京——此后明清两代二十四位皇帝都住在这座宫城里,就是今天的故宫。',
 'The Forbidden City was completed in 1420, and the next year the Yongle Emperor formally moved the capital to Beijing. Twenty-four Ming and Qing emperors would live in this palace — today\'s Palace Museum.'],
'广州|秦': ['前 214 年秦平定百越,设南海郡,郡尉任嚣在珠江边筑番禺城——这是广州建城之始,两千两百多年来城市中心一直没挪过位置。秦末中原大乱,继任的赵佗封关绝道,自立为南越武王。',
 'In 214 BC Qin subdued the Yue peoples and set up Nanhai commandery, whose commandant Ren Xiao walled a town called Panyu on the Pearl River — the founding of Guangzhou, whose centre has not shifted in the twenty-two centuries since. When the Qin fell apart, his successor Zhao Tuo closed the passes and declared himself king of Nanyue.'],
'广州|西汉': ['南越国以番禺为都,历五代九十三年,是岭南第一个有规模的政权。前 111 年汉武帝发兵灭南越,设九郡。1983 年在城中象岗山发现第二代南越王赵眜的墓,出土丝缕玉衣、一只波斯风格的银盒和五支原支象牙(研究认为可能来自非洲)——两千年前这里就已经在做远洋生意了。',
 'Nanyue ruled from Panyu for five reigns and ninety-three years, the first substantial state in the far south. Emperor Wu destroyed it in 111 BC and set up nine commanderies. In 1983 the tomb of the second Nanyue king was found on a hill inside the city, holding a jade burial suit sewn with silk thread, a silver box of Persian workmanship and five whole elephant tusks thought to have come from Africa — this place was already trading across oceans two thousand years ago.'],
'广州|东汉': ['东汉的番禺是交趾刺史部的大港。《汉书》记载的海上航线从徐闻、合浦出发,东汉时番禺的分量越来越重;来自南海诸国乃至罗马东方的商船在这里卸货,珍珠、犀角、玳瑁、香料经陆路北运中原。',
 'Han Panyu was the great port of Jiaozhi province. The sea route recorded in the History of the Han set out from Xuwen and Hepu, but Panyu counted for more and more as the Eastern Han went on; ships from the states of the southern seas and beyond unloaded here, and pearls, rhino horn, tortoiseshell and aromatics went north overland to the Central Plains.'],
'广州|三国': ['226 年孙权把交州一分为二,东边设广州——「广州」这个名字从此叫起,治所就在番禺。东吴需要这条海路换取南方的珍货与马匹,派往南海诸国的使节朱应、康泰也是从这里出发的。',
 'In 226 Sun Quan split Jiaozhou in two and named the eastern half Guangzhou — the origin of the name — with its seat at Panyu. Wu needed this sea route for southern luxuries and for horses, and the envoys Zhu Ying and Kang Tai sailed for the states of the southern seas from here.'],
'广州|西晋': ['西晋的广州仍治番禺。这一带远离中原战乱,又靠海路通商,是当时少有的安稳富庶之地;史书里屡有官员到广州任职「经城门一过,便得三千万」的说法——说的是这里油水之厚,也说明贸易之盛。',
 'The Western Jin still governed Guangzhou from Panyu. Far from the wars of the north and open to seaborne trade, it was one of the few settled and wealthy places of the age; the histories repeat a saying that an official posted to Guangzhou grew rich simply by passing through its gate — a comment on the graft, and equally on the volume of trade.'],
'广州|东晋·十六国': ['海路带来的不只是货物。东晋时不断有天竺、师子国的僧人从海上来广州登陆,再北上传法;由海路进来的最早一批梵文经卷,相当一部分是从这个口岸上岸的。广州因此成了佛教由海路传入中国的门户。',
 'The sea route brought more than goods. Under the Eastern Jin, monks from India and Sri Lanka landed at Guangzhou one after another and went north to teach; a considerable part of the earliest Sanskrit scripture to reach China by sea came in through this port, which made Guangzhou the sea gate of Chinese Buddhism.'],
'广州|南北朝': ['相传菩提达摩在梁武帝时从海路到广州登陆,在今光孝寺一带驻锡,再北上见梁武帝——禅宗的东传故事就从这个港口开始。这个说法多见于唐以后的禅宗文献,是不是当时的实事,史料上很难落实。',
 'Bodhidharma is said to have come by sea to Guangzhou in the reign of Emperor Wu of Liang, staying near what is now the Guangxiao temple before going north to meet the emperor — the story of Chan Buddhism reaching China begins at this port. The account comes mostly from Chan writings of the Tang and after, and is hard to pin down as contemporary fact.'],
'广州|隋': ['隋改广州为番州,大业中又改称南海郡;复名广州要到唐初。隋唐之际,阿拉伯与波斯商船开始成规模地沿海路东来,广州是他们的终点;唐人贾耽把这条航线记作「广州通海夷道」,从广州出发一路可通波斯湾与东非。',
 'The Sui renamed Guangzhou as Fanzhou and then as Nanhai commandery; the old name did not come back until the early Tang. Around this time Arab and Persian ships began coming east by sea in numbers, and Guangzhou was where they ended their voyage; the Tang geographer Jia Dan later set the route down in writing as the sea road from Guangzhou to the foreign countries, running all the way to the Persian Gulf and East Africa.'],
'广州|五代十国': ['南汉以广州为都,称兴王府,历四主五十四年。刘氏在城中大建宫苑,南汉宫殿遗址近年在北京路一带被发掘出来;这个小国靠海上贸易维持了半个多世纪的富庶,直到 971 年被北宋所灭。',
 'The Southern Han made Guangzhou its capital as Xingwang prefecture, through four rulers and fifty-four years. The Liu family built palaces and gardens in the city, whose remains have been excavated in recent years beneath Beijing Road. The little state lived well on seaborne trade for over half a century, until the Song destroyed it in 971.'],
'广州|北宋': ['北宋在广州设市舶司,是北宋诸市舶司中设得最早的一个,也长期是最重要的。城中的蕃坊延续着唐代的规矩:外商聚居、自选蕃长、按本俗断事;怀圣寺的光塔既是宣礼塔,据说也给珠江上的船指过方向。',
 'The Song set up a maritime trade office at Guangzhou, the earliest of the Song offices and for a long time the most important. The foreign quarter carried on the Tang arrangements — merchants living together, choosing their own headman, judged by their own customs — and the minaret of the Huaisheng mosque, besides calling the prayer, is said to have served as a mark for ships on the river.'],
'广州|南宋': ['南宋时泉州后来居上,广州退居第二,但仍是全国两大港之一。1279 年崖山海战就发生在广州西南的海面上,陆秀夫背幼帝投海,南宋至此终结——这场终局之战,离这座城不过百余公里。',
 'Under the Southern Song, Quanzhou overtook it and Guangzhou fell to second, though it remained one of the two great ports of the empire. The battle of Yamen in 1279 was fought on the sea southwest of the city, where Lu Xiufu leapt into the water with the boy emperor on his back and the Song came to an end — a hundred kilometres or so from these walls.'],
'广州|元': ['元代广州路仍设市舶司。元朝对海外贸易一度采取官本船制度,由官府出钱出船、商人出力,利润分成;这套办法几度废立,但泉州与广州两个港口的远洋航线在元代反而比南宋更密。',
 'The Yuan kept a maritime trade office at Guangzhou. For a time the dynasty ran an official-capital shipping system, the state finding the money and the vessels and the merchants the work, with the profit divided; the scheme was abolished and revived more than once, but the ocean routes out of Quanzhou and Guangzhou ran denser under the Yuan than they had under the Song.'],
'广州|明': ['明代大部分时间行海禁,官方贸易只走朝贡一途,广州是接待贡舶的主要口岸之一。1553 年葡萄牙人以晾晒货物为由取得澳门居留权,此后欧洲商船先到澳门、再由中国商人转运广州——后来「一口通商」的格局,雏形就在这时。',
 'For most of the Ming the sea was officially closed and legal trade ran only through the tribute system, with Guangzhou one of the main ports receiving tribute ships. In 1553 the Portuguese obtained a foothold at Macau on the pretext of drying their cargo, and thereafter European ships called at Macau and Chinese merchants carried the goods on to Guangzhou — the shape of the later single-port system already visible.'],
'广州|清': ['1757 年乾隆下令西洋商船只准在广州一口通商,此后八十余年,西洋各国与中国之间的海上合法贸易都经这一座城,由十三行的行商居中经手。1839 年林则徐在虎门销烟,次年鸦片战争爆发;1841 年三元里乡民与英军发生冲突,是近代中国最早的民间抗英事件之一。',
 'In 1757 the Qianlong emperor confined Western shipping to Guangzhou alone, and for the next eighty years all legal seaborne trade between China and the Western nations passed through this one city, handled by the hong merchants of the Thirteen Factories. Lin Zexu destroyed the confiscated opium at Humen in 1839 and the Opium War broke out the next year; in 1841 villagers at Sanyuanli clashed with British troops, among the earliest popular resistance of the modern era.'],
'广州|民国': ['1911 年黄花岗起义在这里失败,七十二烈士葬于城北;半年后武昌起义成功。1924 年国共合作在广州开办黄埔军校,广州国民政府随后北伐——二十世纪中国的许多条线索,都是从这座城牵出去的。',
 'The Huanghuagang uprising failed here in 1911 and its seventy-two dead were buried north of the city; half a year later the rising at Wuchang succeeded. In 1924 the Nationalists and Communists opened the Whampoa Military Academy here together, and the Guangzhou government launched the Northern Expedition — a good many threads of twentieth-century China are pulled out of this one city.'],
'广州|共和国': ['1957 年起广交会每年春秋两届在这里举办,在对外几乎封闭的年代,它一度是中国与西方做生意的唯一稳定渠道。1978 年改革开放后,广东是最早的试验场,广州与相邻的深圳、东莞一起,把珠江三角洲变成了世界最密集的制造业地带之一。',
 'From 1957 the Canton Fair has been held here every spring and autumn; through the years when the country was largely closed, it was for a time the one steady channel for doing business with the West. After 1978 Guangdong was the first testing ground for reform, and Guangzhou together with Shenzhen and Dongguan next door turned the Pearl River delta into one of the densest manufacturing regions on earth.'],
'广州|唐': ['唐在广州设市舶使,管理海路贸易——中国最早的海关雏形。城中蕃坊里聚居着成千上万来自阿拉伯与波斯的商人,这里是海上丝路最大的枢纽。',
 'The Tang stationed a Maritime Trade Commissioner at Guangzhou — the earliest forerunner of a Chinese customs service. Thousands of Arab and Persian merchants lived in its foreign quarter; this was the greatest hub on the maritime Silk Road.'],
'泉州|秦': ['秦平百越时,闽中一带设闽中郡,但只是名义上的管辖,实际仍由当地的闽越人自治。泉州这块地方那时还没有城,人烟稀少;它的历史要到几百年后中原人南迁才真正开始。',
 'When Qin subdued the Yue peoples it created a Minzhong commandery in this region, but the control was nominal and the Minyue people went on governing themselves. There was no town at Quanzhou then and few people; its history really begins several centuries later, with migration from the north.'],
'泉州|西汉': ['前 110 年汉武帝灭闽越国,把闽越人大批迁到江淮之间,闽中一度几乎空了。此后两百年,这一带只有零星的军事据点,直到东汉末年北方战乱,中原移民才开始成规模地进入福建。',
 'Emperor Wu destroyed the kingdom of Minyue in 110 BC and moved its people north to the country between the Yangtze and the Huai, leaving Fujian nearly empty. For two centuries afterwards there were only scattered garrisons here, until the wars at the end of the Eastern Han began pushing migrants south in numbers.'],
'泉州|东汉': ['东汉末年中原动荡,士族与百姓沿海路与山道南下入闽。晋江这个名字就来自这批移民——相传是西晋永嘉之乱后南来的人思念故土,把这条江叫作晋江;泉州城就建在它的入海口。',
 'As the Eastern Han fell into disorder, gentry and commoners came south into Fujian by sea and by the mountain roads. The Jin river takes its name from these migrants: those who came after the Yongjia disaster are said to have named it for the Jin dynasty they had left behind, and Quanzhou stands at its mouth.'],
'泉州|三国': ['三国时这一带属东吴的建安郡。孙吴在福建沿海设过造船的官署,闽中的木材与海岸线开始被用起来;泉州湾一带的港口条件,就是在这个时期被中原政权注意到的。',
 'Under the Three Kingdoms this belonged to Wu\'s Jian\'an commandery. Wu set up shipbuilding offices along the Fujian coast, and the timber and the coastline of the region began to be used; the harbour conditions around Quanzhou bay first came to the notice of a northern court in these years.'],
'泉州|西晋': ['西晋末年的永嘉之乱把大批中原人推向南方,史称「衣冠南渡,八姓入闽」——林、黄、陈、郑等姓氏被认为是这时进入福建的。这批移民带来了中原的农耕技术与宗族制度,福建的开发从此加速。',
 'The Yongjia disaster at the end of the Western Jin drove great numbers of northerners south, in what tradition calls the flight of caps and gowns and the eight surnames entering Fujian — the Lin, Huang, Chen and Zheng families among them are held to have arrived then. They brought northern farming methods and lineage organisation with them, and the settlement of Fujian moved faster from that point.'],
'泉州|东晋·十六国': ['这一带属晋安郡——西晋太康年间从建安郡分出来的,东晋沿袭下来。移民持续南下,沿江河谷地开垦;佛教也在这时传入闽南,泉州最早的一批寺院就出现在东晋南朝之际。这一带从「化外之地」变成编户齐民,用了大约三百年。',
 'The Eastern Jin governed here as Jin\'an commandery, a unit split off from Jian\'an under the Western Jin. Migrants kept coming south and clearing the valleys, and Buddhism reached southern Fujian in these years, when the first monasteries around Quanzhou appear. It took some three centuries for the region to pass from being counted outside the empire to being counted on its tax registers.'],
'泉州|南北朝': ['南朝时这一带先后属晋安郡、南安郡。梁陈之际有印度僧人拘那罗陀(真谛)渡海到晋安译经,泉州与南海的往来在这时已经开始;它后来能成为大港,底子是这几百年一点点积起来的。',
 'Under the Southern Dynasties the district belonged to Jin\'an and then Nan\'an commandery. Around the Liang and Chen the Indian monk Paramartha crossed the sea to Jin\'an and translated scripture there, and traffic between Quanzhou and the southern seas had already begun; the port it later became was built up slowly across these centuries.'],
'泉州|隋': ['隋在这里设南安县,属泉州——不过隋代的「泉州」治所在今福州,与后来的泉州不是一回事。这种地名搬家在福建很常见,读史料时容易弄混。',
 'The Sui made this Nan\'an county under a prefecture called Quanzhou — though the Sui Quanzhou had its seat at today\'s Fuzhou and is not the same place as the later city of that name. Place names shifted about like this often in Fujian, and it is easy to confuse them in the sources.'],
'泉州|唐': ['711 年泉州之名正式落到今天这个位置上。唐代中期以后,泉州港开始出现在海外贸易的记载里,与广州、扬州并称;来自阿拉伯与波斯的商船开始成批停靠,城南沿江的市面因此热闹起来。',
 'In 711 the name Quanzhou settled on the place it now occupies. From the middle Tang the port begins to appear in records of foreign trade, ranked with Guangzhou and Yangzhou; Arab and Persian ships began putting in here in numbers, and the riverside quarter south of the walls grew busy on their account.'],
'泉州|五代十国': ['五代时闽国据有福建,后期泉州由留从效、陈洪进相继割据。这几任统治者都下大力气修城、扩港、招徕商船,泉州的城市规模在这几十年里扩大了几倍。留从效下令环城遍种刺桐,「刺桐城」这个名字从此叫开,后来经阿拉伯商人传遍整个印度洋世界——南宋它能超过广州,起跑就在这一段。',
 'Under the Five Dynasties the kingdom of Min held Fujian, and Quanzhou was later ruled in turn by Liu Congxiao and Chen Hongjin as effectively independent governors. Each of them worked hard at walls, harbour and attracting shipping, and the city grew several times over in these decades. Liu Congxiao had coral trees planted right round the walls, and the name Zayton took hold from them, carried by Arab merchants across the whole Indian Ocean — the running start that let it pass Guangzhou under the Southern Song.'],
'泉州|北宋': ['1087 年北宋在泉州设市舶司,此前北宋已在广州、杭州、明州设过市舶司。设司之后泉州的海外贸易额迅速上升,城南沿江建起成片的码头与货栈;宋代的泉州人开始大规模造尖底海船,这种船能远航,也能装得多。',
 'The Song set up a maritime trade office at Quanzhou in 1087, after earlier offices at Guangzhou, Hangzhou and Mingzhou. Trade rose quickly once it was there, and wharves and warehouses spread along the river south of the city; Song Quanzhou began building keeled seagoing ships in quantity — vessels that could both go far and carry much.'],
'泉州|明': ['明代海禁,泉州的官方贸易萎缩,市舶司先移后废;但民间的走私与出海从未断过,漳州月港一度取代泉州成为闽南的出海口。这一时期福建人大批下南洋谋生,今天东南亚的闽南人社群,源头多在这几百年。',
 'The Ming closed the sea, official trade at Quanzhou shrank and the trade office was moved and then abolished; but smuggling and unlicensed sailing never stopped, and Yuegang in Zhangzhou took over for a time as southern Fujian\'s outlet. In these centuries Fujianese went to Southeast Asia in great numbers to make a living, and most of the Hokkien communities there today trace back to them.'],
'泉州|清': ['清初为对付郑成功而实行迁界令,沿海居民内迁三十至五十里,房屋田地尽毁,泉州沿海一带元气大伤;直到 1683 年台湾归清、次年开海,才逐步恢复。此后泉州人渡海去台湾的更多了,闽南话与信俗也一并带了过去。',
 'To cut off Zheng Chenggong, the early Qing ordered the coast evacuated — inhabitants moved thirty to fifty li inland and their houses and fields destroyed — and the Quanzhou coast was badly hurt; recovery began only after Taiwan came under Qing rule in 1683 and the sea was reopened the next year. More Quanzhou people crossed to Taiwan afterwards, taking their speech and their local cults with them.'],
'泉州|民国': ['民国的泉州是侨乡。南洋华侨的汇款支撑着侨眷的生计,也修了大量学校、医院与道路——陈嘉庚在厦门办集美学校与厦门大学,是这股风气里最有名的一例。侨批(华侨寄回的信与汇款合一的凭证)后来成了世界记忆遗产。',
 'Republican Quanzhou was a home of emigrants. Remittances from the South Seas kept families going and paid for schools, hospitals and roads besides — Tan Kah Kee\'s Jimei schools and Xiamen University are the best known instance. The qiaopi, the combined letters and money orders sent home, were later inscribed on the Memory of the World register.'],
'泉州|共和国': ['2021 年「泉州:宋元中国的世界海洋商贸中心」列入世界遗产,包含二十二处遗址,从九日山祈风石刻、清净寺到洛阳桥、市舶司遗址——把这座城作为一整套海洋贸易体系来认定,而不只是几处古迹。',
 'In 2021 "Quanzhou: Emporium of the World in Song-Yuan China" was inscribed as World Heritage, covering twenty-two component sites — from the wind-prayer inscriptions at Jiuri Mountain and the Qingjing mosque to the Luoyang bridge and the remains of the trade office — recognising the city as a whole system of maritime commerce rather than a handful of monuments.'],
'泉州|南宋': ['南宋后期泉州超过广州,成为全国第一大港。城里住着上万名阿拉伯、波斯商人,清真寺与妈祖庙同城并立、各自香火不断。',
 'Late in the Southern Song, Quanzhou overtook Guangzhou as China\'s greatest port. More than ten thousand Arab and Persian merchants lived here, and a mosque and a Mazu temple both drew worshippers in the same city.'],
'泉州|元': ['元时泉州以「刺桐」之名闻于世界。马可·波罗说,运胡椒去亚历山大港的船若有一条,来刺桐的就有一百条;摩洛哥旅行家伊本·白图泰则说,这是世界上最大的港口之一,甚至可能就是最大的。',
 'Under the Yuan, Quanzhou was known to the world as Zayton. Marco Polo wrote that for every pepper ship bound for Alexandria, a hundred came here; the Moroccan traveller Ibn Battuta called it one of the greatest ports in the world, or perhaps the greatest of all.'],
'拉萨|清': ['1720 年清军入藏,此后设驻藏大臣。1751 年确立了由达赖喇嘛主持地方政务的体制,而驻藏大臣被抬到与达赖同等的地位,要到 1793 年——制度是一步步收紧的。布达拉宫今天的规模,大体是十七世纪五世达赖重建之后历代不断扩建的结果——一座宫殿的样子,记录的是几百年里权力怎么安排。',
 'Qing troops entered Tibet in 1720 and a resident commissioner was posted thereafter. In 1751 an arrangement was fixed under which the Dalai Lama headed the local administration; the resident commissioner was raised to equal rank with him only in 1793 — the system tightened by stages. The Potala at its present size is largely the result of the rebuilding begun by the fifth Dalai Lama in the seventeenth century and additions made by every generation since — the shape of a palace is a record of how power was arranged over centuries.'],
'拉萨|民国': ['民国时期中央政府对这一带的实际管辖很弱,拉萨长期由当地政府自行运作;英属印度方面几度介入,并在拉萨设过代表机构。1933 年十三世达赖喇嘛圆寂,1940 年十四世达赖喇嘛在布达拉宫坐床。',
 'Through the Republic years the central government\'s actual authority here was weak and Lhasa was run largely by the local administration; British India intervened more than once and kept a mission in the city. The thirteenth Dalai Lama died in 1933, and the fourteenth was enthroned at the Potala in 1940.'],
'拉萨|共和国': ['1951 年西藏地方与中央政府签订协议,1965 年西藏自治区成立,拉萨是首府。青藏铁路 2006 年通车,线路有近千公里在海拔四千米以上,车厢要供氧;布达拉宫 1994 年列入世界文化遗产,大昭寺与罗布林卡后来陆续并入。',
 'An agreement was signed between the Tibetan local government and the central government in 1951, and the Tibet Autonomous Region was established in 1965 with Lhasa as its seat. The Qinghai-Tibet railway opened in 2006 with close to a thousand kilometres of track above four thousand metres, its carriages fitted with oxygen supply. The Potala was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1994, with the Jokhang and the Norbulingka added later.'],
'首尔|韩国': ['1948 年大韩民国成立,首尔是首都。朝鲜战争中这座城四度易手、几乎打成废墟;此后几十年的工业化把它变成一座人口两千多万的都会区。2005 年市政府把中文名称从「汉城」正式改为「首尔」,取的是韩语读音的音译。',
 'The Republic of Korea was founded in 1948 with Seoul as its capital. The city changed hands four times during the Korean War and was left close to rubble; decades of industrialisation then turned it into a metropolitan area of over twenty million. In 2005 the city government formally changed its Chinese name to one that transcribes the Korean pronunciation rather than the old Sinitic name.'],
'平壤|蒙古帝国': ['蒙古自 1231 年起反复入侵高丽,前后近三十年。高丽王室退到江华岛坚守,陆上的城镇则一再遭到劫掠;1259 年高丽降附。元朝随后在平壤设东宁府直辖了二十来年,这座城一度被从高丽手里切出去;此后八十多年,高丽国王娶元朝的公主、太子在大都长大——一个政权可以不被灭掉,却被慢慢改变。',
 'The Mongols invaded Goryeo repeatedly from 1231, over close to thirty years. The court withdrew to Ganghwa island and held out there while the towns on the mainland were raided again and again; Goryeo submitted in 1259. The Yuan then governed Pyongyang directly as Dongnyeong prefecture for about twenty years, cutting the city out of Goryeo altogether; and for eighty years afterwards Goryeo kings married Yuan princesses and their heirs grew up at the Yuan capital — a state need not be destroyed to be changed.'],
'台北|民国': ['1945 年日本战败,台湾由中华民国政府接收,台北是行政中心。1949 年国民政府迁台,以台北为所在地;此后数十年,海峡两岸各自沿着不同的路径发展。',
 'Japan was defeated in 1945 and Taiwan was taken over by the government of the Republic of China, with Taipei as its administrative centre. In 1949 that government relocated to Taiwan and based itself in Taipei; in the decades since, the two sides of the strait have developed along separate paths.'],
'台北|共和国': ['1949 年之后,台北由迁台的国民政府管辖,两岸分治至今。台北故宫博物院的那批文物,1948 年底到 1949 年初从南京运到基隆——它们 1933 年就已经从北平南迁,与北京故宫的收藏本是同一批东西。两岸各存一部分,这是二十世纪中国历史留在实物上的一道痕迹。',
 'Since 1949 Taipei has been administered by the Nationalist government that moved there, and the two sides of the strait have been separately governed ever since. The objects in the Taipei palace museum were shipped from Nanjing to Keelung between late 1948 and early 1949 — they had already been moved south out of Beiping back in 1933 — and they come from the same collection as the one in Beijing. Each side of the strait keeps part of it, a mark that twentieth-century Chinese history left on the objects themselves.'],
'吴哥|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['十九世纪法国人「重新发现」吴哥并大力宣传,而当地人其实从没忘记它——吴哥窟一直有僧人住持,日本江户时代有人到过这里、在墙上留下题记,日本也传下一份那个时代画的吴哥窟平面图。1907 年暹罗把吴哥一带归还法属柬埔寨,法国远东学院随即开始大规模清理与修复。',
 'Nineteenth-century French visitors announced the rediscovery of Angkor, though local people had never forgotten it — Angkor Wat had monks living in it throughout, a Japanese visitor of the Edo period left an inscription on its wall, and a plan of Angkor Wat drawn in that era survives in Japan. In 1907 Siam returned the Angkor district to French Cambodia and the French school of the Far East began clearing and restoring it on a large scale.'],
'吴哥|现代东南亚': ['1992 年吴哥列入世界文化遗产,同一年就被列入濒危名单——柬埔寨当时刚结束长期战乱,遗址遭到大量盗掘。2004 年它从濒危名单上除名。今天最大的压力来自游客与地下水:抽水太多,地基会跟着沉下去。',
 'Angkor was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1992 and placed on the danger list the same year — Cambodia had just come out of long war and the site was being heavily looted. It came off that list in 2004. The pressures now are visitors and groundwater: pump too much and the foundations settle with it.'],
'曼谷|高棉·吴哥': ['吴哥鼎盛时,势力伸到今天泰国中部的湄南河流域;而曼谷所在的这片河口当时还是滩涂,要到十五世纪才有村落的记载。今天泰国的王室礼仪、宫廷用语与不少制度,仍留着高棉的痕迹——一个政权衰落之后,它做事的方式常常被继承者留下来。',
 'At its height Angkor reached into the Chao Phraya basin in what is now central Thailand; the estuary where Bangkok stands was still tidal flat then, and no village is recorded there until the fifteenth century. Thai court ritual, palace vocabulary and a good deal of institutional practice still carry Khmer traces — when a power declines, the way it did things is often what its successors keep.'],
'曼谷|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['十九世纪的曼谷挖运河、修铁路、架电报,拉玛五世逐步废除奴隶制、改革官制,还把王子们送去欧洲读书。这些改动不只是因为新东西好用:让外人看见这是一个「文明国家」,本身就是在拿掉别人动手的理由。',
 'Nineteenth-century Bangkok cut canals, laid railways, strung telegraph lines; Rama V phased out slavery, reorganised the administration and sent his sons to study in Europe. These changes were not only about what worked better: being seen from outside as a civilised state was itself a way of removing other people\'s reasons to intervene.'],
'曼谷|现代东南亚': ['曼谷今天是东南亚最大的都会区之一,也是全球接待外国游客最多的城市之一。它建在湄南河三角洲的软土上,城市每年下沉一到两厘米;加上海平面上升,防洪是这座城长期要面对的事。',
 'Bangkok is one of the largest metropolitan areas in Southeast Asia and among the most visited cities in the world. It stands on the soft ground of the Chao Phraya delta and sinks a centimetre or two a year; with the sea rising as well, keeping the water out is a permanent problem here.'],
'蒲甘|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1885 年第三次英缅战争后,缅甸全境并入英属印度,末代国王被流放到印度。那时蒲甘已经不做都城几百年了,塔林散在伊洛瓦底江边的平原上;最早的一批系统测绘与编号,是英国人做的。',
 'After the third Anglo-Burmese war in 1885 the whole of Burma was absorbed into British India and the last king was exiled to India. Bagan had not been a capital for centuries by then, its pagodas standing scattered over the plain by the Irrawaddy; the first systematic survey and numbering of them was British work.'],
'蒲甘|现代东南亚': ['1975 年一场大地震毁坏了蒲甘的许多佛塔,此后的修复被批评为用水泥和现代砖草率重建。蒲甘 1995 年首次提名世界文化遗产,却因为修复方式的争议拖了二十四年,到 2019 年才列入。',
 'An earthquake in 1975 damaged many of Bagan\'s pagodas, and the restorations that followed were criticised as hasty work in cement and modern brick. Bagan was first nominated for World Heritage listing in 1995, and the dispute over those restorations held it back for twenty-four years; it was finally inscribed in 2019.'],
'仰光|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1852 年第二次英缅战争后英国占领下缅甸,把仰光重建成一座棋盘街道的港口城市,1885 年后又定为整个缅甸的行政中心。这一时期大量印度人迁入,一度占到城市人口的一半以上——一座城的人口构成,可以在几十年里被一条航线改写。',
 'After the second Anglo-Burmese war in 1852 Britain took lower Burma and rebuilt Rangoon as a grid-plan port, making it the administrative centre of the whole country after 1885. Indians moved in in great numbers in these years and at one point made up more than half the city\'s population — a shipping route can rewrite who lives in a city within a few decades.'],
'仰光|现代东南亚': ['1948 年缅甸独立,仰光是首都。2005 年政府把首都迁到内陆新建的内比都,仰光仍是最大的城市与经济中心。它成片的殖民时期建筑保存得相当完整;一个常见的解释是,几十年的经济停滞让人没有余力拆了重建。',
 'Burma became independent in 1948 with Rangoon as its capital. In 2005 the government moved the capital to a new inland city, and Yangon remained the largest city and the economic centre. Its colonial-era buildings survive in unusually complete blocks; the usual explanation is that decades of economic stagnation left no means to knock them down and start over.'],
'雅加达|满者伯夷': ['满者伯夷的中心在东爪哇,雅加达一带当时属另一个政权巽他王国。1527 年一支来自北方的穆斯林军队攻下这里,取名「查雅加尔达」,意思是「胜利之城」——「雅加达」这个名字就是从它简化来的。',
 'Majapahit had its centre in eastern Java, while the Jakarta district belonged to the separate kingdom of Sunda. In 1527 a Muslim force from the north took the port and named it Jayakarta, the city of victory — and Jakarta is that name worn down.'],
'雅加达|荷兰共和国': ['荷兰人把巴达维亚按自己家乡的样子建了起来:挖运河、盖砖房、临水而居。可热带的死水成了蚊子与疟疾的温床,十八世纪这里被叫作「欧洲人的墓地」——把一套北欧的城市做法原样搬到赤道,代价极大。',
 'The Dutch laid Batavia out to look like home: canals cut through it, brick houses along the water. Standing water in the tropics bred mosquitoes and malaria, and by the eighteenth century the place was known as the graveyard of Europeans — transplanting a northern European way of building to the equator turned out to be very expensive.'],
'雅加达|现代东南亚': ['1945 年印尼宣布独立、1949 年荷兰承认,雅加达是首都。这座城建在沼泽与河口上,过度抽取地下水使地面持续下沉,北部部分城区已经低于海平面;2019 年政府宣布把首都迁往加里曼丹岛——一座城沉得太快,国家可以选择搬走。',
 'Indonesia declared independence in 1945 and the Dutch recognised it in 1949, with Jakarta as the capital. The city sits on marsh and estuary, and over-pumping of groundwater has made it sink steadily, with parts of the north already below sea level; in 2019 the government announced that the capital would move to Kalimantan — when a city subsides fast enough, a country can decide to leave.'],
'马尼拉|现代东南亚': ['1945 年的马尼拉之战把这座城打成了废墟,它常被列为二战中受损最重的城市之一。1946 年菲律宾独立,马尼拉重建;老城区里的圣奥古斯丁教堂是少数完整留下来的建筑,1993 年列入世界文化遗产。',
 'The battle of Manila in 1945 left the city in ruins and it is often counted among the worst-damaged cities of the Second World War. The Philippines became independent in 1946 and Manila was rebuilt; the church of San Agustin in the old walled quarter is one of the few buildings that came through whole, and was made a World Heritage Site in 1993.'],
'巨港|荷兰共和国': ['三佛齐之后,巨港长期是一个苏丹国。1659 年它与荷兰东印度公司冲突,城被焚毁;此后荷兰逐步控制了这一带胡椒与锡的贸易——公司先烧掉一座城,再接管它的生意。',
 'After Srivijaya, Palembang was for a long time a sultanate. It clashed with the Dutch East India Company in 1659 and the city was burned; the Dutch then took over the pepper and tin trade of the district by degrees — the company burned a city first and inherited its business after.'],
'巨港|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1820 年代荷兰军事接管巨港、废掉苏丹国,改为直接统治。十九世纪末二十世纪初这一带发现石油,巨港成了荷属东印度最早的石油工业中心之一——一个靠转口活了一千年的河口,改成靠地下的东西活。',
 'In the 1820s the Dutch took Palembang by force, abolished the sultanate and ruled directly. Oil was found in the district around the turn of the twentieth century and Palembang became one of the earliest centres of the oil industry in the Dutch East Indies — an estuary that had lived a thousand years off goods passing through began living off what lay under it.'],
'巨港|现代东南亚': ['巨港今天是南苏门答腊省的首府。三佛齐留下的实物极少:一个掌握海峡六百年的政权,能摸得到的遗存比它的影响小得多。一个常见的解释是它多用木头与竹子建造,在热带留不住。',
 'Palembang is the capital of South Sumatra today. Very little of Srivijaya survives in material form: a power that controlled the strait for six centuries left far less to touch than it left in consequence. The usual explanation is that it built in wood and bamboo, which the tropics do not preserve.'],
'麦加|阿尤布王朝': ['萨拉丁的政权把汉志纳入版图,埃及的统治者从此以「两圣地的仆人」自居——这个称号是萨拉丁第一个用的。控制麦加与麦地那不只是宗教上的荣誉——朝觐路线上的补给、治安与税收,是一笔实在的权力。',
 'Saladin\'s state brought the Hejaz under its authority, and the rulers of Egypt styled themselves servants of the two holy places from then on — a title Saladin was the first to use. Holding Mecca and Medina was not only an honour — supply, security and tolls along the pilgrim roads were real power.'],
'麦加|奥斯曼帝国': ['1517 年奥斯曼取得埃及之后接管汉志,苏丹此后称「两圣地的仆人」。奥斯曼修缮禁寺、维护朝觐路上的水井与驿站;每年从大马士革与开罗出发的朝觐商队,是这套体系里最显眼的一环。',
 'The Ottomans took over the Hejaz after conquering Egypt in 1517, and their sultans took the title of servant of the two holy places. They repaired the sanctuary and maintained the wells and stations along the pilgrim roads; the caravans that set out each year from Damascus and Cairo were the visible part of that system.'],
'麦加|现代中东': ['1925 年沙特家族取得汉志,1932 年沙特阿拉伯建国。二十世纪后期,石油收入支持了禁寺的多次大规模扩建;今天每年朝觐的人数以百万计——从骆驼商队到包机,朝觐这件事的规模在一百年里变了几十倍。',
 'The house of Saud took the Hejaz in 1925 and the kingdom of Saudi Arabia was founded in 1932. In the later twentieth century oil revenue paid for repeated enlargements of the sanctuary, and the pilgrimage now brings millions each year — from camel caravan to chartered aircraft, its scale has grown many times over in a century.'],
'麦地那|阿尤布王朝': ['麦地那与麦加一同归入阿尤布的势力范围。1256 年城东的火山口喷发,岩浆流到城边停住,这件事被当时的人详细记了下来,是伊斯兰史料里对火山喷发最完整的一次记录。先知清真寺则在这几百年里反复扩建重修——一座建筑被一代代人不断加高加大,本身就是信仰延续的实物记录。',
 'Medina came under Ayyubid authority together with Mecca. In 1256 a fissure east of the city erupted and the lava flow halted at its edge; people wrote the event down in detail, and it remains the fullest account of a volcanic eruption in Islamic sources. The Prophet\'s mosque meanwhile was enlarged and rebuilt again and again over these centuries — a building raised and widened by one generation after another is itself a physical record of a faith continuing.'],
'麦地那|奥斯曼帝国': ['奥斯曼在麦地那大规模修缮先知清真寺,今天那座绿色的圆顶就是十九世纪奥斯曼时期漆成的。1908 年汉志铁路通到麦地那,从大马士革坐火车过来只要几天——朝觐第一次不再意味着几个月的沙漠跋涉。',
 'The Ottomans carried out major repairs to the Prophet\'s mosque at Medina, and the green dome it is known by was painted in the Ottoman nineteenth century. In 1908 the Hejaz railway reached Medina and the journey from Damascus took a few days — for the first time the pilgrimage no longer meant months of desert travel.'],
'麦地那|现代中东': ['一战期间汉志铁路被反复破坏,通往麦地那的南段此后再没有修复(北边靠近大马士革的一段至今还在跑)。1925 年后麦地那归沙特;先知清真寺经过几轮扩建,今天可以容纳上百万人。2018 年麦地那到麦加的高铁通车——这条路等了一百一十年,才重新有了铁轨。',
 'The Hejaz railway was wrecked repeatedly during the First World War and the southern section to Medina was never rebuilt, though the stretch near Damascus still runs. Medina passed to the Saudis after 1925, and successive enlargements have left the Prophet\'s mosque able to hold over a million people. A high-speed line from Medina to Mecca opened in 2018 — the route waited a hundred and ten years to have rails on it again.'],
'伊斯坦布尔|罗马共和国': ['拜占庭城由希腊人在前七世纪建立,扼着黑海与地中海之间唯一的水道。前二世纪罗马控制了这一带。那时它只是一座中等规模的港市——还要再等四百多年,才有人看出这个位置有多要紧。',
 'Byzantion was founded by Greeks in the seventh century BC on the only water passage between the Black Sea and the Mediterranean. Rome took control of the district in the second century BC. It was then a middling port town — four centuries would pass before anyone saw what that position was worth.'],
'伊斯坦布尔|罗马帝国': ['196 年塞维鲁攻破拜占庭、夷平城墙,后来又把它重建起来。真正的转折在 330 年——君士坦丁看中的正是这个位置:三面环水、扼守海峡,从这里既盯得住多瑙河,也盯得住幼发拉底河。',
 'Severus stormed Byzantium in 196 and levelled its walls, then rebuilt the place. The turn came in 330 — what Constantine wanted was exactly this position: water on three sides, command of the strait, and a point from which both the Danube and the Euphrates could be watched.'],
'伊斯坦布尔|现代中东': ['1923 年土耳其共和国把首都迁往安卡拉,伊斯坦布尔一千六百年来第一次不再是首都。它至今是土耳其最大的城市;这座城一部分在欧洲、一部分在亚洲,海峡对岸的几个区几百年前就属于它;1973 年第一座跨海峡大桥通车之后,两边才第一次可以开车往来。',
 'In 1923 the Turkish republic moved the capital to Ankara and Istanbul ceased to be a capital for the first time in sixteen centuries. It remains the largest city in Turkey; part of the city lies in Europe and part in Asia, and the districts on the far shore have belonged to it for centuries; only with the first bridge across the Bosphorus in 1973 could people drive between the two.'],
'科尔多瓦|罗马共和国': ['前二世纪罗马在瓜达尔基维尔河边建起科尔杜巴,是它在伊比利亚半岛最早的殖民城之一。那时这条河可以行船到这里,内陆的银与橄榄油从这里装船下海——一座城的位置,往往由船能开到哪儿决定。',
 'Rome founded Corduba on the Guadalquivir in the second century BC, among its earliest colonies in Iberia. The river was navigable this far up, and the silver and olive oil of the interior were loaded here for the sea — where a city stands is usually decided by how far the boats can come.'],
'科尔多瓦|罗马帝国': ['科尔杜巴是罗马贝提卡行省的首府(共和国时期这一带叫「远西班牙」,帝国改制后才叫贝提卡)。哲学家小塞内加出生在这里,后来做了尼禄的老师,写下大量关于如何面对权力与死亡的文字;最后他被自己的学生下令赐死——他写过的那些道理,他自己用上了。',
 'Corduba was the capital of the Roman province of Baetica — the district had been called Further Spain under the republic and was renamed when the empire reorganised it. The philosopher Seneca the Younger was born here and later tutored Nero, writing at length on how to face power and how to face death; in the end his own pupil ordered him to die — and he had to use what he had written.'],
'科尔多瓦|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['1236 年卡斯蒂利亚攻下科尔多瓦之后,这座城迅速衰落:十世纪它是欧洲最大的城市之一,此后一直只是安达卢西亚的一座省城。真正留下来的是那座大清真寺——它因为被改成主教座堂而没有被拆掉,这大概是它能站到今天的唯一原因。',
 'After Castile took Córdoba in 1236 the city fell away fast: one of the largest in Europe in the tenth century, it was never again more than a provincial town of Andalusia. What did survive was the great mosque — it was not pulled down because it had been turned into a cathedral, which is probably the only reason it is still standing.'],
'拉萨|吐蕃': ['松赞干布把都城定在逻些——今天的拉萨,相传在红山上最早筑宫,今天的布达拉宫就建在那里(现在这座宫是十七世纪重建的)。大昭寺里供奉的佛像,相传就是文成公主从长安带来的。',
 'Songtsen Gampo fixed his capital at Rasa — today\'s Lhasa — and first built a palace on the Red Hill where the Potala now stands. The Buddha statue in the Jokhang temple is said to be the one Princess Wencheng brought from Chang\'an.'],
'伊斯坦布尔|拜占庭': ['330 年君士坦丁在此建新都,城以他命名。537 年建成的圣索菲亚大教堂罩着当时世界上最大的室内空间;此后六百多年,直到 1204 年被十字军洗劫,君士坦丁堡一直是欧洲最大最富的城市。',
 'Constantine dedicated his new capital here in 330 and gave it his name. Hagia Sophia, finished in 537, enclosed the largest interior space then on earth; and for the next six centuries, until the crusaders sacked it in 1204, Constantinople was Europe\'s greatest and richest city.'],
'伊斯坦布尔|奥斯曼帝国': ['1453 年 21 岁的穆罕默德二世攻下这座千年都城,奥斯曼迁都于此。圣索菲亚改作清真寺,托普卡帕宫在海角上建起——城市换了名字与信仰,仍是帝国的心脏。',
 'In 1453 the 21-year-old Mehmed II took the thousand-year capital, and the Ottomans made it their own. Hagia Sophia became a mosque, Topkapi Palace rose on the point — a new name, a new faith, still the heart of an empire.'],
'罗马|罗马帝国': ['帝国盛期的罗马城约有百万人口,是古代西方最大的城市。80 年启用的斗兽场能容五万观众,引水道从几十公里外把清水送进全城的浴场与喷泉。',
 'At the empire\'s height Rome held about a million people — the largest city of the ancient West. The Colosseum, opened in 80 CE, seated fifty thousand; aqueducts carried water from dozens of kilometers away to baths and fountains across the city.'],
'大马士革|古埃及': ['前 15 世纪图特摩斯三世北伐叙利亚,大马士革第一次出现在埃及人的记载里。阿马尔纳出土的泥板书信中,叙利亚各城的城主用阿卡德语写信给法老——那时的近东,埃及人和叙利亚人通信用的是第三方的语言。',
 'Thutmose III campaigned into Syria in the fifteenth century BC, and Damascus makes its first appearance in Egyptian records. In the clay letters found at Amarna the rulers of the Syrian cities write to pharaoh in Akkadian — in the Near East of that age, Egyptians and Syrians corresponded in a third party\'s language.'],
'大马士革|亚述': ['前 732 年提格拉特帕拉沙尔三世攻陷大马士革,亚兰王国灭亡,居民被大批迁走。亚述对付反叛城市的办法就是把人口打散、迁到帝国另一头去——这样一来,被征服者连回来的路都没有了。',
 'Tiglath-Pileser III stormed Damascus in 732 BC, the Aramaean kingdom ended and its people were deported in numbers. Assyria dealt with rebellious cities by breaking up their populations and resettling them at the far side of the empire — which left the conquered with no road home.'],
'大马士革|新巴比伦': ['新巴比伦接手了亚述在叙利亚的地盘,大马士革是它西线的一座省城。腓尼基的港口与内陆的大马士革一起,把地中海和两河流域连在了一起;巴比伦要的不是这些城的忠诚,而是它们缴上来的税与货。',
 'The Neo-Babylonians took over Assyria\'s holdings in Syria and Damascus became a provincial city on their western side. Together with the Phoenician ports it linked the Mediterranean to the Two Rivers; what Babylon wanted from such cities was not loyalty but the goods and taxes they sent in.'],
'大马士革|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['波斯把叙利亚划进「河西」总督辖区,大马士革是其中一座重镇。前 333 年伊苏斯战役之后,大流士三世存放在大马士革的辎重与家眷被亚历山大的部将一举缴获——那批财物后来成了他继续东征的军费。',
 'Persia put Syria into the satrapy beyond the river and Damascus was one of its main towns. After the battle of Issus in 333 BC, the baggage train and household Darius III had left at Damascus were seized whole by one of Alexander\'s generals — and paid for much of the march east that followed.'],
'大马士革|希腊化王朝': ['塞琉古王朝按希腊城市的样子重新规划了大马士革的街区。老城里那条笔直的主干道「直街」,就是那个时候定下的——两千三百年过去,今天走在老城里,脚下还是那张棋盘。',
 'The Seleucids laid Damascus out again on the Greek plan. The dead-straight main road through the old city, the Street called Straight, was fixed then — and twenty-three centuries later anyone walking the old town is still walking that grid.'],
'大马士革|罗马治下近东': ['前 64 年庞培把叙利亚变成罗马的行省。罗马人在城中大兴土木,修起一座朱庇特神庙;那座神庙的地基后来先变成教堂,再变成倭马亚大清真寺——同一块地基上换过三种信仰,墙还是那道墙。',
 'Pompey made Syria a Roman province in 64 BC. The Romans built heavily in the city, including a temple of Jupiter; its foundations later carried a church, and later still the Umayyad Mosque — three faiths in turn on one platform, and the same walls under all of them.'],
'大马士革|罗马帝国': ['罗马帝国时期的大马士革是叙利亚行省的大城,商队从这里出发穿越沙漠去往两河。《使徒行传》记载保罗在去大马士革的路上改变了信仰,后来又被人用筐子从城墙上缒下去逃走——「去大马士革的路上」这个说法,后来专指一个人突然翻转了自己的主张。',
 'Under the empire Damascus was a major city of the province of Syria and the point where caravans set out across the desert for Mesopotamia. Acts records that Paul changed his faith on the road to Damascus and later escaped the city lowered from the wall in a basket — and the road to Damascus has meant a sudden reversal of conviction ever since.'],
'大马士革|拜占庭': ['拜占庭时期这里是基督教叙利亚的重镇,施洗约翰的圣髑相传就存放在城中的大教堂里。635 年阿拉伯军队围城后取得大马士革,次年雅尔穆克一战,整个黎凡特易手——拜占庭失去叙利亚,只用了两年。',
 'Under Byzantium this was a chief city of Christian Syria, and the relics of John the Baptist were said to rest in its cathedral. Arab armies besieged and took Damascus in 635, and at Yarmouk the following year the whole Levant changed hands — Byzantium lost Syria in the space of two years.'],
'大马士革|阿拉伯哈里发': ['661 年穆阿维叶在大马士革立朝,倭马亚王朝把这里定为都城——伊斯兰世界第一次有了一个王朝式的首都,版图西到西班牙、东到印度河。倭马亚大清真寺 705 年动工,用的是罗马神庙的地基和拜占庭工匠的镶嵌画。750 年阿拔斯取而代之、把中心迁往伊拉克,大马士革从此不再是中心。',
 'Muawiya founded his dynasty at Damascus in 661 and the Umayyads made it their capital — the first time the Islamic world had a dynastic seat, ruling from Spain to the Indus. The Umayyad Mosque was begun in 705 on the Roman temple platform, its mosaics laid by Byzantine craftsmen. When the Abbasids took over in 750 and moved the centre to Iraq, Damascus stopped being the centre of anything.'],
'大马士革|法蒂玛王朝': ['法蒂玛一度把大马士革收入版图,却始终没能牢牢管住:当地的逊尼派居民与来自埃及的什叶派政权彼此不服,城中屡有骚乱。这一段的大马士革夹在开罗与巴格达两个中心之间,谁也没能当它太久的主人。',
 'The Fatimids brought Damascus into their territory for a time but never held it firmly: its largely Sunni townspeople and the Shia regime out of Egypt did not accept each other, and there was recurring unrest. In these years Damascus lay between the two centres of Cairo and Baghdad, and neither was its master for long.'],
'大马士革|马穆鲁克': ['马穆鲁克把大马士革当作叙利亚的首府。1401 年帖木儿攻破此城,屠戮居民,唯独把工匠成批掳往撒马尔罕——他每打下一座城都这么办,好手艺人对他比金银有用。城后来重建了,可大马士革的玻璃器再没恢复到从前的水准。',
 'The Mamluks governed Syria from Damascus. In 1401 Timur stormed the city and killed its people, sparing the craftsmen only to deport them to Samarkand — he did this wherever he went, since good artisans were worth more to him than silver. The city was rebuilt, but its glasswork never came back to what it had been.'],
'大马士革|奥斯曼帝国': ['1516 年奥斯曼取得叙利亚,大马士革成为省城,也是每年麦加朝觐商队的两大集结地之一(另一处是开罗)——朝觐季节,几万人带着骆驼从这里出发穿越沙漠。这条路给这座城带来了长期而稳定的生意,一年一度,持续了四百年。',
 'The Ottomans took Syria in 1516 and Damascus became a provincial capital — and one of the two great assembly points, with Cairo, for the yearly pilgrim caravan to Mecca, which set out from here across the desert tens of thousands strong. That road gave the city a steady trade, once a year, for four hundred years.'],
'大马士革|现代中东': ['第一次世界大战后叙利亚成为法国委任统治地,1946 年独立,大马士革是首都。老城因为几千年从未中断的居住史,1979 年就列入了世界遗产名录;2011 年起的内战使部分城区严重损毁,数百万叙利亚人离开了国家。',
 'After the First World War Syria became a French mandate; it gained independence in 1946 with Damascus as capital. The old city, lived in without a break for thousands of years, was made a World Heritage Site as early as 1979; the war that began in 2011 wrecked parts of the city and drove millions of Syrians out of the country.'],
'耶路撒冷|罗马治下近东': ['70 年提图斯镇压犹太起义,焚毁第二圣殿,留下的是希律当年扩建圣殿山时筑的挡土墙,其中西边那一段就是今天的西墙。哈德良把城改建为罗马式的「爱利亚加比多连」,132 年犹太人再度起事,135 年兵败后被禁止进入故城——大流散由此加深。',
 'In 70 CE Titus crushed the Jewish revolt and burned the Second Temple; what stood were the retaining walls Herod had built when he enlarged the Temple Mount, the western stretch of them being today\'s Western Wall. Hadrian rebuilt the city as Roman "Aelia Capitolina"; a second revolt broke out in 132 and was crushed in 135, after which Jews were barred from the city, deepening the diaspora.'],
'巴格达|阿拉伯哈里发': ['762 年哈里发曼苏尔在底格里斯河畔建起正圆形的新都。此后近两百年,一般认为巴格达是世上最大的城市,城中的学者把希腊、波斯、印度的典籍译成阿拉伯文。',
 'In 762 Caliph al-Mansur founded a perfectly round new capital on the Tigris. For nearly two centuries Baghdad replaced Chang\'an as the largest city on earth, and its scholars translated Greek, Persian and Indian works into Arabic.'],
'耶路撒冷|古埃及': ['耶路撒冷最早见于埃及的「诅咒文书」,年代约在前十九到十八世纪;后来又出现在阿马尔纳的泥板书信里——当地城主写信给法老求援,说自己快守不住了。那时它只是犹地亚山地上的一座小城。',
 'Jerusalem first appears in the Egyptian execration texts of roughly the nineteenth and eighteenth centuries BC, and again in the Amarna letters, where its local ruler writes to pharaoh asking for troops because he cannot hold on. It was then a small town in the hills of Judah.'],
'耶路撒冷|亚述': ['前 701 年亚述王辛那赫里布围攻耶路撒冷,城没有攻下来。围城之前希西家王凿通了一条穿山的引水隧道,把城外的泉水引进城内;隧道壁上留着当时工匠刻的字,记的是两队人从两头对挖、最后凿通的那一刻——这是现存最早的希伯来文石刻之一。',
 'Sennacherib of Assyria besieged Jerusalem in 701 BC and did not take it. Before the siege king Hezekiah had a tunnel cut through the rock to bring the spring outside the wall in to the city; an inscription left on its wall records the moment the two gangs digging from opposite ends broke through to each other — one of the oldest pieces of written Hebrew that survives.'],
'耶路撒冷|新巴比伦': ['前 586 年尼布甲尼撒二世攻破耶路撒冷,焚毁第一圣殿,把犹地亚的上层人口掳往巴比伦。此后近五十年,这批人在异乡保住了自己的文字与信仰,并把口传的经典整理成书——被迫离开故土,反而促成了经典的成形。',
 'Nebuchadnezzar II broke into Jerusalem in 586 BC, burned the first temple and deported the leading families of Judah to Babylon. Over nearly fifty years in exile they held on to their script and their faith and set down in writing what had been carried orally — the forced departure was what gave the scriptures their shape.'],
'耶路撒冷|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['前 539 年居鲁士灭巴比伦后,准许被掳的人回耶路撒冷重建圣殿;第二圣殿约在前 516 年建成。波斯让当地人自治、按时纳贡,不插手他们的宗教与内部事务——这是波斯治理各地的一贯做法。',
 'After Cyrus took Babylon in 539 BC he let the exiles return to Jerusalem and rebuild; the second temple was finished around 516 BC. Persia left the locals to govern themselves and send tribute on time, without interfering in their religion or internal affairs — the way it handled its provinces generally.'],
'耶路撒冷|希腊化王朝': ['亚历山大之后,耶路撒冷先归托勒密、后归塞琉古。前 167 年塞琉古王安条克四世禁止犹太人的宗教活动、在圣殿里另立祭祀,引发马加比起义;三年后圣殿被重新洁净——光明节纪念的就是这件事。',
 'After Alexander, Jerusalem belonged first to the Ptolemies and then to the Seleucids. In 167 BC Antiochus IV banned Jewish worship and set up other rites in the temple, which set off the Maccabean revolt; three years later the temple was cleansed again — the event Hanukkah remembers.'],
'耶路撒冷|罗马帝国': ['326 年前后,君士坦丁的母亲海伦娜到耶路撒冷寻访圣迹;同一段时间里,君士坦丁下令在传说中的墓地上建圣墓教堂,335 年落成。一座被罗马摧毁又改了名字的城,两百多年后由罗马自己重新立成圣城。',
 'Around 326 Constantine\'s mother Helena came to Jerusalem looking for the holy sites, and in those same years the emperor ordered a church built over what was held to be the tomb; it was consecrated in 335. A city Rome had destroyed and renamed was made a holy city, two centuries later, by Rome itself.'],
'耶路撒冷|拜占庭': ['拜占庭时期耶路撒冷成为基督教朝圣的中心,城中修满教堂与修道院,人口回升。614 年萨珊波斯军队攻陷此城,圣墓教堂被毁、真十字架被掳走;629 年希拉克略把它夺回,九年之后,阿拉伯人来了。',
 'Under Byzantium Jerusalem became the centre of Christian pilgrimage, filled with churches and monasteries, and its population grew again. Sasanian Persian troops stormed it in 614, wrecking the Church of the Holy Sepulchre and carrying off the True Cross; Heraclius won it back in 629, and nine years after that the Arabs arrived.'],
'耶路撒冷|阿拉伯哈里发': ['638 年哈里发欧麦尔接管耶路撒冷。691 年圆顶清真寺在圣殿山上建成,是现存最早的伊斯兰建筑。今天那个金色的圆顶是二十世纪重新镀上去的——在那之前的几百年里,它一直是深色的铅顶。三种一神教都把这里当作圣地,这一点从那时起再没有改变过。',
 'The caliph Umar took over Jerusalem in 638. In 691 the Dome of the Rock was completed on the Temple Mount, the oldest work of Islamic architecture still standing. The gold dome it is known by today was re-covered in the twentieth century; for centuries before that the dome was dark lead. All three of the monotheistic faiths hold this place sacred, and that has not changed since.'],
'耶路撒冷|法蒂玛王朝': ['法蒂玛治下的耶路撒冷大体安定,但 1009 年哈里发哈基姆下令拆毁圣墓教堂,这件事在欧洲引起长久的震动,后来被十字军反复提起。1099 年第一次十字军攻陷耶路撒冷,城中居民遭到大规模屠杀。',
 'Jerusalem was largely quiet under the Fatimids, but in 1009 the caliph al-Hakim ordered the Church of the Holy Sepulchre pulled down, which shocked Europe for a long time afterwards and was raised again and again by the crusaders. In 1099 the First Crusade took the city and killed great numbers of its inhabitants.'],
'耶路撒冷|阿尤布王朝': ['1187 年萨拉丁在哈丁击溃十字军的野战军,同年收复耶路撒冷。与八十八年前十字军进城时不同,这次没有屠城:居民按人头交赎金就可以走,男的十第纳尔、女的五、小孩二;交不出的被卖为奴,人数以千计。基督徒此后仍可付费前来朝圣。这个处置在当时的欧洲被反复议论,连对手写的编年史都把它记了下来。',
 'Saladin destroyed the crusader field army at Hattin in 1187 and took Jerusalem the same year. Unlike the crusaders eighty-eight years before, he did not put the city to the sword: people could buy their way out at ten dinars a man, five a woman, two a child, and those who could not pay were sold into slavery, thousands of them. Christians could still come as pilgrims afterwards, for a fee. The terms were argued over in Europe for a long time, and chroniclers on the other side recorded them too.'],
'耶路撒冷|马穆鲁克': ['马穆鲁克把耶路撒冷当作宗教城市来经营:修经学院、修苏非道堂、修引水渠。老城里今天还看得见的马穆鲁克式石砌门楣、黑白相间的条纹拱券,大多是这两百多年留下的。政治与军事中心在开罗,这里不设重兵。',
 'The Mamluks ran Jerusalem as a religious city, endowing colleges, Sufi lodges and water channels. The Mamluk doorways in the old city, with their banded black-and-white stone arches, mostly date from these two centuries. The political and military weight sat in Cairo; no large garrison was kept here.'],
'耶路撒冷|奥斯曼帝国': ['1517 年奥斯曼取得这里——前一年他们刚拿下叙利亚。1535 到 1542 年苏莱曼一世重修城墙,今天老城外面那一圈墙就是那次修的,四百多年大体没有再变。他还修了引水渠与公共水池;至于老城分成四个区的画法,要到十九世纪才定型。',
 'The Ottomans took the city in 1517, the year after they took Syria. Between 1535 and 1542 Suleiman I rebuilt the walls — the circuit that still rings the old city, largely unchanged for over four centuries. He also restored the aqueduct and the public fountains; the familiar division of the old city into four quarters, however, only settled into its present form in the nineteenth century.'],
'耶路撒冷|现代中东': ['第一次世界大战后这里成为英国委任统治地。1948 年之后这座城被分开:西边归以色列,东边连同老城归约旦。1967 年以色列取得东耶路撒冷与老城并宣布合并,这一步没有得到国际普遍承认;巴勒斯坦方面主张东耶路撒冷是自己的首都。这座城的地位问题至今没有国际公认的解决方案。老城与城墙 1981 年列入世界文化遗产名录,次年即被列入濒危名单,至今仍在名单上。',
 'After the First World War this became British mandate territory. From 1948 the city was divided: the west under Israel, the east including the old city under Jordan. In 1967 Israel took East Jerusalem and the old city and declared them annexed, a step that has not been generally recognised internationally; the Palestinian side claims East Jerusalem as its own capital. There is still no internationally agreed settlement of the city\'s status. The old city and its walls were inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1981 and placed on the danger list the following year, where they remain.'],
'开罗|法蒂玛王朝': ['969 年法蒂玛军队征服埃及,在旧城之北建新都「开罗」——意为「胜利者」。次年动工的爱资哈尔清真寺,历经近百年中断后复兴,是伊斯兰世界延续至今的最古老学府之一。',
 'In 969 the Fatimid army took Egypt and founded a new capital north of the old town: al-Qahira, "the Victorious." The al-Azhar mosque, begun the next year, came back after nearly a century of suppression and is one of the oldest centers of learning still running in the Islamic world.'],
'撒马尔罕|帖木儿帝国': ['帖木儿把都城定在撒马尔罕,每征服一地就把最好的工匠掳回来营建它。比比哈努姆清真寺在他生前大体建成;他的孙子兀鲁伯后来在城里建起大天文台,测出的星表精度两百年内无人超越。',
 'Timur made Samarkand his capital and shipped home the best craftsmen from every conquest to build it. The Bibi-Khanym mosque rose in his lifetime; his grandson Ulugh Beg later built here the most precise observatory of the age.'],
'德里|印度河文明': ['印度河文明的核心在西边的印度河流域,德里一带只有零星的小聚落,没有摩亨佐达罗那样规划整齐的大城。这块地方要成为南亚的中心,还得再等三千年。',
 'The Indus civilisation had its centre on the Indus itself, well to the west; around Delhi there were only scattered small settlements, nothing like the planned cities of Mohenjo-daro. It would be three thousand years before this spot became a centre of anything.'],
'德里|吠陀时代': ['《摩诃婆罗多》里般度五子的都城因陀罗普拉斯塔,传说就在今天德里的老堡一带。老堡下面确实挖出过前 1000 年前后的彩绘灰陶,年代和史诗讲的时代对得上——但那只能证明这里那时有人住,证明不了故事是真的。',
 'The Mahabharata places Indraprastha, capital of the five Pandava brothers, at what is now the Purana Qila in Delhi. Painted Grey Ware of around 1000 BC has indeed been dug up beneath it, matching the epic\'s period — which proves people lived here then, not that the story happened.'],
'德里|孔雀王朝': ['孔雀王朝的都城在东边的华氏城,德里一带只是恒河与亚穆纳河之间平原上的一段通道。今天德里的两根阿育王石柱并不是原地立的——是十四世纪的苏丹菲鲁兹沙从别处整根运过来的,连怎么运的都留下了记载。',
 'The Mauryan capital was Pataliputra far to the east; Delhi was a stretch of the corridor between the Ganges and the Yamuna. The two Ashokan pillars in Delhi today were not raised here — sultan Firuz Shah had them brought whole from elsewhere in the fourteenth century, and even the method of moving them was written down.'],
'德里|贵霜帝国': ['贵霜的中心在西北的白沙瓦与马图拉,德里一带在它的东南方向。这一时期南亚与中亚、中国之间的商路格外热闹,佛教正是沿着这条路从犍陀罗一路传向东方的。',
 'The Kushans centred on Peshawar and Mathura to the northwest, with Delhi lying off to their southeast. Trade between South Asia, Central Asia and China was unusually busy in these years, and it was along that road that Buddhism travelled east out of Gandhara.'],
'德里|笈多王朝': ['德里的铁柱铸于笈多时期,高七米多,一千六百年几乎没有生锈。它抗锈的原因是铁里的磷在表面结成了一层保护膜,这件事现代冶金学到二十世纪才讲清楚。柱子原本也不在德里,是后来被移到顾特卜塔旁边的。',
 'The iron pillar of Delhi was cast in the Gupta period, stands over seven metres, and has scarcely rusted in sixteen hundred years. The reason is a protective film formed by phosphorus in the iron — something modern metallurgy only worked out in the twentieth century. The pillar was not originally in Delhi either; it was moved here beside the Qutb Minar.'],
'德里|中世纪诸王朝': ['八世纪起,拉杰普特的托马拉与乔汉两族先后在这一带筑城,「拉尔科特」是德里最早的一圈城墙。1192 年第二次德赖战役,乔汉王普里特维拉杰战败——通往德里的路就此打开,北印度此后进入另一段历史。',
 'From the eighth century the Rajput Tomara and Chauhan houses built here in turn, and Lal Kot was Delhi\'s first ring of walls. At the second battle of Tarain in 1192 the Chauhan king Prithviraj was beaten — the road to Delhi lay open, and northern India entered a different age.'],
'德里|马拉塔': ['十八世纪马拉塔一度控制德里,莫卧儿皇帝成了他们手里的一块招牌。1761 年第三次帕尼帕特战役,马拉塔败给阿富汗的阿卜达利,损失极重;这一败让他们无力填上莫卧儿留下的空缺,几十年后,填上那个空缺的是英国人。',
 'The Marathas held Delhi for a time in the eighteenth century, with the Mughal emperor as a signboard in their hands. At the third battle of Panipat in 1761 they were beaten by Abdali of Afghanistan and lost heavily; the defeat left them unable to fill the space the Mughals had left — and decades later the British filled it.'],
'德里|大英帝国·英国': ['1803 年东印度公司在德里城外击败马拉塔军队后接管这座城,莫卧儿皇帝变成领年金的名义君主。1857 年起义中德里是中心,起义者拥立年迈的巴哈杜尔·沙二世;城被攻破后他被流放到仰光,莫卧儿王朝到此结束。',
 'After beating a Maratha army outside Delhi in 1803 the East India Company took the city, and the Mughal emperor became a titular sovereign on a pension. Delhi was the centre of the rising of 1857, whose leaders proclaimed the aged Bahadur Shah II; when the city fell he was exiled to Rangoon, and the Mughal dynasty ended there.'],
'德里|英属印度': ['1911 年英国宣布把首都从加尔各答迁到德里,在老城南边另建新德里,1931 年正式启用。设计者鲁琴斯把英国的古典柱式与印度的圆顶、遮阳檐拼在一起。这是一座为了显示统治长久而建的城——建成之后十六年,那个统治就结束了。',
 'In 1911 Britain announced that the capital would move from Calcutta to Delhi, and New Delhi was laid out south of the old city, opening formally in 1931. Its designer Lutyens set English classical orders against Indian domes and deep eaves. It was a city built to show that the rule would last — and sixteen years after it opened, that rule was over.'],
'德里|印度·南亚诸国': ['1947 年独立与分治:约五十万印度教徒与锡克教徒迁入德里,约三十万穆斯林迁出,这座城在几年之内换掉了很大一部分居民。此后它从一座行政城市长成南亚最大的都会区之一。今天的德里其实是三座城叠在一起:旧德里、新德里,和不断向外摊开的卫星城带。',
 'At independence and partition in 1947 some half a million Hindus and Sikhs moved into Delhi and around three hundred thousand Muslims left; within a few years much of the city\'s population had been replaced. From an administrative city it grew into one of the largest metropolitan areas in South Asia. Today\'s Delhi is really three cities laid over each other: the old city, New Delhi, and the belt of satellite towns spreading outward.'],
'瓦拉纳西|孔雀王朝': ['瓦拉纳西是恒河边最古老的城市之一。城郊的鹿野苑是佛陀第一次讲法的地方,那大约是前 528 年、公元前六世纪的事;阿育王在这里立了石柱,柱头上的四只狮子,今天是印度的国徽。',
 'Varanasi is among the oldest cities on the Ganges. At Sarnath just outside it the Buddha gave his first teaching, around 528 BC, in the sixth century BC; Ashoka raised a pillar there, and the four lions of its capital are the state emblem of India today.'],
'瓦拉纳西|笈多王朝': ['笈多时期梵语文学与印度教哲学一同复兴,瓦拉纳西是几个学问中心之一。城中的湿婆信仰在这一时期大致定型;它的古名「迦尸」意思是「光之城」,这个名字比「瓦拉纳西」还要老。',
 'Sanskrit letters and Hindu philosophy revived together under the Guptas, and Varanasi was one of the centres of that learning. Its Shaiva worship took roughly its lasting form in these years. Its old name Kashi means the city of light, and is older still than Varanasi.'],
'瓦拉纳西|中世纪诸王朝': ['七世纪玄奘到访时,记下这里寺院与天祠并存、居民多信湿婆。此后几百年瓦拉纳西一直是印度教学问的中心,同时也见证了佛教在印度本土的退潮。鹿野苑一直撑到十二世纪末——那里最后一批建筑还是十二世纪中叶造的。',
 'When Xuanzang came in the seventh century he noted Buddhist monasteries and Hindu temples side by side, and a population mostly devoted to Shiva. For centuries afterwards Varanasi remained a centre of Hindu learning, and also watched Buddhism ebb away in the land of its birth. Sarnath held on to the end of the twelfth century — its last buildings went up in the middle of that century.'],
'瓦拉纳西|德里苏丹国': ['1194 年前后穆罕默德·古尔的部将攻入这一带,城中大量神庙被毁,鹿野苑的佛寺也在这一时期彻底废弃。此后几百年瓦拉纳西的神庙一再被拆、又一再重建——这座城的建筑大多不老,老的是它的位置和它的仪式。',
 'Around 1194 the generals of Muhammad of Ghor came through, many temples were destroyed, and the Buddhist establishment at Sarnath was finally abandoned. For centuries afterwards the temples of Varanasi were pulled down and rebuilt again and again — most of the city\'s buildings are not old; what is old is its site and its rituals.'],
'瓦拉纳西|马拉塔': ['十八世纪马拉塔与当地王公出钱,在恒河边修起大批石阶码头。今天游人看到的那一长排河阶,大多建于十八世纪——比大多数人以为的年轻得多。仪式很古老,承载仪式的石头却很新。',
 'In the eighteenth century Maratha rulers and local princes paid for the long flights of stone steps down to the Ganges. Most of the ghats visitors see today were built then — far younger than people assume. The rituals are ancient; the stone that carries them is not.'],
'瓦拉纳西|大英帝国·英国': ['1775 年后瓦拉纳西归东印度公司控制,后来设为一个受保护的土邦。英国人 1791 年在这里办起梵文学院,把印度教经典系统地整理与刊印——统治这个地方和整理它的经典,是同一批人做的事。',
 'After 1775 Varanasi came under East India Company control and was later run as a protected princely state. The British founded a Sanskrit college here in 1791 and set about editing and printing the Hindu classics systematically — governing the place and codifying its scriptures were done by the same people.'],
'瓦拉纳西|英属印度': ['1916 年印度教大学在这里创办,后来成为南亚最大的住宿制大学之一。同一年甘地在奠基典礼期间的讲座上讲话,当着满座王公的面批评他们的排场与铺张——这场演讲通常被看作他进入印度政治的起点之一。',
 'Banaras Hindu University was founded here in 1916 and became one of the largest residential universities in South Asia. Gandhi spoke there the same year, during the week of the foundation ceremony, and in front of the assembled princes criticised their display and extravagance — a speech usually counted as one of the beginnings of his political life in India.'],
'瓦拉纳西|印度·南亚诸国': ['今天的瓦拉纳西每天有几万人到河边沐浴,火化场终年不熄。恒河的治理是个长期难题:上游取水、沿岸排污与宗教用途彼此冲突,几十年来投入巨大而进展缓慢——一条河同时是水源、下水道和圣物,这三件事很难同时办好。',
 'Tens of thousands come down to the river to bathe every day, and the cremation grounds never go cold. Cleaning the Ganges is a long-running problem: upstream abstraction, riverside discharge and religious use pull against one another, and decades of heavy spending have moved slowly — a river that is at once water supply, sewer and sacred object is hard to serve in all three ways at once.'],
'巴特那|笈多王朝': ['笈多以华氏城为都的那段时间,这里仍是恒河平原的中心。法显五世纪初到访,记下城中的大寺与阿育王的宫殿——那时它还立着,他说这样的石工「非世所造」。两百多年后玄奘再来,这座城已经大半荒废了。',
 'While the Guptas ruled from Pataliputra this was still the centre of the Ganges plain. Faxian, arriving early in the fifth century, described the great monastery and Ashoka\'s palace, still standing then, and wrote that such stonework was not made by this world. When Xuanzang came two centuries later the city was largely deserted.'],
'巴特那|波罗王朝': ['波罗王朝的重心在东边的孟加拉,巴特那一带属于它的西部。这个王朝长期护持佛教:超戒寺是它新建并在这段时间达到鼎盛的,而那烂陀此前已经运转了三百多年,靠它继续供养。那烂陀离巴特那约九十公里,是当时世界上规模最大的佛教学问中心之一。',
 'The Pala kings had their weight in Bengal to the east, with Patna in their western half. They patronised Buddhism for generations: Vikramashila was their own foundation and reached its height under them, while Nalanda, already running for three centuries, went on under their endowments. Nalanda lies about ninety kilometres from Patna and was among the largest centres of Buddhist learning anywhere at the time.'],
'巴特那|莫卧儿帝国': ['莫卧儿把这里改名「阿兹马巴德」,可人们照旧叫它巴特那。它是恒河上重要的贸易口岸:硝石、鸦片与棉布从这里装船东下,十七世纪荷兰与英国的商馆都设在这一带。硝石是当时的火药原料,这门生意直接关系到欧洲人打得起多少仗。',
 'The Mughals renamed it Azimabad, and everyone went on calling it Patna. It was a major trading port on the Ganges — saltpetre, opium and cotton cloth were loaded here and taken downriver, and both Dutch and English factories stood nearby in the seventeenth century. Saltpetre was gunpowder\'s raw material, so that trade bore directly on how much war Europeans could afford.'],
'巴特那|马拉塔': ['十八世纪马拉塔骑兵多次深入比哈尔与孟加拉劫掠,当地把这些袭击叫作「博尔吉」。莫卧儿衰落之后,这一带的农村长期不得安宁,直到东印度公司接手——对种地的人来说,换谁来收税并不是最要紧的,要紧的是有没有人来抢。',
 'Maratha cavalry raided deep into Bihar and Bengal repeatedly in the eighteenth century; locally the raids were called bargi. After the Mughal decline the countryside here had no quiet for decades, until the East India Company took over — to the people farming it, who collected the tax mattered less than whether anyone came to plunder.'],
'巴特那|大英帝国·英国': ['1763 年巴特那发生英国人质被杀的事件,史称「巴特那屠杀」;次年布克萨尔战役英军得胜,1765 年东印度公司取得孟加拉与比哈尔的税收权。此后公司把鸦片的收购与加工中心设在这一带,产出的鸦片经加尔各答运往中国。',
 'In 1763 English prisoners were killed here in what became known as the Patna massacre; the company won the battle of Buxar the next year and in 1765 took the right to collect revenue in Bengal and Bihar. It then placed its opium buying and processing here, and the opium went out through Calcutta to China.'],
'巴特那|英属印度': ['1912 年比哈尔与奥里萨从孟加拉管区分出来,巴特那成为省会。1917 年甘地到附近的占巴朗,为被迫种植靛蓝的佃农出面交涉——那是他回国后在印度做的第一场群众运动,方法也是在那里第一次试出来的。',
 'In 1912 Bihar and Orissa were separated from the Bengal Presidency and Patna became the provincial capital. In 1917 Gandhi went to nearby Champaran to act for tenant farmers forced to grow indigo — his first mass campaign in India after returning home, and the first test of the method he would use afterwards.'],
'巴特那|印度·南亚诸国': ['今天巴特那是比哈尔邦的首府。它脚下就压着古代的华氏城遗址,考古发掘只能在几处零星展开——一座活着的城压在一座古城上面,这是南亚许多古都共同的处境:知道底下有什么,但挖不了。',
 'Patna is the capital of Bihar today. Ancient Pataliputra lies directly beneath it, and excavation is possible only in scattered patches — a living city sitting on top of an old one, the common situation of many South Asian capitals: everyone knows what is under there, and no one can dig it.'],
'德里|德里苏丹国': ['1206 年顾特卜丁·艾伊拜克在拉合尔登位,几年后德里成为都城,统治北印三百年的伊斯兰军人政权由此开端。他动工的顾特卜塔高七十余米,红砂岩砌成,是世界上最高的砖砌宣礼塔;塔旁清真寺的柱子按碑铭所记取自二十七座被拆的庙宇。',
 'In 1206 Qutb al-Din Aibak was raised to power at Lahore, and within a few years Delhi became the capital of a Turkic military regime that would rule north India for three centuries. The Qutb Minar he began stands over seventy metres in red sandstone, the tallest brick minaret in the world; the columns of the mosque beside it were taken, its inscription records, from twenty-seven demolished temples.'],
'德里|莫卧儿帝国': ['1648 年沙贾汗把都城从阿格拉迁到德里,新城以他自己命名为沙贾汉纳巴德。红堡与贾玛清真寺前后建起,今天的德里老城仍沿着那座城的骨架。',
 'In 1648 Shah Jahan moved the capital from Agra to Delhi and named the new city Shahjahanabad after himself. The Red Fort and then the Jama Masjid went up; Old Delhi still follows that city\'s plan.'],
'德里|巽伽与恒河诸国': ['这几百年德里一带仍是通道而不是中心:巽伽的都城在东边的华氏城,另一个中心在南边的毗底沙,而德里所在的这片恒河与亚穆纳河之间的平原,是两头往来必经的一段。这一时期的遗存并不少——城址、钱币、陶器都有,只是没有一处是都城。德里要再等一千多年才轮得到它。',
 'Through these centuries the country around Delhi remained a corridor rather than a centre: the Shunga capital lay east at Pataliputra and another centre south at Vidisha, while the plain between the Ganges and the Yamuna, where Delhi stands, was the stretch traffic had to cross. Remains from the period are not scarce — settlements, coins and pottery all turn up — but none of it is a capital. Delhi\'s turn was still more than a thousand years away.'],
'雅典|古希腊': ['前五世纪的雅典,公职多用抽签轮流担任,戏剧节上几千人同看一场悲剧。伯里克利主持重修卫城,帕特农神庙前后建了约十五年——它在山上立了两千多年,1687 年才被一发炮弹炸开。',
 'In fifth-century Athens most public offices were filled by lot, and several thousand would watch a tragedy together at the festivals. Pericles rebuilt the Acropolis; the Parthenon took some fifteen years. It stood on the hill for over two thousand years, until a shell blew it open in 1687.'],
'科尔多瓦|后倭马亚·安达卢斯': ['十世纪的科尔多瓦是当时欧洲最大的城市之一,哈卡姆二世的宫廷藏书以规模闻名。大清真寺的双层叠拱(下层是马蹄拱)架在罗马与西哥特的旧柱上;十六世纪又在正中盖起一座教堂,两种建筑至今套在一起。',
 'Tenth-century Cordoba was among the largest cities in Europe, and the palace library of al-Hakam II was famous for its size. The Great Mosque\'s two-tiered arches — horseshoe below, round above — rest on columns reused from Roman and Visigothic buildings; in the sixteenth century a cathedral was built into its middle, and the two still stand one inside the other.'],
'威尼斯|文艺复兴意大利': ['威尼斯是选举总督的贵族共和国,靠东方香料的转口生意致富。1497 年达·伽马绕过好望角、次年抵达印度,这条老商路的垄断从此松动。',
 'Venice was an aristocratic republic under an elected doge, made rich by the spice trade passing through from the East. When Vasco da Gama rounded the Cape in 1497 and sailed on to India, its hold on that old route began to slip.'],
'京都|日本': ['794 年桓武天皇迁都平安京,格局仿的是唐长安。此后一千多年这里一直是天皇所在,直到 1868 年江户奉诏改称东京,明治天皇随后东迁,次年定居下来。',
 'In 794 Emperor Kanmu moved the capital to Heian-kyo, laid out in imitation of Tang Chang\'an. It stayed the emperor\'s seat for over a thousand years, until Edo was renamed Tokyo by decree in 1868 and Emperor Meiji moved east, settling there the following year.'],
'墨西哥城|阿兹特克': ['特诺奇蒂特兰建在特斯科科湖中的岛上,靠三条堤道与陆地相连,城边是一畦畦浮田。1521 年西班牙人围城,切断堤道与饮水;今天的墨西哥城就压在这片排干的湖床上,又年年抽走地下的水,城至今还在往下沉。',
 'Tenochtitlan stood on an island in Lake Texcoco, joined to the shore by three causeways, its edges ringed with chinampa plots. In 1521 the Spanish besieged it and cut the causeways and the water supply; Mexico City sits on that drained lakebed today, and as groundwater keeps being pumped out from under it, the city is still sinking.'],
'廷巴克图|桑海帝国': ['1468 年桑海取得廷巴克图,此后一百多年这里是西非最重要的学问中心。桑科雷清真寺周围聚着大批学者,书籍是城中最贵的商品之一——当时一位到过这里的作者写道,做书的生意比做别的都赚钱。',
 'Songhai took Timbuktu in 1468 and for the next century and more it was the chief seat of learning in West Africa. Scholars gathered around the Sankore mosque and books were among the most valuable goods in the city — a writer who visited then recorded that more profit was made in the book trade than in any other line.'],
'廷巴克图|欧洲殖民非洲': ['十九世纪的欧洲人把廷巴克图想象成一座黄金之城,几支探险队为它送了命。1828 年法国人卡耶第一个到达并活着回来,他看到的是一座土屋组成的沙漠小城——传说破灭了,而真正值钱的东西(那些手稿)当时没人认。1893 年底一小队法军进城宣布吞并,次年才站稳。',
 'Nineteenth-century Europeans imagined Timbuktu as a city of gold and several expeditions died trying to reach it. In 1828 the Frenchman Caillié got there and came back alive; what he found was a small desert town of mud houses — the legend collapsed, and the thing that was actually valuable, the manuscripts, went unrecognised. A small French detachment entered the town and annexed it at the end of 1893, and only made that stick the following year.'],
'廷巴克图|现代非洲': ['廷巴克图 1988 年列入世界文化遗产。2012 年武装组织占据此城、毁掉多座陵墓,当地人把大批手稿偷偷运往南方保存了下来。2016 年国际刑事法院第一次以「破坏文化遗产」为罪名作出判决,针对的正是这件事。',
 'Timbuktu was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1988. In 2012 an armed group occupied the town and destroyed several mausoleums, while local people smuggled great numbers of manuscripts south to safety. In 2016 the International Criminal Court handed down its first conviction for the destruction of cultural heritage, and this was the case.'],
'加奥|马里帝国': ['加奥在马里帝国治下是它东边的一座大城。这一带的统治者很早就接受了伊斯兰教——加奥出土过十二世纪初的一批墓碑,大理石来自西班牙南部的阿尔梅里亚,是从地中海一路运过来的。为一块墓碑跨越撒哈拉,说明这条路当时有多通。',
 'Gao was a major city on the eastern side of the Mali empire. The local rulers here had adopted Islam long before that — tombstones from the early twelfth century found at Gao are cut from marble quarried at Almería in southern Spain and carried the whole way from the Mediterranean. That anyone would haul a gravestone across the Sahara says how open that road then was.'],
'加奥|欧洲殖民非洲': ['桑海崩溃之后加奥迅速衰落,到十九世纪只剩一个小镇。1898 年法军占领这里。跨撒哈拉的商路在这一时期被海运彻底取代——尼日尔河湾曾经是西非最富的地方,后来成了最偏远的地方之一。',
 'Gao fell away quickly after Songhai collapsed and by the nineteenth century was a small town. French troops occupied it in 1898. The trans-Saharan roads were finally displaced by sea traffic in these years — the bend of the Niger, once the richest country in West Africa, became one of its most remote.'],
'加奥|现代非洲': ['加奥今天是马里北部的一座城。1591 年之后它一直没能恢复,而阿斯基亚陵墓还立在那里——那座土坯垒成的金字塔式陵墓 2004 年列入世界文化遗产,是桑海留下的最显眼的一处建筑。',
 'Gao is a town in northern Mali today. It never recovered after 1591, but the tomb of Askia still stands — a stepped pyramid built of mud brick, inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 2004 and the most conspicuous thing Songhai left behind.'],
'卡诺|现代非洲': ['卡诺是尼日利亚北部最大的城市。城里的靛蓝染坑还在用,据说始于十五世纪末,是西非现存最老的一批;老城墙曾长达十几公里,如今只剩断断续续的土垄。它至今是撒哈拉南缘最重要的商业城市之一。',
 'Kano is the largest city in northern Nigeria. Its indigo dye pits are still worked and are said to date from the end of the fifteenth century, among the oldest surviving in West Africa; the old city wall once ran for more than ten kilometres and survives now only as broken earthen ridges. It remains one of the chief commercial cities along the southern edge of the Sahara.'],
'金沙萨|现代非洲': ['1960 年刚果独立,1966 年利奥波德维尔才改名金沙萨。此后几十年动荡不断,而城市人口从几十万涨到今天的一千八百多万,是撒哈拉以南最大的城市之一。它与对岸的布拉柴维尔隔刚果河相望;除了罗马与梵蒂冈这种特例,这是世界上距离最近的一对国家首都。',
 'Congo became independent in 1960, and Léopoldville was renamed Kinshasa only in 1966. Decades of upheaval followed, while the city grew from a few hundred thousand people to more than eighteen million, among the largest south of the Sahara. It faces Brazzaville across the Congo river; leaving aside a special case like Rome and the Vatican, these are the closest pair of national capitals anywhere.'],
'阿克苏姆|埃塞俄比亚帝国': ['阿克苏姆衰落之后,埃塞俄比亚的中心南移,但阿克苏姆一直是宗教上的圣城,历代皇帝按传统要来这里加冕。锡安圣母堂据信藏着约柜,只有一名指定的修士能进去看;这个说法无法查证,也从未被放弃。',
 'After Aksum declined the centre of Ethiopia moved south, but Aksum remained the holy city and emperors were by tradition crowned there. The church of Our Lady of Zion is held to keep the Ark of the Covenant, seen only by one appointed monk; the claim cannot be checked and has never been given up.'],
'阿克苏姆|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1937 年意大利占领期间,墨索里尼把阿克苏姆的一根方尖碑运到罗马竖了起来。2005 年它被运回埃塞俄比亚,分三批空运,是当时最重的空运货物之一;2008 年在原地重新立起。',
 'During the Italian occupation Mussolini had one of the Aksum obelisks taken to Rome and set up there in 1937. It was flown back to Ethiopia in three loads in 2005, among the heaviest air cargo ever moved at the time, and re-erected on its own ground in 2008.'],
'阿克苏姆|现代非洲': ['阿克苏姆 1980 年列入世界文化遗产。二十世纪以来的发掘揭出大片墓葬与宫殿地基;这个国家早期的文字材料主要是石碑与教会文献,而阿克苏姆当年铸的金币散落在印度与阿拉伯半岛,反倒成了断代最可靠的证据之一。',
 'Aksum was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1980. Excavation through the twentieth century uncovered extensive tombs and palace foundations. The written record for early Ethiopia is mostly stelae and church documents, while the gold coins Aksum struck, found scattered in India and Arabia, turn out to be among the firmest evidence for dating it.'],
'亚的斯亚贝巴|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1936 年意大利军队占领亚的斯亚贝巴,皇帝流亡英国;1941 年英军与埃塞俄比亚的抵抗力量把意大利人赶走,皇帝返回。这五年通常被算作这个国家历史上仅有的一段被外国统治的时期——非洲绝大多数地方在同一时期都处在殖民统治下,埃塞俄比亚是少数的例外。',
 'Italian troops occupied Addis Ababa in 1936 and the emperor went into exile in Britain; in 1941 British forces and Ethiopian resistance drove the Italians out and he returned. Those five years are usually counted as the only stretch of foreign rule in the country\'s history — while nearly all of Africa was under colonial rule in the same period, Ethiopia was one of the few exceptions.'],
'亚的斯亚贝巴|现代非洲': ['1963 年非洲统一组织在亚的斯亚贝巴成立,总部就设在这里;它后来改组为非洲联盟,总部仍在这座城。把一个从未被长期殖民的国家的首都选作整个非洲的政治会场,这个选择本身就是一句话。',
 'The Organisation of African Unity was founded at Addis Ababa in 1963 and headquartered there; it was later reconstituted as the African Union, still based in the city. Choosing the capital of one of the two countries never long colonised as the meeting place of the whole continent was itself a statement.'],
'大津巴布韦|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1871 年德国探险家毛赫到达这片废墟,认定它是仿照示巴女王的宫殿建的。真正的破坏发生在此后:1890 年代罗得斯手下的公司以搜寻黄金为名把这一带的石城翻了个遍,金器被熔掉,地层被彻底搅乱——今天研究大津巴布韦最大的困难不是年代久远,是那几年。',
 'The German explorer Karl Mauch reached the ruins in 1871 and decided they had been built in imitation of the Queen of Sheba\'s palace. The real damage came later: in the 1890s a company set up under Rhodes to hunt for gold went through the stone sites of this country, melting down what it found and churning the archaeological layers beyond recovery — the hardest obstacle to studying Great Zimbabwe today is not age but those few years.'],
'大津巴布韦|现代非洲': ['1980 年独立时,这个国家用这座石城的名字给自己命名。遗址 1986 年列入世界文化遗产;遗址上出土的皂石鸟出现在国旗与货币上——一个国家用一座废墟给自己起名,是在说这段历史属于谁。',
 'At independence in 1980 the country took its name from these stone ruins. The site was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1986, and the soapstone bird found there appears on the flag and the currency — naming a country after a ruin is a way of saying whose history it is.'],
'蒙巴萨|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1895 年英国把这一带设为东非保护地,蒙巴萨是首府与港口。1896 年动工的乌干达铁路从这里往内陆修,工程极其艰难;招来的印度劳工中有不少人留了下来,东非的南亚社群有很多可以追到这条铁路。',
 'Britain made this coast the East Africa Protectorate in 1895 with Mombasa as its capital and port. The Uganda Railway, begun in 1896, was driven inland from here at great difficulty; many of the Indian labourers brought in for it stayed, and much of the South Asian community in East Africa traces back to that line.'],
'蒙巴萨|现代非洲': ['蒙巴萨今天是肯尼亚最大的港口。耶稣堡 2011 年列入世界文化遗产;老城的巷道、门楣与阳台混着阿拉伯、印度、葡萄牙与斯瓦希里的做法——印度洋这一岸的城市,长相都是被季风吹出来的。',
 'Mombasa is Kenya\'s largest port today. Fort Jesus was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 2011, and the lanes, doorways and balconies of the old town mix Arab, Indian, Portuguese and Swahili practice — the look of the towns on this shore of the Indian Ocean was blown into shape by the monsoon.'],
'基尔瓦|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1505 年葡萄牙人攻占基尔瓦并筑堡,城邦的黄金转口生意随之断掉。此后基尔瓦一蹶不振,到十九世纪只剩渔村;德国人在十九世纪末控制这一带时,岛上的大清真寺早已是废墟。',
 'The Portuguese stormed Kilwa in 1505 and built a fort there, and the gold trade the city lived on was cut off. Kilwa never recovered; by the nineteenth century it was a fishing village, and when the Germans took this coast at the end of that century the great mosque on the island had long been a ruin.'],
'基尔瓦|现代非洲': ['基尔瓦遗址 1981 年列入世界文化遗产。那座珊瑚石砌的大清真寺是撒哈拉以南最早的一批石构清真寺之一;遗址长期缺乏维护,一度被列入濒危名单,到 2014 年才除名。',
 'The Kilwa ruins were inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1981. Its great mosque, built of coral stone, is among the earliest stone mosques south of the Sahara; the site went untended for a long time and sat on the danger list until it was removed in 2014.'],
'拉各斯|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1851 年英国海军炮击拉各斯,1861 年正式吞并,理由之一是取缔奴隶贸易——而在此之前的三百年里,这一带正是大西洋奴隶贸易最主要的出口点之一。1914 年南北尼日利亚合并,拉各斯成为首都。',
 'The British navy bombarded Lagos in 1851 and annexed it in 1861, one stated reason being the suppression of the slave trade — while for the three centuries before that this coast had been among the principal points of export for that same trade. Northern and southern Nigeria were amalgamated in 1914 with Lagos as the capital.'],
'开普敦|欧洲殖民非洲': ['荷兰与英国先后统治期间,开普敦的人口来自四面八方:欧洲移民、从东南亚与东非贩运来的奴隶、当地的科伊桑人。今天南非的有色人社群与开普马来人社群的形成,都可以追到这一段。',
 'Under Dutch and then British rule the population of Cape Town came from every direction: European settlers, people enslaved and shipped from Southeast Asia and East Africa, and the Khoisan of the country itself. The Coloured community of South Africa and the Cape Malay community both took shape in these years.'],
'开普敦|现代非洲': ['1948 年后种族隔离制度把开普敦按肤色分区,第六区的居民被整体迁走、房屋推平。1990 年曼德拉出狱当天,正是在开普敦市政厅的阳台上发表了第一次公开讲话;关过他十八年的罗本岛 1999 年列入世界文化遗产。',
 'After 1948 apartheid zoned Cape Town by colour and the people of District Six were removed wholesale and their houses bulldozed. On the day Mandela walked free in 1990 he gave his first public speech from the balcony of Cape Town city hall; Robben Island, where he had been held for eighteen years, was made a World Heritage Site in 1999.'],
'麦罗埃|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1834 年一名意大利医生费利尼为找财宝炸开了麦罗埃金字塔的塔顶,他自述拆了五六座;跟着他来的盗宝者又毁掉几十座。十九世纪末英国控制苏丹。盗宝对遗址的破坏,常常比时间还快——金字塔在沙漠里立了两千年,几个月就被拆掉一批。',
 'In 1834 an Italian doctor named Ferlini blew the tops off pyramids at Meroe looking for treasure — five or six by his own account; the imitators who followed him wrecked dozens more. Britain took control of Sudan at the end of that century. Treasure hunting damages a site faster than time does — pyramids that had stood two thousand years in the desert were pulled apart in a few months.'],
'麦罗埃|现代非洲': ['麦罗埃 2011 年列入世界文化遗产。遗址边上堆着大片冶铁留下的炉渣,规模大到十九世纪的旅行者一度以为那是天然的黑色土丘——库施的冶铁产量在当时的非洲少有对手,而这些渣堆至今是判断它规模最直接的证据。一个王国留下的最硬的痕迹,有时不是它的王陵,是它的垃圾。',
 'Meroe was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 2011. Beside the site lie great banks of slag left from ironworking, so large that nineteenth-century travellers took them for natural black hills — Kush smelted iron on a scale few in Africa matched, and those heaps remain the most direct evidence of how much. The hardest trace a kingdom leaves is sometimes not its royal tombs but its rubbish.'],
'墨西哥城|特奥蒂瓦坎': ['特奥蒂瓦坎在今天墨西哥城东北约四十公里。它鼎盛时是美洲最大的城市,墨西哥谷地的其他聚落都在它的影响之下;七百多年后阿兹特克人来到这片废墟,给它起名「众神诞生之地」——他们并不知道建城的是谁。',
 'Teotihuacan lies about forty kilometres northeast of Mexico City. At its height it was the largest city in the Americas and every other settlement in the valley of Mexico stood under its influence; some seven hundred years later the Aztecs came upon the ruins and named the place where the gods were born — they had no idea who had built it.'],
'墨西哥城|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['1521 年西班牙人攻陷特诺奇蒂特兰之后,在原址上建新城:神庙被拆,石头用来盖主教座堂,湖被逐步排干。一座城压在另一座城上面,而底下那座至今还在往上顶——大神庙的遗址 1978 年被发现,起因是电力工人挖到了一块巨石。',
 'After the Spanish took Tenochtitlan in 1521 they built a new city on the same ground: the temples came down, their stone went into the cathedral, and the lake was drained by degrees. One city sits on another, and the one underneath keeps pushing up — the Templo Mayor was found in 1978 because electrical workers digging a trench struck a great carved stone.'],
'墨西哥城|西葡殖民美洲': ['墨西哥城是新西班牙总督区的中心,美洲最大的城市之一。1551 年这里创办了美洲最早的一批大学之一。白银从萨卡特卡斯运来,一部分经阿卡普尔科运往马尼拉,换回中国的丝绸与瓷器——这条航线让墨西哥城成了两个大洋之间的枢纽。',
 'Mexico City was the seat of the viceroyalty of New Spain and among the largest cities in the Americas. One of the earliest universities in the Americas was founded here in 1551. Silver came down from Zacatecas, and part of it went out through Acapulco to Manila and came back as Chinese silk and porcelain — that route made the city a hinge between two oceans.'],
'墨西哥城|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1821 年墨西哥独立。今天的墨西哥城是西半球人口最多的都会区之一,而它建在排干的湖床上:抽取地下水使地面持续下沉,近百年来市中心沉了将近十米,而且各处沉得不一样快——大教堂的地板是歪的,那就是沉出来的。',
 'Mexico gained independence in 1821. Mexico City is now among the most populous metropolitan areas in the western hemisphere, and it stands on a drained lakebed: groundwater extraction has made it sink steadily, the centre dropping close to ten metres over the past century and at different rates in different places — the cathedral floor slopes, and that is what did it.'],
'墨西哥城|托尔特克与谷地诸邦': ['阿兹特克人到来之前的几百年,这片谷地不属于任何一个大政权,而是散落着许多小城邦,各自守着湖边的一块地。图拉在今天墨西哥城西北约六十公里,是其中最强的一个,但它更像盟主而不是帝国。后来阿兹特克人建三方同盟、靠联姻与朝贡统治谷地,用的还是这几百年里摸出来的那套办法——他们接手的不只是这片土地,还有一套怎么管它的规矩。',
 'For the centuries before the Aztecs arrived, this valley belonged to no single power: it held a scatter of city-states, each holding a stretch of lakeshore. Tula, some sixty kilometres northwest of today\'s Mexico City, was the strongest of them, though it looks more like the head of a league than an empire. When the Aztecs later built their triple alliance and ran the valley on marriage and tribute, they were using the method these centuries had worked out — what they inherited was not only the land but a way of holding it.'],
'特奥蒂瓦坎|阿兹特克': ['阿兹特克人到达墨西哥谷地时,特奥蒂瓦坎已经废弃了七百多年。他们把这里当作圣地,给几座金字塔起了名字,并相信众神就是在这里造出太阳与月亮的——一个民族替另一个他们并不认识的民族的废墟,编了一套来历。',
 'By the time the Aztecs reached the valley of Mexico, Teotihuacan had been abandoned for over seven hundred years. They treated it as a holy place, gave its pyramids names, and believed the gods had made the sun and the moon there — one people supplying an origin story for the ruins of another it knew nothing about.'],
'特奥蒂瓦坎|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['西班牙人来的时候,这片废墟已经被土和草盖住,看上去只是几座山丘。整个殖民时代它都没被当回事——一座曾经是美洲最大的城市,在地图上什么也不是。',
 'When the Spanish arrived the ruins were under earth and grass and looked like nothing more than hills. Through the whole colonial period the site counted for nothing — a city that had once been the largest in the Americas was not even a mark on the map.'],
'特奥蒂瓦坎|西葡殖民美洲': ['殖民时期这一带是农田与村庄。金字塔的石料被拆走盖房、修路——一座已经没有主人的城,通常会被当成采石场,这件事在世界各地都一样。',
 'Through the colonial centuries this was farmland and villages. Stone was carried off the pyramids for houses and roads — a city with no one left to own it usually ends up as a quarry, and that is as true here as anywhere.'],
'特奥蒂瓦坎|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1905 年起墨西哥政府开始大规模发掘与修复特奥蒂瓦坎,1910 年独立百年庆典时对外开放,1987 年列入世界文化遗产。它有没有一套完整的文字,学界至今没有定论;遗址上那些符号至今还读不通,近年才有人提出部分解读的方案——这座美洲曾经最大的城,到现在也没有留下一段大家都读得懂的记录。',
 'From 1905 the Mexican government began large-scale excavation and restoration at Teotihuacan, opening it for the centenary of independence in 1910; it was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1987. Whether it had a full writing system at all is still argued over, and the signs found on the site still cannot be read through, though partial readings have lately been proposed — the largest city the Americas ever had has yet to yield a record anyone can follow.'],
'奇琴伊察|西葡殖民美洲': ['1530 年代西班牙人一度想在奇琴伊察建城,被玛雅人赶走;尤卡坦的征服前后打了近二十年。1562 年主教兰达在玛尼焚烧了大批玛雅文书,后来又写了一本详细记录玛雅文字与历法的书。他记下的那份「字母表」长期被认为不可靠,直到 1950 年代有人看出它其实是一份音节表,玛雅文的破译才真正开始——烧书的人留下了后来解锁这套文字的钥匙。',
 'The Spanish tried to plant a town at Chichen Itza in the 1530s and were driven out by the Maya; the conquest of Yucatan took the better part of twenty years. In 1562 Bishop Landa burned a great many Maya books at Mani, and then wrote a detailed account of Maya writing and the calendar. The alphabet he recorded was long dismissed as worthless, until in the 1950s someone saw that it was really a syllabary — and only then did decipherment begin. The man who burned the books left the key that opened the script.'],
'奇琴伊察|拉丁美洲诸国': ['奇琴伊察 1988 年列入世界文化遗产,是墨西哥参观人数最多的遗址之一。春分秋分前后的那些下午,卡斯蒂略金字塔的台阶边缘会投出一道锯齿形的影子,像一条蛇顺阶而下——是不是有意这么设计的,至今还没有定论。',
 'Chichen Itza was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1988 and is among the most visited sites in Mexico. On afternoons around the equinoxes a saw-toothed shadow falls along the edge of the Castillo\'s stair like a serpent coming down it — whether that was deliberately designed is still an open question.'],
'蒂卡尔|西葡殖民美洲': ['蒂卡尔在西班牙人到来之前几百年就被放弃了,雨林把它盖住。佩滕地区的伊察王国一直撑到 1697 年才被西班牙人攻灭——那是最后一个独立的玛雅王国。美洲还有撑得更久的:南边的马普切人和西班牙人隔河对峙了近三百年。',
 'Tikal had been abandoned for centuries before the Spanish came and the forest had closed over it. The Itza of the Peten held out until 1697 — the last independent Maya kingdom to fall. Others in the Americas lasted longer: the Mapuche in the far south faced the Spanish across a river for close to three centuries.'],
'蒂卡尔|拉丁美洲诸国': ['蒂卡尔 1979 年列入世界遗产,是最早一批同时以文化与自然价值入选的遗址之一。神庙金字塔从雨林树冠上顶出来,《星球大战》曾在这里取景;而遗址周围的雨林本身,也在保护范围之内。',
 'Tikal was inscribed in 1979 among the first sites listed for both cultural and natural value. Its temple pyramids push up through the forest canopy — Star Wars was filmed here — and the rainforest around the ruins is itself part of what is protected.'],
'库斯科|西葡殖民美洲': ['1533 年西班牙人进入库斯科,拆掉印加的神庙,在原来的墙基上盖起教堂与宅第。今天老城的下半截是印加的石墙、上半截是西班牙的建筑;1950 年一场大地震震塌了不少殖民时期的房子,而底下那些不用灰浆的印加石墙纹丝没动。',
 'The Spanish entered Cusco in 1533, pulled down the Inca temples and raised churches and mansions on their foundations. The lower half of the old town is Inca stonework and the upper half is Spanish; an earthquake in 1950 brought down a good deal of the colonial building while the mortarless Inca walls beneath did not move.'],
'库斯科|拉丁美洲诸国': ['库斯科 1983 年列入世界文化遗产。1911 年美国人宾厄姆在附近山脊上「发现」了马丘比丘——当地农民一直知道它在那里,还有人住在遗址上种地。今天那里是南美洲游客最多的地方之一。',
 'Cusco was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1983. In 1911 the American Hiram Bingham announced the discovery of Machu Picchu on a ridge nearby — local farmers had always known it was there and some were living on the site and working the terraces. It is now among the most visited places in South America.'],
'利马|查文文化': ['查文文化的中心查文德万塔尔在安第斯山中,直线离利马约二百七十公里,走山路要四百多公里。这是安第斯最早的一次大范围文化统一——不是靠军队,是靠一套宗教图像:同一种猫科神像的样式,出现在相隔几百公里的遗址上。',
 'Chavín de Huántar, the centre of the Chavín culture, lies in the Andes about two hundred and seventy kilometres from Lima as the crow flies, and over four hundred by road. It marks the first wide cultural unification in the Andes — achieved not by armies but by a body of religious imagery: the same feline deity style turns up at sites hundreds of kilometres apart.'],
'利马|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['皮萨罗把新城选在这里,看中的是离海近、有河、气候干燥——而不是因为原住民的中心在这里。西班牙人在美洲反复做同一件事:不用原来的都城,自己另选一个便于把东西运回欧洲的位置。',
 'Pizarro put his new city here because it was near the sea, had a river and a dry climate — not because it was where the indigenous centre had been. The Spanish did the same thing again and again in the Americas: leave the old capital and pick a site convenient for shipping things back to Europe.'],
'利马|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1821 年秘鲁在利马宣布独立。今天的利马住着全国约三分之一的人口,而它建在世界上最干旱的海岸之一,几乎不下雨,主要靠安第斯山上下来的几条河、再加上地下水井供水——一座上千万人的城市,水源都在山里。',
 'Peru declared independence at Lima in 1821. Around a third of the country\'s people now live there, on one of the driest coasts on earth where it almost never rains; the city runs mostly on a few rivers coming down out of the Andes, with wells making up the rest — ten million people whose water is all up in the mountains.'],
'波哥大|西葡殖民美洲': ['1538 年西班牙人在穆伊斯卡人的土地上建起波哥大。穆伊斯卡的黄金工艺极精,「黄金国」的传说就出自他们的一项仪式:新首领全身涂满金粉,乘筏到瓜塔维塔湖中把金器投进湖里。西班牙人为此几次想抽干那座湖,收获寥寥。',
 'The Spanish founded Bogotá in 1538 in Muisca country. Muisca goldwork was very fine, and the legend of El Dorado comes from one of their rites: a new chief covered head to foot in gold dust would go out on a raft into Lake Guatavita and cast gold objects into the water. The Spanish tried more than once to drain that lake and got very little for it.'],
'布宜诺斯艾利斯|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1810 年五月革命之后,布宜诺斯艾利斯逐步成为阿根廷的中心。十九世纪末到二十世纪初,数以百万计的意大利与西班牙移民在这里上岸,城市人口几十年里翻了好几番;探戈就是在这批移民聚居的港区形成的——拉普拉塔河对岸的蒙得维的亚同样是它的发源地。',
 'After the May revolution of 1810 Buenos Aires became the centre of Argentina by degrees. Between the end of the nineteenth century and the start of the twentieth, millions of Italian and Spanish immigrants landed here and the city multiplied several times over within decades; the tango took shape in the dockside districts where they settled — and equally across the estuary in Montevideo.'],
'里约热内卢|西葡殖民美洲': ['1763 年葡萄牙把巴西的首府从萨尔瓦多迁到里约——因为米纳斯吉拉斯的黄金要从这里出海。十八世纪巴西产的黄金有相当一部分并没有留在葡萄牙,而是通过贸易逆差流向了英国:金子经过谁的手,和最后归谁所有,是两回事。',
 'In 1763 Portugal moved the capital of Brazil from Salvador to Rio, because the gold of Minas Gerais went out through this harbour. A large share of the gold Brazil produced in the eighteenth century did not stay in Portugal but flowed on to Britain through the trade balance — whose hands gold passes through and whose it finally becomes are two different questions.'],
'圣地亚哥|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1818 年智利独立,圣地亚哥是首都。这座城夹在安第斯山与海岸山脉之间的盆地里,冬天空气不流通,污染物积在城市上空散不掉——地形决定了这座城最难解决的问题之一。',
 'Chile became independent in 1818 with Santiago as its capital. The city sits in a basin between the Andes and the coastal range, and in winter the air does not move, so pollution collects over it and stays — the shape of the land decides one of the hardest problems this city has.'],
'哈瓦那|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1898 年美西战争后西班牙退出古巴,1902 年古巴独立。1959 年革命之后的禁运让这座城的时间在某种意义上停住了:街上还跑着五十年代的美国车,没有钱大拆大建,老城的街巷格局反而没被推平改掉——不过房子本身塌了不少,失修一直是这里最大的问题。老哈瓦那 1982 年列入世界文化遗产。',
 'Spain left Cuba after the war of 1898 and the country became independent in 1902. After the revolution of 1959 the embargo stopped the city\'s clock in a certain sense: American cars from the fifties still run in the streets, and with no money for wholesale rebuilding the street pattern of the old town was never bulldozed away — though many of the buildings themselves have fallen in, and decay remains the worst problem here. Old Havana was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1982.'],
'卡霍基亚|美国': ['十九世纪的美国人普遍不相信这些土丘是本地原住民建的,提出过各种「失落民族」的说法;考古学早已把这些说法一一否掉。卡霍基亚 1982 年列入世界文化遗产。今天从僧侣丘顶上望出去,能看见对岸圣路易斯的天际线。',
 'Nineteenth-century Americans mostly refused to believe the mounds were built by Native people and proposed a series of lost-race theories; archaeology has disposed of every one of them. Cahokia was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1982. From the top of Monks Mound today you can see the skyline of St Louis across the river.'],
'廷巴克图|马里帝国': ['1325 年曼萨·穆萨朝觐归来,出资在廷巴克图造起津加里贝尔清真寺(约 1327 年)。这座沙漠边的商城此后成了西非的书籍集散地,一代代抄本传到今天,是撒哈拉以南最大的手稿群之一。',
 'Mansa Musa came home from his pilgrimage in 1325 and paid for the Djinguereber mosque at Timbuktu, finished around 1327. The desert trading town became West Africa\'s book market, and the manuscripts copied there have been handed down to this day — among the largest such collections in sub-Saharan Africa.'],
'巴格达|苏美尔·阿卡德': ['巴格达所在的这段两河平原,是苏美尔城邦向北的边缘。阿卡德王萨尔贡的都城阿伽德一般认为就在这一带,但至今没有找到——两河流域出过那么多被挖出来的城,最有名的那座首都反而是找不到的。',
 'The stretch of the Two Rivers where Baghdad stands was the northern edge of the Sumerian city-states. Sargon\'s capital Agade is generally placed somewhere near here, but it has never been found — of all the cities Mesopotamia has given up to the spade, its most famous capital is the one still missing.'],
'巴格达|古巴比伦': ['汉谟拉比的巴比伦在这里往南约八十公里。巴格达一带当时是巴比伦王国北部的农田,靠运河灌溉——两河流域的城市从来不是靠下雨活着,而是靠一套要不断清淤的渠网,谁管住了渠,谁就管住了这片平原。',
 'Hammurabi\'s Babylon lay some eighty kilometres south of here. This was farmland in the north of his kingdom, watered by canals — cities in Mesopotamia never lived on rainfall but on a network of channels that had to be dredged without stopping, and whoever controlled the channels controlled the plain.'],
'巴格达|亚述': ['亚述的都城在更北的尼尼微与尼姆鲁德,巴格达一带是亚述南下控制巴比伦尼亚的通道。亚述人靠铁器与成建制的工兵打仗,又把征服地的人口成批迁走、打散安置——这套做法让帝国扩张得很快,也让它境内到处是不认同它的人。',
 'The Assyrian capitals lay further north at Nineveh and Nimrud, and this stretch was the corridor by which Assyria reached down into Babylonia. The Assyrians fought with iron and with organised engineer units, and moved conquered populations wholesale, breaking them up and resettling them elsewhere — a method that expanded the empire fast and filled it with people who did not think of themselves as belonging to it.'],
'巴格达|新巴比伦': ['新巴比伦重新以巴比伦为都,这一带回到它的直辖区。尼布甲尼撒二世修城墙、建伊什塔尔门,又在前 586 年攻破耶路撒冷、把犹地亚的上层人口掳到巴比伦——《圣经》里的「巴比伦之囚」就是这一段。',
 'The Neo-Babylonian kings ruled again from Babylon and this land came back under it directly. Nebuchadnezzar II rebuilt the walls and raised the Ishtar Gate, and in 586 BC he took Jerusalem and carried the leading families of Judah off to Babylon — the captivity the Bible remembers.'],
'巴格达|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['前 539 年居鲁士进巴比伦,两河流域归波斯。波斯把这里划为总督辖区,修了贯通帝国的御道与驿站;巴比伦仍是帝国最富的城市之一,波斯王每年在这里过冬——征服者住进了被征服者的城,而不是把它拆掉。',
 'Cyrus entered Babylon in 539 BC and Mesopotamia became Persian. It was made a satrapy, and the royal road with its posthouses was run across the empire; Babylon stayed one of its richest cities and the king wintered there each year — the conqueror moved into the conquered city rather than pulling it down.'],
'巴格达|希腊化王朝': ['塞琉古一世在底格里斯河畔建了塞琉西亚,就在今天巴格达南边不远。巴比伦的人口被大批迁进新城——传统说法记在他名下,而楔形文字的一手记录写的是他儿子安条克一世下的令。巴比伦从此一路衰落:一座新都吸干一座旧都,这件事在两河流域发生过不止一次。',
 'Seleucus I founded Seleucia on the Tigris, not far south of today\'s Baghdad, and much of Babylon\'s population was moved into it — the old accounts credit him, while the cuneiform record of the move names his son Antiochus I. Babylon declined from then on: a new capital draining an old one, which happened in Mesopotamia more than once.'],
'巴格达|帕提亚·萨珊': ['帕提亚人在塞琉西亚对岸建了泰西封,萨珊接着拿它做都城,前后当了约七百年的两河首府——遗址就在巴格达东南三十多公里。那座宫殿留下的砖砌大拱跨度二十五米多,没有钢筋也没有骨架,一千五百年后还立着。',
 'The Parthians built Ctesiphon across the river from Seleucia and the Sasanians kept it as their capital; for some seven hundred years it was the chief city of Mesopotamia, and its ruins stand about thirty-five kilometres southeast of Baghdad. The great brick arch of its hall spans over twenty-five metres with no steel and no frame, and it is still standing fifteen centuries later.'],
'巴格达|罗马帝国': ['罗马军队五次攻下泰西封:图拉真 116 年、卡西乌斯 165 年、塞维鲁 197 年、卡鲁斯 283 年、伽列里乌斯 298 年,每次都没能守住;尤利安 363 年打到城下,连攻都没攻下来。两河下游是罗马与波斯之间拉锯了几百年的战场,罗马始终没能在这里长期立足。',
 'Roman armies took Ctesiphon five times — Trajan in 116, Cassius in 165, Severus in 197, Carus in 283, Galerius in 298 — and could hold it none of those times; Julian reached its walls in 363 and could not take it at all. The lower Two Rivers were the ground on which Rome and Persia pushed at each other for centuries, and Rome never managed to stay.'],
'巴格达|塞尔柱突厥': ['早在 945 年白益王朝进入巴格达时,哈里发就已经被架空。1055 年塞尔柱的图格里勒进城换掉了白益人,哈里发依旧保住宗教领袖的名分,实权归苏丹。此后哈里发是名义上的共主、苏丹是真正管事的人——这套「哈里发加苏丹」的双头结构,后来在伊斯兰世界用了好几百年。',
 'The caliph had already been reduced to a figurehead in 945, when the Buyids entered Baghdad. Tughril the Seljuk came in 1055 and replaced them; the caliph still kept his standing as religious head, and real power stayed with the sultan. From then on the caliph reigned in name and the sultan governed in fact — a two-headed arrangement that the Islamic world would use for centuries.'],
'巴格达|伊尔汗国': ['1258 年旭烈兀攻破巴格达,末代哈里发被处死,延续五百多年的阿拔斯王朝在这里终结。城中的藏书与周边的灌溉渠网都遭重创;此后巴格达再没回到它最盛时的地位,伊斯兰世界的重心转向了开罗,后来又转向伊斯坦布尔。',
 'Hulagu stormed Baghdad in 1258 and had the last caliph put to death, ending the Abbasid line after more than five hundred years. The city\'s libraries and the irrigation canals around it were both wrecked; Baghdad never returned to what it had been, and the weight of the Islamic world shifted to Cairo and later to Istanbul.'],
'巴格达|奥斯曼帝国': ['1534 年苏莱曼从萨法维手里取得巴格达。此后两百年,它一直是奥斯曼与波斯争夺的边城:易手集中在头一百年里,再往后波斯几次围城都没能破城。从帝国的心脏变成帝国的边疆,城市规模长期没有恢复。',
 'Suleiman took Baghdad from the Safavids in 1534. For the next two hundred years it was a frontier town contested by Ottomans and Persians: it changed hands within the first century of that, and later Persian sieges failed to take it. From the heart of an empire to the edge of one, and it did not grow back.'],
'巴格达|萨法维·波斯': ['萨法维两次拿下巴格达:1508 年伊斯玛仪一世,1623 年阿拔斯一世。什叶派与逊尼派的分野在这几次易手里被一再加深——两河下游什叶派聚居、巴格达以北逊尼派居多,这条线一直影响到今天。',
 'The Safavids took Baghdad twice, under Ismail I in 1508 and Abbas I in 1623. Each change of hands deepened the split between Shia and Sunni — the lower Two Rivers largely Shia, the country north of Baghdad largely Sunni, a line that still matters.'],
'巴格达|现代中东': ['1920 年英国取得两河流域的委任统治权,1921 年把奥斯曼的三个省合成伊拉克、首都设在巴格达。此后一百年,这座城经历了君主制、共和国、两伊战争,以及 1991 与 2003 两场战争。2003 年伊拉克国家博物馆遭大规模劫掠,上万件文物流失,追讨至今还在进行。',
 'Britain took the mandate over Mesopotamia in 1920 and in 1921 joined three Ottoman provinces into Iraq, with its capital at Baghdad. In the century since, the city has been through a monarchy, a republic, the war with Iran and the wars of 1991 and 2003. The National Museum was looted on a large scale in 2003, some fifteen thousand objects went missing, and the work of recovering them is still going on.'],
'巴格达|加喜特巴比伦': ['加喜特诸王在今天巴格达西边约三十公里处另建了一座都城,叫杜尔-库瑞加尔祖——意思是「库瑞加尔祖的堡垒」,用国王自己的名字命名。那座塔庙的夯土芯至今还立着,残高约五十米,是巴格达周边最显眼的一处古代建筑。一个从山里来的外来王朝,建新城用的却是最本地的形制:塔庙、神庙、王宫,一样不少。',
 'The Kassite kings built a second capital about thirty kilometres west of today\'s Baghdad and named it Dur-Kurigalzu — "the fortress of Kurigalzu", after the king himself. The mudbrick core of its ziggurat still stands some fifty metres high, the most conspicuous ancient structure anywhere near Baghdad. A dynasty out of the hills built its new city to the most local of plans: ziggurat, temples, palace, nothing left out.'],
'巴比伦|古巴比伦': ['汉谟拉比把两河流域重新拼成一个国家,把 282 条判例刻在一根黑色石柱上立于神庙。石柱后来被埃兰人当战利品掳走,1901 年在今伊朗的苏萨出土——所以它今天不在巴比伦,在卢浮宫。',
 'Hammurabi pulled Mesopotamia back into one state and had 282 rulings carved on a black stone stele set up in a temple. Elamite raiders later carried it off as loot; it was dug up at Susa in Iran in 1901, which is why it stands today not in Babylon but in the Louvre.'],
'亚历山大|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['亚历山大城建于前 331 年,那时波斯对埃及的统治刚刚结束。城址原来只有一个叫拉科提斯的渔村,对面的法罗斯岛在《奥德赛》里就被提到过。选在这里建城看中的是地形:南边马雷奥提斯湖的湖港通着尼罗河,北边正对地中海;后来又修了一条七斯塔迪昂长的堤道连上法罗斯岛,把北面的水域隔成两个天然良港。',
 'Alexandria was founded in 331 BC, just as Persian rule over Egypt ended. The site held nothing but a fishing village called Rhakotis, with the island of Pharos offshore — an island the Odyssey already knew. What recommended the spot was its shape: the lake harbour of Mareotis behind it, joined to the Nile, and the open Mediterranean in front; a causeway seven stades long was later run out to the island of Pharos, splitting the water to the north into two natural harbours.'],
'亚历山大|罗马共和国': ['前 48 年凯撒卷入托勒密王室的内争,在亚历山大打了一场巷战。著名的图书馆藏书在这场混战中受了损失,究竟损失多大,古代作者说法不一,今天也没有定论。前 30 年罗马正式接管埃及。',
 'Caesar was drawn into a Ptolemaic family quarrel in 48 BC and fought a street war in Alexandria. The famous library lost books in the fighting; how many, ancient writers disagreed, and there is still no settled answer. Rome took Egypt formally in 30 BC.'],
'亚历山大|罗马帝国': ['罗马帝国时期的亚历山大是帝国的第二大城,人口可能有几十万,粮船从这里一船船开往罗马。法罗斯灯塔仍在使用——古代世界七大奇迹里,它是最实用的一个:别的都是给神看的,它是给船看的。',
 'Under the empire Alexandria was Rome\'s second city, with a population probably in the hundreds of thousands, and the grain fleets sailed from here. The Pharos lighthouse was still working — of the seven wonders it was the useful one: the others were built for gods, this one for ships.'],
'亚历山大|罗马治下近东': ['天文学家托勒密在这里写下《天文学大成》。此后一千多年,这本书一直是天文学的底本——先是在伊斯兰世界;欧洲要等到十二世纪有人把它从阿拉伯文译成拉丁文,才用得上。同一座城里,基督教、犹太教与希腊多神信仰的社群长期共处,也不时冲突;391 年塞拉皮雍神庙在一次冲突中被毁。',
 'The astronomer Ptolemy wrote the Almagest here. For more than a thousand years afterwards it was the standard text of astronomy — first in the Islamic world; Europe could not use it until someone turned it from Arabic into Latin in the twelfth century. In the same city Christian, Jewish and Greek communities lived side by side and periodically clashed; the Serapeum was destroyed in one such clash in 391.'],
'亚历山大|拜占庭': ['拜占庭时期亚历山大是教会重镇,它的主教与君士坦丁堡屡屡争夺话语权。城市仍是埃及粮食的出口港,但泥沙淤积与地震让港口一年年变差。641 年阿拉伯军队来攻,围了十四个月;双方谈定条件后,守军在 642 年秋撤出。645 年拜占庭的舰队一度把城夺回,次年又丢掉——那才是真的结束。',
 'Under Byzantium Alexandria was a great church city whose patriarchs contended repeatedly with Constantinople. It still shipped Egypt\'s grain, though silt and earthquakes were making the harbours worse year by year. The Arab army came in 641 and the siege ran fourteen months; terms were agreed and the garrison withdrew in the autumn of 642. A Byzantine fleet retook the city in 645 and lost it again the year after — that was the real end.'],
'亚历山大|法蒂玛王朝': ['法蒂玛建了开罗之后,亚历山大退成一座港口城市。它仍是地中海贸易的窗口——意大利各城邦的商船在这里装货,把东方的香料转运往欧洲;但政治与财富的中心,已经在两百公里外的开罗了。',
 'Once the Fatimids built Cairo, Alexandria settled into being a port. It remained the window on Mediterranean trade — ships from the Italian cities loaded here and carried eastern spices on to Europe — but power and money now sat two hundred kilometres away at Cairo.'],
'亚历山大|阿尤布王朝': ['阿尤布时期亚历山大是埃及面向地中海的门户,萨拉丁在这里加固了城防。1174 年一支西西里舰队来袭,被守军击退——十字军几次想从海上打埃及,都是先冲着这座城来的。',
 'Under the Ayyubids Alexandria was Egypt\'s door onto the Mediterranean and Saladin strengthened its defences. A Sicilian fleet attacked in 1174 and was driven off — whenever the crusaders thought of striking Egypt by sea, this was the city they came for first.'],
'亚历山大|马穆鲁克': ['1365 年塞浦路斯的十字军突袭亚历山大,劫掠数日后撤走,这座城元气大伤。法罗斯灯塔此前已在地震中倒塌,1477 年马穆鲁克苏丹凯特贝用它的石料在原址上修了一座堡垒——那座堡垒今天还在海边站着。',
 'Crusaders from Cyprus raided Alexandria in 1365, plundered it for days and left; the city never quite recovered. The Pharos had already come down in earthquakes, and in 1477 the Mamluk sultan Qaitbay used its stone to raise a fort on the same rock — the fort is still standing at the water\'s edge.'],
'亚历山大|奥斯曼帝国': ['奥斯曼治下的亚历山大长期萧条,十八世纪末城里只剩一万上下。让它重新活过来的是十九世纪的棉花:埃及大规模种棉出口,亚历山大成了棉花的装船口,人口在几十年里从一万上下涨到几十万。',
 'Alexandria languished under the Ottomans; by the end of the eighteenth century only about ten thousand people lived there. Cotton brought it back in the nineteenth: Egypt planted cotton for export on a large scale, Alexandria became the port it shipped from, and the population went from around ten thousand to several hundred thousand within decades.'],
'亚历山大|现代中东': ['1952 年之后大批外国侨民离开,亚历山大从一座讲许多种语言的港口城市,变回一座埃及城市。2002 年新的亚历山大图书馆在古馆旧址附近落成——它复原不了那座图书馆,但它记得那座图书馆。',
 'After 1952 most of the foreign communities left and Alexandria went from a port that spoke many languages back to being an Egyptian city. In 2002 a new Library of Alexandria opened near the site of the old one — it cannot restore that library, but it remembers it.'],
'亚历山大|希腊化王朝': ['托勒密王朝把亚历山大城建成希腊世界的学问中心:缪斯宫里养着领薪水的学者,欧几里得相传在这里教书、《几何原本》出自这个时代,埃拉托色尼算出了地球的周长。港口外的法罗斯灯塔是古代七大奇迹之一。',
 'The Ptolemies made Alexandria the learned centre of the Greek world: the Museum kept scholars on salary, Euclid is said to have taught here and the Elements comes from this age, and Eratosthenes worked out the circumference of the earth. The Pharos lighthouse at the harbour mouth was one of the seven wonders of the ancient world.'],
'基辅|蒙古帝国': ['1240 年拔都的军队攻破基辅,罗斯诸公国先后臣服,此后两百多年向金帐汗国纳贡;基辅本城则在 1362 年后转归立陶宛。诺夫哥罗德没有被攻打,后来也不得不纳贡,是少数免于屠城的大城。',
 'In 1240 Batu\'s army stormed Kyiv, and one Rus principality after another submitted; for more than two centuries they paid tribute to the Golden Horde, though Kyiv itself passed to Lithuania after 1362. Novgorod was never attacked, though it too ended up paying tribute — one of the few great cities spared a sack.'],
'库斯科|印加': ['库斯科的名字传统上解作「世界的肚脐」(词源另有他说),四方大道从城中广场通向帝国四区。太阳神殿的墙上曾包着金板;萨克萨瓦曼的巨石墙不用灰浆,石缝紧到常被形容为连一张纸都插不进去。',
 'Cusco\'s name is traditionally read as "the navel of the world" (other etymologies have been proposed); roads to the empire\'s four quarters set out from its central plaza. The Sun Temple\'s walls were once sheathed in gold, and the dry-fitted megaliths of Sacsayhuaman still leave no room for a sheet of paper.'],
'吴哥|高棉·吴哥': ['吴哥窟由苏利耶跋摩二世于 1113 年前后动工,原是献给毗湿奴的印度教神庙,后来改作佛寺沿用至今。城的命脉是水:巨型水库与沟渠把季风雨存下来调节旱雨两季,养起了一片人口以十万计的城市群。',
 'Angkor Wat was begun under Suryavarman II around 1113 as a Hindu temple to Vishnu; it was later turned to Buddhist use and has been in use ever since. Water was the city\'s lifeline: huge reservoirs and channels held the monsoon rains for the dry season, supporting an urban complex of hundreds of thousands.'],
'蒲甘|蒲甘': ['1044 年阿奴律陀立国后,历代君王在伊洛瓦底江边的平原上不断建塔。当年建了上万座,今天还立着两千多座,连成一片望不到头的砖塔林。',
 'After Anawrahta founded the kingdom in 1044, king after king raised pagodas on the plain by the Irrawaddy. Of the more than ten thousand built, over two thousand still stand — a brick forest that runs to the horizon.'],
'蒲甘|阿瓦·勃固': ['1287 年蒙古军南下之后,蒲甘不再是都城,王权移到上游的阿瓦(今因瓦)。这座城并没有被毁,只是被绕开了:塔还在,人还在,朝廷不在了。此后两百多年,上缅甸的国王在阿瓦，下缅甸的在勃固,两边为伊洛瓦底江下游打了四十年——而蒲甘留在中间,慢慢从一座都城变成一片塔林。',
 'After the Mongol advance of 1287 Pagan was no longer a capital; power moved upriver to Ava, today\'s Inwa. The city was not destroyed so much as bypassed: the pagodas remained, the people remained, the court did not. For the next two centuries the kings of upper Burma sat at Ava and those of the lower country at Pegu, fighting forty years over the lower Irrawaddy — while Pagan, left in between, slowly turned from a capital into a field of temples.'],
'河内|西汉': ['前 111 年汉武帝灭南越,在红河三角洲设交趾郡。交趾是这次所设三郡里最北的一个,九真、日南都在它南边;而它是三郡中最大的一片稻作平原,史籍记载这里的稻一年可以收两季。从海上来的商船也在这一带靠岸,再往北去番禺(今广州)。',
 'Emperor Wu destroyed Nanyue in 111 BC and set up Jiaozhi commandery on the Red River delta. Jiaozhi was the northernmost of the three commanderies set up then, with Jiuzhen and Rinan to its south, and the largest rice plain among them — the histories record two harvests a year here. Ships coming in from the sea put in along this coast before going on north to Panyu, today\'s Guangzhou.'],
'河内|东汉': ['40 年征侧、征贰姐妹起兵反抗汉朝的地方官,一度控制了六十多座城;43 年马援率军平定。这对姐妹在越南被尊为民族英雄,河内至今有纪念她们的庙——同一件事,中越两边的史书写出来是两种味道。',
 'In AD 40 the sisters Trung Trac and Trung Nhi rose against the Han officials and for a time held sixty-odd towns; Ma Yuan put the rising down in 43. In Vietnam the sisters are national heroes and Hanoi still has temples to them — the same events, and the Chinese and Vietnamese histories read nothing alike.'],
'河内|隋': ['隋在这里先设交州,大业年间改称交趾郡。从长安走到这里要几个月,朝廷的控制常常松到只剩收税与派官;真正把这一带和中原连在一起的,不是官府,是水稻、汉字,和一批批从北边南下的移民。',
 'The Sui governed here first as Jiaozhou prefecture and then, after the reorganisation of the Daye years, as Jiaozhi commandery. It took months to travel from the capital, and the court\'s grip often came down to collecting taxes and appointing officials; what actually tied this delta to the north was not the administration but rice, Chinese writing, and wave after wave of migrants coming south.'],
'河内|唐': ['唐设安南都护府,治所就在今天的河内。866 年节度使高骈修筑大罗城,那是河内城址的直接前身;「安南」这个名字从唐代留了下来,一直用到近代。',
 'The Tang ran the Protectorate of Annam from what is now Hanoi. In 866 the governor Gao Pian built the citadel of Dai La, the direct ancestor of the city on this site; the name Annam dates from the Tang and stayed in use into modern times.'],
'河内|明': ['1407 年明军灭胡朝,把这里设为交趾承宣布政使司,直辖了二十年。1427 年黎利起兵取胜,明军撤走。这二十年在越南的史书里分量极重,是它讲「我们是谁」时绕不开的一段。',
 'Ming armies destroyed the Ho dynasty in 1407 and ruled the delta directly as a province for twenty years. In 1427 Le Loi\'s rising prevailed and the Ming withdrew. Those twenty years carry great weight in Vietnamese history — no account of who the Vietnamese are gets past them.'],
'河内|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1902 年法国把法属印度支那的首府设在河内。法国人修了歌剧院、大教堂和跨红河的长桥,而老城那片按行业分的街巷保留了下来——今天在河内走一圈,这两层是叠在一起的。',
 'In 1902 the French made Hanoi the capital of French Indochina. They built an opera house, a cathedral and a long bridge over the Red River, while the old quarter of streets named for the trades that worked them stayed where it was — walk through Hanoi today and the two layers sit on top of each other.'],
'河内|现代东南亚': ['1945 年 9 月胡志明在巴亭广场宣布越南独立,随后是与法国的九年战争。1954 年奠边府一役后法国撤出,越南以北纬十七度线分成南北两半,河内是北方的首都。1972 年底河内遭到大规模空袭;1976 年南北统一,它成为全国的首都。',
 'In September 1945 Ho Chi Minh declared Vietnam independent in Ba Dinh square, and nine years of war with France followed. After Dien Bien Phu in 1954 the French withdrew and the country was split at the seventeenth parallel, with Hanoi the capital of the north. The city was heavily bombed at the end of 1972; in 1976, with the country reunified, it became the capital of all of it.'],
'安卡拉|赫梯': ['安卡拉在安纳托利亚高原中部,赫梯的都城哈图沙就在它东边一百多公里。赫梯人很早就会炼铁,又在卡叠什与埃及打了一仗,随后签下一份和约——那份条约的泥板抄本今天还在,是现存最早的国际和平条约。',
 'Ankara sits in the middle of the Anatolian plateau, with the Hittite capital Hattusa a hundred-odd kilometres to its east. The Hittites worked iron early, fought Egypt at Kadesh and then made a treaty with it — a clay copy of that treaty survives, the oldest international peace treaty anyone still has.'],
'安卡拉|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['波斯把安纳托利亚划成几个总督辖区,那条从苏萨通到西边萨第斯的御道,经过安卡拉西南不远的戈尔迪翁(它在安纳托利亚的确切走向,学界至今有争论)。御道沿途设驿站换马,一封公文能在两千多公里上跑得很快——希罗多德形容这些信使的那句话,后来被刻在了纽约一座邮局的门楣上。',
 'Persia divided Anatolia into satrapies, and the royal road running from Susa to Sardis in the west passed through Gordion, not far southwest of here — its exact line across Anatolia is still argued over. Relay stations along it changed horses, so a dispatch could cover two thousand kilometres remarkably fast — the line Herodotus wrote about those couriers ended up carved over the door of a post office in New York.'],
'安卡拉|罗马共和国': ['前三世纪,一支从巴尔干迁来的凯尔特人在这片高原定居,希腊人管他们叫「加拉太人」。安卡拉的古名安基拉就是他们的中心之一;《圣经》里保罗写给加拉太人的那封信,有一种说法认为收信的就是这批人的后代;也有不少学者认为收信人在行省南边,并不是凯尔特人的后代。',
 'In the third century BC a body of Celts migrated from the Balkans and settled on this plateau; the Greeks called them Galatians. Ancyra, the old name of Ankara, was one of their centres — and on one reading Paul\'s letter to the Galatians was addressed to their descendants — though many scholars place its recipients in the south of the province instead, among people who were not Celts at all.'],
'安卡拉|罗马帝国': ['前 25 年罗马把加拉太设为行省,安基拉是首府。城中奥古斯都神庙的墙上刻着《奥古斯都功业录》——那位皇帝自述一生功绩的铭文,别处的抄本都残了,现存最完整的一份就在这座城里。',
 'Rome made Galatia a province in 25 BC with Ancyra as its capital. On the walls of the temple of Augustus there the emperor\'s own account of his deeds was carved — copies elsewhere survive only in fragments, and the fullest one anyone has is in this city.'],
'安卡拉|罗马治下近东': ['安基拉是安纳托利亚中部的交通枢纽,几条大道在这里交汇。基督教沿着这些路传进内陆;314 年这里开过一次教会会议,会上定下的教规文本流传下来,是研究早期教会的重要材料。',
 'Ancyra was the road junction of central Anatolia, where several highways met. Christianity travelled inland along those roads, and a church council met here in 314 whose canons survive as an important source for the early church.'],
'安卡拉|拜占庭': ['拜占庭时期安卡拉是军区制下的一座要塞城,城堡修在山上。七世纪起阿拉伯军队多次北上劫掠安纳托利亚,这座城几度易手——它从一座商路上的城,变成了一座要守的城。',
 'Under Byzantium Ankara was a fortress town within the theme system, its citadel set on the hill. From the seventh century Arab armies raided up into Anatolia repeatedly and the town changed hands more than once — it went from a city on a trade road to a city to be held.'],
'安卡拉|塞尔柱突厥': ['1071 年曼齐克特之战后突厥人进入安纳托利亚,安卡拉在这一时期几度易手。此后几百年,这片高原上的语言、宗教与人口结构逐渐改变——今天的土耳其,轮廓是从这时开始成形的。',
 'After the battle of Manzikert in 1071 Turkic peoples moved into Anatolia and Ankara changed hands several times. Over the following centuries the language, religion and population of the plateau shifted — the outline of today\'s Turkey begins here.'],
'安卡拉|现代中东': ['1919 年底凯末尔移驻安卡拉,次年在这里开出大国民议会。1923 年 10 月先定安卡拉为首都,半个月后才宣布共和国成立——挑一座内陆城市当首都,本身就是一句宣言:新国家不打算再做那个横跨欧亚的帝国。',
 'Kemal moved to Ankara at the end of 1919 and opened the Grand National Assembly here the following year. In October 1923 Ankara was named the capital first, and the republic was proclaimed a fortnight later — choosing an inland town was itself a statement: the new state did not intend to go on being an empire astride two continents.'],
'布哈拉|粟特': ['布哈拉是粟特诸城之一,和撒马尔罕同在泽拉夫尚河的绿洲带上。这片绿洲原本是泽拉夫尚河下游的沼泽,靠人工开渠排水才变成农田——布哈拉是先有渠、后有城的。当地的「布哈拉胡大」王族长期铸自己的钱币,连阿拉伯人来了很久以后都还在铸。',
 'Bukhara was one of the Sogdian cities, on the same Zarafshan oasis belt as Samarkand. The oasis began as marshland at the tail of the Zarafshan and became farmland only once channels were cut to drain it — Bukhara had its canals before it had its city. The local Bukhar Khudah rulers struck their own coinage, and went on striking it long after the Arabs arrived.'],
'布哈拉|阿拉伯哈里发': ['阿拉伯军队在八世纪初取得布哈拉,这一带逐步改信伊斯兰教。此后两百年,中亚从波斯与突厥文化交界的地方,变成了伊斯兰世界学问最密集的地区之一——编纂逊尼派最重要圣训集的布哈里,就出生在这座城。',
 'Arab armies took Bukhara early in the eighth century and the oasis gradually turned to Islam. Over the next two centuries Central Asia went from a meeting ground of Persian and Turkic culture to one of the densest concentrations of learning in the Islamic world — al-Bukhari, who compiled the most important Sunni collection of hadith, was born in this city.'],
'布哈拉|花剌子模': ['花剌子模崛起后取得布哈拉,这一带成为它的核心区之一。这个王朝从塞尔柱的一个总督府起家,靠在塞尔柱、西辽、古尔王朝之间来回周旋,打了一百多年才做到中亚最强,版图一度从里海延伸到印度河。它遇到的最后一个对手是成吉思汗。',
 'Khwarazm took Bukhara as it rose, and the oasis became one of its core districts. The dynasty began as a Seljuk governorship and spent well over a century manoeuvring between the Seljuks, Qara Khitai and the Ghurids before it became the strongest power in Central Asia, reaching at its height from the Caspian to the Indus. The last adversary it met was Genghis Khan.'],
'布哈拉|蒙古帝国': ['1220 年成吉思汗攻下布哈拉。四十年后成书的波斯史书《世界征服者史》记载,他在城中的聚礼清真寺里对居民讲话,自称是上天派来惩罚他们的;城被焚毁,居民被驱去当攻城的人肉盾牌。中亚的城市与灌溉体系,此后用了很久才恢复。',
 'Genghis Khan took Bukhara in 1220. Accounts written not long after say he addressed the townspeople in the Friday mosque and called himself the punishment sent by God; the city was burned and its people driven ahead of the army as living shields at the next siege. The cities and irrigation of Central Asia took a long time to recover.'],
'布哈拉|帖木儿帝国': ['这一朝的重心在撒马尔罕,布哈拉退居第二。帖木儿的孙子兀鲁伯 1417 年在这里建了一座经学院,门楣上刻着「求知是每个穆斯林男女的天职」。布哈拉真正一座座修满经学院要再晚一百年,但「布哈拉」这个名字在伊斯兰世界代表学问,这件事从没断过——一座城的名声,可以比它的实际地位活得更久。',
 'The weight of this dynasty lay at Samarkand and Bukhara came second. Timur\'s grandson Ulugh Beg built a college here in 1417, its portal carved with the line that seeking knowledge is the duty of every Muslim man and woman. Bukhara would not fill up with colleges for another hundred years, yet across the Islamic world its name never stopped standing for learning — a city\'s reputation can outlive its actual position.'],
'布哈拉|俄国治下中亚': ['俄国的铁路 1888 年修到布哈拉,车站却设在城外十二公里的卡甘;按当时的安排,铁路不进老城,于是站旁自己长出一座俄国人的新城。埃米尔照旧住在老城里,但这片绿洲种什么、卖给谁,越来越由几千公里外的纺织厂决定——中亚在这一百年里最深的改变不是换了谁当官,是种什么由别人说了算。',
 'The Russian railway reached Bukhara in 1888, but its station was put at Kagan, twelve kilometres outside; the line was kept out of the old city, and a Russian town grew up beside the tracks instead. The emir went on living in the old city, but what the oasis planted and who bought it were increasingly settled by textile mills thousands of kilometres away — the deepest change in Central Asia that century was not who governed but who decided what the land grew.'],
'布哈拉|现代中亚': ['1920 年布哈拉的埃米尔被推翻,这里先归苏联,后来成为独立的乌兹别克斯坦的一座城。今天看到的老城主体是十六世纪以后重建的——1220 年那场焚城之后,布哈拉是一层层重新长起来的;它的格局与建筑保存得相当完整,1993 年列入世界文化遗产名录。城中的卡扬宣礼塔据说因为成吉思汗下令留下,躲过了 1220 年那场焚城。',
 'The emir of Bukhara was overthrown in 1920; the city became Soviet, and later a city of independent Uzbekistan. Most of the old town standing today was rebuilt from the sixteenth century on — after the burning of 1220 Bukhara grew back layer by layer; the quarter survives largely intact and was made a World Heritage Site in 1993. The Kalyan minaret is said to have been spared on Genghis Khan\'s own order, and so came through the burning of 1220.'],
'撒马尔罕|萨曼王朝': ['萨曼早期就以撒马尔罕为都,892 年伊斯玛仪一世才把都城迁到布哈拉。撒马尔罕很早就以造纸出名,纸从这里继续西传,最后到了地中海;至于造纸术是怎么到撒马尔罕的,流传最广的那个说法(怛罗斯之战的战俘带来的)其实史料很薄。',
 'The early Samanids ruled from Samarkand; Ismail I moved the capital to Bukhara in 892. Samarkand was known for papermaking early on, and paper travelled west from here and eventually reached the Mediterranean. As for how papermaking got to Samarkand, the story everyone repeats — prisoners taken at the battle of Talas — rests on very thin evidence.'],
'撒马尔罕|花剌子模': ['花剌子模把撒马尔罕当作都城之一。这片绿洲靠泽拉夫尚河的水,城外那套灌溉渠网养活了城里的人;中亚大城的命脉不在城墙而在水渠:渠一断,城既守不住也活不下去。',
 'Khwarazm used Samarkand as one of its capitals. The oasis lived on the Zarafshan, and the canal network outside the walls fed the people inside them; the lifeline of a great Central Asian city was never its walls but its water: cut the channels and it can neither hold out nor live.'],
'撒马尔罕|蒙古帝国': ['1220 年成吉思汗围撒马尔罕。外城只守了几天,大部分守军投降、城中人开门迎降;内城又撑了约一个月才被攻破。工匠被挑出来送往东方,其余人口大批被杀或驱散。旧城此后逐渐被放弃,城市重心移到今天的位置——遗址上那片土丘,就是被留在原地的那座撒马尔罕。',
 'Genghis Khan besieged Samarkand in 1220. The outer city held only days, most of the garrison surrendering and the townspeople opening the gates; the inner citadel held out about a month longer. Craftsmen were picked out and sent east and the rest of the population was killed or scattered. The old city was gradually given up and the centre of settlement shifted to where Samarkand stands now — the mounds on the site are the city that stayed behind.'],
'撒马尔罕|布哈拉·希瓦·浩罕三汗国': ['帖木儿之后,撒马尔罕的分量被布哈拉压了过去。十八世纪这座城一度几乎空了,街上长满荒草;十八世纪中叶起,布哈拉的埃米尔陆续迁人进来,它才慢慢住满。一座城可以被放弃,也可以被重新住回来。',
 'After Timur, Samarkand was eclipsed by Bukhara. In the eighteenth century it stood nearly empty for a time, with grass growing in the streets, and filled up again only as the emirs of Bukhara resettled people there from the middle of the eighteenth century onward. A city can be abandoned and then lived in again.'],
'撒马尔罕|俄国治下中亚': ['1868 年俄军占领撒马尔罕。俄国人没有拆老城,而是在旁边另建一座欧洲式的新城:街道笔直、有林荫道与行政楼。中亚许多城市今天「老城加新城」并排的样子,就是从这一时期开始的。',
 'Russian troops occupied Samarkand in 1868. Rather than pull the old town down, the Russians built a European town beside it — straight streets, avenues of trees, administrative buildings. The pattern of an old city and a new one side by side, which many Central Asian cities still show, dates from these years.'],
'撒马尔罕|现代中亚': ['苏联初期撒马尔罕做过乌兹别克的首都,后来让给了塔什干。雷吉斯坦广场那三座经学院经过长期修复,2001 年整座城以「文化交汇之地」的名义列入世界文化遗产名录。兀鲁伯天文台的遗址也在城郊——那座建筑早被毁掉,埋在地下的巨大六分仪弧槽却一直留着,二十世纪初才被挖出来。',
 'Samarkand was briefly the capital of Soviet Uzbekistan before the seat moved to Tashkent. The three colleges on the Registan have been restored over many years, and in 2001 the whole city was inscribed as a World Heritage Site under the name Crossroads of Cultures. The remains of Ulugh Beg\'s observatory lie on the edge of town — the building itself was destroyed long ago, but the great curved track of its sextant stayed buried and was dug out at the start of the twentieth century.'],
'河内|大越': ['938 年吴权在白藤江大败南汉水军,越南结束了一千年的北属时期。1010 年李太祖迁都于此,取名升龙——传说他见江上有龙腾起。此后蒙古大军三次南下,三次都攻进了这座城,而大越每次都靠主动弃城、再回头反击把他们赶走——1288 年陈兴道又在白藤江把木桩插进江底,等退潮时敌船被扎穿。同一条江,同一招,隔了三百五十年。',
 'In 938 Ngo Quyen destroyed a Southern Han fleet on the Bach Dang river, ending a thousand years of rule from the north. In 1010 Ly Thai To moved his capital here and named it Thang Long, "the ascending dragon," after a dragon he was said to have seen rise from the river. Three times the Mongols came south and three times they took the city, yet Dai Viet drove them out each time by abandoning the capital and striking back — in 1288 Tran Hung Dao again had stakes driven into the bed of the Bach Dang, and the ebbing tide impaled the enemy fleet. Same river, same trick, three hundred and fifty years apart.'],
'河内|三国': ['士燮 187 年出任交趾太守,一直做到 226 年去世,中间在 210 年归附了孙权——这四十年跨过东汉与孙吴两个朝廷。中原正在打仗,这里反而是最太平的地方,大批士人渡海南下避难,在他门下讲学注经。越南后来的史书把他单列一代,称他「士王」,又叫他「南交学祖」。他一死,孙权就把交州拆成两半,再没让哪一家人管这么久。',
 'Shi Xie became governor of Jiaozhi in 187 and held the post until his death in 226, transferring his allegiance to Sun Quan along the way in 210 — forty years spanning two dynasties, the Han and then Wu. The north was at war and this was the quietest place around, so scholars came south by sea to sit out the troubles, lecturing and annotating the classics under his patronage. Later Vietnamese histories give him a reign of his own and call him Si Vuong, King Shi, and the founding teacher of learning in the south. The moment he died Sun Quan split Jiaozhi in two, and no family was ever left in charge that long again.'],
'河内|西晋': ['280 年吴亡,交州归晋。原来吴的交州刺史陶璜投降后,晋朝让他留在原任上,直到十年后去世;《晋书》说他「在南三十年」——这三十年跨了吴、晋两个朝廷,而始终是同一个人。他死时交州人「举州号哭」。朝廷换了,管这里的人没换:从洛阳走到交州要几个月,谁真的在这里,比谁在纸上受命更要紧。',
 'Wu fell in 280 and Jiaozhi passed to the Jin. Tao Huang, who had been Wu\'s inspector there, surrendered and was simply left in the same post until his death about ten years later. The Book of Jin says he was "thirty years in the south" — thirty years spanning two dynasties, Wu and then Jin, with the same man in place throughout. The whole province wept when he died. The dynasty changed and the man on the ground did not: it took months to travel from Luoyang to Jiaozhi, and who was actually here mattered more than whose name was on the appointment.'],
'河内|东晋·十六国': ['这几百年交州实际上由在本地生了根的大族在管:杜瑗、杜慧度父子相继做交州刺史,前后几十年。南边的林邑(后来的占婆)一再北上,杜慧度在 413 年和 420 年两次把它的军队打回去。朝廷远在建康,守不守得住这里,靠的是这些人家而不是那道任命。',
 'For these centuries Jiaozhi was in practice run by families that had put down roots there: Du Yuan and his son Du Huidu held the inspectorate in succession for decades. Lam Ap — later Champa — pushed north again and again from below, and Du Huidu turned its armies back twice, in 413 and 420. The court was far away at Jiankang, and whether this country held depended on such families rather than on the appointment scroll.'],
'河内|南北朝': ['541 年李贲起兵反梁,544 年称帝,国号万春,都城就在今天河内一带。这是越南史书里第一次有人在这里自立为帝,后世称他这一支为「前李朝」。李贲死后赵光复接着打,断断续续维持了六十年,602 年隋军南下灭掉。越南把前 111 年到 938 年整段叫「北属时期」,而这六十年,是这一千年里被反复讲起的那次中断。',
 'In 541 Ly Bi rose against the Liang, and in 544 he took the imperial title and named his state Van Xuan, with its capital near today\'s Hanoi. It was the first time anyone here had declared himself emperor, and Vietnamese histories call his line the Early Ly. After Ly Bi\'s death Trieu Quang Phuc fought on; the state held out on and off for some sixty years until Sui armies came south and ended it in 602. Vietnam calls the whole stretch from 111 BC to 938 the period of northern rule — and these sixty years are the break within that millennium that gets told and retold.'],
'巨港|三佛齐': ['巨港扼着马六甲海峡的咽喉,三佛齐靠向过往商船收税立国六百年。671 年唐僧义净取经途中在这里停留半年学梵文,回程又住了好几年译经,说这里佛学之盛可比印度。',
 'Palembang sat at the throat of the Malacca Strait, and Srivijaya lived for six centuries on tolls from the ships that passed. In 671 the Chinese monk Yijing broke his journey here for half a year to study Sanskrit, and on the way home stayed several years more translating texts; he reported Buddhist learning here to rival India\'s.'],
'巨港|满者伯夷': ['1377 年满者伯夷派兵攻破巨港,三佛齐的最后残余就此结束——收了六百年过路费的这座河口,自己成了被收的一方。但满者伯夷对外岛用的是纳贡称臣那一套,不是直接治理,巨港因此成了各路人马混杂的港口:1407 年郑和的船队经过这里,抓走了盘踞多年的海盗头子陈祖义。',
 'In 1377 Majapahit stormed Palembang and finished off the last remnant of Srivijaya — the river mouth that had taken tolls for six centuries now paid them itself. But Majapahit ruled its outer islands by tribute rather than administration, and Palembang became a port of mixed and shifting powers: when Zheng He\'s fleet came through in 1407 it carried off Chen Zuyi, a pirate chief who had held the place for years.'],
'马六甲|马六甲及诸苏丹国': ['1400 年前后拜里米苏拉在此建港,靠季风换船的中转生意迅速兴起,苏丹改宗伊斯兰教后,这里成了伊斯兰教向东南亚岛屿传播的枢纽。1511 年葡萄牙人攻占此城,是欧洲人在东南亚拿下的第一座大港。',
 'Parameswara founded the port around 1400; it grew fast on transshipment as the monsoon winds turned, and after its sultans took up Islam it became the hinge from which Islam spread through the islands of Southeast Asia. The Portuguese stormed it in 1511 — the first great Southeast Asian port to fall to Europeans.'],
'雅加达|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1619 年荷兰东印度公司攻毁本地的查雅加尔达(Jayakarta,雅加达之名的由来),在原址建起巴达维亚,作为它在亚洲的总部。这家公司自己有军队、能签条约、能宣战——一间公司在这片群岛上说了近二百年的算。',
 'In 1619 the Dutch East India Company destroyed the local town of Jayakarta and built Batavia on the site as its Asian headquarters. The company kept its own armies and could sign treaties and declare war — a corporation called the shots across these islands for nearly two centuries.'],
'大津巴布韦|大津巴布韦': ['石城的外墙不用一点灰浆,全靠石块相互咬合,最高处约十一米。它靠内陆黄金与牛群立国,黄金经索法拉出海接进印度洋贸易;殖民时代的欧洲人不肯相信这是非洲人自己建的,考古学早在 1905 年就给出了相反的结论。',
 'The great walls were laid without a scrap of mortar, block locked against block, rising to some eleven metres at their highest. The state lived on inland gold and cattle, its gold reaching the Indian Ocean through the port of Sofala. Colonial-era Europeans refused to believe Africans had built it; archaeology had answered the question by 1905.'],
'阿克苏姆|阿克苏姆': ['阿克苏姆铸自己的金币,是当时少数几个这么做的国家之一。城里立着整块巨石凿成的方尖碑,立住的最高一根约二十四米;还有一根长三十三米,一般认为竖立时就断了。四世纪埃扎纳王皈依基督教,埃塞俄比亚的基督教传统从此不断。',
 'Aksum struck its own gold coinage, one of only a handful of states then doing so. Giant stelae cut from single blocks of stone stood in the city; the tallest one still standing is about twenty-four metres, and a thirty-three-metre one is thought to have broken as it was being raised. In the fourth century King Ezana adopted Christianity, and Ethiopia\'s Christian tradition has run unbroken since.'],
'布哈拉|萨曼王朝': ['十世纪的布哈拉是新波斯语复兴的中心,宫廷养着诗人与学者。少年伊本·西那在这里读遍了萨曼王室的藏书,后来写出《医典》——它在欧洲的医学院当了几百年教材。',
 'Tenth-century Bukhara was the heart of the New Persian revival, with poets and scholars kept at court. As a boy Ibn Sina read his way through the Samanid royal library here, and went on to write the Canon of Medicine — a textbook in European medical schools for centuries.'],
'麦加|阿拉伯哈里发': ['麦加是穆罕默德的出生地,城中的克尔白是穆斯林礼拜时面朝的方向。630 年他率众返回麦加,此后每年的朝觐把整个伊斯兰世界的人往这一个点上聚,商路、消息与学问也跟着一起走。',
 'Mecca was Muhammad\'s birthplace, and the Kaaba at its centre is the direction Muslims face in prayer. He returned to the city with his followers in 630; from then on the yearly pilgrimage drew people from across the Islamic world to this one point, and trade, news and learning travelled with them.'],
'平壤|朝鲜半岛诸王朝': ['427 年高句丽从鸭绿江边迁都平壤,此后两百多年这里是半岛北部的中心。668 年唐与新罗联手灭高句丽,城由此易主;高丽时代它被定为「西京」,地位仅次于开京。',
 'In 427 Goguryeo moved its capital from the Yalu to Pyongyang, and for over two centuries it was the centre of the northern peninsula. Tang and Silla together destroyed Goguryeo in 668 and the city changed hands; under Goryeo it was named the Western Capital, second only to Kaesong.'],
'特奥蒂瓦坎|特奥蒂瓦坎': ['这座城按方格规划,主街沿线排开日月金字塔与神庙,鼎盛时是美洲最大的城市。它 550 年前后城中心被焚毁,原因至今无定论;七百多年后阿兹特克人面对废墟,称它为「众神诞生之地」——特奥蒂瓦坎这个名字是他们起的,建城者自称什么,没人知道。',
 'The city was laid out on a grid, with the Pyramids of the Sun and Moon and its temples ranged along the main avenue; at its height it was the largest city in the Americas. Its centre burned around 550 for reasons still argued over. A thousand years later the Aztecs, facing the ruins, called it "the place where the gods were born" — Teotihuacan is their name for it; what its builders called themselves is unknown.'],
'特奥蒂瓦坎|托尔特克与谷地诸邦': ['这几百年里特奥蒂瓦坎已经是废墟,但没有被忘掉:废墟边上有村落,人们从倒塌的神庙里取石料盖房,同时又在金字塔附近留下这一时期的祭祀遗存——一边当采石场用,一边当圣地拜。图拉后来的规划、球场与羽蛇母题,处处看得出是照着这座城学的。一座城死了两百年,还在教后来的人怎么盖城。',
 'Through these centuries Teotihuacan was already a ruin, but not a forgotten one: villages stood beside it, people took stone from the fallen temples to build with, and at the same time left offerings of this period around the pyramids — quarry and shrine at once. Tula\'s later layout, its ball court and its feathered-serpent motifs all show the older city being studied and copied. A city two centuries dead was still teaching people how to build one.'],
'蒂卡尔|玛雅': ['蒂卡尔是古典期玛雅最大的城邦之一,神庙金字塔从雨林树冠上顶出来。它与北方的卡拉克穆尔各领一个联盟,争了一百多年谁也没能统一;八、九世纪间低地城邦陆续被弃,但玛雅人从未消失,今天仍有数百万人说玛雅语。',
 'Tikal was among the largest Maya city-states of the Classic period, its temple-pyramids pushing up through the rainforest canopy. It led one alliance and Calakmul to the north led another; a century and a half of war settled nothing. Through the eighth and ninth centuries the lowland cities were abandoned one by one — but the Maya never vanished, and millions still speak Mayan languages today.'],
'卡霍基亚|密西西比文化·卡霍基亚': ['1050 年前后这里突然大规模扩张,考古学家称之为「大爆炸」。僧侣丘是墨西哥以北最大的土丘,底面积和埃及胡夫金字塔差不多大;城里还立过成圈的木柱,一般认为是用来观测日出方位的。没有文字留下来,我们对它的了解全部来自地下。',
 'Around 1050 the site expanded suddenly — archaeologists call it the Big Bang. Monks Mound is the largest earthen mound north of Mexico, with a base about the same size as the Great Pyramid of Giza; rings of upright posts once stood here, thought to have tracked the sunrise. No writing survives: everything we know comes out of the ground.'],
'利马|西葡殖民美洲': ['1535 年皮萨罗在这里建城,取名「诸王之城」,后来成了西班牙秘鲁总督区的中心。波托西的白银用骡马队运下高原,在太平洋岸装船北上,经利马的外港卡亚俄转运,再穿过巴拿马地峡运往塞维利亚;另一股白银经阿卡普尔科由大帆船去马尼拉。十六、十七世纪的全球白银循环,这里是关键一环。',
 'Pizarro founded the city in 1535 as the City of Kings; it became the seat of Spain\'s Viceroyalty of Peru. Silver from Potosi came down by mule train, was shipped up the Pacific coast through Callao, Lima\'s port, and carried across the isthmus of Panama for Seville; another stream went by galleon from Acapulco to Manila. Lima was a key link in the global silver circuit of the sixteenth and seventeenth centuries.'],
'利马|帕查卡马克与中部海岸': ['今天利马以南三十公里,有一片土黄色的台地遗址,叫帕查卡马克。它从约 200 年开始建,一直用到 1533 年,前后一千三百年——利马文化、瓦里、伊奇马、印加,四拨人先后经手,每一拨都来扩建它。它出名不是因为哪位国王,而是因为神谕:各地的人长途赶来问收成、问病、问要不要打仗。印加征服这一带之后没有拆它,在旁边加建了自己的太阳神庙,让原来的神谕继续开口。今天城市几乎已经长到它脚下。',
 'Thirty kilometres south of today\'s Lima lies a spread of ochre terraces called Pachacamac. Building began there around 200 CE and continued until 1533 — thirteen centuries, through the Lima culture, the Wari, the Ychsma and the Inca, each of whom enlarged it in turn. Its fame rested not on any king but on its oracle: people came long distances to ask about harvests, about illness, about whether to go to war. When the Inca took this coast they did not pull it down but built their own sun temple beside it and let the old oracle go on speaking. The city has now grown almost to its edge.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|印度河文明': ['摩亨佐达罗按方格布局,有砖砌下水道、公共大浴池和统一规格的砖。它的文字至今没人能读懂,所以我们知道这座城怎么建,却不知道住在里面的人叫什么、信什么、说什么话。',
 'Mohenjo-daro was laid out on a grid, with brick drains, a great public bath and bricks made to a standard size. Its script has never been deciphered — so we know how the city was built, but not what its people called themselves, what they believed, or what language they spoke.'],
'汉皮|维查耶纳伽尔': ['都城毗奢耶那伽罗建在乱石岗与河流之间,天然是座要塞,鼎盛时人口可能有数十万。1565 年塔利科塔之战战败后,城被攻破洗劫数月;今天汉皮满地是神庙、水渠与市场的石头遗迹。',
 'The capital Vijayanagara sat among boulder hills and rivers, a fortress by nature, and at its height may have held several hundred thousand people. After defeat at Talikota in 1565 the city was stormed and looted for months; what stands at Hampi today is a field of temples, water channels and market colonnades in stone.'],
'瓦拉纳西|莫卧儿帝国': ['瓦拉纳西是印度教最重要的圣城之一,人们到恒河边沐浴、火化。1669 年奥朗则布下令拆毁城中的湿婆神庙,在原址建起清真寺。那座清真寺至今还在;旁边那座庙是一百多年后(1780 年)由印多尔的阿霍尔雅拜出资重建的。',
 'Varanasi is among the holiest cities of Hinduism, where people come to bathe in the Ganges and to be cremated. In 1669 Aurangzeb ordered the city\'s Shiva temple pulled down and a mosque raised on the site. That mosque still stands; the temple beside it was rebuilt more than a century later, in 1780, at the expense of Ahilyabai Holkar of Indore.'],
'瓦拉纳西|巽伽与恒河诸国': ['这几百年没有一个大朝廷罩着,出钱办事的反而是商人。沿商路一座座建起来的佛塔与石窟,栏楯上刻着捐款人的名字:布商、香料商、金匠行会,还有他们的妻子——这是印度最早的一批「谁出的钱」名单。瓦拉纳西正卡在恒河商路上,城里的作坊与市集在这一时期兴盛起来;它以织物出名,一直到今天。',
 'For these centuries no great court presided, and the money came from merchants instead. Stupas and rock-cut halls went up along the trade roads with the donors\' names carved into their railings: cloth merchants, spice dealers, goldsmiths\' guilds, and their wives — among the earliest records anywhere of who actually paid. Varanasi sat squarely on the Ganges trade road, and its workshops and markets flourished in this period. It was known for its textiles then, and still is.'],
'麦地那|阿拉伯哈里发': ['622 年穆罕默德从麦加迁到这里,伊斯兰历就从这一年算起。他到这里第一天就建起库巴清真寺,后来又建先知清真寺,并葬在其中;此后二十余年,这座绿洲城是整个哈里发国的政治中心,直到都城他迁。',
 'In 622 Muhammad moved here from Mecca — the year the Islamic calendar counts from. On his first day here he raised the Quba mosque, later built the Prophet\'s Mosque, and lies buried in it; for the next two decades and more this oasis town was the political centre of the whole caliphate, until the capital moved elsewhere.'],
'巴比伦|苏美尔·阿卡德': ['苏美尔时代的巴比伦只是幼发拉底河边一个不起眼的地方,最早的记载出现在阿卡德王朝的文书里。真正的大城在南边——乌鲁克、乌尔、拉格什,它们比巴比伦的鼎盛早了一千多年。',
 'In Sumerian times Babylon was an unremarkable place on the Euphrates, first mentioned in tablets of the Akkadian period. The great cities lay to the south — Uruk, Ur, Lagash — and their height came more than a thousand years before Babylon\'s.'],
'巴比伦|亚述': ['亚述几次征服巴比伦,又几次拿它没办法:巴比伦是两河文化的老家,连亚述国王都要来这里行礼才算名正言顺。前 689 年辛那赫里布干脆下令毁城、引水灌淹;可他的继任者又把城重建了起来——城能毁,「巴比伦」这个名分毁不掉。',
 'Assyria conquered Babylon several times and never quite knew what to do with it: Babylon was the old home of Mesopotamian culture, and even Assyrian kings had to take its honours to be counted legitimate. In 689 BC Sennacherib ordered the city destroyed and water turned onto the ruins — and his successor rebuilt it. The city could be levelled; the name could not.'],
'巴比伦|新巴比伦': ['这是巴比伦最后也是最辉煌的一段。尼布甲尼撒二世重修城墙与神庙,建起伊什塔尔门——蓝釉砖上贴着公牛与神兽,原件今天在柏林。城中的马尔杜克神庙塔,一般认为就是《圣经》里巴别塔的原型。至于空中花园,记载只见于后世用希腊文写作的人——最早提到它的贝罗索斯本人还是巴比伦的祭司;而巴比伦本地的泥板文书里,一个字都没提到过。',
 'This was Babylon\'s last and greatest age. Nebuchadnezzar II rebuilt the walls and temples and raised the Ishtar Gate, its blue glazed brick set with bulls and dragons — the original is now in Berlin. The ziggurat of Marduk in the city is generally taken to be the tower the Bible calls Babel. As for the hanging gardens, they appear only in later writers working in Greek — the earliest of them, Berossus, was himself a Babylonian priest; and not one of Babylon\'s own tablets mentions them.'],
'巴比伦|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['前 539 年居鲁士几乎没打就进了巴比伦,还下令让被掳的犹太人回耶路撒冷重建圣殿。巴比伦成了波斯的行政中心之一,王室在这里过冬;到前 331 年亚历山大进城时,这座城还是完好的。',
 'Cyrus entered Babylon in 539 BC with hardly a fight and gave the deported Jews leave to return to Jerusalem and rebuild their temple. Babylon became one of Persia\'s administrative centres and the royal house wintered there; when Alexander marched in in 331 BC the city was still whole.'],
'巴比伦|希腊化王朝': ['前 323 年亚历山大在巴比伦病死,他原打算把这里做成帝国的首都。接手的塞琉古一世却在底格里斯河边另建了塞琉西亚,巴比伦的人口被迁了过去(一手的泥板记录写的是他儿子安条克一世下的令)——巴比伦从此一路衰落,到公元前后已基本荒废。',
 'Alexander died at Babylon in 323 BC; he had meant to make it the capital of his empire. Seleucus I, who took over, built Seleucia on the Tigris instead, and Babylon\'s people were moved there — the cuneiform record of the move names his son Antiochus I. Babylon declined from then on and was all but deserted by the turn of the era.'],
'巴比伦|帕提亚·萨珊': ['帕提亚与萨珊时期,巴比伦只剩下少量居民和一片土丘。巴比伦最后一批楔形文字泥板写于公元一世纪;整个两河流域目前所知年代最晚的一块,出自不远处的乌鲁克,定在公元 79 或 80 年。一种写了三千年的文字,就在这片平原上安静地断了。',
 'Under the Parthians and Sasanians only a few people and a spread of mounds were left. Babylon\'s last cuneiform tablets were written in the first century AD; the latest firmly dated tablet from anywhere in Mesopotamia comes from Uruk nearby, placed at AD 79 or 80. A script that had been written for three thousand years came quietly to an end on this plain.'],
'巴比伦|阿拉伯哈里发': ['阿拉伯人来时,巴比伦已经是一片废墟。此后一千年,这堆土丘成了周边村庄的采石场:尼布甲尼撒的砖上印着他的名字,被一块块搬走,砌进了别人的墙和沟渠。一座城的消失,往往不是被谁一次毁掉的,而是被后来的人慢慢搬空的。',
 'By the time the Arabs came Babylon was already ruins. For the next thousand years the mounds served as a quarry for the villages around: bricks stamped with Nebuchadnezzar\'s name were carried off one at a time and built into other people\'s walls and canal linings. Cities usually vanish not because someone destroys them but because those who come after carry them away.'],
'巴比伦|塞尔柱突厥': ['塞尔柱时期这一带属于伊拉克的农业区,土丘上散着村落。此时已经没有人知道那些土丘下面埋着什么——楔形文字已经近千年没人能读,巴比伦只剩下《圣经》和希腊史家笔下的一个名字。',
 'Under the Seljuks this was farming country in Iraq, with villages scattered over the mounds. By then nobody knew what lay beneath them: cuneiform had been unreadable for close to a thousand years, and Babylon survived only as a name in the Bible and in Greek historians.'],
'巴比伦|伊尔汗国': ['蒙古人攻陷巴格达之后,两河下游的灌溉渠网大面积失修,农田退回荒地。巴比伦所在的这片平原人口锐减,遗址被沙土进一步掩埋——它要到十九世纪欧洲人来发掘,才重新露出来。',
 'After the Mongols took Baghdad the canal system of the lower Two Rivers fell out of repair over wide areas and farmland went back to waste. The plain around Babylon lost most of its people and the ruins sank further under sand — they would not be uncovered again until Europeans came to dig in the nineteenth century.'],
'巴比伦|奥斯曼帝国': ['奥斯曼治下,这里是巴格达省的一片乡野。1899 年德国考古学家科尔德威在这里开始大规模发掘,一挖十几年,把伊什塔尔门的釉砖成箱运回柏林——今天在柏林佩加蒙博物馆看到的那座蓝色城门,就是用这些原件重新砌起来的。',
 'Under the Ottomans this was countryside in the province of Baghdad. In 1899 the German archaeologist Robert Koldewey began digging here on a large scale and kept at it for well over a decade, shipping the glazed brick of the Ishtar Gate to Berlin in crates — the blue gate people see in the Pergamon Museum today was reassembled from them.'],
'巴比伦|萨法维·波斯': ['萨法维与奥斯曼在两河反复争夺时,巴比伦一带是双方行军的必经之地。这一时期波斯与欧洲的旅行者开始把这些土丘记下来,并把它们和《圣经》里的巴别塔联系起来——巴比伦重新进入西方视野,靠的不是考古而是宗教。',
 'While the Safavids and Ottomans fought back and forth across Mesopotamia, armies passed through this district again and again. Persian and European travellers of these years began to write the mounds down and to connect them with the tower of Babel — Babylon returned to Western attention through scripture rather than through excavation.'],
'巴比伦|现代中东': ['1980 年代萨达姆下令在遗址上重建宫墙,新砖上刻着自己的名字,压在尼布甲尼撒的旧砖之上;这种做法后来被广泛批评为对遗址的破坏。2003 年之后驻军曾在遗址上建营地,平出直升机停机坪与重型车辆的停车场,又造成损伤。2019 年巴比伦列入世界文化遗产名录。',
 'In the 1980s Saddam Hussein had palace walls rebuilt on the site with new bricks bearing his own name, laid straight on top of Nebuchadnezzar\'s; the work was later widely condemned as damage to the site. After 2003 troops built a camp over the ruins, levelling ground for helicopter pads and heavy-vehicle parking, doing further harm. Babylon was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 2019.'],
'巴比伦|加喜特巴比伦': ['加喜特人从东边山里来,却把巴比伦的一切原样接了过去:阿卡德语、楔形文字、马尔杜克神。他们留下的标志物叫「库杜鲁」——一块刻着神的符号的界石,写明国王把哪块地封给了谁,末尾照例有一句诅咒:谁挪动它,这些神就找谁。这是已知最早的一批地契,把「这地是谁的」从人的记忆里搬到了石头上。',
 'The Kassites came out of the hills to the east and took over everything Babylonian as it stood: Akkadian, cuneiform, the god Marduk. Their signature object is the kudurru — a boundary stone carved with the emblems of the gods, recording which land the king had granted to whom and closing, as a rule, with a curse: whoever moves it will answer to these gods. They are among the earliest land deeds known, moving the question of who owns what out of human memory and onto stone.'],
'大马士革|阿尤布王朝': ['萨拉丁把埃及与叙利亚合到一起,大马士革是他的北方大本营。1193 年他病逝于此,葬在倭马亚大清真寺旁——据记载他死时私产极少,连办丧事的钱都要人代垫。',
 'Saladin joined Egypt and Syria under one house, and Damascus was his northern base. He died here in 1193 and lies buried beside the Umayyad Mosque; as the story is told he left so little of his own that his funeral had to be paid for by others.'],
'开罗|古埃及': ['开罗往南约二十公里就是孟菲斯——古王国的都城;吉萨的三座金字塔就在它西边的沙漠边缘,前二十六世纪建成。金字塔真正证明的不是国王多想不朽,而是那时的埃及已经能把几万人组织起来、连着干上几十年。',
 'About twenty kilometres south of Cairo stood Memphis, capital of the Old Kingdom, and the three pyramids of Giza rise at the desert edge west of it, finished in the twenty-sixth century BC. What the pyramids really prove is not how badly a king wanted to live forever but that Egypt could already organise tens of thousands of people and keep them at one task for decades.'],
'开罗|亚述': ['前 671 年亚述王以撒哈顿攻入埃及、占领孟菲斯,前 663 年亚述巴尼拔又洗劫了底比斯。亚述在埃及待的时间不长——而且它赶走的塔哈尔卡,自己就是来自南方的努比亚法老;在努比亚人之前,埃及还被利比亚裔的王朝统治过。这个几千年自己管自己的国家,那几百年里一直在被外人轮流管。',
 'Esarhaddon of Assyria invaded Egypt in 671 BC and took Memphis; in 663 BC Ashurbanipal sacked Thebes. Assyria did not stay long — and the pharaoh it drove out, Taharqa, was himself a Nubian from the south, while dynasties of Libyan descent had ruled before the Nubians. For those few centuries the country that had governed itself for millennia was governed by one set of outsiders after another.'],
'开罗|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['前 525 年冈比西斯二世击败埃及军队,埃及成为波斯的一个总督辖区。连接尼罗河与红海的运河,埃及王尼科二世当年就动过工;大流士把它续修下去并立石碑纪念,不过古代作者对他到底修通没有说法不一。那条渠走的是三角洲东边的干河谷、并不经过开罗——运河口南移到今天老开罗这个位置,要等到罗马的图拉真时期。比苏伊士运河早了两千多年,想法是一样的。',
 'Cambyses II beat the Egyptian army in 525 BC and Egypt became a Persian satrapy. A canal from the Nile to the Red Sea had already been begun by the Egyptian king Necho II; Darius carried the work on and set up stelae to mark it, though ancient writers disagree over whether he ever finished. That channel ran through the dry valley east of the delta and nowhere near Cairo — its mouth only moved south to where old Cairo stands under the Roman emperor Trajan. More than two thousand years before Suez, and the same idea.'],
'开罗|罗马共和国': ['前 30 年屋大维击败安东尼与克娄巴特拉,托勒密王朝终结,埃及归了罗马。罗马把埃及当粮仓,而今天开罗所在的这一段正卡在尼罗河谷进入三角洲的口子上——上游运下来的粮食都要先过这里,才能顺流去亚历山大装船运往罗马。守住这个口子,就等于握住了罗马的饭。',
 'Octavian defeated Antony and Cleopatra in 30 BC, the Ptolemies ended and Egypt passed to Rome. Rome treated Egypt as a granary, and the stretch where Cairo now stands sits at the neck where the Nile valley opens into the delta — grain from upriver had to pass this point before going on to Alexandria and the ships for Rome. To hold that neck was to hold Rome\'s dinner.'],
'开罗|罗马帝国': ['罗马在今天开罗老城的位置修了一座要塞,名字叫「巴比伦」——和两河流域那个巴比伦没有关系,来源一般认为是某个埃及地名的转写。要塞的圆塔至今还立在那里,后来的老开罗就是围着它长起来的。',
 'Rome built a fortress where old Cairo now stands, called Babylon — no relation to the Babylon of Mesopotamia; the name is generally taken to be a garbled Egyptian place name. Its round towers are still standing, and old Cairo grew up around them.'],
'开罗|罗马治下近东': ['这几百年里,埃及的教会走出了自己的路:科普特教会用埃及本地的语言诵经,沙漠里出现了最早的一批修道院。基督教的修道制度就是从埃及的沙漠开始的,后来传遍整个基督教世界——一种生活方式从这里出发,走了很远。',
 'Over these centuries the Egyptian church went its own way: the Coptic church prayed in the language of the country, and the first monasteries appeared out in the desert. Christian monasticism began in the Egyptian desert and spread from there through the whole Christian world — a way of life that started here and travelled a long way.'],
'开罗|拜占庭': ['拜占庭治下的埃及是帝国最重要的粮食来源,君士坦丁堡的口粮有很大一部分从这里运去;今天开罗老城位置上的巴比伦要塞,就是拜占庭守着这个河口的据点。埃及的教会与君士坦丁堡在教义上长期不合,朝廷屡次强压;641 年阿拉伯军队围攻巴比伦要塞时,当地的抵抗并不坚决。',
 'Under Byzantium Egypt was the empire\'s chief source of grain, and much of what Constantinople ate came up from here; the fortress of Babylon, on the site of old Cairo, was the Byzantine strongpoint holding that neck of the river. The Egyptian church and the capital disagreed on doctrine for centuries and the court kept pressing its view, and when the Arab army laid siege to Babylon in 641, local resistance was not wholehearted.'],
'开罗|阿拉伯哈里发': ['641 年阿拉伯军队攻下巴比伦要塞后,就在旁边扎营建城,取名福斯塔特——这是埃及第一座伊斯兰城市,也是开罗的前身。阿慕尔清真寺就建在那里,是埃及第一座清真寺,也是非洲最早的清真寺之一;三百多年后法蒂玛人在它北边另建新都,才有了「开罗」这个名字。',
 'After taking the fortress of Babylon in 641 the Arab army pitched camp beside it and built a town called Fustat — the first Islamic city in Egypt and the seed of Cairo. The mosque of Amr went up there, the first in Egypt and one of the earliest in Africa; three centuries later the Fatimids founded a new capital just north of it, and that one was named Cairo.'],
'开罗|阿尤布王朝': ['萨拉丁在开罗东边的山冈上修了城堡,又动工修一道城墙,想把福斯塔特与开罗圈到一起——那道墙他死后几十年还在修,始终没有完全合拢。此后近七百年,埃及的统治者一直住在这座城堡里,直到十九世纪才搬出来——一座为防十字军而修的军事建筑,后来成了这个国家的办公室。',
 'Saladin built a citadel on the hill east of Cairo and began a wall meant to enclose both Fustat and Cairo — decades after his death it was still being built, and it never fully closed. For nearly seven hundred years after that the rulers of Egypt lived in it, moving out only in the nineteenth century — a fortress raised against the crusaders that ended up as the country\'s office.'],
'开罗|奥斯曼帝国': ['1517 年奥斯曼灭马穆鲁克,埃及成为一个省,开罗从帝国的首都降成省城。此前欧洲人绕过好望角开辟了直达印度的航线,经开罗转运的香料生意已经萎缩;不过它仍是阿拉伯世界最大的几座城市之一——只是规模在缩:马穆鲁克鼎盛时开罗有五十万人上下,1798 年拿破仑来时已不到三十万。',
 'The Ottomans destroyed the Mamluk state in 1517; Egypt became a province and Cairo went from imperial capital to provincial town. The spice trade that had passed through it was already shrinking, now that Europeans sailed round the Cape straight to India — even so it stayed one of the largest cities in the Arab world — though it was shrinking: Cairo had held something like half a million people at the Mamluk height, and fewer than three hundred thousand when Napoleon arrived in 1798.'],
'开罗|现代中东': ['1869 年苏伊士运河通航,开罗重新回到欧亚航线的枢纽位置。1922 年埃及取得名义上的独立,1952 年革命后成为共和国。今天的开罗都会区住着两千多万人,是非洲与阿拉伯世界最大的城市之一。',
 'The Suez Canal opened in 1869 and Cairo was back on the hinge between Europe and Asia. Egypt gained nominal independence in 1922 and became a republic after the revolution of 1952. Greater Cairo now holds well over twenty million people, among the largest cities in Africa and the Arab world.'],
'开罗|马穆鲁克': ['1258 年巴格达被蒙古军攻灭后,开罗接过了伊斯兰世界的中心位置——阿拔斯家族的一支逃到这里,被马穆鲁克苏丹奉为哈里发,虽无实权却给了政权名分。1260 年马穆鲁克在阿音扎鲁特击败蒙古军,这是蒙古扩张在西亚方向第一次被明确挡住;现代研究指出当时蒙古主力已因大汗去世东撤,这一战的分量仍有争论。',
 'After the Mongols destroyed Baghdad in 1258, Cairo took over as the centre of the Islamic world: a surviving Abbasid was brought here and installed as caliph by the Mamluk sultans — powerless, but a source of legitimacy. In 1260 the Mamluks beat a Mongol army at Ain Jalut, the first clear check on Mongol expansion in western Asia — though modern scholarship notes the main Mongol force had already withdrawn east on the death of the great khan, and the battle\'s weight is still argued over.'],
'特拉布宗|拜占庭': ['特拉布宗是黑海南岸的港口,从内亚来的商路在这里下海。1204 年,几乎与十字军攻陷君士坦丁堡同时,拜占庭皇族的一支从格鲁吉亚出兵占了这里、另立政权;它一直撑到 1461 年,比君士坦丁堡本身还多活了八年。',
 'Trebizond was the Black Sea port where the overland routes from inner Asia reached the water. In 1204, almost at the same moment as the crusaders took Constantinople, a branch of the imperial family marched in from Georgia and set up its own state here — and it held out until 1461, eight years longer than Constantinople itself.'],
'香港|秦': ['前 214 年秦置南海郡,今天的香港一带划归番禺县,第一次进入中原王朝的版图。这时的香港只是珠江口外的一片海岛与海岸,居民多是以船为家的越人与山地部族。',
 'Qin created Nanhai commandery in 214 BC and what is now Hong Kong was placed under Panyu county, entering the map of a Chinese dynasty for the first time. It was then a stretch of islands and shoreline outside the Pearl River mouth, its people mostly Yue, some living on boats and some in the hills.'],
'香港|西汉': ['西汉先属南越国、后属南海郡。李郑屋出土的东汉砖室墓说明,至迟到汉代已有中原式的墓葬制度传到这里;不过整个汉代,这一带的人口都很稀薄。',
 'It belonged first to Nanyue and then, after the conquest, to Nanhai commandery. The Eastern Han brick tomb found at Lei Cheng Uk shows that Central Plains burial practice had reached here by the Han at the latest — though through the whole Han period the population remained thin.'],
'香港|东汉': ['东汉时这一带产盐。珠江口的浅滩适合产盐,汉代在番禺设有盐官管这一片的盐务——西汉行专卖,东汉改成征税。香港岸线上具体的汉代盐场至今没有找到确证,但此后一千多年,盐业一直是这片海岸最重要的生计之一,直到近代才衰落。',
 'Salt was made here under the Eastern Han. The shallows at the mouth of the Pearl River suited it, and the Han posted a salt officer at Panyu over this stretch of coast — a state monopoly under the Western Han, taxed rather than monopolised under the Eastern. No Han salt field has yet been confirmed on the Hong Kong shoreline itself, but for over a thousand years afterwards salt remained one of the chief livelihoods of this coast, fading only in modern times.'],
'香港|三国': ['三国时属东吴。孙吴在今深圳南头一带设司盐都尉,管南海沿岸的官营盐场,这一带的海岸线开始被系统利用;不过在东吴眼里,这里主要还是一段航路与一处盐产地,而不是一个值得设城的地方。',
 'It belonged to Wu under the Three Kingdoms. Wu posted a salt commandant around today\'s Nantou in Shenzhen to run the state salt fields of this coast, and the shoreline began to be used systematically — though to Wu it was mainly a stretch of sea route and a source of salt, not a place worth walling a town.'],
'香港|西晋': ['西晋时这一带仍属南海郡番禺县——东官郡要到东晋咸和六年(331 年)才从南海郡分出来。这一带地处偏远,历代政权对它的管理都很松,真正把人口带过来的是几次北方战乱——每一次中原大乱,都会有一批人沿海路南下,在珠江口的岛屿与海湾间落脚。',
 'Under the Western Jin it still lay in Panyu county of Nanhai commandery; Dongguan commandery was not split off until 331, under the Eastern Jin. Remote and lightly governed by every dynasty, it filled up mainly through the wars of the north: each time the Central Plains came apart, another group came south by sea and settled among the islands and inlets of the estuary.'],
'香港|东晋·十六国': ['东晋末年孙恩、卢循的起义军曾沿海南下,一度到过珠江口一带。这类沿海的流动政权与海盗势力,在此后一千多年里反复出现——珠江口岛屿众多、官府力量薄弱,历来是这类势力的活动区。',
 'At the end of the Eastern Jin the rebel fleets of Sun En and Lu Xun came down the coast and reached the Pearl River estuary. Seaborne rebels and pirates of this kind recur through the next thousand years: the estuary is full of islands and thin on government, and has always suited them.'],
'香港|南北朝': ['南朝时这一带属东官郡。相传南朝的杯渡禅师到过屯门,不过「屯门」这个地名要到《新唐书》才见于正史;它是船只自南海入珠江前的一个停泊点,从东南亚与印度洋来的商船,常在这里等潮水与季风,再上溯到广州。',
 'The district belonged to Dongguan commandery under the Southern Dynasties. The monk Bei Du is said to have come to Tuen Mun in these years, though the name itself only enters the histories with the Tang; it was an anchorage where ships lay before entering the Pearl River, vessels from Southeast Asia and the Indian Ocean often waited here for tide and monsoon before going up to Guangzhou.'],
'香港|隋': ['隋属宝安县。屯门的位置越发要紧:凡从南海来的番舶,想进珠江都要先经过这里,再上溯广州。到唐代,朝廷干脆在屯门设镇驻军。',
 'Under the Sui it lay in Bao\'an county. Tuen Mun grew more important: any ship from the southern seas had to pass it before entering the Pearl River and going up to Guangzhou. Under the Tang the court would station a garrison there outright.'],
'香港|唐': ['唐在屯门设镇,驻兵两千,是广州的外港与海防前哨,「广州通海夷道」的第一站就是这里。阿拉伯与波斯的商船先在屯门停靠、报关,再溯江而上——今天香港这片水域,一千二百年前就已经是国际航路的一环。',
 'The Tang stationed a garrison of two thousand at Tuen Mun, the outer port and seaward picket of Guangzhou and the first stop on the sea route to the western lands. Arab and Persian ships put in at Tuen Mun and reported before going up the river — these waters were part of an international shipping lane twelve centuries ago.'],
'香港|五代十国': ['南汉据有岭南,在大埔一带(当时称大步海,今吐露港)设过采珠的官署,称媚川都,征调数千人下海采珠,溺死者众。南汉亡后北宋一度禁绝,但珠江口的采珠业断断续续延续到明代。',
 'The Southern Han held the far south and set up a pearling office around Tai Po, on what was then Tai Po Hoi, today\'s Tolo Harbour, the Meichuan Command, pressing thousands of men to dive, many of whom drowned. The Song banned it for a time after the Southern Han fell, but pearling in the estuary carried on intermittently into the Ming.'],
'香港|北宋': ['北宋在这一带设官富场,是广东沿海的重要盐场之一,场官驻在今九龙城一带。今天新界的几个大族——邓、文、廖、侯、彭——里,邓氏在北宋就从江西迁来,侯氏来自广东番禺,彭、廖、文三族则多在元末到明代之间陆续从江西、福建迁入。',
 'The Song ran the Guanfu salt field here, one of the important ones on the Guangdong coast, with its officer stationed around today\'s Kowloon City. Of the great New Territories clans, the Tang came from Jiangxi in the Northern Song and the Hau from Panyu in Guangdong, while the Pang, Liu and Man mostly arrived later, between the end of the Yuan and the Ming, from Jiangxi and Fujian.'],
'香港|南宋': ['南宋末年,陆秀夫、张世杰护送幼帝一路南逃,曾在今九龙一带停留;宋王台的传说就出自这段。1279 年崖山之后南宋覆灭,而那批随行南下的人,有一部分就留在了这片海岸。',
 'At the end of the Southern Song, Lu Xiufu and Zhang Shijie fled south with the boy emperor and are said to have stopped in what is now Kowloon; the Sung Wong Toi rock takes its story from that episode. The dynasty ended at Yamen in 1279, and some of those who had come south with the court stayed on this coast.'],
'香港|元': ['元代这一带属东莞县,盐场与渔业照旧。元朝的海外贸易比宋代更盛,珠江口的航运随之更密;不过对元廷来说,这里始终是广州这个大港外围的一片水域。',
 'Under the Yuan the district belonged to Dongguan county and the salt fields and fisheries went on as before. Overseas trade was busier under the Yuan than the Song and shipping in the estuary thickened with it — though to the Yuan court this remained a stretch of water on the edge of the great port of Guangzhou.'],
'香港|明': ['1573 年从东莞析置新安县,今天香港的大部分土地归入其中。明代葡萄牙人曾在屯门一带盘踞,1521 年被明军逐走,史称屯门海战——这是中国与欧洲国家之间最早的几次军事冲突之一。',
 'In 1573 Xin\'an county was split off from Dongguan, taking in most of what is now Hong Kong. The Portuguese had earlier established themselves around Tuen Mun and were driven out by Ming forces in 1521 — among the first armed clashes between China and a European power.'],
'香港|清': ['清初迁界令下,新安沿海居民内迁,田园尽废,复界后官府招客家人入垦,新界的客家村落多始于此。1842 年《南京条约》割香港岛给英国,这片海岸从此走上另一条路。',
 'The early Qing coastal evacuation emptied the shores of Xin\'an and ruined its fields; when the ban was lifted the government recruited Hakka settlers to take up the land, and most Hakka villages in the New Territories date from then. The Treaty of Nanking ceded Hong Kong Island to Britain in 1842, and this coast took a different road from that point.'],
'香港|民国': ['这段时间香港在英国治下。1937 年后大批内地人口涌入香港避战,人口从不足一百万涨到一百六十余万。1941 年 12 月日军进攻,守军抵抗十八天后投降,此后三年零八个月的日据时期里,人口又被强制疏散回内地,降到约六十万。',
 'Hong Kong was under British rule throughout these years. After 1937 people poured in from the mainland to escape the war and the population rose from under a million to more than 1.6 million. Japanese forces attacked in December 1941, the garrison surrendered after eighteen days, and through the three years and eight months of occupation the population was forced back to the mainland until only some six hundred thousand remained.'],
'香港|共和国': ['1997 年 7 月 1 日香港回归,实行「一国两制」。此前几十年里,这座城从转口港转为制造业中心、再转为金融与航运中心;它长期是内地与世界之间的中转站,改革开放初期的外资有很大一部分是经香港进来的。',
 'Hong Kong returned to Chinese sovereignty on 1 July 1997 under the formula of one country, two systems. Over the preceding decades the city had turned from an entrepot into a manufacturing centre and then into a centre of finance and shipping; it long served as the way-station between the mainland and the world, and much of the foreign investment of the early reform years came in through it.'],
'香港|大英帝国·英国': ['1842 年鸦片战争后清朝割让香港岛,1860 年再割九龙半岛界限街以南的一段,1898 年把新界租给英国九十九年——正是这份九十九年租约,定下了 1997 年这个日子。割让时岛上已有二十多条村落,赤柱是其中最大的一处墟市;此后它变成远东最繁忙的港口之一。',
 'The Qing ceded Hong Kong Island after the Opium War in 1842, the part of the Kowloon peninsula south of Boundary Street in 1860, and in 1898 leased the New Territories to Britain for ninety-nine years — it was that lease that fixed the date 1997. The island already held more than twenty villages when it was ceded, Stanley the largest with its market; from there it grew into one of the busiest ports in the Far East.'],
'基尔瓦|斯瓦希里城邦': ['基尔瓦扼住内陆黄金的出海口——索法拉的金子必须经这里北运,城邦因此富起来。1331 年伊本·白图泰到访,称它是他见过最美的城市之一;岛上的大清真寺用珊瑚石砌成,遗址至今还在。',
 'Kilwa held the outlet for inland gold: bullion from Sofala had to pass through on its way north, and the city grew rich on it. Ibn Battuta came in 1331 and called it one of the finest cities he had seen; its Great Mosque, built of coral stone, still stands in ruins on the island.'],
'加奥|桑海帝国': ['加奥是桑海的都城,阿斯基亚·穆罕默德在这里推行行政与度量衡改革,把帝国撑到西非最大。1591 年摩洛哥军队带着火枪穿过撒哈拉,在通迪比击溃桑海军——弓箭对火枪,桑海主力一战而溃;但朝廷东撤登地,又延续了两个多世纪。',
 'Gao was the Songhai capital, where Askia Muhammad pushed through reforms of administration and weights and measures that carried the empire to the largest in West Africa. In 1591 a Moroccan army crossed the Sahara with firearms and broke the Songhai at Tondibi — bows against muskets, and the Songhai army went down in a single battle; the court withdrew east to Dendi, where the line carried on for another two centuries and more.'],
'曼谷|暹罗': ['1767 年旧都阿瑜陀耶被缅甸军焚毁,郑昭在河对岸的吞武里重整旗鼓;十五年后拉玛一世继位,把都城搬到今天的曼谷这一侧。此后一百多年,暹罗在英法两大殖民势力之间反复周旋,是东南亚唯一没有被殖民的国家。',
 'The old capital Ayutthaya was burned by a Burmese army in 1767 and Taksin regrouped at Thonburi across the river; fifteen years later Rama I came to the throne and moved the capital to the Bangkok side. Over the next century Siam manoeuvred between the British and the French and came through as the one Southeast Asian state never colonized.'],
'首尔|朝鲜半岛诸王朝': ['1394 年李成桂把都城迁到汉阳,就是今天的首尔,此后五百多年基本一直是朝鲜的京城。景福宫在这里建起;1443 年世宗创制谚文,让不识汉字的百姓也能写自己的话;三年后颁行《训民正音》。',
 'In 1394 Yi Seong-gye moved the capital to Hanyang — today\'s Seoul — and apart from a few years early on it stayed the seat of Joseon for over five centuries. Gyeongbokgung palace was raised here, and in 1443 King Sejong devised Hangul so that people who did not know Chinese characters could write their own speech, promulgating it three years later.'],
'台北|清': ['清朝 1683 年取台湾,起初只设一府归福建管。1885 年台湾建省,首任巡抚刘铭传驻在台北,修铁路、架电报;省城原本定在今天的台中一带,一直没建成,1894 年才正式改到台北。第二年,马关条约把台湾割给了日本。',
 'The Qing took Taiwan in 1683 and at first governed it as a single prefecture under Fujian. In 1885 Taiwan was made a province; its first governor Liu Mingchuan sat at Taipei and built railways and telegraph lines. The provincial capital had been planned inland at today\'s Taichung, was never finished, and was formally moved to Taipei only in 1894. The very next year the Treaty of Shimonoseki handed Taiwan to Japan.'],
'喀什|唐': ['唐设安西四镇,疏勒(今喀什)是其中之一,朝廷在这里驻兵屯田。玄奘东归时经过疏勒,在《大唐西域记》里记下这里的文字取法印度、佛寺数百所——那时的喀什还是一座佛教城市。',
 'The Tang held four garrison towns in the western regions and Shule, today\'s Kashgar, was one of them, with troops posted and land put under cultivation. Xuanzang passed through on his way home and noted in his record that the local script followed Indian models and that there were hundreds of monasteries — Kashgar was a Buddhist city then.'],
'喀什|西辽·哈剌契丹': ['西辽把喀什一带交给当地的喀喇汗王族继续管,只收贡赋、不改宗教。1211 年乃蛮部的屈出律夺了西辽的权,他反过来强迫这一带的穆斯林改宗、关闭清真寺;几年后蒙古军队来到,当地人几乎没有抵抗。',
 'Qara Khitai left Kashgar to its own Qarakhanid family, taking tribute and leaving religion alone. In 1211 Kuchlug of the Naiman seized power in the state and did the reverse — forcing conversions and closing mosques in this district. When Mongol troops arrived a few years later, the local people put up almost no resistance.'],
'喀什|蒙古帝国': ['1218 年哲别率蒙古军进入喀什一带,屈出律败死,他强加的宗教迫害随之结束。此后喀什属察合台汗国,是蒙古治下东西商路上的一站——商路重新打通,是蒙古扩张少有的、对沿途的人有好处的一面。',
 'Jebe brought a Mongol force into the Kashgar district in 1218; Kuchlug was defeated and killed and the persecution he had imposed ended with him. Kashgar then belonged to the Chagatai khanate, a stop on the east-west roads under Mongol rule — the reopening of those roads being one of the few parts of Mongol expansion that did the people along them any good.'],
'喀什|清': ['1759 年清朝取得喀什,设参赞大臣。1865 年阿古柏从中亚进入新疆、以喀什为据点建立政权,1877 年左宗棠率军收复,1884 年新疆建省——这段反复,是清朝在西北投入最大的一次。',
 'The Qing took Kashgar in 1759 and stationed a councillor-commandant there. In 1865 Yaqub Beg came in from Central Asia and set up a state with Kashgar as his base; Zuo Zongtang recovered the region in 1877, and Xinjiang was made a province in 1884 — the largest effort the Qing ever put into the northwest.'],
'喀什|民国': ['民国时期喀什长期由地方势力实际控制,中央的政令常常到不了。英国与俄国都在这里设了领事馆,表面上办侨务,实际上是两个帝国在中亚较劲的一个前哨——一座城里两家领事馆,盯的其实是彼此。',
 'Through the Republic years Kashgar was effectively run by local power holders and orders from the centre often never arrived. Britain and Russia both kept consulates here, nominally for their nationals but in fact as listening posts in the contest between two empires — two consulates in one town, each watching the other.'],
'喀什|共和国': ['喀什老城经过多年加固与改造,一部分保留了原有的巷道格局。它离伊斯兰堡比离北京近,离德黑兰比离上海近——这个位置决定了它两千年来一直是个中转站,今天通往巴基斯坦的公路,起点也在这一带。',
 'The old town of Kashgar has been reinforced and rebuilt over many years, with part of its lane pattern kept. It is closer to Islamabad than to Beijing, and closer to Tehran than to Shanghai — a position that has made it a place of transit for two thousand years, and the road over the mountains to Pakistan still starts here.'],
'乌兰巴托|匈奴': ['乌兰巴托北边的诺音乌拉山里发掘出匈奴贵族的墓,随葬品里有中原的漆器与丝绸,也有来自更西方的毛织品。一个游牧政权的墓,埋着三个方向来的东西——草原不是隔断,是通道。',
 'In the Noin-Ula hills north of Ulaanbaatar, tombs of the Xiongnu nobility have been excavated holding Chinese lacquer and silk alongside woollens from much further west. A nomad grave with goods from three directions in it — the steppe was not a barrier but a corridor.'],
'乌兰巴托|柔然': ['柔然的王庭在鄂尔浑河与土拉河一带,离今天的乌兰巴托不远。草原政权的「都城」往往不是一座城,而是可汗大帐所在的地方——牲畜要跟着草走,首都也就跟着走。这片河谷水草好,所以一个又一个政权把中心放在这里。',
 'The Rouran court lay along the Orkhon and Tuul rivers, not far from where Ulaanbaatar stands. A steppe capital was usually not a city but wherever the khan\'s great tent happened to be — the herds followed the grass and the capital followed the herds. This valley had good water and pasture, which is why one power after another put its centre here.'],
'乌兰巴托|突厥汗国': ['突厥的政治中心在乌兰巴托西边约三百多公里的鄂尔浑河谷。那里立着阙特勤碑与毗伽可汗碑,一面刻突厥文、一面刻汉文;两面讲的还不完全是一回事——这是草原史里少见的、由草原人自己写下的第一手材料。',
 'The Turkic political centre lay in the Orkhon valley, some three hundred and more kilometres west of Ulaanbaatar. The stelae of Kul Tigin and Bilge Qaghan stand there, cut with Turkic on one face and Chinese on the other — and the two faces do not say quite the same thing. They are that rare thing in steppe history: a first-hand account written by steppe people themselves.'],
'乌兰巴托|回鹘': ['回鹘在鄂尔浑河谷建起斡耳朵八里,是草原上最早的一批常住城市之一。一个游牧政权开始筑城,说明它要管税、管仓库、管使节了——城是治理方式变了的结果,不是原因。',
 'The Uyghurs built Ordu-Baliq in the Orkhon valley, among the first permanent cities on the steppe. When a nomad power starts building a town it is because it now has taxes to collect, stores to keep and envoys to receive — the town is the consequence of a change in how it governs, not the cause.'],
'乌兰巴托|蒙古帝国': ['成吉思汗起家的地方就在这一带的河谷。今天乌兰巴托所在的土拉河边,当时是各部夏季驻牧的草场;帝国的都城后来定在西边的哈拉和林,而不是这里——乌兰巴托要再等四百多年才出现。',
 'Genghis Khan rose in these valleys. The stretch of the Tuul where Ulaanbaatar now stands was summer pasture for the tribes; the empire\'s capital was fixed further west at Karakorum, not here — Ulaanbaatar would not exist for another four centuries.'],
'乌兰巴托|元': ['元朝把都城设在大都(今北京),漠北改设岭北行省,治所在哈拉和林。这片草原从帝国的心脏变成了帝国的北边——统治者搬去了他们征服的地方,这是草原帝国反复出现的结局。',
 'The Yuan put their capital at Dadu, today\'s Beijing, and governed the northern steppe as a province administered from Karakorum. This grassland went from being the heart of the empire to being its northern edge — the rulers moved to the country they had conquered, which is how steppe empires usually end up.'],
'哈拉和林|匈奴': ['鄂尔浑河谷从匈奴时代起就是草原政权的中心地带。这里有山有河、水草丰美,又正好卡在漠北通往西域与中原的路口;此后一千多年,匈奴、柔然、突厥、回鹘、蒙古先后把自己的中心放在这一小片河谷里。',
 'The Orkhon valley was the heartland of steppe powers from Xiongnu times on. It has hills and rivers and good grazing, and it sits at the junction of the roads from the northern steppe to the western regions and to China. For more than a thousand years afterwards the Xiongnu, Rouran, Turks, Uyghurs and Mongols each put their centre in this one small valley.'],
'哈拉和林|柔然': ['柔然的王庭也在这一带。草原上的政权换得很快,中心的位置却很稳定——不是因为传统,是因为地理:能同时养住牲畜、控住商路、又便于向四面出兵的地方,整个蒙古高原上并不多。',
 'The Rouran court was here too. Powers changed fast on the steppe while the location of the centre hardly moved — not out of tradition but out of geography: places that can feed the herds, command the trade roads and let you strike in every direction are not common on the Mongolian plateau.'],
'哈拉和林|突厥汗国': ['突厥人把这一带的于都斤山看作圣地。732 与 735 年立起的阙特勤碑与毗伽可汗碑就在离哈拉和林不远处,碑上突厥文那一面反复告诫族人别搬到汉地去住、别贪图丝绸与金银——一个帝国用自己的文字,留下的第一句话是提防。',
 'The Turks held the Otuken massif in this district sacred. The stelae of Kul Tigin and Bilge Qaghan, raised in 732 and 735, stand not far from Karakorum, and the Turkic face of them warns the people again and again not to go and live among the Chinese, not to be tempted by silk and gold — the first thing an empire wrote in its own script was a warning.'],
'哈拉和林|回鹘': ['回鹘在这条河谷的下游建起斡耳朵八里,城中有城墙、宫殿、佛寺与摩尼教寺。840 年黠戛斯人攻破此城;四百年后蒙古人筑哈拉和林,就在它上游二十多公里的地方——同一条河谷,换了一批人,又立起一座都城。',
 'The Uyghurs built Ordu-Baliq downstream in this same valley, with walls, palaces, Buddhist temples and Manichaean ones. The Kyrgyz stormed it in 840; four centuries later the Mongols raised Karakorum a little over twenty kilometres upstream — the same valley, a different people, another capital.'],
'哈拉和林|元': ['忽必烈迁都大都之后,哈拉和林降为岭北行省的治所。1260 年代他与阿里不哥争位时,这座城被双方反复争夺。元亡后北元一度以它为中心,明军数次北伐把它焚毁,此后再没有重建起来。',
 'After Kublai moved his capital to Dadu, Karakorum was reduced to the seat of the northern province. It changed hands repeatedly during his struggle with Ariq Boke in the 1260s. The Northern Yuan used it as a centre for a time after the dynasty fell, and Ming expeditions burned it; it was never rebuilt.'],
'哈拉和林|清': ['清代这里只剩废墟。1585 年蒙古人在遗址旁建起额尔德尼召寺院,大量石料直接从哈拉和林的旧城取来——今天寺院外墙上那一百多座白塔下面,压着的就是那座都城的石头。',
 'By Qing times only ruins were left. In 1585 the Mongols built the monastery of Erdene Zuu beside the site, taking much of its stone straight from the old capital — the hundred-odd white stupas along the monastery wall today stand on the stones of Karakorum.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['这时的摩亨佐达罗已经废弃了一千多年,只剩长着草的土丘。大流士把印度河下游设为一个总督辖区,据希罗多德说这是波斯帝国纳税最多的一个省;而没有人知道,那片土丘底下埋着一座比波斯古老得多的城。',
 'By now Mohenjo-daro had been abandoned for over a thousand years and was nothing but grassed-over mounds. Darius made the lower Indus a satrapy which Herodotus says paid the highest tribute in the Persian empire — and nobody knew that under those mounds lay a city far older than Persia.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|孔雀王朝': ['孔雀王朝控制了印度河流域,阿育王在西北留下石柱与摩崖法敕。摩亨佐达罗的遗址就在这条路的旁边,而当时没有任何人知道它是什么——整个印度河文明被彻底遗忘了将近四千年,直到二十世纪才重新被挖出来。',
 'The Mauryas held the Indus, and Ashoka left pillars and rock edicts across the northwest. The ruins of Mohenjo-daro lay beside that road and nobody knew what they were — the whole Indus civilisation was forgotten for close to four thousand years and only came out of the ground in the twentieth century.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|贵霜帝国': ['贵霜时期,这片土丘最高处建起一座佛塔,就压在旧城的废墟上。1922 年考古队正是循着这座佛塔往下挖,才发现底下还有一座更古老、更大的城——一座塔救了一座城,因为它替后人标出了位置。',
 'In Kushan times a Buddhist stupa was raised on the highest of the mounds, sitting directly on the ruins of the old city. In 1922 archaeologists digging down beneath that stupa found an older and far larger city underneath — a shrine saved a city, because it marked the spot for whoever came later.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|莫卧儿帝国': ['莫卧儿治下,这一带是信德地区的农田与牧场。印度河每隔几十年就改一次道,把整片平原上的村落与渠道重新洗一遍——这条河的脾气,大概也是四千年前那座城最终被放弃的原因之一。',
 'Under the Mughals this was farmland and pasture in Sindh. The Indus shifts its course every few decades and rearranges the villages and channels of the whole plain — that temper is probably among the reasons the city here was given up four thousand years ago.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|英属印度': ['1922 年印度考古调查局的班纳吉在这片土丘上发掘,认出这里是一座极古老的城;前一年哈拉帕也被挖开。两处一比对,一个此前完全不知道的文明出现了——它比当时任何人猜想的都更早、也更大。',
 'In 1922 R. D. Banerji of the Archaeological Survey of India dug here and recognised a very old city; Harappa had been opened the year before. Set side by side, the two sites revealed a civilisation nobody had known existed — earlier and larger than anyone had guessed.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|印度·南亚诸国': ['摩亨佐达罗 1980 年列入世界文化遗产。它最大的威胁不是人而是盐:地下水位上升,盐随水渗进砖里,水干之后把砖撑碎。为了保护,已经挖出来的一些部分又被重新填埋了——保住一座城的办法,有时是把它再埋回去。',
 'Mohenjo-daro was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1980. Its worst enemy is not people but salt: the water table has risen, salt travels up into the brick with the water, and as it dries it splits the brick apart. Some of what has been excavated has been buried again to protect it — sometimes the way to keep a city is to put it back under the ground.'],
'拉合尔|印度河文明': ['拉合尔在印度河文明的东缘,哈拉帕遗址离它约一百五十公里。哈拉帕是这个文明最早被认出来的城,整个文明也就以它命名;不过十九世纪修铁路时,那里的古砖被大量拆去垫路基,遗址损失很大。',
 'Lahore lies on the eastern edge of the Indus civilisation, with the site of Harappa about a hundred and fifty kilometres away. Harappa was the first of its cities to be recognised and gave the whole civilisation its name — though in the nineteenth century its ancient brick was carted off in quantity to ballast a railway, and much of the site went with it.'],
'拉合尔|孔雀王朝': ['孔雀王朝控制旁遮普,拉合尔一带在它的西北。这条路上走过亚历山大的军队,也走过后来一批批从西北进来的人——旁遮普是南亚的门厅,想进印度的,先得从这里过。',
 'The Mauryas held the Punjab, with the Lahore district in their northwest. Alexander\'s army had come this way, and so did wave after wave of later arrivals from the northwest — the Punjab is South Asia\'s front hall, and anyone entering India had to come through it first.'],
'拉合尔|贵霜帝国': ['贵霜时期,旁遮普是犍陀罗艺术往东传播的边上。犍陀罗把希腊的雕刻手法用在佛像上,佛陀第一次有了人的面孔与衣褶——这套样式后来沿丝路一路传到中国、朝鲜与日本,今天在敦煌与奈良都还看得见它的影子。',
 'Under the Kushans the Punjab lay along the eastern edge of Gandharan art. Gandhara applied Greek sculptural technique to the Buddha, who for the first time was given a human face and folded robes — a manner that travelled the Silk Road to China, Korea and Japan, and can still be seen at Dunhuang and Nara.'],
'拉合尔|嚈哒·白匈奴': ['五到六世纪嚈哒人从中亚南下,旁遮普一带反复遭到劫掠,佛教寺院与犍陀罗的作坊在这一时期大量荒废。一百多年后玄奘经过这里,记下的已经是成片的废寺。',
 'The Hephthalites came down from Central Asia in the fifth and sixth centuries and the Punjab was raided again and again; Buddhist monasteries and Gandharan workshops were abandoned in numbers. When Xuanzang came through more than a century later, what he recorded was ruined monasteries by the score.'],
'拉合尔|英属印度': ['1849 年英国吞并旁遮普,拉合尔成为省会。英国人在这里办起大学与博物馆——吉卜林的父亲当过那座博物馆的馆长,他本人少年时在拉合尔的报馆做过事。1940 年穆斯林联盟在这座城通过决议,提出在南亚西北与东北另建国家,那是巴基斯坦的起点。',
 'Britain annexed the Punjab in 1849 and Lahore became the provincial capital. The British founded a university and a museum here — Kipling\'s father was curator of that museum, and Kipling himself worked on a Lahore newspaper as a young man. In 1940 the Muslim League passed a resolution in this city calling for separate states in the northwest and northeast of South Asia; that was the beginning of Pakistan.'],
'拉合尔|印度·南亚诸国': ['1947 年分治时拉合尔归了巴基斯坦。分治前后旁遮普两侧发生大规模迁徙与暴力,这座城的印度教与锡克教居民几乎全部离开,从东边过来的穆斯林难民同时涌入——一座城的人口,在几个月里换掉了一大半。',
 'At partition in 1947 Lahore went to Pakistan. Enormous migration and violence swept both sides of the Punjab: almost the whole Hindu and Sikh population of the city left, while Muslim refugees poured in from the east — most of a city\'s people were replaced within a few months.'],
'喀什|喀喇汗王朝': ['喀喇汗是最早皈依伊斯兰教的突厥王朝之一,喀什是它的重镇。十一世纪喀喇汗治下出了两部大书:玉素甫的《福乐智慧》与麻赫穆德·喀什噶里的《突厥语大词典》——后者是在巴格达编的,为了向阿拉伯人解释突厥语,今天成了研究十一世纪突厥语言与部落最重要的材料。',
 'The Karakhanids were among the first Turkic dynasties to take up Islam, and Kashgar was one of their chief cities. Two great books came out of the Karakhanid realm in the eleventh century: Yusuf\'s Kutadgu Bilig and Mahmud al-Kashgari\'s Compendium of the Turkic Dialects — the latter compiled in Baghdad to explain Turkic to Arabic speakers, and now the single most important source on the Turkic languages and peoples of that century.'],
'喀什|东察合台·叶尔羌': ['叶尔羌汗国有两座中心:都城叶尔羌(今莎车),和喀什噶尔。按规矩汗必须是成吉思汗的后代,可真正调兵征税的常常是异密,到后来是和卓——从中亚来的宗教世家。白山派与黑山派在这里斗到最后,一派请准噶尔人入境助战,请进来就没有再走。1705 年最后一位汗被废,成吉思汗的血脉在天山南北当汗当了三百五十多年,到此为止。',
 'The Yarkand Khanate had two centres: its capital at Yarkand, today\'s Shache, and Kashgar. By custom the khan had to be a descendant of Chinggis, but the men who actually raised troops and collected taxes were the emirs, and later the khojas — religious families out of Central Asia. The White Mountain and Black Mountain factions fought here to the end, until one of them invited the Dzungars in to help, and the Dzungars did not leave. The last khan was deposed in 1705, closing more than three hundred and fifty years of Chinggisid rule on both sides of the Tian Shan.'],
'布哈拉|布哈拉·希瓦·浩罕三汗国': ['布哈拉是三个汗国中最有名的一个,城中心的雅克城堡既是王宫也是监狱。1868 年布哈拉在泽拉布拉克一战败给俄军,成了俄国的保护国,名义上的埃米尔一直保留到 1920 年。',
 'Bukhara was the best known of the three khanates, and the Ark citadel at its centre served as both palace and prison. After losing to the Russians at Zerabulak in 1868, Bukhara became a Russian protectorate; a nominal emir was kept on until 1920.'],
'奇琴伊察|玛雅': ['奇琴伊察在南部古典期城邦衰落的同时崛起,是后古典期前期尤卡坦的中心,1100 年前后才让位给玛雅潘。卡斯蒂略金字塔每边九十一级,四面加上顶台一般数作三百六十五级——正好一年的天数;城边的圣井是献祭与投物的地方,井底捞出过玉器、金器与人骨。',
 'Chichen Itza rose as the southern Classic cities were declining, and was the centre of northern Yucatan in the early Postclassic until Mayapan took its place around 1100. Its main pyramid has ninety-one steps on each of four sides, which with the top platform is usually counted as three hundred and sixty-five — the days of a year; the sacred cenote beside the city received offerings, and jade, gold and human bone have been dredged from it.'],
'里约热内卢|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['1807 年拿破仑军队入侵葡萄牙,王室渡海出逃,次年抵达里约。此后十三年,这座殖民地城市是整个葡萄牙帝国的首都——欧洲国家的朝廷搬到殖民地去,历史上仅此一例。',
 'When Napoleon\'s armies invaded Portugal in 1807 the royal court sailed for Brazil, reaching Rio the next year. For the next thirteen years this colonial city was the capital of the entire Portuguese empire — the only time a European court moved to its own colony.'],
'巴黎|法兰西': ['路易十四把朝廷搬到城外的凡尔赛,巴黎反倒成了另一种中心:沙龙、咖啡馆与印刷所把新想法传开。1789 年 7 月 14 日巴士底狱被攻破,这一天后来成了法国国庆日。',
 'Louis XIV moved his court out to Versailles, and Paris became a centre of another kind: salons, coffee houses and printing shops spread new ideas. On 14 July 1789 the Bastille was stormed — the day France still keeps as its national holiday.'],
'伦敦|大英帝国·英国': ['1666 年一场大火烧掉城里大半房屋,重建时改用砖石。到十九世纪,伦敦长成了世界上最大的城市,也是全球航运与保险的结算地,一百年后才被纽约超过;而今天世界通用的时间起点,就定在城东格林尼治的那条子午线上。',
 'A fire in 1666 destroyed most of the houses inside the walls, and the city was rebuilt in brick and stone. By the nineteenth century London had grown into the largest city on earth and the place where the world\'s shipping and insurance were settled; a century later New York passed it. The line the world still counts time from runs through Greenwich, on its eastern edge.'],
'莫斯科|俄罗斯·苏联': ['1480 年莫斯科大公伊凡三世不再向金帐汗国纳贡,罗斯从此不再是附庸。1712 年彼得一世把都城迁到圣彼得堡,两百年后又搬了回来——1918 年苏俄迁都莫斯科,克里姆林宫再次成为权力中心。',
 'In 1480 Grand Prince Ivan III stopped paying tribute to the Golden Horde, and Rus was a vassal no longer. Peter I moved the capital to St Petersburg in 1712; two centuries later it came back — Soviet Russia returned the capital to Moscow in 1918, and the Kremlin was once again the seat of power.'],
'柏林|德意志': ['1871 年德意志在凡尔赛宫宣布统一,柏林成了新帝国的首都,四十年间人口翻了一倍多。1961 年一道墙把这座城劈成两半,1989 年 11 月 9 日夜里墙被推开,不到一年德国就重新统一了。',
 'The German Empire was proclaimed at Versailles in 1871 and Berlin became its capital, more than doubling in population over the next forty years. In 1961 a wall cut the city in two; on the night of 9 November 1989 it was opened, and Germany was reunified less than a year later.'],
'维也纳|奥地利·哈布斯堡': ['1683 年奥斯曼大军第二次围攻维也纳,波兰与帝国的联军赶到解围、由波兰国王索别斯基统率,奥斯曼在中欧的扩张就此止步。此后这座城成了哈布斯堡的音乐之都,海顿、莫扎特、贝多芬都在这里住过。',
 'In 1683 an Ottoman army besieged Vienna for the second time; a combined Polish and imperial relief force under King Sobieski of Poland arrived and broke the siege, and Ottoman expansion into central Europe stopped there. The city became the Habsburgs\' capital of music — Haydn, Mozart and Beethoven all lived here.'],
'纽约|美国': ['这里本是荷兰人的新阿姆斯特丹,1664 年被英国人拿下改名纽约。十九世纪末起,坐统舱来的移民先在港口外的埃利斯岛登记再进城,前后约一千二百万人由此入境;自由女神像 1886 年立在港口,是法国送的礼物。',
 'This was Dutch New Amsterdam until the English took it in 1664 and renamed it New York. From the late nineteenth century immigrants travelling steerage were processed on Ellis Island in the harbour before entering the city — some twelve million passed through — and the Statue of Liberty, a gift from France, was raised at the harbour mouth in 1886.'],
'东京|日本': ['江户在德川幕府治下长到百万人口,是当时世界上最大的城市之一。1868 年它改称东京,明治天皇次年迁来定居;1923 年关东大地震与 1945 年的空袭两次烧掉大半座城,又两次重建起来。',
 'Under the Tokugawa shoguns Edo grew to a million people, among the largest cities in the world. In 1868 it was renamed Tokyo, and the emperor settled here the following year; the 1923 Kanto earthquake and the air raids of 1945 each burned out much of it, and each time it was rebuilt.'],
'孟买|英属印度': ['孟买本是葡萄牙人的地盘,1661 年作为公主的嫁妆转给英国王室,七年后以每年十英镑租给东印度公司。美国内战断了棉花供应,孟买靠棉花生意暴富,城市面貌就是那几十年里定下来的。',
 'Bombay was Portuguese until 1661, when it came to the English crown as part of a royal dowry; seven years later it was leased to the East India Company for ten pounds a year. When the American Civil War cut off cotton supplies Bombay boomed on the trade, and the city took the shape it still largely has.'],
'德黑兰|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['德黑兰以南十几公里的雷伊(古称拉伽)是米底与波斯时代的名城,大流士的贝希斯敦铭文里就提到过它。德黑兰本身那时只是山脚下的一个村子——它要成为首都,还得再等两千三百年。',
 'Some fifteen kilometres south of Tehran lay Rhagae, a city of note in Median and Persian times and named in Darius\'s Behistun inscription. Tehran itself was then a village at the foot of the mountains — twenty-three centuries away from being anyone\'s capital.'],
'德黑兰|希腊化王朝': ['塞琉古时期雷伊被重建,改名「欧罗巴」,后来安息人又把它叫作「阿尔萨基亚」。希腊化的新名字在伊朗高原上换来换去,当地人照旧用老名字叫它——地名往往比政权活得久。',
 'Under the Seleucids Rhagae was rebuilt and renamed Europos, and the Parthians later called it Arsacia. Hellenistic names came and went across the Iranian plateau while the locals went on using the old one — place names tend to outlive the governments that rename them.'],
'德黑兰|帕提亚·萨珊': ['帕提亚时期雷伊是高原上的重要城市之一;萨珊时期它是米底地区的中心,城中有拜火教的火庙。这一带正压在连接两河流域与呼罗珊的大路上,后来丝路的北线也走这里。',
 'Rhagae was one of the plateau\'s important cities under the Parthians, and under the Sasanians the centre of the Median region, with Zoroastrian fire temples in it. It sat squarely on the road linking Mesopotamia to Khorasan, the road the northern branch of the Silk Road would later use.'],
'德黑兰|阿拉伯哈里发': ['阿拉伯人在 640 年代取得雷伊。此后几百年它是伊朗高原北部最大的城市之一,也出学者——医学家拉齐就是雷伊人,他写的天花与麻疹专论把这两种病分了开来,是这方面最早的著作之一。',
 'The Arabs took Rhagae in the 640s. For centuries afterwards it was among the largest cities of the northern plateau, and it produced scholars — the physician al-Razi was born there, and his treatise separating smallpox from measles was among the first to tell the two diseases apart.'],
'德黑兰|塞尔柱突厥': ['塞尔柱一度以雷伊作为都城之一,城市规模在这一时期很大。德黑兰仍旧是它旁边的一个村子,以出产好石榴出名;一部十二世纪初的书里已经夸过这里的石榴。两个地方的位置后来完全对调,不过那要再等五百多年。',
 'The Seljuks used Rhagae as one of their capitals and the city was large in these years. Tehran was still the village next door, known for good pomegranates — a book of the early twelfth century already praises them. The two places would eventually swap positions altogether, though that took more than five hundred years.'],
'德黑兰|蒙古帝国': ['1220 年蒙古军队攻破雷伊,城被彻底毁掉,居民大批被杀,此后再没恢复。旁边的德黑兰因为只是个村子、不值得攻打,反而活了下来。十三世纪的地理学家雅古特记下:雷伊人躲进了地下的聚落。一座城的机会,有时来自它当时不重要。',
 'The Mongols stormed Rhagae in 1220, destroyed it and killed great numbers of its people; it never recovered. Tehran next door was only a village and not worth attacking, so it survived. The geographer Yaqut, writing in the thirteenth century, records that the people of Rhagae took shelter in underground settlements. A city\'s chance sometimes comes from having been unimportant.'],
'德黑兰|伊尔汗国': ['伊尔汗国把伊朗的重心放在西北的大不里士与苏丹尼耶,德黑兰一带无足轻重。雷伊的废墟成了周边取石料的地方,德黑兰就在这堆废墟旁边慢慢长大——它最初的建材,有一部分是上一座城的。',
 'The Ilkhanate put Iran\'s weight in the northwest, at Tabriz and Sultaniyya, and the Tehran district counted for little. The ruins of Rhagae became a quarry for the neighbourhood, and Tehran grew up beside them — some of its first building material came out of the city before it.'],
'德黑兰|帖木儿帝国': ['1404 年西班牙使节克拉维霍出使帖木儿,路过德黑兰,把它记成一座没有城墙的村镇。一个不设城墙的地方能在这条路上活下来,靠的不是防御,是不值得攻打。',
 'In 1404 the Spanish envoy Clavijo passed through Tehran on his way to Timur and set it down as a town without walls. A place with no walls survived on this road not by defending itself but by not being worth attacking.'],
'德黑兰|萨法维·波斯': ['萨法维的塔赫马斯普一世给德黑兰加筑了城墙、扩建了集市,它第一次有了城的样子(集市本身更早就有,雅古特十三世纪就记过这里的市场)。不过萨法维的都城先在大不里士、后在加兹温与伊斯法罕,德黑兰始终只是路上的一站——它当上首都要等到 1786 年,由恺加王朝定下。',
 'Tahmasp I of the Safavids walled Tehran and enlarged its bazaar, and it looked like a town for the first time — the bazaar itself was older, Yaqut having noted a market here in the thirteenth century. But the Safavid capital sat at Tabriz, then Qazvin, then Isfahan, and Tehran remained a stop on the road — it became the capital only in 1786, under the Qajars.'],
'伊斯法罕|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['伊斯法罕在伊朗高原中部的绿洲上,扎因代河从旁边流过。阿契美尼德时期这一带叫「加巴埃」,后来才演化成「盖伊」;它是波斯本土通往东方的节点。「伊斯法罕」这个名字来自波斯语的「军队」——它长期是集结军队的地方,名字就这么留下了。',
 'Isfahan stands on an oasis in the middle of the Iranian plateau with the Zayandeh river running past. In Achaemenid times the district was called Gabae, which later became Gay; it was a node on the road east out of the Persian homeland. The name Isfahan comes from the Persian word for army — this was long a place where armies assembled, and the name stuck.'],
'伊斯法罕|希腊化王朝': ['亚历山大东征之后,伊朗高原上的希腊化王国在这里驻过兵。这一段留下的实物不多,但希腊的度量、钱币与城市规划在伊朗留了很久:安息人的钱币上,希腊文一印就是好几百年。',
 'After Alexander\'s campaigns the Hellenistic kingdoms of the plateau garrisoned this place. Little of that survives here in stone, but Greek weights, coinage and town planning stayed in Iran a long while: Parthian coins carried Greek lettering for centuries.'],
'伊斯法罕|帕提亚·萨珊': ['萨珊时期伊斯法罕是一个行省的首府,城中有相当规模的犹太社区——按一种传统说法,这个社区可以上溯到巴比伦之囚以后的迁徙,不过很难证实。城郊山上的火庙遗址至今还在。',
 'Under the Sasanians Isfahan was a provincial capital with a sizeable Jewish community — by one traditional account descended from migrations after the Babylonian exile, though that is hard to confirm. The ruins of a fire temple still stand on the hill outside town.'],
'伊斯法罕|阿拉伯哈里发': ['阿拉伯人来后,伊斯法罕实际上是两座挨着的城:一座是犹太人聚居的「犹太城」,一座是原来的盖伊,后来才合成一座。这一带是高原上的粮食产区,谁想在这里立足,都得先管住扎因代河的水。',
 'After the Arab conquest Isfahan was really two towns side by side — Jayy, the old settlement, and Yahudiyya, the Jewish quarter — which only later grew together. This was grain country on the plateau, and anyone who wanted to hold it had first to control the water of the Zayandeh.'],
'伊斯法罕|塞尔柱突厥': ['1050 年代图格里勒取得伊斯法罕并定为都城,这是它第一次做大帝国的首都。城中的聚礼清真寺在塞尔柱一朝陆续扩建,1080 年代加的那两座砖砌穹顶是这一朝建筑的代表作;宰相尼扎姆·穆勒克在这里主政,他推行的经学院制度后来影响了整个伊斯兰世界。',
 'Tughril took Isfahan in the 1050s and made it his capital — its first turn as the seat of a great empire. The Friday mosque was enlarged through the Seljuk period, and the two brick domes added in the 1080s are among the finest work of that dynasty; the vizier Nizam al-Mulk governed from here, and the college system he built up went on to shape the whole Islamic world.'],
'伊斯法罕|蒙古帝国': ['蒙古军队在 1220 到 1240 年代之间几次攻掠伊斯法罕,1240 年代取得此城。它没有像雷伊、内沙布尔那样被夷平,城市延续了下来——三百多年后它还能再次成为首都,这一点大概不是偶然。哪些城被毁、哪些城被留,常常决定了后面几百年的格局。',
 'Mongol forces raided Isfahan several times between the 1220s and the 1240s and took it in the 1240s. It was not levelled as Rhagae and Nishapur were, and the city carried on — that it could become a capital again three centuries later was probably not a coincidence. Which cities were destroyed and which were spared often set the shape of the next several hundred years.'],
'伊斯法罕|伊尔汗国': ['伊尔汗国时期伊斯法罕是伊朗中部的重镇。城中的聚礼清真寺又添了新的部分——那座清真寺从八世纪一直修到近代,每个朝代各加各的,今天走进去,等于走进一部伊朗建筑史。',
 'Isfahan was a principal city of central Iran under the Ilkhanate, and more was added to its Friday mosque. That building was worked on from the eighth century into modern times, each dynasty adding its own part — walking into it today is walking through a history of Iranian architecture.'],
'伊斯法罕|帖木儿帝国': ['1387 年帖木儿取得伊斯法罕。城中起事杀了他的收税官,他随即下令屠城,据同时代的记载,尸首的头被堆成塔立在城外。这是他惯用的立威手段,也是他的名声在中亚几百年都没洗掉的原因。',
 'Timur took Isfahan in 1387. The city rose and killed his tax collectors, whereupon he ordered a general massacre, and contemporary accounts describe towers built of the heads outside the walls. It was his standard way of making an example, and the reason his name stayed what it is in Central Asia for centuries.'],
'伊斯法罕|现代中东': ['二十世纪伊斯法罕成为伊朗的工业城市之一,钢铁厂与炼油厂建在城外。它同时是国内旅游与手工艺的中心——铜器、地毯与细密画的作坊还在老集市里。城中那片十七世纪的广场与建筑群,1979 年列入世界文化遗产名录。',
 'In the twentieth century Isfahan became one of Iran\'s industrial cities, with steelworks and refineries outside it. It is at the same time the centre of domestic tourism and of craft — the coppersmiths, carpet weavers and miniature painters still work in the old bazaar. Its seventeenth-century square and the buildings around it were inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1979.'],
'德黑兰|现代中东': ['1979 年伊朗革命推翻巴列维王朝,建立起教士主导的体制——这是中东最近一次影响全局的转折,同一年还发生了苏联出兵阿富汗与麦加大清真寺被占。此后区域格局沿着教派与阵营重新划线。',
 'The 1979 revolution overthrew the Pahlavi monarchy and established clerical rule — the last turning point to reshape the whole region, and one of three things that happened that same year, along with the Soviet invasion of Afghanistan and the seizure of the Grand Mosque in Mecca. The region has been redrawn along sectarian and bloc lines ever since.'],
'塔什干|喀喇汗王朝': ['塔什干的古名是「石国」,是中亚商路上的一处绿洲。「塔什干」这个名字在喀喇汗时期前后开始通行,在突厥语里意思就是「石头城」——比鲁尼与喀什噶里都写到过这个名字。',
 'Tashkent\'s older name meant the stone country, and it was an oasis on the Central Asian trade roads. The name Tashkent came into general use around the Qarakhanid period; in Turkic it means stone city, and both al-Biruni and Kashgari wrote about it.'],
'塔什干|花剌子模': ['花剌子模把塔什干一带纳入版图。这片绿洲靠奇尔奇克河的水,是北面草原通往河中的门口;游牧的部落与种地的农人在这里交易,一座城同时面对两种生活方式——中亚的城大多是这么长起来的。',
 'Khwarazm brought the Tashkent oasis into its territory. It lives on the water of the Chirchiq and stands at the gateway from the northern steppe into Transoxiana; herders and farmers traded here, and the city faced two ways of life at once — which is how most Central Asian cities grew.'],
'塔什干|蒙古帝国': ['1220 年前后蒙古军队取得塔什干一带。与撒马尔罕、布哈拉相比,这里受到的破坏轻得多;此后它属察合台汗国,长期在游牧贵族与绿洲城市之间摇摆——察合台汗国后来正是沿着这条线裂成两半的。',
 'Mongol forces took the Tashkent district around 1220. It suffered far less than Samarkand or Bukhara, and afterwards belonged to the Chagatai khanate, pulled for a long time between nomadic nobles and settled oasis towns — the line along which that khanate eventually split in two.'],
'塔什干|布哈拉·希瓦·浩罕三汗国': ['十八世纪末塔什干一度自立,后来归了浩罕汗国。它卡在浩罕与布哈拉之间,又是草原商路的终点,几个汗国为它反复动兵——一座城太好用,反而不得安宁。',
 'Tashkent governed itself for a time at the end of the eighteenth century and then passed to the khanate of Kokand. Wedged between Kokand and Bukhara and sitting at the end of the steppe trade roads, it was fought over repeatedly — a city too useful to be left in peace.'],
'塔什干|现代中亚': ['1966 年一场地震把塔什干市中心几乎夷平,苏联各加盟共和国派工程队来重建,城市因此换了一副苏式面貌。1991 年后它成为乌兹别克斯坦的首都,也是中亚人口最多的城市。',
 'An earthquake in 1966 flattened most of central Tashkent, and building teams came from across the Soviet republics to rebuild it, which is why the city wears a Soviet face today. Since 1991 it has been the capital of Uzbekistan and the most populous city in Central Asia.'],
'阿拉木图|喀喇汗王朝': ['阿拉木图在天山北麓的七河地区,喀喇汗时期这一带是丝路北线上的一段。中亚的突厥人在这个王朝下大批改信伊斯兰教,而更北的草原上仍是萨满信仰与佛教并存——宗教的边界在这一带来回移动了几百年。',
 'Almaty lies in the Seven Rivers country on the northern flank of the Tien Shan, a stretch of the northern Silk Road in Qarakhanid times. Turkic peoples of Central Asia converted to Islam in numbers under that dynasty, while further north on the steppe shamanic practice and Buddhism went on side by side — the religious boundary moved back and forth across this district for centuries.'],
'阿拉木图|西辽·哈剌契丹': ['耶律大石西迁后在七河一带立国,都城虎思斡耳朵离阿拉木图不算远。西辽是一个佛教政权统治着以穆斯林为主的人口,不强制改宗,也不设针对宗教的重税——这在当时的中亚很少见。',
 'After Yelu Dashi led his people west he founded a state in the Seven Rivers country, with his capital not far from Almaty. Qara Khitai was a Buddhist dynasty ruling a largely Muslim population, imposing neither conversion nor a religious surtax — a rarity in the Central Asia of that day.'],
'阿拉木图|蒙古帝国': ['蒙古人取得七河之后,这一带成了察合台汗国的牧场。原有的绿洲城镇与灌溉农业大片衰退,土地重新变回草场——蒙古征服在中亚留下的最长远影响之一,是把一些已经定居的地方变回了游牧区。',
 'Once the Mongols held the Seven Rivers, the district became pasture for the Chagatai khanate. The oasis towns and irrigated fields fell away and the land went back to grass — one of the longest-lasting effects of the Mongol conquest in Central Asia was turning settled country back into herding country.'],
'阿拉木图|俄国治下中亚': ['1854 年俄国在这里建起维尔内堡,那是今天阿拉木图的起点。1887 与 1911 年两次大地震把城震毁,重建时改用木结构;城中那座全木造的大教堂 1907 年建成,在 1911 年的地震里几乎没有受损。',
 'Russia built the fort of Verny here in 1854, and that is where Almaty begins. Earthquakes in 1887 and 1911 destroyed the town, which was rebuilt in timber; the all-wooden cathedral finished in 1907 came through the 1911 shock almost untouched.'],
'阿拉木图|现代中亚': ['1929 年阿拉木图成为哈萨克的首都,1997 年首都迁往北方。它至今是哈萨克斯坦最大的城市与经济中心。城名在哈萨克语里意思近于「苹果之地」——天山北麓正是今天所有栽培苹果的野生祖先的原产地。',
 'Almaty became the Kazakh capital in 1929 and lost that role to a northern city in 1997. It remains the largest city and the economic centre of Kazakhstan. Its name means something like the place of apples — and the northern slopes of the Tien Shan are where the wild ancestor of every cultivated apple comes from.'],
'喀布尔|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['喀布尔一带属波斯东端的山地边区。这里有几条山口通往印度河平原,谁控制了山口,谁就决定往南的路通不通——喀布尔两千多年的分量,基本都来自这一点。',
 'The Kabul district was mountain frontier at the eastern end of the Persian empire. Several passes lead from here down to the Indus plain, and whoever holds the passes decides whether the road south is open — nearly all of Kabul\'s importance over two thousand years comes from that one fact.'],
'喀布尔|贵霜帝国': ['贵霜从这一带起家,后来把重心南移到白沙瓦与马图拉。喀布尔河谷是犍陀罗艺术的核心地带之一;巴米扬的大佛虽然晚一些,也在同一条山路上——佛教正是从这里翻过山口,传向东方。',
 'The Kushans rose in this country before shifting their weight south to Peshawar and Mathura. The Kabul valley was one of the heartlands of Gandharan art, and the great Buddhas of Bamiyan, though later, stand on the same mountain road — it was here that Buddhism crossed the passes and went east.'],
'喀布尔|嚈哒·白匈奴': ['五到六世纪嚈哒人控制这一带,佛教寺院与商路都受到冲击。此后喀布尔一带由一支被称作「喀布尔沙希」的王朝统治了几百年,长期挡住从西边来的军队——这也是这一带改信伊斯兰教比波斯晚得多的原因之一。',
 'The Hephthalites held this country in the fifth and sixth centuries and both the monasteries and the trade roads suffered. Afterwards a line known as the Kabul Shahi ruled here for centuries and held off the armies coming from the west — part of the reason this district turned to Islam so much later than Persia did.'],
'喀布尔|阿拉伯哈里发': ['阿拉伯军队七世纪就打到过这一带,却始终没能站稳:山地易守,喀布尔沙希一次次把他们逼退。真正让这里改信伊斯兰教的不是某一场征服,而是几百年的商路往来与逐步渗透。',
 'Arab armies reached this country as early as the seventh century and never managed to hold it: the mountains favour the defender, and the Kabul Shahi pushed them back time and again. What eventually made the district Muslim was not any one conquest but centuries of trade and gradual settlement.'],
'喀布尔|萨曼王朝': ['萨曼王朝的势力伸到这一带。后来从萨曼军中出身的突厥将领在南边的加兹尼自立,建起加兹尼王朝,并以那里为基地一再南下印度。喀布尔从此成了通往印度那条路上最要紧的一站。',
 'Samanid power reached this district. Turkic commanders who had risen in Samanid service later set up on their own at Ghazni to the south and raided down into India from there again and again. Kabul became the key station on the road to India, and stayed one.'],
'特拉布宗|波斯(阿契美尼德)': ['特拉布宗是希腊人在黑海南岸建的殖民城市。前 400 年前后,色诺芬带着上万名希腊雇佣兵从波斯腹地一路退到这一带,登上山顶看见大海,全军高喊「海啊!海啊!」——那声呼喊后来成了西方文学里最有名的句子之一。',
 'Trebizond was a Greek colony on the southern shore of the Black Sea. Around 400 BC Xenophon brought ten thousand Greek mercenaries back from deep inside Persia to this coast; when they climbed a ridge and saw the water, the whole column shouted \'The sea! The sea!\' — one of the best-known lines in Western literature ever since.'],
'特拉布宗|罗马帝国': ['罗马把特拉比松设为黑海南岸的军港与商港,哈德良在这里修了人工港。从内亚来的商队在这里下海,货物再运往君士坦丁堡——一条陆路的终点,就是一条海路的起点。',
 'Rome made Trapezus a naval and trading port on the southern Black Sea, and Hadrian built an artificial harbour here. Caravans from inner Asia took to the water at this point and their goods went on to Constantinople — the end of one road being the start of another.'],
'特拉布宗|塞尔柱突厥': ['塞尔柱进入安纳托利亚之后,特拉布宗一带仍在拜占庭手中,靠山险与海路撑住。这一时期的黑海南岸成了两个世界的接缝:内陆已经突厥化、伊斯兰化,沿海一线还讲希腊语、信基督教。',
 'After the Seljuks came into Anatolia, the Trebizond district stayed Byzantine, held by its mountains and its sea lanes. The southern Black Sea coast became the seam between two worlds in these years: the interior Turkic and Muslim, the shore still Greek-speaking and Christian.'],
'特拉布宗|奥斯曼帝国': ['1461 年穆罕默德二世攻下特拉布宗,拜占庭延续下来的最后一块政权就此结束——比君士坦丁堡的陷落晚了八年。此后它是奥斯曼东北边的省城,也是通往波斯的商路口岸。',
 'Mehmed II took Trebizond in 1461, ending the last surviving Byzantine state — eight years after Constantinople itself fell. It became an Ottoman provincial town in the northeast and the port for the trade road into Persia.'],
'特拉布宗|现代中东': ['十九世纪的特拉布宗是波斯与欧洲之间转运贸易的要港,一度相当繁荣。1869 年苏伊士运河通航后,货物改走海路,这条陆路迅速衰落——一座城的兴衰,有时是由几千公里外的一条运河决定的。',
 'In the nineteenth century Trabzon was a major transit port between Persia and Europe and prospered on it. After the Suez Canal opened in 1869 the goods went by sea instead and the overland route fell away fast — a city\'s fortunes settled by a canal thousands of kilometres off.'],
'突尼斯|罗马共和国': ['前 146 年迦太基城被攻破焚毁,罗马把它的土地设为阿非利加行省。「罗马人在废墟上撒盐,让这里长不出东西」这个说法流传很广,但古代史料里并没有这样的记载——它是十九世纪以后才出现的。',
 'Carthage was stormed and burned in 146 BC and Rome made its land the province of Africa. The story that the Romans sowed the ruins with salt so that nothing would grow is widely repeated, but no ancient source says it — the tale only appears from the nineteenth century on.'],
'突尼斯|罗马帝国': ['罗马在迦太基旧址上重建了一座新城,它一度是帝国西部数一数二的大城。这一带的橄榄油与谷物大量运往罗马——北非在罗马时代是粮仓,和今天的干旱景象并不一样。',
 'Rome rebuilt a new city on the site of Carthage, and it became one of the largest in the western empire. Olive oil and grain went from this country to Rome in quantity — North Africa was a granary in Roman times, which is not how it looks today.'],
'突尼斯|拜占庭': ['533 年贝利撒留从汪达尔人手中夺回北非,这一带重归拜占庭。但这次统治只维持了一个半世纪多:698 年阿拉伯军队攻陷迦太基,居民迁往附近的突尼斯城——旧城就此终结,新城取而代之。',
 'Belisarius took North Africa back from the Vandals in 533 and the district returned to Byzantium. That rule lasted only a century and a half: in 698 an Arab army stormed Carthage and its people moved to nearby Tunis — the old city ended and the new one took its place.'],
'突尼斯|奥斯曼帝国': ['十六世纪突尼斯在西班牙与奥斯曼之间几度易手,1574 年最终归奥斯曼。此后它以「突尼斯摄政」的名义高度自治,靠地中海上的私掠与贸易维生——名义上听伊斯坦布尔的,实际上自己做主。',
 'Tunis changed hands several times between Spain and the Ottomans in the sixteenth century and went finally to the Ottomans in 1574. It was then largely self-governing as the Regency of Tunis, living on Mediterranean privateering and trade — nominally answering to Istanbul, in practice deciding for itself.'],
'突尼斯|现代中东': ['1881 年突尼斯成为法国保护国,1956 年独立。2010 年底一场抗议从内陆的小城开始,几周之内蔓延全国,次年初总统离职;此后同类的变动扩散到多个阿拉伯国家——它的起点不在首都,而在一座地图上很难找到的小城。',
 'Tunisia became a French protectorate in 1881 and independent in 1956. At the end of 2010 a protest began in a small inland town, spread across the country within weeks, and the president left early the next year; comparable upheavals then spread through several Arab countries — and it had started not in the capital but in a town most maps barely show.'],
'塔什干|俄国治下中亚': ['1865 年俄军攻占塔什干,此后它成了俄属突厥斯坦的总督驻地。铁路修通后,中亚大片土地改种棉花运往俄国的纺织厂——这套单一作物的格局一直延续到苏联时期;后来苏联把两条大河的水大规模引去灌溉棉田,咸海从 1960 年代起急剧萎缩。',
 'Russian troops took Tashkent in 1865, and it became the seat of the Governor-General of Russian Turkestan. Once the railway arrived, great stretches of Central Asia were turned over to cotton for Russian mills — a monoculture that lasted through the Soviet period; later the Soviets diverted the two great rivers on a huge scale to irrigate cotton, and from 1960 onward the Aral Sea shrank fast.'],
'哈拉和林|蒙古帝国': ['1235 年窝阔台在这里筑城,作为帝国的都城。法国国王派来的鲁不鲁乞见过城中一棵银树做的喷泉,四条管子分别流出马奶酒、蜜酒、米酒与葡萄酒。忽必烈迁都大都后这里迅速衰落,石料后来被拆去建额尔德尼召寺。',
 'Ogedei walled the city in 1235 as the empire\'s capital. William of Rubruck, sent by the king of France, saw a fountain here in the form of a silver tree with four pipes pouring mare\'s milk, mead, rice wine and grape wine. After Kublai moved the capital to Dadu it declined fast, and its stone was later carted off to build the Erdene Zuu monastery.'],
'亚的斯亚贝巴|埃塞俄比亚帝国': ['1886 年孟尼利克(当时还是绍阿国王)与王后泰图在这里建城,取名「新花」;1889 年他称帝后,这里成了全国的首都。十年后的 1896 年,埃塞俄比亚在阿杜瓦击败入侵的意大利军队——那个年代里,非洲国家打赢欧洲列强的战例极少。',
 'Menelik — then still king of Shewa — and Queen Taytu founded the town here in 1886 and named it "new flower"; after he was crowned emperor in 1889 it became the capital of the whole country. Ten years later, in 1896, Ethiopia defeated an invading Italian army at Adwa — one of very few occasions in that era when an African state beat a European power.'],
'开普敦|大英帝国·英国': ['荷兰东印度公司 1652 年在这里设补给站,英国在拿破仑战争期间接手,1814 年正式获得。开普敦此后是欧洲往返印度最主要的补给中转站,直到 1869 年苏伊士运河通航才失去这个位置。',
 'The Dutch East India Company set up a supply station here in 1652; Britain took it during the Napoleonic wars and gained it formally in 1814. Cape Town was then the main way-station between Europe and India, until the Suez Canal opened in 1869 and took that role away.'],
'哈瓦那|西葡殖民美洲': ['哈瓦那是西班牙珍宝船队的集合地:各地的白银先运到这里编队,再一起横渡大西洋,以防海盗。城口的莫罗炮台就是为此而建;1762 年英国人还是攻下了这座城,占了将近一年,次年拿它跟西班牙换了佛罗里达。',
 'Havana was where Spain\'s treasure fleets assembled: silver from across the Americas was gathered here and convoyed across the Atlantic together, out of reach of raiders. The Morro fortress at the harbour mouth was built for that. The British took the city anyway in 1762, held it for the better part of a year, and the next year traded it back to Spain for Florida.'],
'成都|北宋': ['北宋时成都的商人发行「交子」——一般认为是世上最早的纸币,起因是四川用铁钱,重而不便——买一匹布要背上百斤钱。官府后来接管发行,设了专门的交子务。',
 'Merchants in Song-era Chengdu issued jiaozi, generally reckoned the earliest paper money in the world. It began because Sichuan used iron coins so heavy that buying a bolt of cloth meant carrying a hundred catties of them. The government later took over the issue and set up an office for it.'],
'仰光|蒲甘': ['蒲甘王朝往南推到伊洛瓦底江口,仰光一带的孟人地区归入版图。城中的大金寺相传更早就在,历代不断加高贴金,今天塔身外覆的金箔与宝顶上的钻石,是几百年里一层层捐上去的。',
 'The Pagan kingdom pushed south to the mouth of the Irrawaddy, bringing the Mon country around Yangon under its rule. The Shwedagon pagoda is held to be older still; raised and regilded again and again, the gold on it and the jewels at its tip were donated layer upon layer over centuries.'],
'仰光|阿瓦·勃固': ['1453 年信修浮成为勃固的女王,这在东南亚很少见。她捐出与自己体重相等的黄金,用来给大金塔贴金箔;塔今天的高度,来自这一时期的几次加高。她没有把王位传给自己的儿孙,而是挑了一位僧侣出身的人——达摩悉提,后来还把女儿嫁给了他。他铸过一口巨大的铜钟,1608 年葡萄牙人把它抢走、运过江的时候钟沉了下去;四百年里找过很多次,至今没有找到。',
 'In 1453 Shin Sawbu became queen of Pegu, a rare thing in Southeast Asia. She gave her own weight in gold for the gilding of the Shwedagon, whose present height dates from the raisings of this period. She passed the throne not to a child or grandchild but to a former monk, Dhammazedi, and later married her daughter to him. He cast an enormous bronze bell; in 1608 the Portuguese carried it off and it went to the bottom while being ferried across the river. Four centuries of searching have not found it.'],
'马尼拉|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1571 年西班牙人在马尼拉建城,此后两百多年,大帆船每年往返阿卡普尔科一次:美洲的白银运来,中国的丝绸瓷器运走。城里的涧内住着数以万计的华人商匠,是这条航线的另一半。',
 'The Spanish founded Manila in 1571, and for the next two and a half centuries a galleon crossed to Acapulco and back once a year: American silver out one way, Chinese silk and porcelain the other. Tens of thousands of Chinese merchants and craftsmen lived in the Parian quarter — the other half of that trade.'],
'加尔各答|孔雀王朝': ['加尔各答所在的恒河三角洲下游,在孔雀王朝时属于「般伽」一带。这片土地是恒河与布拉马普特拉河一起冲出来的,每年泛滥、每年重新铺一层肥土——它养得起极多的人,也从来不是一个安稳的地方。',
 'The lower Ganges delta, where Calcutta stands, was the country the Mauryas knew as Vanga. The land is what the Ganges and the Brahmaputra have laid down together, flooding every year and spreading fresh silt every year — it can feed a great many people and has never been a settled place.'],
'加尔各答|波罗王朝': ['波罗王朝以孟加拉为核心,这一带正是它的腹地。波罗护持佛教四百来年,而它的邻居与继承者多信印度教,孟加拉后来又有大批人改信伊斯兰教——这片三角洲在一千年里换过三种主要信仰。',
 'The Palas had their core in Bengal and this delta was their heartland. They patronised Buddhism for some four centuries while their neighbours and successors were mostly Hindu, and large numbers in Bengal later became Muslim — three principal faiths across a thousand years on one river delta.'],
'加尔各答|莫卧儿帝国': ['莫卧儿治下的孟加拉是帝国最富的一个省,棉布与生丝销往世界各地。加尔各答这个位置当时只有几个村子;1690 年东印度公司的一名代理人在这里设了商站,选中它是因为河道够深、又有沼泽在旁边挡着。',
 'Bengal was the richest province of the Mughal empire, its cottons and raw silk sold across the world. Where Calcutta stands there were then only a few villages; in 1690 an East India Company agent set up a trading post here, choosing the spot because the river ran deep and marshland covered his flank.'],
'加尔各答|大英帝国·英国': ['1757 年普拉西之战后,东印度公司实际控制了孟加拉,加尔各答从一个商站变成收税与统治的中枢。1765 年公司取得孟加拉的税收权,从此一边做生意一边当政府——一家股份公司统治几千万人,这样的安排在历史上极少见,而更早做到这一步的是荷兰的东印度公司。',
 'After the battle of Plassey in 1757 the East India Company effectively controlled Bengal, and Calcutta went from trading post to the seat of revenue and government. In 1765 the Company took the right to collect Bengal\'s taxes and from then on traded and governed at once — a joint-stock company ruling tens of millions, an arrangement with very few parallels, the earlier one being the Dutch East India Company.'],
'加尔各答|印度·南亚诸国': ['1947 年分治把孟加拉一分为二:加尔各答留在印度,而它原来的腹地划到了另一边,大批难民涌入,城市负担极重。它至今是印度东部最大的城市,也是现代印度文学、电影与政治思潮的一个重要发源地。',
 'Partition in 1947 cut Bengal in two: Calcutta stayed in India while the countryside that had fed it went to the other side, refugees poured in and the city was pushed far past its capacity. It is still the largest city in eastern India and one of the springs of modern Indian literature, cinema and political thought.'],
'汉皮|孔雀王朝': ['汉皮一带的乱石岗上留着新石器时代的遗址,阿育王的小摩崖法敕就刻在不远处的岩石上——那是他的统治伸到南印度的直接证据。这片地方在成为都城之前,已经有人住了几千年。',
 'Neolithic sites lie among the boulder hills around Hampi, and Ashoka\'s minor rock edicts are cut into stone not far away — direct evidence that his rule reached into the south. People had lived here for thousands of years before it was ever a capital.'],
'汉皮|百乘王朝': ['百乘王朝控制德干高原时,这一带在它的南部。百乘是印度最早大量铸币的政权之一,也把罗马的金币吸进了内陆——德干各地出土的罗马金币窖藏,大多是这段时间进来的。',
 'When the Satavahanas held the Deccan this country lay in their south. They were among the first powers in India to strike coin in quantity, and they drew Roman gold inland — most of the hoards of Roman coins found across the Deccan came in during these years.'],
'汉皮|大英帝国·英国': ['1799 年英国击败迈索尔的提普苏丹之后,德干这一带陆续落入英国的势力范围。那时汉皮的废墟只是牧羊人放羊的地方——而两百多年前,它曾是世界上最大的城市之一。',
 'After the British defeated Tipu Sultan of Mysore in 1799, this part of the Deccan passed into their sphere. The ruins of Hampi were by then grazing ground for shepherds — two centuries earlier the city here had been among the largest in the world.'],
'汉皮|英属印度': ['1800 年前后,苏格兰测量员科林·麦肯齐系统测绘了汉皮的废墟,画下平面图、抄录碑铭。这批测绘是印度考古工作最早的成果之一——一座作为都城被冷落了两百多年的城,靠一个测量员重新回到纸面上。城里的维鲁巴克沙神庙倒是一直有人烧香,从没断过。',
 'Around 1800 the Scottish surveyor Colin Mackenzie made a systematic survey of the ruins of Hampi, drawing plans and copying inscriptions. His work is among the earliest of Indian archaeology — a city neglected as a capital for two centuries came back onto paper through a surveyor. The Virupaksha temple inside it, meanwhile, had never stopped receiving worshippers.'],
'汉皮|印度·南亚诸国': ['汉皮 1986 年列入世界文化遗产。遗址铺开在几十平方公里的乱石之间:神庙、水渠、王宫,还有一条长长的市集街,两边至今立着成排的石柱。十六世纪到过这里的葡萄牙旅行者写道,红宝石、钻石、祖母绿与珍珠就公开摆在那条街上卖。',
 'Hampi was inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 1986. The remains are spread over tens of square kilometres of boulder country — temples, water channels, palaces, and a long bazaar street still lined with rows of stone columns. A Portuguese traveller who saw it in the sixteenth century wrote of rubies, diamonds, emeralds and pearls being sold openly along that street.'],
'汉皮|中世纪诸王朝': ['维查耶纳伽尔在这里建都之前的几百年,这片乱石岗先后属于遮娄其、拉施特拉库塔与后遮娄其。离汉皮不远的巴达米、艾霍莱与帕塔达卡尔留着他们开的石窟和神庙——南印度的神庙样式就是在那几处试出来的,不同的屋顶与柱式一座挨一座地摆着,像一排做到一半的作业(帕塔达卡尔今天是世界文化遗产)。同一片石头地,先当了几百年试验场,后来才长出汉皮那座城。',
 'For centuries before Vijayanagara built its capital here, this boulder country passed between the Chalukyas, the Rashtrakutas and the Later Chalukyas. Badami, Aihole and Pattadakal, all within reach of Hampi, still hold the cave shrines and temples they cut — this is where the southern Indian temple was worked out, different roof-lines and column styles standing side by side like a row of half-finished exercises (Pattadakal is a World Heritage site today). The same field of stone served as a workshop for centuries before the city of Hampi grew out of it.'],
'汉皮|伐卡塔卡与德干诸国': ['维查耶纳伽尔在这里建都之前一千年,这片乱石岗属于德干诸国轮流管辖的南缘:先是伐卡塔卡的势力所及,再往南是卡丹巴与西恒伽。这一段几乎没有留下史书,知道的事情大多来自石头——刻在崖壁上的敕令、铜板上的赠地文书。同一片石头地,这一次留下的是字,不是城。',
 'A thousand years before Vijayanagara built its capital here, this boulder country lay along the southern edge of the Deccan states — within reach of the Vakatakas, with the Kadambas and Western Gangas further south. Almost no chronicle survives from the period; what is known comes mostly from stone — edicts cut into cliffs and land grants written on copper plates. The same field of stone, this time leaving writing rather than a city.'],
'孟买|孔雀王朝': ['孟买的七座岛屿在孔雀王朝时属于西海岸的贸易海岸。附近的坎赫里石窟大约从公元一世纪起开凿,一直修到十世纪——僧人住在离港口不远的山里,靠往来商人供养,这是印度佛教石窟常见的位置。',
 'The seven islands of Bombay lay on the trading coast the Mauryas knew on the western shore. The Kanheri caves nearby were cut from about the first century AD and worked on into the tenth — monks living in hills within reach of a port, supported by the merchants who used it, which is where Indian Buddhist cave sites usually are.'],
'孟买|马拉塔': ['十七、十八世纪马拉塔控制着孟买周边的大片土地,而七座岛屿在英国人手里。象岛石窟就在孟买湾中,那尊六世纪凿出来的湿婆三面像高约六米;岛上的雕像有不少损坏,一般归因于葡萄牙人占据的那段时间。',
 'In the seventeenth and eighteenth centuries the Marathas held the country all around Bombay while the seven islands were English. The Elephanta caves stand in the bay, their sixth-century three-faced Shiva about six metres high; much of the sculpture on the island is damaged, and the damage is generally put down to the Portuguese period.'],
'孟买|大英帝国·英国': ['从 1780 年代起,英国人陆续把七座岛之间的浅海填起来。这项工程断续做了六十多年,到十九世纪中叶七岛已经连成一整块陆地;后来的填海一直做到二十世纪,今天孟买市区有相当一部分是填出来的——一座城可以先有规划,再有土地。',
 'From the 1780s the British filled in the shallows between the seven islands. That work took some sixty years and by the middle of the nineteenth century the islands had become one landmass; reclamation carried on into the twentieth century, and a good part of central Mumbai today stands on made ground — a city can have its plan before it has its land.'],
'孟买|印度·南亚诸国': ['孟买是印度的金融中心,也是印地语电影工业的所在地。这座城同时住着全国最贵的房子和亚洲最大的一批棚户区,两者常常只隔一条马路——这种极端的并置,是南亚许多大城市共同的面貌。',
 'Mumbai is India\'s financial centre and the home of its Hindi film industry. It holds both the most expensive housing in the country and some of the largest informal settlements in Asia, often with a single road between them — an extremity of juxtaposition that many South Asian cities share.'],
'马六甲|三佛齐': ['马六甲建城之前,这条海峡的中转生意由更南边的巨港与占碑掌握。三佛齐衰落后,传为它的一支王室北上到这里另起炉灶(拜里米苏拉的出身,葡萄牙与马来两边的记载并不一致)——1400 年前后拜里米苏拉在马六甲建港,靠的还是同一条海峡、同一门生意。',
 'Before Malacca existed, the business of the strait was run from Palembang and Jambi further south. When Srivijaya declined, a branch of its royal house is said to have moved north and begun again here — Portuguese and Malay accounts of Parameswara\'s origins do not agree — around 1400 Parameswara founded the port of Malacca, living off the same strait and the same trade.'],
'马六甲|荷兰共和国': ['1641 年荷兰东印度公司从葡萄牙手里夺下马六甲,统治了一个半世纪多。但荷兰人真正要经营的是巴达维亚(今雅加达),马六甲在他们手里始终是次要的一个港——一座港口的衰落,有时不是因为它不行了,而是因为它的主人另有打算。',
 'The Dutch East India Company took Malacca from the Portuguese in 1641 and held it for over a century and a half. What the Dutch actually wanted to build up was Batavia, today\'s Jakarta, and Malacca stayed the lesser port in their hands throughout — a port sometimes declines not because it has failed but because its owner\'s plans lie elsewhere.'],
'马六甲|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1824 年英国与荷兰签约,把马六甲划给英国、把苏门答腊划给荷兰。一纸条约把一条海峡的两岸分进了两个殖民体系——今天马来西亚与印度尼西亚之间的国界,大体就是那一次划下的。',
 'By a treaty of 1824 Britain and the Netherlands assigned Malacca to Britain and Sumatra to the Dutch. One agreement put the two shores of a single strait into two colonial systems — and the border between Malaysia and Indonesia today follows roughly the line drawn then.'],
'马六甲|现代东南亚': ['马六甲今天是马来西亚的一个州,城市不大,但老城里葡、荷、英三层殖民建筑与更早的华人、马来社区并排立着,2008 年与槟城一起列入世界文化遗产。海峡本身仍是世界上最繁忙的航道之一。',
 'Malacca is a state of Malaysia now and not a large city, but its old town holds Portuguese, Dutch and British layers standing beside older Chinese and Malay quarters, and it was inscribed as a World Heritage Site together with George Town in 2008. The strait itself remains one of the busiest shipping lanes in the world.'],
'非斯|迦太基': ['迦太基的势力沿北非海岸伸展,而非斯所在的这道内陆山谷不在它的范围内。不过再往西六十公里的瓦卢比利斯已经有迦太基人的痕迹:那里出土过巴力神庙的遗迹与腓尼基文的刻石,当地首领用的也是布匿人的头衔。',
 'Carthaginian power ran along the North African coast; the inland valley where Fez stands lay outside it. Sixty kilometres west, though, Volubilis already shows Carthaginian traces: remains of a temple to Baal, stones cut with Phoenician, and local chiefs using a Punic title.'],
'非斯|罗马共和国': ['前 146 年迦太基灭亡后,罗马逐步接手北非。这一带属毛里塔尼亚王国,长期是罗马的属国而不是行省——罗马在西北非的统治,一直比它在别处松。',
 'After Carthage fell in 146 BC Rome took over North Africa by degrees. This country belonged to the kingdom of Mauretania, a client state rather than a province for a long time — Rome\'s hold on the northwest of Africa was always looser than elsewhere.'],
'非斯|罗马帝国': ['非斯西边约六十公里的瓦卢比利斯,先是柏柏尔人的聚落、后由毛里塔尼亚的客王营建,罗马吞并之后把它扩成了这一带经营得最深入内陆的一座城,今天还留着凯旋门与成片的马赛克地面。八世纪末伊德里斯一世正是从瓦卢比利斯出发,在非斯建起新城——一座罗马城的终点,是一座伊斯兰城的起点。',
 'Volubilis, some sixty kilometres west of Fez, began as a Berber settlement and was developed by a client king of Mauretania; after Rome annexed the kingdom it built the place up into the furthest inland of its cities here, where a triumphal arch and wide floors of mosaic still stand. At the end of the eighth century Idris I set out from Volubilis and founded a new city at Fez — where one Roman town ended, an Islamic one began.'],
'非斯|现代中东': ['1912 年《非斯条约》在这里签订,摩洛哥成为法国保护国;1956 年独立。非斯老城因为格局与手工业几乎没有中断,1981 年列入世界文化遗产;那里的巷道太窄,货物至今主要靠驴和手推车运。',
 'The Treaty of Fes was signed here in 1912, making Morocco a French protectorate; independence came in 1956. The old city, whose plan and crafts have carried on with hardly a break, was made a World Heritage Site in 1981 — its lanes are too narrow for vehicles, and goods still move by donkey and handcart.'],
'威尼斯|罗马共和国': ['威尼斯泻湖一带在罗马共和国时属山南高卢。岸上的帕多瓦是大城,泻湖里只有渔民和盐场——盐是这片浅水最早的财富。这座城本身要到四百多年后才出现,而且是被逼出来的。',
 'The lagoon country belonged to Cisalpine Gaul under the Roman republic. Padua on the mainland was a substantial city; in the lagoon there were only fishermen and salt pans — salt was the first wealth of these shallows. The city itself would not exist for another four centuries and more, and then only under duress.'],
'威尼斯|罗马帝国': ['罗马帝国晚期,阿奎莱亚是意大利北部最重要的城市之一。452 年匈人阿提拉攻毁阿奎莱亚,沿岸居民逃进泻湖的沙洲上避难——威尼斯的起源,传统上就从这一批难民算起:一座后来富甲地中海的城,起点是无处可去。',
 'In the late empire Aquileia was one of the chief cities of northern Italy. Attila destroyed it in 452 and people from the coast fled onto the sandbanks of the lagoon — traditionally this is where Venice begins: a city that would grow rich beyond any other in the Mediterranean started with people who had nowhere else to go.'],
'威尼斯|中世纪西欧': ['威尼斯名义上属拜占庭,实际上越来越自主。828 年两名威尼斯商人把圣马可的遗骨从亚历山大运了回来,据说是藏在猪肉里躲过检查的。有了一位福音书作者做主保圣人,这座泻湖里的商人城在基督教世界的位置一下就不同了。',
 'Venice belonged to Byzantium in name and grew steadily more independent in fact. In 828 two Venetian merchants brought the relics of Saint Mark back from Alexandria — hidden under pork, the story goes, to get them past inspection. With an evangelist as its patron, a town of traders in a lagoon stood quite differently in the Christian world.'],
'威尼斯|法兰西': ['1797 年拿破仑的军队开到,延续一千一百年的威尼斯共和国投降解体,末代总督交出权力。此后威尼斯先归奥地利,后并入意大利。一个从未被外敌攻破过的共和国,是在没有打仗的情况下结束的。',
 'Napoleon\'s army arrived in 1797 and the Venetian republic, eleven centuries old, gave up and dissolved itself; the last doge handed over his powers. Venice went first to Austria and later into Italy. A republic that had never been taken by an enemy ended without a battle.'],
'佛罗伦萨|罗马共和国': ['佛罗伦萨一带原是伊特鲁里亚人的地方,山上的菲耶索莱是他们的城。罗马人后来在阿尔诺河边的平地上另建了一座——山上的城为了守,河边的城为了过路,两个位置说明的是两种活法。',
 'This country was Etruscan, and their town was Fiesole up on the hill. The Romans later built another on the flat ground by the Arno — the hill town built to be defended, the river town built to be passed through: two sites, two ways of living.'],
'佛罗伦萨|罗马帝国': ['前 59 年前后,罗马在这里建起殖民城「弗洛伦提亚」,给退伍军人分地。城按罗马军营的方格布局规划,今天佛罗伦萨老城中心那几条街的走向,还是当年定下的——两千年过去,人走的还是同一张网格。',
 'Around 59 BC Rome founded the colony of Florentia here and allotted land to discharged soldiers. It was laid out on the grid of a Roman camp, and the run of the streets in the centre of Florence today still follows it — two thousand years on, people walk the same grid.'],
'佛罗伦萨|中世纪西欧': ['十三世纪佛罗伦萨的银行家开始向整个欧洲放贷。1252 年它铸出金弗罗林,含金量一直稳定,成了跨国贸易通用的结算货币之一——一座内陆城市靠一枚可信的金币在欧洲说话,信用比军队走得远。',
 'In the thirteenth century Florentine bankers began lending across Europe. The gold florin was struck in 1252 and held its gold content, becoming one of the standard settlement currencies of international trade — an inland city speaking to Europe through a coin people trusted, credit travelling further than any army.'],
'佛罗伦萨|法兰西': ['1799 年之后佛罗伦萨几度被法国军队占领,拿破仑把托斯卡纳并入法国。这一时期大量艺术品被运往巴黎,后来才陆续归还。意大利统一之后,佛罗伦萨在 1865 到 1871 年短暂做过意大利王国的首都。',
 'From 1799 French troops occupied Florence more than once and Napoleon annexed Tuscany to France. A great deal of art went to Paris in these years and was only returned later. After Italian unification Florence served briefly, from 1865 to 1871, as the capital of the kingdom of Italy.'],
'加尔各答|英属印度': ['加尔各答从东印度公司的一个商站长成印度最大的城市,1772 到 1911 年是英属印度的首都。1943 年孟加拉大饥荒中约有二三百万人死亡(各家估算差距很大)。当年的粮食是否真的绝对短缺,学界至今有争论;战时政策与运输管制被认为是主因之一。',
 'Calcutta grew from an East India Company trading post into India\'s largest city and was the capital of British India from 1772 to 1911. In the Bengal famine of 1943 some two to three million people died, though estimates vary widely. Whether food was truly in absolute shortage is still argued over; wartime policy and transport controls are held to be among the main causes.'],
'拉合尔|莫卧儿帝国': ['阿克巴 1585 年把朝廷移到拉合尔,一驻十三年,城墙与拉合尔堡是那时立起来的。他的孙子沙贾汗在城中造了夏利马尔花园,贾汉吉尔与努尔贾汉都葬在城郊。',
 'Akbar moved his court to Lahore in 1585 and kept it there thirteen years, and the city walls and Lahore Fort date from then. His grandson Shah Jahan laid out the Shalimar Gardens here, and Jahangir and Nur Jahan are both buried on the city\'s outskirts.'],
'科伦坡|朱罗王朝': ['朱罗是印度史上少见的海权王朝,舰队征服了斯里兰卡北部,把它当作一个省管了几十年。这次征服把南印度的湿婆神庙建筑带到岛上,也让岛上早已存在的泰米尔人社群第一次有了自己的政治中心。',
 'The Cholas were that rare thing in Indian history, a sea power: their fleets took the north of Sri Lanka and ran it as a province for decades. The conquest brought south Indian Shiva temple architecture to the island, and gave the Tamil communities long settled there a political centre of their own for the first time.'],
'巴特那|孔雀王朝': ['孔雀王朝的都城华氏城就在这里,希腊使节麦加斯梯尼记下它有木头城墙、几百座塔楼与深壕。据上座部的记载,阿育王在这里召集过一次结集,并派人把佛法送往斯里兰卡与更远的地方。',
 'Pataliputra, the Mauryan capital, stood here; the Greek envoy Megasthenes described its timber walls, hundreds of towers and deep moat. By the Theravada account Ashoka convened a Buddhist council in the city and sent missions carrying the teaching to Sri Lanka and beyond.'],
'阿拉木图|哈萨克汗国': ['1465 年前后,两位不满乌兹别克汗的王子带着部众东走七河草原,自立门户——「哈萨克」一词本意近于「脱离者」,汗国由此开端。阿拉木图所在的七河地区,就是这个汗国的摇篮。',
 'Around 1465 two princes at odds with the Uzbek khan led their followers east into the Zhetysu steppe and set up on their own — the word "Kazakh" carries the sense of one who breaks away, and the khanate begins there. Zhetysu, where Almaty stands, was its cradle.'],
'安卡拉|奥斯曼帝国': ['1402 年帖木儿在安卡拉城外击溃奥斯曼军,苏丹巴耶塞特一世被俘,奥斯曼几个王子随即内战十一年,帝国差点就此散架。这是它扩张路上受过的最重一次挫折,君士坦丁堡因此又多撑了半个世纪。',
 'Outside Ankara in 1402 Timur shattered the Ottoman army and captured Sultan Bayezid I; the sultan\'s sons then fought each other for eleven years and the empire nearly came apart. It was the heaviest check the Ottomans took while they were still expanding, and it bought Constantinople another half-century.'],
'突尼斯|迦太基': ['迦太基城就在今天突尼斯城的近郊,靠海上贸易与雇佣兵立国。三次布匿战争打了一百多年,前 146 年城被罗马攻破焚毁;一百年后罗马人又在原址上重建了一座罗马城市。',
 'Carthage stood on the outskirts of today\'s Tunis, living by seaborne trade and hired soldiers. The three Punic Wars ran for over a century, and in 146 BC the city was stormed and burned by Rome — which a hundred years later rebuilt a Roman city on the same ground.'],
'非斯|阿拉伯哈里发': ['非斯由伊德里斯家族在八世纪末建城,是马格里布最早的伊斯兰城市之一。城中的卡鲁因清真寺建于九世纪中叶,后来在寺里形成了延续至今的讲学传统,常被列为世界上最古老的高等学府之一。',
 'Fez was founded by the Idrisids at the end of the eighth century, among the earliest Islamic cities of the Maghreb. Its Qarawiyyin mosque was built in the middle of the ninth century, and the teaching that later grew up inside it has never stopped — it is often listed among the oldest institutions of higher learning in the world.'],
'马德里|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['马德里本是小城,1561 年腓力二世把朝廷搬来,理由之一是它正好在半岛的地理中心。城外几十公里的埃斯科里亚尔既是宫殿也是修道院和陵墓,腓力二世常年在那里办公,帝国的文书从这里发往两个大洋。',
 'Madrid was a small town until Philip II moved his court here in 1561, partly because it sits at the geographical centre of the peninsula. El Escorial, some forty kilometres out of town, was palace, monastery and royal tomb at once; Philip worked there for years, and the empire\'s paperwork went out from here to two oceans.'],
'里斯本|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['里斯本是通往印度的航线起点,1497 年达·伽马从这里出发,绕过好望角,次年抵达印度。1755 年万圣节一场大地震加上海啸与火灾,把城市毁掉大半,重建时按抗震要求做了木结构骨架,是欧洲最早的一批抗震设计。',
 'Lisbon was where the route to India began: Vasco da Gama sailed from here in 1497, round the Cape, and reached India the next year. On All Saints\' Day 1755 an earthquake with a tsunami and fires destroyed most of the city; the rebuilding used a timber cage frame designed to resist shaking — among the earliest earthquake-resistant construction in Europe.'],
'佛罗伦萨|文艺复兴意大利': ['布鲁内莱斯基给佛罗伦萨主教堂造的穹顶,不用中心木架就砌了起来,至今仍是世界上最大的砌体穹顶。美第奇家族靠银行业起家,再用钱供养艺术家——文艺复兴的账,有一大半记在他们的账本上。',
 'Brunelleschi raised the dome of Florence cathedral without a central wooden centring, and it remains the largest masonry dome in the world. The Medici made their money in banking and spent it on artists — a great deal of the Renaissance was paid for out of their ledgers.'],
'乌兰巴托|清': ['这座城起初是一座跟着活佛走的帐篷寺院,搬过近三十次,1778 年才在今天的位置定下来,当时叫库伦。清朝在这里派驻办事大臣,管着库伦一带(喀尔喀东边两个部);1911 年辛亥革命一起,库伦的王公与活佛随即宣布独立。',
 'The city began as a tent monastery that travelled with its living Buddha, moving nearly thirty times before settling on this site in 1778, when it was called Urga. The Qing stationed an amban here over the Urga country — the two eastern Khalkha banners; when revolution broke out in China in 1911, the nobles and the living Buddha at Urga declared independence.'],
'喀布尔|帖木儿帝国': ['帖木儿的五世孙巴布尔在中亚屡战屡败,退到喀布尔立足二十来年,再从这里南下印度,开创了莫卧儿王朝。他遗嘱要葬回喀布尔,墓园至今在城中的山坡上。',
 'Timur\'s great-great-great-grandson Babur, beaten again and again in Central Asia, fell back on Kabul and held it for some twenty years before going south into India to found the Mughal dynasty. He asked to be buried back in Kabul, and his garden tomb is still on the hillside above the city.'],
'布拉格|中世纪西欧': ['查理四世既是波希米亚国王也是神圣罗马皇帝,他把布拉格当作帝国的中心来经营:1348 年在这里创办了中欧最早的大学,又动工修跨伏尔塔瓦河的石桥,今天叫查理桥。城堡里的圣维特主教座堂也是他那时开工的,前后修了将近六百年才完工。',
 'Charles IV was king of Bohemia and Holy Roman Emperor at once, and he built Prague up as the centre of his empire: in 1348 he founded here the first university in central Europe, and began the stone bridge over the Vltava that now carries his name. St Vitus cathedral in the castle was started under him too — and took nearly six hundred years to finish.'],
'华沙|波兰-立陶宛': ['1596 年前后王室把驻地从克拉科夫迁到华沙,这里位置更靠近立陶宛一侧,方便管两头;而议会从 1569 年起就固定在这里开了。波兰的国王由贵族选举产生,议会里任何一名议员都能一票否决全部决议,这套制度后来把国家拖垮了。',
 'Around 1596 the royal seat moved from Krakow to Warsaw, closer to the Lithuanian half of the union and easier to govern both from; the Sejm had already been meeting here since 1569. Poland\'s kings were elected by the nobility, and any single deputy could veto the whole session — a rule that in the end wrecked the state.'],
'卡诺|欧洲殖民非洲': ['卡诺是跨撒哈拉商路的南端终点之一,以染布闻名,城里的靛蓝染坑用了几百年。1903 年英军攻破这座有厚土墙的城,此后用「间接统治」——保留埃米尔的位子,让他替英国人收税断案。',
 'Kano was one of the southern termini of the trans-Saharan trade and famous for its cloth; its indigo dye pits have been in use for centuries. British troops took the thick-walled city in 1903, and Britain then ruled by "indirect rule" — keeping the emir in place to collect taxes and judge cases on its behalf.'],
'金沙萨|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1881 年斯坦利在这里建站,取名利奥波德维尔。刚果自由邦不是比利时的殖民地,而是国王利奥波德二世的私人领地;橡胶配额制度造成的死亡与残害,是记录最充分的殖民暴行之一。1908 年比利时议会才把它收归国有。',
 'Stanley founded a station here in 1881 and named it Leopoldville. The Congo Free State was not a Belgian colony but the personal property of King Leopold II; the deaths and mutilations caused by its rubber quotas are among the best-documented colonial atrocities. Only in 1908 did the Belgian parliament take it over as a state colony.'],
'蒙巴萨|斯瓦希里城邦': ['蒙巴萨是斯瓦希里海岸的老港之一。1593 年葡萄牙人在这里筑起耶稣堡,想扼住印度洋航线。这座堡垒后来成了争夺的焦点——当地统治者、葡萄牙人、阿曼人轮流占据,前后至少易手九次。',
 'Mombasa is one of the old ports of the Swahili coast. The Portuguese built Fort Jesus here in 1593 to command the Indian Ocean route. The fort became the prize everyone fought over — local rulers, Portuguese and Omanis in turn — and changed hands at least nine times.'],
'拉各斯|现代非洲': ['拉各斯是今天非洲人口最多的城市之一,人口还在快速增长。尼日利亚的电影业「诺莱坞」以低成本、高产量著称,产量长期居世界前列,片子在整个非洲乃至海外的非洲人社区流通。',
 'Lagos is among the most populous cities in Africa today and still growing fast. Nigeria\'s film industry, Nollywood, is known for low budgets and very high output — for years among the largest in the world by number of films — and its work circulates across Africa and among Africans abroad.'],
'波哥大|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1819 年玻利瓦尔翻过安第斯山、在博亚卡击败西班牙军,几天后进入波哥大,大哥伦比亚随即成立。这个联邦包括今天的哥伦比亚、委内瑞拉、厄瓜多尔与巴拿马,但只维持了十来年就分裂了。',
 'In 1819 Bolívar crossed the Andes, beat the Spanish at Boyacá and entered Bogotá days later, and Gran Colombia was proclaimed. The federation covered what is now Colombia, Venezuela, Ecuador and Panama — and broke apart little more than a decade later.'],
'布宜诺斯艾利斯|西葡殖民美洲': ['布宜诺斯艾利斯建过两次,第一次的移民撑不下去、弃城而走,1580 年才重建成功。它长期只是个走私口岸——白银按规定必须走利马与巴拿马,直到 1776 年西班牙设立拉普拉塔总督区,这里才被扶正。',
 'Buenos Aires was founded twice: the first settlers could not hold on and abandoned it, and only the refounding of 1580 stuck. For a long time it was little more than a smuggling port — silver was supposed to go out through Lima and Panama — until Spain created the Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata in 1776 and the city was made a capital.'],
'圣地亚哥|西葡殖民美洲': ['1541 年瓦尔迪维亚在这里建城,当年就被马普切人烧毁过一次。西班牙人始终没能征服比奥比奥河以南的马普切地区,双方沿河对峙了近三百年,是美洲少有的长期未被征服的原住民地带。',
 'Valdivia founded the city in 1541 and the Mapuche burned it the same year. The Spanish never conquered the Mapuche country south of the Bío Bío river; the two sides faced each other across it for nearly three centuries — one of the few parts of the Americas to stay unconquered that long.'],
'洛杉矶|美国': ['洛杉矶原是西班牙人 1781 年建的小镇,1848 年美墨战争后随加利福尼亚归入美国。二十世纪初电影业从东岸搬来,看中的是这里一年到头的晴天与紧挨着的沙漠、海滩和山地——一个地方能拍出各种外景。',
 'Los Angeles began as a Spanish town founded in 1781 and passed to the United States with California after the war with Mexico in 1848. Early in the twentieth century the film business moved out from the east coast, drawn by year-round sunshine and by desert, beach and mountains all within reach — every kind of location in one place.'],
'成都|三星堆·古蜀': ['成都东北四十公里的三星堆,1986 年偶然挖出两个祭祀坑,里面是成百上千件青铜人像、面具与神树,还有黄金面具——样式在中国别处从没见过。城市中心后来移到今天成都市区的金沙,那里出土了太阳神鸟金箔,如今是成都的城市标志。这套文明没有留下文字,谁建的、为什么突然衰落,至今没有答案。',
 'At Sanxingdui, forty kilometres northeast of Chengdu, two sacrificial pits were opened by accident in 1986 and found to hold hundreds of bronze figures, masks and sacred trees, and a mask of gold — nothing like them had been seen anywhere else in China. The centre later moved to Jinsha, inside modern Chengdu, where a gold foil of birds circling a sun was found and is now the city\'s emblem. The civilization left no writing: who built it, and why it broke off, are still unanswered.'],
'成都|战国': ['成都平原上原本是蜀国,与中原来往不多、自成一路。前 316 年秦军翻过秦岭灭掉蜀国,几年后张仪、张若在这里筑城,街道按秦制铺开——成都作为一座城的历史,通常从这时算起。此后蜀郡守李冰主持修都江堰,把岷江分成两股:一股防洪、一股灌田,不用水坝而靠分水与排沙,两千二百多年后仍在用。',
 'The Chengdu plain was the kingdom of Shu, which kept largely to itself and had little to do with the central states. In 316 BC a Qin army crossed the Qinling and destroyed it; a few years later Zhang Yi and Zhang Ruo walled a city here on the Qin pattern — and Chengdu as a city is usually counted from then. Later the commandery governor Li Bing built the Dujiangyan works, splitting the Min river in two — one channel to carry floods away, one to water the fields — with no dam, only a divide and a sluice for silt. It still works after twenty-two centuries.'],
'成都|秦': ['秦统一后成都是蜀郡治所。城分大城与少城,少城是工商区,官营的盐铁与织造都在那里;秦又把六国的富户成批迁进蜀地,带来了技术与资本。有了都江堰浇出的这片水田,巴蜀成了关中之外最稳的粮仓——秦末刘邦据巴蜀汉中起家,靠的正是这条后路。',
 'After unification Chengdu was the seat of Shu commandery. It had a great city and a lesser city, the lesser one given over to crafts and trade, with the state salt, iron and weaving works inside it; Qin also moved wealthy households from the conquered states into Shu in batches, bringing skills and capital with them. Watered by Dujiangyan, the Sichuan basin became the steadiest granary outside Guanzhong — and when the Qin fell, it was this rear country that Liu Bang built his rise upon.'],
'成都|西汉': ['成都的织锦好到设了专门的官署管,「蜀锦」这个名字从此叫开;绕城而过的那条河叫锦江,是漂洗丝绸的地方。太守文翁在这里办起石室学堂,一般被认为是中国最早的地方官办学校,汉武帝后来下令各郡照办。',
 'Chengdu\'s brocade was good enough to warrant its own government office, and the name Shu brocade dates from then; the river that curves past the city is the Jin — Brocade — river, where the silk was rinsed. The governor Wen Weng founded a stone-chamber school here, generally reckoned China\'s earliest state school outside the capital, and Emperor Wu later ordered every commandery to do the same.'],
'成都|东汉': ['东汉的成都是全国最富的几座城之一。这一带出土了大量画像砖与陶俑,其中「击鼓说唱俑」笑得咧开嘴、耸着肩,是汉代最著名的陶塑之一——它告诉我们那时的市井有说书卖艺这一行。',
 'Han Chengdu was among the richest cities in the empire. The area has yielded quantities of moulded tomb bricks and pottery figures, among them the famous drumming storyteller — grinning, shoulders hunched — one of the best known Han sculptures, and evidence that street entertainers were already a trade.'],
'成都|三国': ['221 年刘备在成都称帝,国号仍叫汉,后世称蜀汉。诸葛亮在这里主政十余年,南征、北伐、治蜀都从这座城发出;他死后朝廷起初不许专门立庙,直到 263 年才准在沔阳的墓旁建;成都的武侯祠要晚得多,一般认为是成汉时所建,明初与刘备的惠陵、汉昭烈庙合到了一处。',
 'In 221 Liu Bei took the imperial title at Chengdu, still calling his state Han — later known as Shu Han. Zhuge Liang governed from here for over a decade; the southern campaigns, the northern expeditions and the running of Shu all went out from this city. After his death the court at first refused him a temple of his own, allowing one only in 263, beside his grave at Mianyang. The Wuhou shrine at Chengdu came much later — generally dated to the Cheng-Han — and in the early Ming it was merged with Liu Bei\'s tomb and the Zhaolie temple into one precinct.'],
'成都|西晋': ['西晋的成都是益州治所。到王朝末年,关中连年饥荒,几万户流民翻过秦岭涌进四川找饭吃;官府几次下令赶他们回原籍,流民不肯走,冲突越积越深——李特兄弟就是在这场对峙里被推为首领的。',
 'Under the Western Jin, Chengdu was the seat of Yizhou province. In the dynasty\'s last years famine emptied the Guanzhong plain and tens of thousands of refugee households crossed the Qinling into Sichuan looking for food. The authorities ordered them home again and again; they would not go, and out of that standoff the Li brothers were raised up as their leaders.'],
'成都|南北朝': ['南北朝时四川是南朝的西边屏障,益州刺史历来是重镇。553 年西魏乘南朝内乱出兵取蜀,四川从此归了北方;四年后北周代西魏,又二十多年后隋代北周;隋能顺江东下灭陈,先拿下四川是重要一步。',
 'Through the Northern and Southern Dynasties Sichuan was the southern courts\' western shield, and the governorship of Yizhou always went to a man of weight. In 553 the Western Wei took Shu while the south was in disorder, and Sichuan passed to the north; four years later the Northern Zhou replaced the Western Wei, and some twenty-five years after that the Sui replaced the Northern Zhou — and holding Sichuan was a large part of how the Sui came down the Yangtze to finish off the Chen.'],
'成都|隋': ['隋文帝把儿子杨秀封为蜀王、镇成都近二十年,城墙与官署都是那时整修的。四川在隋代是少受战乱的地方,粮和布往外调,支撑着关中的开销——这个「天府供中原」的格局,唐代还会重演一次。',
 'Emperor Wen of Sui made his son Yang Xiu Prince of Shu and stationed him at Chengdu for nearly twenty years, and the walls and offices were put in order then. Sichuan saw little fighting under the Sui and sent grain and cloth out to pay for the capital region\'s needs — a pattern of the plain feeding the centre that would repeat under the Tang.'],
'成都|蒙古帝国': ['1236 年蒙古军由汉中南下攻入成都,这是四川战场最惨烈的一段。此后四十多年,蒙宋在四川反复拉锯,南宋把防线撤到重庆一带的山城,成都长期在拉锯区里,户口锐减。',
 'A Mongol army came south from Hanzhong and broke into Chengdu in 1236, the worst stretch of the war in Sichuan. For more than forty years afterwards Mongols and Song fought back and forth across the province; the Song pulled their line back to the hill forts around Chongqing, and Chengdu, left in the contested middle, lost most of its households.'],
'成都|元': ['元朝设四川行省,治所在成都。战乱之后四川人口只剩很少,元廷从外地迁民入川、又减免赋税招人复垦;成都平原的水利也是这时重新修起来的,都江堰在元代有过一次大规模整治。',
 'The Yuan set up a Sichuan province with its seat at Chengdu. War had left very few people in the province, so the court moved settlers in from elsewhere and cut taxes to draw farmers back to the land. The irrigation of the Chengdu plain was put back in order in these years too, and Dujiangyan had a major overhaul under the Yuan.'],
'成都|东晋·十六国': ['西晋末年关中饥荒,流民成群涌进四川。304 年李雄在成都称王、306 年称帝,国号大成,后来改称汉——史称成汉,是十六国里最早立起来的政权之一。它在成都撑了四十来年,347 年被东晋的桓温所灭。',
 'As famine emptied the Guanzhong plain at the end of the Western Jin, refugees poured into Sichuan in bands. Li Xiong took the title of king at Chengdu in 304 and emperor in 306, calling his state Cheng and later Han — the Cheng-Han, among the first of the Sixteen Kingdoms to be founded. It held Chengdu for some forty years until Huan Wen of the Eastern Jin destroyed it in 347.'],
'成都|唐': ['755 年安史之乱爆发,次年唐玄宗西奔入蜀,成都因此升为「南京」,与长安洛阳并列。杜甫也在这时避乱来蜀,在浣花溪边搭了草堂,住了三年多、写下二百多首诗——今天的杜甫草堂就在那片地方。当时有「扬一益二」的说法,益州即成都。',
 'The An Lushan rebellion broke out in 755 and the next year Emperor Xuanzong fled west into Shu; Chengdu was raised to "Southern Capital," ranked with Chang\'an and Luoyang. Du Fu came south in the same upheaval, put up a thatched hut by the Huanhua stream, lived there over three years and wrote more than two hundred poems — the site is the Du Fu Thatched Cottage today. The saying of the age ran "Yangzhou first, Yizhou second," and Yizhou was Chengdu.'],
'成都|五代十国': ['中原打成一锅粥的时候,四川关起门来过了两段安稳日子:前蜀与后蜀,都城都在成都。后蜀主孟昶让人把儒家经典刻石、又组织雕版印九经,后蜀人赵崇祚编成《花间集》——一般认为是中国最早的文人词总集。相传他还在城墙上遍种芙蓉,成都「蓉城」的别名由此而来。',
 'While the north tore itself apart, Sichuan shut its gates and had two quiet spells — Former Shu and Later Shu, both with their capital at Chengdu. The Later Shu ruler Meng Chang had the Confucian classics cut in stone and the Nine Classics printed from blocks, and in his reign Zhao Chongzuo compiled the Huajian ji — generally taken as the earliest anthology of literati song lyrics. He is said to have planted hibiscus along the city walls, which is why Chengdu is still nicknamed the Hibiscus City.'],
'成都|南宋': ['南宋的四川是抗蒙的正面战场。1236 年蒙古军攻入成都,城破后遭到严重屠戮(死伤数字各家记载出入很大);此后四川的防御重心南移到重庆一带的山城,成都长期残破,直到元代才慢慢恢复。',
 'Sichuan was the front line against the Mongols under the Southern Song. A Mongol army broke into Chengdu in 1236 and the sack that followed was severe — the casualty figures given in the sources differ wildly. The defence of Sichuan afterwards shifted south to the hill forts around Chongqing, and Chengdu lay in ruins for a long time, recovering only under the Yuan.'],
'成都|明': ['明太祖封儿子朱椿为蜀王,王府就建在今天天府广场一带,规制仿南京宫城,当地叫它「皇城」。1644 年张献忠入成都建大西政权,两年后撤走;明末清初四川人口锐减是公认的,但责任分摊——张献忠、清军、南明残部、瘟疫各占多少——史学界至今争论。',
 'The first Ming emperor made his son Zhu Chun Prince of Shu, and the palace went up where Tianfu Square now is, modelled on the palace city at Nanjing; locals called it the Imperial City. In 1644 Zhang Xianzhong entered Chengdu and set up his Great Western state, withdrawing two years later. That Sichuan\'s population collapsed in the years around the fall of the Ming is not disputed; how the blame divides — between Zhang, the Qing armies, Ming loyalist remnants and epidemic — still is.'],
'成都|清': ['四川人少地荒,清初起官府组织和默许外省移民入川,前后延续百余年,湖北湖南来的最多,民间叫「湖广填四川」。今天四川话、川菜与各地会馆的格局,大半是这场移民留下的。',
 'With Sichuan emptied of people, from the early Qing the government organised and allowed migration in from other provinces for more than a century — most of all from Hubei and Hunan, which is why it is remembered as "Huguang fills Sichuan." Much of today\'s Sichuan speech, its cooking and its pattern of native-place guild halls comes out of that migration.'],
'成都|民国': ['抗战时四川是大后方,成都的机场是轰炸日本本土的起降地之一。四所内迁大学挤进本地的华西协合大学同时上课,合称「五大学时期」;这几年是这座城近代教育最密集的一段。',
 'In the war with Japan, Sichuan was the rear base, and airfields around Chengdu were among those used for raids on the Japanese home islands. Four universities evacuated from the east crowded onto the campus of the local West China Union University and taught side by side — the "five universities" years, the densest stretch of modern education the city has known.'],
'成都|共和国': ['三线建设时期,大批工厂与研究所从沿海迁进四川,电子与航空工业在成都扎下根。城北的大熊猫繁育研究基地 1987 年建起,如今是这座城最广为人知的去处之一。',
 'During the Third Front build-up, factories and research institutes were moved inland from the coast, and electronics and aviation took root in Chengdu. The panda breeding research base north of the city was set up in 1987 and is now among the best known places in it.'],
'巴黎|罗马共和国': ['前 53 年凯撒把全高卢的会议召集到塞纳河中沙洲上的高卢人聚落卢泰西亚,这是巴黎见于文字的开端;第二年罗马军队再来时,巴黎西人烧掉了自己的城镇和桥才撤走。凯撒在《高卢战记》里记下了这个地名和住在这里的巴黎西人——今天「巴黎」这个名字就来自这个部族。',
 'In 53 BC Caesar summoned the assembly of all Gaul to Lutetia, a Gaulish settlement on an island in the Seine — the first appearance of Paris in writing; when Roman troops came back the next year the Parisii burned their own town and bridges before pulling out. Caesar records the name and the Parisii who lived there in his account of the Gallic war, and the city\'s name comes from that tribe.'],
'巴黎|罗马帝国': ['罗马人把卢泰西亚重建在塞纳河左岸的山坡上,修了广场、剧场、引水道和至今仍能看到的克吕尼浴场。它在罗马高卢只是一座中等城市,真正的大城在里昂;巴黎的分量要等到中世纪才起来。',
 'The Romans rebuilt Lutetia on the slope of the left bank, with a forum, a theatre, an aqueduct and the baths at Cluny that can still be seen. It was a middling town in Roman Gaul — the great city was Lyon — and Paris would not count for much until the middle ages.'],
'巴黎|中世纪西欧': ['987 年于格·卡佩即位,王室驻在巴黎,这座城才真正成为法国的中心。此后三百年间,西岱岛上建起巴黎圣母院(1163 年动工)、左岸聚起学者形成巴黎大学——欧洲最早的一批大学之一,神学在这里的地位相当于今天的顶尖学科。',
 'When Hugh Capet took the throne in 987 with his seat at Paris, the city became the centre of France in earnest. Over the next three centuries Notre-Dame rose on the island — begun in 1163 — and the scholars gathering on the left bank formed the University of Paris, among the earliest in Europe, where theology held the standing a leading science holds today.'],
'伦敦|罗马帝国': ['罗马人约在公元 47 年前后在泰晤士河一处能架桥的地方建起伦第尼恩。60 年布狄卡起义把它烧成白地,重建后成了不列颠行省的首府,城墙圈起的范围大体就是今天伦敦金融城的界线——两千年后,这条界线还在。',
 'The Romans founded Londinium around AD 47 at a point on the Thames where a bridge could be built. Boudica\'s revolt burned it flat in 60; rebuilt, it became the capital of the province, and the line of its walls is roughly the boundary of the City of London today — still there after two thousand years.'],
'伦敦|中世纪西欧': ['1066 年诺曼征服后,威廉在城东建起伦敦塔镇住这座城。1215 年贵族逼约翰王签署《大宪章》,伦敦市民是逼宫的一方——这座城很早就学会了拿商业实力换政治特权,自治市的地位就是这么一点点谈下来的。',
 'After the Norman conquest of 1066 William raised the Tower at the east end of the city to hold it down. When the barons forced King John to seal Magna Carta in 1215, the citizens of London were among those doing the forcing — the city learned early to trade its commercial weight for political privilege, and its self-government was negotiated that way, piece by piece.'],
'罗马|罗马共和国': ['传说前 753 年建城,共和国从前 509 年赶走最后一位国王开始。城中心的广场是政治的舞台:元老院在这里开会、执政官在这里演说、公民大会在这里投票。前 390 年高卢人一度攻入罗马城,此后城墙修了起来;此后近八百年,再没有外敌攻进过罗马城——汉尼拔前 211 年一路打到城下,也只是在城外绕了一圈。',
 'The city was traditionally founded in 753 BC, and the republic began in 509 BC with the expulsion of the last king. The Forum at its centre was the stage of politics: the senate met there, consuls spoke there, the assemblies voted there. Gauls broke into Rome in 390 BC and walls went up afterwards; for nearly eight hundred years after that no foreign army entered the city — Hannibal rode up to its gates in 211 BC and no further.'],
'罗马|拜占庭': ['西罗马灭亡后,罗马城名义上仍属东罗马,由君士坦丁堡派驻拉文纳的总督节制。六世纪的哥特战争把这座城打得残破,渡槽被切断,人口从鼎盛时的百万跌到几万;此后填补权力真空的是教宗,罗马从帝国之都变成了教会之都。',
 'After the western empire fell, Rome nominally belonged to the east and was governed on Constantinople\'s behalf from Ravenna. The Gothic wars of the sixth century wrecked it, its aqueducts were cut, and the population fell from a million at its height to a few tens of thousands. It was the popes who filled the vacuum, and Rome turned from the capital of an empire into the capital of a church.'],
'罗马|中世纪西欧': ['中世纪的罗马人口最少时不过两三万,牛羊在古广场上吃草,当地人把那里叫「牛场」。800 年查理曼在圣彼得大教堂由教宗加冕为皇帝——这一幕后来被反复援引,成了教权与皇权关系的原点。1309 年教廷迁到阿维尼翁,罗马一度连教宗都没有了。',
 'Medieval Rome fell to twenty or thirty thousand people, with cattle grazing in the ancient Forum, which the locals called the cow field. In 800 the pope crowned Charlemagne emperor in St Peter\'s — a scene cited ever after as the origin of the whole question of church and empire. In 1309 the papacy moved to Avignon, and for a time Rome did not even have a pope.'],
'罗马|文艺复兴意大利': ['十五世纪教廷回到罗马后大兴土木,想把它重建成基督教世界的首都。1506 年圣彼得大教堂重建动工,前后一百二十年;米开朗基罗画西斯廷天顶用了四年,拉斐尔画梵蒂冈的签字厅。1527 年查理五世的军队洗劫罗马,盛期文艺复兴在这一年被打断。',
 'After the papacy returned in the fifteenth century Rome was rebuilt on a great scale, meant to be the capital of Christendom. Work on the new St Peter\'s began in 1506 and ran a hundred and twenty years; Michelangelo spent four years on the Sistine ceiling and Raphael painted the pope\'s library. In 1527 the armies of Charles V sacked the city, and the High Renaissance was cut off in that year.'],
'雅典|米诺斯·迈锡尼': ['迈锡尼时代的雅典卫城上已经有一座设防的宫殿,城墙用巨石垒成,后人以为是独眼巨人所砌,称之为「巨石墙」。青铜时代大崩溃时,伯罗奔尼撒的迈锡尼、皮洛斯等宫殿都被焚毁,雅典却似乎没有被攻破——后来的雅典人一直以此自豪,说自己是「土生土长」的。',
 'By Mycenaean times there was a fortified palace on the Athenian acropolis, walled with blocks so large that later Greeks credited them to the Cyclopes. When the Bronze Age collapsed, the palaces at Mycenae and Pylos burned, but Athens seems not to have been taken — a point later Athenians were proud of, claiming they had sprung from their own soil.'],
'雅典|罗马共和国': ['前 146 年罗马征服希腊,雅典成为罗马的属地,但享有相当的自治。罗马贵族把子弟送到雅典读哲学,西塞罗年轻时就在这里跟着学园派的哲学家读过书——政治上被征服的城市,在文化上反过来征服了征服者。前 86 年苏拉围城,雅典遭到严重破坏。',
 'Rome conquered Greece in 146 BC and Athens became subject territory, though with a good deal of self-government. Roman nobles sent their sons here to study philosophy — Cicero among them, as a young man under an Academic philosopher — so that a city conquered politically conquered its conquerors in culture. In 86 BC Sulla besieged Athens and did it serious damage.'],
'雅典|罗马帝国': ['哈德良皇帝爱雅典,在这里建了图书馆和奥林匹亚宙斯神庙——那座神庙从前六世纪动工,拖了六百多年,到他手上才完工;城里那座「哈德良拱门」则是雅典人为他立的。罗马帝国时期的雅典是地中海世界的大学城,529 年查士丁尼下令关闭雅典的哲学学校,不过这道命令实际造成多大影响,学界至今仍有争论。',
 'The emperor Hadrian loved Athens and gave it a library and the temple of Olympian Zeus — begun in the sixth century BC and left unfinished for six hundred years until he completed it; the arch that carries his name was raised by the Athenians in his honour. Under the empire Athens was the university town of the Mediterranean. Justinian ordered its philosophical schools closed in 529, though how much that decree actually changed is still debated.'],
'雅典|拜占庭': ['拜占庭治下的雅典是个小城。帕特农神庙被改成教堂,供奉圣母;卫城成了要塞。1204 年第四次十字军之后,雅典落到西欧封建领主手里,先后由勃艮第人、加泰罗尼亚人、佛罗伦萨人统治——这段历史今天很少有人提起。',
 'Athens under Byzantium was a small town. The Parthenon was turned into a church of the Virgin and the acropolis into a fortress. After the Fourth Crusade in 1204 the city passed to western feudal lords and was ruled in turn by Burgundians, Catalans and Florentines — a stretch of its history now seldom mentioned.'],
'雅典|奥斯曼帝国': ['1458 年奥斯曼取雅典,帕特农神庙改作清真寺,加了一座宣礼塔。1687 年威尼斯军队围攻卫城,一发炮弹击中奥斯曼存放在神庙里的火药,把这座立了两千年的建筑炸开——今天看到的残破样子,就是那一炮留下的。',
 'The Ottomans took Athens in 1458 and the Parthenon became a mosque with a minaret added. In 1687 a Venetian army besieged the acropolis and a shell struck the powder the Ottomans had stored inside the temple, blowing open a building that had stood two thousand years — the ruin seen today is what that one shell left.'],
'马德里|罗马共和国': ['罗马征服伊比利亚是从前 218 年第二次布匿战争开始的,前后打了两百年才彻底平定。马德里这个位置在罗马时代没有城市,附近的大城是托莱多与塞哥维亚——塞哥维亚的引水渠至今仍横在城中。',
 'Rome\'s conquest of Iberia began with the Second Punic War in 218 BC and took two centuries to complete. There was no town where Madrid now stands in Roman times; the cities of the region were Toledo and Segovia — and Segovia\'s aqueduct still strides across it.'],
'马德里|罗马帝国': ['罗马治下的西班牙出过三位皇帝——图拉真、哈德良与狄奥多西,还有塞内加、卢坎这些作家。伊比利亚的橄榄油、酒与银经海路运往罗马,是帝国最富庶的行省之一;而马德里所在的这片高原当时只有零星村落。',
 'Roman Spain produced three emperors — Trajan, Hadrian and Theodosius — and writers such as Seneca and Lucan. Iberian oil, wine and silver went to Rome by sea and the peninsula was among the richest provinces of the empire, while the plateau where Madrid stands held only scattered villages.'],
'马德里|后倭马亚·安达卢斯': ['九世纪后期,科尔多瓦的埃米尔在这里筑起一座边境要塞,守着通往托莱多的山口,取名「马格里特」——「马德里」这个名字就从这里来。城中至今留着一段安达卢斯时期的城墙,是这座城最古老的建筑。',
 'Late in the ninth century the emir of Cordoba built a frontier fort here to guard the pass toward Toledo and called it Mayrit — the origin of the name Madrid. A stretch of that Andalusi wall still stands in the city, its oldest structure.'],
'马德里|中世纪西欧': ['1085 年卡斯蒂利亚国王阿方索六世取托莱多,马德里随之易手。此后四百年它只是卡斯蒂利亚的一座小城,人口几千;它被选作都城是 1561 年的事,靠的不是自身的分量,而是位置——正好在半岛中央。',
 'Alfonso VI of Castile took Toledo in 1085 and Madrid changed hands with it. For the next four centuries it was a small Castilian town of a few thousand people. Its selection as capital came in 1561, and owed nothing to its own importance — only to its position at the centre of the peninsula.'],
'里斯本|罗马共和国': ['罗马人前 138 年前后取得这一带。又过了约一百年,塔霍河口的这座城镇才被设为自治市,称「费利西塔斯·尤利亚·奥利西波」。这里出产的鱼酱经海路运往罗马,是当时的名产;老城地下至今能看到罗马时代的剧场与鱼酱作坊遗址。',
 'The Romans took this region around 138 BC. About a century later the town at the mouth of the Tagus was made a municipium, Felicitas Julia Olisipo. The fish sauce made here went to Rome by sea and was well known; a Roman theatre and the vats of the fish-sauce works can still be seen under the old town.'],
'里斯本|罗马帝国': ['罗马治下的奥利西波是卢西塔尼亚行省的重要港口。塔霍河口水深、避风,又正对着大西洋——这个地理条件在罗马时代只是方便沿海航运,一千四百年后却让这座城成了通往印度与巴西的起点。',
 'Olisipo under the empire was an important port of the province of Lusitania. The mouth of the Tagus is deep and sheltered and faces the open Atlantic — a geography that in Roman times merely eased coastal shipping, but fourteen centuries later made this the city from which ships left for India and Brazil.'],
'里斯本|后倭马亚·安达卢斯': ['711 年穆斯林军队渡海进入伊比利亚,里斯本随之易手,城名成了「阿尔·乌什布纳」。此后四百多年这里是安达卢斯的西北边城,几度在基督教王国与穆斯林政权之间易手,直到 1147 年阿方索一世借第二次十字军的船队攻下它。',
 'Muslim armies crossed into Iberia in 711 and Lisbon changed hands with the rest, becoming al-Ushbuna. For over four centuries it was a northwestern frontier town of al-Andalus, taken and retaken between Christian kingdoms and Muslim powers, until Afonso I captured it in 1147 with the help of a Second Crusade fleet.'],
'柏林|中世纪西欧': ['柏林与对岸的科隆是十三世纪初出现在施普雷河两岸的一对贸易小镇,1237 年第一次见于文书,那一年后来被定为建城年。它们靠河上的渡口与商路起家,1307 年结盟共用一座市政厅,1359 年加入汉萨同盟,直到 1432 年才正式合并成一座城——那时它离「首都」还很远。',
 'Berlin and Cölln across the water were a pair of trading towns that appeared on the banks of the Spree early in the thirteenth century; the first document naming one of them dates from 1237, now taken as the city\'s founding year. They lived off the crossing and the trade road, allied in 1307 to share one town hall, joined the Hanseatic League in 1359, and only formally merged into a single town in 1432 — still a long way from being anyone\'s capital.'],
'维也纳|罗马帝国': ['罗马人在多瑙河南岸建起军营温多博纳,是潘诺尼亚行省的边防据点,驻扎着一个军团。皇帝马可·奥勒留在多瑙河前线征战多年,180 年很可能就死在这里;他的《沉思录》有一部分就是在这条战线上写的。',
 'The Romans built the legionary camp of Vindobona on the south bank of the Danube, a frontier post of the province of Pannonia. The emperor Marcus Aurelius campaigned for years on this front and very likely died here in 180; part of his Meditations was written along this line.'],
'布拉格|德意志': ['1918 年捷克斯洛伐克独立,布拉格成为首都。1938 年慕尼黑协定把苏台德地区划给德国,次年德军进占布拉格,捷克成为「波希米亚和摩拉维亚保护国」,直到 1945 年。这段历史今天仍是欧洲讨论「绥靖」时最常引的例子。',
 'Czechoslovakia became independent in 1918 with Prague as its capital. The Munich agreement of 1938 handed the Sudetenland to Germany, German troops entered Prague the following year and the Czech lands became the Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia until 1945 — still the case most often cited in Europe when appeasement is discussed.'],
'华沙|德意志': ['1939 年德国入侵波兰,华沙被围后陷落。1943 年犹太人在隔都起义,1944 年全城起义,两次都被镇压;德军随后按计划系统炸毁这座城,战后估计八成以上的建筑被毁。今天的华沙老城是 1950 年后照着战前的图纸与画作重建的,1980 年因此列入世界遗产。',
 'Germany invaded Poland in 1939 and Warsaw fell after a siege. The ghetto rose in 1943 and the whole city rose in 1944; both were crushed, and German forces then demolished the city systematically to plan, destroying an estimated four-fifths or more of its buildings. The old town standing today was rebuilt from 1950 on, worked up from prewar drawings and paintings, and was listed as World Heritage in 1980 for that reason.'],
'基辅|波兰-立陶宛': ['1569 年卢布林联合后,基辅由立陶宛转归波兰王国管辖。这一时期第聂伯河下游的哥萨克逐渐成势,1648 年赫梅利尼茨基起义把波兰在乌克兰的统治打垮;1667 年安德鲁索沃停战,第聂伯河以东归了俄国;基辅本来只说交割两年,直到 1686 年的《永久和约》才定死。',
 'After the Union of Lublin in 1569, Kyiv passed from Lithuania to the Polish crown. In these years the Cossacks of the lower Dnieper grew strong, and Khmelnytsky\'s rising of 1648 broke Polish rule in Ukraine; by the truce of Andrusovo in 1667 the land east of the Dnieper went to Russia, while Kyiv itself was handed over for two years only — not settled for good until the treaty of 1686.'],
'基辅|俄罗斯·苏联': ['1686 年的《永久和约》把基辅定给俄国,此后两百多年是俄罗斯帝国的一座省城。1932 至 1933 年的大饥荒(乌克兰称「霍洛多莫尔」,1933 年最烈)在乌克兰造成数百万人死亡;1941 至 1943 年基辅被德军占领,巴比亚尔的屠杀就发生在城郊。1991 年苏联解体,基辅成为独立的乌克兰的首都。',
 'The treaty of 1686 confirmed Kyiv as Russian, and for over two centuries it was a provincial capital of the Russian empire for over two centuries. The famine of 1932 and 1933, which Ukrainians call the Holodomor and which was worst in 1933, killed millions there; the Germans occupied Kyiv from 1941 to 1943 and the massacre at Babi Yar took place on its outskirts. With the collapse of the Soviet Union in 1991 Kyiv became the capital of an independent Ukraine.'],
'阿姆斯特丹|中世纪西欧': ['十三世纪人们在阿姆斯特尔河上筑坝防潮,坝边的聚落就叫「阿姆斯特尔丹」——这个名字的意思就是「阿姆斯特尔河上的坝」。1275 年伯爵给了它免税通行的特许,这座城从此靠转运波罗的海的谷物与鲱鱼起家。',
 'In the thirteenth century a dam was thrown across the Amstel against the tides, and the settlement beside it was called Amstelredam — the dam on the Amstel. In 1275 the count granted it freedom from tolls, and the city began its rise on Baltic grain and herring.'],
'麦罗埃|库施·努比亚': ['库施把都城从纳帕塔迁到麦罗埃后,发展出自己的文字与冶铁业。王陵是一片陡峭的小金字塔,苏丹境内留下的金字塔数量比埃及还多;麦罗埃文字的音值已被读出,语言却至今还读不全。',
 'After Kush moved its capital from Napata to Meroe it developed its own script and an ironworking industry. Its royal tombs are steep little pyramids — Sudan holds more pyramids than Egypt does — and Meroitic can be sounded out but the language is still not properly understood.'],
'撒马尔罕|粟特': ['粟特人是丝绸之路的实际经营者,撒马尔罕是他们的老家。他们的商队铺满欧亚,粟特语一度是丝路上的通用商业语言;敦煌以西烽燧下出土的一批粟特家书,写着账目、行情,还有「洛阳被烧了」这样的坏消息。',
 'The Sogdians were the people who actually ran the Silk Road, and Samarkand was their home. Their caravans spread across Eurasia and Sogdian served for a time as the road\'s commercial lingua franca; a bundle of Sogdian letters found under a watchtower west of Dunhuang carries accounts, prices — and news that Luoyang had burned.'],
'伊斯法罕|萨法维·波斯': ['1598 年前后阿拔斯大帝迁都伊斯法罕,在城中辟出一个巨大的广场,四边是清真寺、宫殿与集市。当地谚语称它「半个世界」——这座城的建筑群至今是伊朗最著名的建筑群之一。',
 'Around 1598 Shah Abbas moved his capital to Isfahan and laid out an enormous square there, with a mosque, a palace and a bazaar on its sides. A local saying calls it "half the world"; its ensemble of buildings remains among the most celebrated in Iran.'],
'斯德哥尔摩|瑞典帝国': ['十七世纪的瑞典靠着铜矿、铁矿与一支训练有素的军队,把波罗的海几乎变成内海。1628 年新造的战舰瓦萨号在斯德哥尔摩港内驶出不到一海里就翻沉了;1961 年整船被打捞出水,今天在专门的博物馆里展出。',
 'Seventeenth-century Sweden — copper, iron and a well-drilled army — turned the Baltic into something close to a home lake. In 1628 the new warship Vasa capsized less than a nautical mile out of Stockholm harbour; salvaged whole in 1961, she is now shown in a museum built for her.'],
'阿姆斯特丹|荷兰共和国': ['十七世纪的阿姆斯特丹是欧洲的金融与航运中心:阿姆斯特丹银行、世界上最早的股票交易所之一都在这里,东印度公司的股票就在这座城里买卖。1637 年郁金香球茎的价格崩盘,是后世常被引用的早期投机泡沫。',
 'Seventeenth-century Amsterdam was Europe\'s hub of finance and shipping: the Bank of Amsterdam and one of the world\'s first stock exchanges were here, and shares in the East India Company changed hands in this city. When tulip bulb prices collapsed in 1637, it left one of the most cited early speculative bubbles.'],
/* v203:补 v188 新增城市的空行(苏州等) */
'杭州|春秋': ['春秋时杭州一带属越国,还谈不上城市:今天市区大半还是钱塘江口的浅海与滩涂,聚落散在西边的山脚。越王勾践卧薪尝胆的都城在会稽(今绍兴),杭州只是越国北境靠近吴国的边地。',
 'In the Spring and Autumn period this was Yue territory and not yet a town: most of today\'s city was still shallows and mudflats at the mouth of the Qiantang, with settlements scattered along the hills to the west. King Goujian\'s capital was at Kuaiji, today\'s Shaoxing; Hangzhou was Yue\'s northern borderland facing Wu.'],
'苏州|春秋': ['传为前 514 年伍子胥为吴王阖闾筑阖闾大城,城址就在今天的苏州古城,水陆城门各八座——中国许多城市换过地方,苏州两千五百年基本没挪。吴国从这里北上争霸,前 473 年被越所灭。',
 'Tradition has Wu Zixu laying out the great city of Helü for the king of Wu in 514 BC, on the site of today\'s old town, with eight land gates and eight water gates — many Chinese cities have moved, Suzhou has barely shifted in two and a half thousand years. From here Wu pushed north to contend for hegemony; Yue destroyed it in 473 BC.'],
'苏州|战国': ['吴亡后先属越,前 333 年前后楚灭越,这里归了楚国;战国末年楚考烈王封春申君黄歇于吴地,苏州民间至今有城隍供春申君的说法。此时的城仍是阖闾大城的格局,是江南少数成规模的城邑之一。',
 'After Wu fell the place passed to Yue, and when Chu destroyed Yue around 333 BC it went to Chu; at the end of the period the king of Chu enfeoffed Lord Chunshen here, and Suzhou folklore still makes him the city god. The town kept Helü\'s layout, one of the few sizeable walled towns in the lower Yangtze.'],
'苏州|秦': ['秦置会稽郡,郡治就设在吴县,即今苏州——它是秦帝国东南一隅的行政中心。前 209 年项梁、项羽叔侄就在这里杀郡守起兵,次年带着八千江东子弟渡江北上。',
 'The Qin created Kuaiji commandery and put its seat at Wu county, today\'s Suzhou — the administrative centre of the empire\'s south-eastern corner. In 209 BC Xiang Liang and his nephew Xiang Yu killed the governor here and rose in revolt, crossing the Yangtze north the next year with eight thousand men of the region.'],
'苏州|西汉': ['西汉的吴县仍是会稽郡治,管着今天江浙沿海一大片。前 154 年吴王刘濞发动七国之乱,他的都城在广陵(今扬州),会稽郡是他封国的一部分,铸钱煮盐积下的家底不少就出自这一带;乱平后朝廷对东南的控制加紧,但地方仍以农渔为主,远不及中原繁华。',
 'Under the Western Han Wu county remained the seat of Kuaiji commandery, governing a wide stretch of the Jiangsu-Zhejiang coast. In 154 BC Liu Pi, king of Wu, launched the Revolt of the Seven Kingdoms from his capital at Guangling, today\'s Yangzhou; Kuaiji was part of his kingdom, and much of the wealth he had built from minting coins and boiling salt came from this region; after the revolt the court tightened its grip on the south-east, but the area lived on farming and fishing, far behind the central plain.'],
'苏州|东汉': ['东汉顺帝时把会稽郡一分为二,129 年吴县成为新设的吴郡的郡治——「吴郡」这个名字从此和苏州绑在一起。东汉末年北方大乱,南下的人口开始增多,孙氏一族就是从吴郡富春起家的。',
 'In 129 the Eastern Han split Kuaiji in two and Wu county became the seat of the new Wu commandery — a name tied to Suzhou ever since. As the north fell apart at the end of the dynasty more people began moving south; the Sun family that would found the state of Wu rose from Fuchun in this commandery.'],
'苏州|三国': ['孙权的父兄起家于吴郡,吴郡是东吴最早的根据地之一;后来都城定在建业(今南京),苏州成了东吴腹地富庶的郡治。孙吴在太湖流域大规模屯田,是江南开发加速的开端。',
 'The Sun brothers rose in Wu commandery, one of the earliest bases of the state of Wu; when the capital settled at Jianye, today\'s Nanjing, Suzhou became a prosperous commandery seat in the interior. Wu ran large military-agricultural colonies around Lake Tai — the beginning of the accelerated opening-up of the lower Yangtze.'],
'苏州|西晋': ['西晋短暂统一,吴郡的世家大族(顾、陆、朱、张)在朝中有了位置,陆机、陆云兄弟就是吴郡人,北上洛阳以文才闻名。永嘉之乱后北方士族大批南渡,吴地是主要落脚点之一。',
 'Under the brief Western Jin unification the great clans of Wu commandery — the Gu, Lu, Zhu and Zhang — found places at court; the brothers Lu Ji and Lu Yun, natives of Wu, went north to Luoyang and were famous for their writing. After the disorder of the Yongjia era the northern gentry came south in numbers, and the Wu region was one of their main landing places.'],
'苏州|东晋·十六国': ['东晋偏安建康,吴郡是京畿以东最富的地方,南渡的北方大族与本地吴姓大族在这里并存、也常有摩擦。这一时期太湖周边的圩田大量开垦,苏州一带开始有「鱼米」之名。',
 'With the Eastern Jin settled at Jiankang, Wu commandery was the richest place east of the capital, where the northern émigré clans and the native Wu clans lived side by side and often rubbed against each other. Diked polder fields spread around Lake Tai in these years, and the region began to be known for fish and rice.'],
'苏州|南北朝': ['南朝宋齐梁陈都以建康为都,吴郡是南朝最重要的粮仓与赋税来源之一。梁武帝时佛寺大盛,苏州城内外的许多古寺(如寒山寺的前身)相传创于此时;侯景之乱(548—552)江南残破,吴郡也受重创。',
 'The Southern Dynasties all ruled from Jiankang, and Wu commandery was among their most important granaries and sources of tax. Buddhism flourished under Emperor Wu of Liang, and many old temples in and around Suzhou — the forerunner of Hanshan Temple among them — are traditionally dated to this time; the Hou Jing rebellion of 548-552 devastated the lower Yangtze, Wu included.'],
'苏州|隋': ['589 年隋灭陈,废吴郡改置苏州——因城西的姑苏山得名,「苏州」这个名字第一次出现。大运河江南段(江南河)在隋炀帝时开通,苏州从此在运河线上,南北漕运都要经过这里。',
 'When the Sui destroyed Chen in 589 they abolished Wu commandery and created Suzhou, named after Gusu hill west of the city — the first appearance of the name. The southern section of the Grand Canal was opened under Emperor Yang, and from then on Suzhou sat on the canal, with grain and goods between north and south passing through.'],
'苏州|唐': ['唐代苏州是江南东道的大州,人口与赋税在全国名列前茅,韦应物、白居易、刘禹锡先后来做刺史。白居易在任时开凿山塘河、筑山塘街,从阊门通到虎丘,至今还是苏州最有名的一条街;张继的《枫桥夜泊》写的也是这里。',
 'Under the Tang Suzhou was a great prefecture of Jiangnan, near the top of the empire in population and tax, and Wei Yingwu, Bai Juyi and Liu Yuxi each served as its prefect. Bai Juyi had the Shantang canal and street cut from Chang gate out to Tiger Hill, still Suzhou\'s most famous street; Zhang Ji\'s poem on a night mooring at Maple Bridge was written here.'],
'苏州|五代十国': ['五代时苏州属吴越国,钱氏几代人不打仗、修水利,在太湖流域设撩浅军专管疏浚河道,苏州的塘浦圩田体系在这时定型。978 年钱弘俶纳土归宋,苏州没经过战火就进入了宋朝。',
 'In the Five Dynasties Suzhou belonged to Wuyue, whose Qian rulers for several generations avoided war and built waterworks, keeping a standing corps to dredge the channels around Lake Tai; the system of dikes, canals and polders took its lasting shape then. In 978 Qian Hongchu handed his lands to the Song, and Suzhou passed into the new dynasty without a battle.'],
'苏州|北宋': ['北宋的苏州是平江军,太湖流域的稻米已是朝廷仰赖的粮源(「苏湖熟,天下足」的谚语见于南宋文献)。1035 年范仲淹知苏州,创办府学,把自己的宅地捐出来办学——苏州文庙府学从此成为江南文风的源头之一;城内的园林在这时已经不少。',
 'Under the Northern Song Suzhou was Pingjiang, and the court already leaned on the rice of the Lake Tai basin — the saying that when Su and Hu have a good harvest the whole realm is fed appears in Southern Song writings. In 1035 Fan Zhongyan governed Suzhou and founded the prefectural school, giving up his own house-plot for it — the Confucian temple and school became one of the wellsprings of learning in the lower Yangtze; the town already had many gardens.'],
'苏州|南宋': ['南宋定都临安(杭州)后,苏州就在都城旁边,更加富庶。1229 年刻的《平江图》碑至今立在苏州文庙,是现存最早的中国城市平面图之一,上面的河道、桥梁、坊巷布局与今天的古城大体能对上。',
 'With the Southern Song capital at Lin\'an, today\'s Hangzhou, Suzhou lay right beside the court and grew richer still. The Pingjiang map, cut in stone in 1229 and still standing in the Confucian temple, is among the oldest surviving city plans in China, and its canals, bridges and lanes can largely be matched to the old town today.'],
'苏州|蒙古帝国': ['1276 年元军进入平江府,苏州并入蒙古人的版图。蒙古帝国的这段年代对苏州而言就是元朝:城没有被毁,运河与市面很快恢复,不久之后马可·波罗笔下的「苏州」已是商贾云集的大城。',
 'Yuan troops entered Pingjiang in 1276 and Suzhou passed into the Mongol realm. For Suzhou these years simply mean the Yuan: the city was not destroyed, the canal and the markets soon recovered, and before long the Suzhou of Marco Polo\'s account was a great city crowded with merchants.'],
'苏州|元': ['元代苏州是平江路治所,棉纺织业开始兴起——黄道婆把海南的棉纺技术带回松江,苏州一带很快跟上。元末张士诚据苏州称吴王达十余年,1367 年朱元璋攻破苏州,张士诚被俘;明初对苏州课以重赋,据说与此有关。',
 'Under the Yuan Suzhou was the seat of Pingjiang circuit, and cotton weaving began to rise — Huang Daopo brought Hainan cotton techniques back to Songjiang and the Suzhou area soon followed. At the end of the dynasty Zhang Shicheng held Suzhou as king of Wu for over a decade; Zhu Yuanzhang took the city in 1367 and captured him, and the heavy taxes the early Ming laid on Suzhou are said to go back to that.'],
'苏州|明': ['明代苏州是全国最富的府之一,丝织与手工业极盛,城里的私家园林大量兴建——拙政园(约 1509)与留园都是这时候的;沈周、文徵明、唐寅、仇英「吴门四家」在这里作画。1601 年织工葛成带头反对矿监税使,是市民抗税的著名事件。',
 'Under the Ming Suzhou was among the richest prefectures in the empire, its silk weaving and crafts at their height, and private gardens went up across the city — the Humble Administrator\'s Garden of about 1509 and the Lingering Garden both date from then; Shen Zhou, Wen Zhengming, Tang Yin and Qiu Ying, the four masters of Wu, painted here. In 1601 the weaver Ge Cheng led a famous protest against the imperial tax agents.'],
'苏州|清': ['清代苏州是江苏巡抚驻地,与南京分掌一省;康熙、乾隆南巡都多次驻跸。苏州的织造府专为宫廷织造丝绸,评弹、苏绣、桃花坞年画都在这一时期成熟,明代成熟的昆曲在清初仍极盛。1860 年太平军占领苏州,1863 年李鸿章淮军收复,城市受创不小。',
 'Under the Qing Suzhou was the seat of the governor of Jiangsu, sharing the province with Nanjing, and the Kangxi and Qianlong emperors stayed here repeatedly on their southern tours. The imperial silk works wove for the palace, and pingtan storytelling, Suzhou embroidery and Taohuawu New Year prints all matured in these years, while Kunqu opera, perfected under the Ming, was still at its height in the early Qing. The Taiping took the city in 1860 and Li Hongzhang\'s Huai army retook it in 1863, at a heavy cost to the town.'],
'苏州|民国': ['民国时苏州是江苏的重要城市但已让位于上海——沪宁铁路 1908 年通车后,苏州成了上海的后院,许多上海富商在这里置园养老。1937 年 11 月苏州陷落,古城与园林在战争中多有损毁。',
 'In the Republic Suzhou remained an important city of Jiangsu but had yielded first place to Shanghai; after the Shanghai-Nanjing railway opened in 1908 it became Shanghai\'s back garden, where wealthy merchants bought gardens to retire to. The city fell in November 1937, and the old town and its gardens suffered in the war.'],
'苏州|共和国': ['1997 年苏州古典园林列入世界文化遗产;1994 年起中新合作的苏州工业园区在城东建起,苏州成为中国制造业最强的地级市之一。古城的格局与《平江图》仍能对上,城墙大部分已拆,只余盘门等几段。',
 'Suzhou\'s classical gardens were listed as World Heritage in 1997, and from 1994 the China-Singapore industrial park rose east of the city, making Suzhou one of the strongest manufacturing cities in the country. The old town still matches the Pingjiang map; most of the walls are gone, with only a few stretches such as Pan Gate left.'],
'大同|战国': ['战国时大同一带是赵国的北境。赵武灵王推行胡服骑射(前 307 年)后向北开拓,设云中、雁门、代三郡,今大同属代郡与雁门郡之间的边地,并沿阴山、桑干河一线筑长城防御林胡、楼烦。',
 'In the Warring States this was the northern frontier of Zhao. After King Wuling adopted nomad dress and mounted archery in 307 BC, Zhao pushed north and set up the Yunzhong, Yanmen and Dai commanderies; the Datong area lay on the border between Dai and Yanmen, and Zhao built long walls along the Yin mountains and the Sanggan river against the Linhu and Loufan.'],
'大同|秦': ['秦统一后这里属雁门郡,设平城县——「平城」是大同最早的名字。蒙恬北击匈奴,把赵国旧长城连缀加固,平城正处在长城线以内不远的地方,是屯兵备边之地。',
 'After the Qin unification the area belonged to Yanmen commandery, with a county called Pingcheng — Datong\'s earliest name. Meng Tian drove the Xiongnu north and joined up and strengthened the old Zhao walls; Pingcheng lay just inside the wall line, a garrison post on the frontier.'],
'大同|西汉': ['前 200 年刘邦亲征匈奴,被冒顿单于围在平城东面的白登山七天七夜,靠陈平之计才脱身——「白登之围」就发生在今大同城东。此后汉朝改行和亲,平城长期是汉匈对峙的前线。',
 'In 200 BC Liu Bang led an army against the Xiongnu and was surrounded by Modu\'s horsemen for seven days on Baideng hill east of Pingcheng, escaping only through Chen Ping\'s stratagem — the Siege of Baideng happened just east of today\'s Datong. The Han then turned to marriage alliances, and Pingcheng stayed a front line between Han and Xiongnu for a long time.'],
'大同|东汉': ['东汉时平城仍属雁门郡,是抵御匈奴、后来是鲜卑的边县。东汉末年边郡人口大量内迁,雁门郡治一度南移,平城一带逐渐荒废,成了鲜卑各部活动的地方。',
 'Under the Eastern Han Pingcheng remained a border county of Yanmen, facing the Xiongnu and then the Xianbei. At the end of the dynasty the frontier population was pulled south and the commandery seat moved inward; the Pingcheng area fell into neglect and became ground for the Xianbei tribes.'],
'大同|三国': ['三国时这里名义上属曹魏并州,实际是拓跋鲜卑南下活动的边地。魏在雁门以北的控制力很弱,平城附近多为鲜卑牧地——一百多年后建都于此的北魏,祖先这时已在附近游牧。',
 'In the Three Kingdoms the area nominally belonged to Wei\'s Bing province, but in practice it was frontier ground where the Tuoba Xianbei were moving south. Wei\'s hold north of Yanmen was weak, and the country around Pingcheng was mostly Xianbei pasture — the ancestors of the Northern Wei, who would make their capital here a century and more later, were already herding nearby.'],
'大同|西晋': ['西晋时拓跋部首领猗卢帮晋朝并州刺史刘琨打匈奴刘渊,310 年被封为代公、得到雁门以北五县,313 年把都城定在盛乐并以平城为南都——大同第一次成为一个政权的都城。',
 'Under the Western Jin the Tuoba chief Yilu helped Liu Kun, the Jin governor of Bing province, against the Xiongnu ruler Liu Yuan; he was made Duke of Dai in 310 and received five counties north of Yanmen, and in 313 set his capital at Shengle with Pingcheng as his southern capital — the first time Datong served as the seat of a state.'],
'大同|南北朝': ['398 年拓跋珪定都平城,北魏在这里建都近一个世纪,是当时北中国的中心。城西武州山的云冈石窟从 460 年前后开凿,昙曜五窟的大佛以北魏皇帝为原型;冯太后的永固陵在城北方山。494 年孝文帝迁都洛阳,平城降为北都,渐趋衰落。',
 'In 398 Tuoba Gui made Pingcheng his capital, and the Northern Wei ruled from here for nearly a century — the centre of northern China. The Yungang grottoes in the Wuzhou hills west of the city were begun around 460, the great Buddhas of the five Tanyao caves modelled on Wei emperors; the Empress Dowager Feng\'s tomb stands on Fang mountain to the north. In 494 Emperor Xiaowen moved the capital to Luoyang and Pingcheng, now the northern capital, slowly declined.'],
'大同|隋': ['隋代这里属马邑郡,是对突厥的前线。隋文帝、炀帝几次北巡,都要沿这一线布防;炀帝在附近的雁门被突厥始毕可汗围困(615 年)是隋朝北边失控的信号。',
 'Under the Sui the area belonged to Mayi commandery, a front line against the Turks. Emperors Wen and Yang both came north on inspection and fortified this line; in 615 Emperor Yang was besieged by the Turkic Shibi Khan at nearby Yanmen — a sign that the northern frontier was slipping.'],
'大同|唐': ['唐代置云州,是河东道北部的边镇,长期与突厥、回鹘、后来的契丹相持;安史之乱后这里驻有重兵。唐末沙陀人李克用以云州一带为根据地起家,五代后唐、后晋、后汉的开国者都出自这一支。',
 'The Tang set up Yun prefecture here, a northern garrison town of the Hedong circuit facing the Turks, the Uyghurs and later the Khitan; after the An Lushan rebellion heavy forces were stationed here. At the end of the Tang the Shatuo leader Li Keyong made the Yun region his base, and the founders of the Later Tang, Later Jin and Later Han of the Five Dynasties all came from that line.'],
'大同|辽': ['938 年石敬瑭把燕云十六州割给契丹,云州从此归辽;1044 年辽升云州为西京大同府——「大同」这个名字由此而来,是辽五京之一。华严寺(1038 年建薄伽教藏殿)与善化寺都是辽代留下的,是今天大同最重要的古建。',
 'In 938 Shi Jingtang ceded the Sixteen Prefectures to the Khitan and Yun prefecture passed to the Liao; in 1044 the Liao raised it to Datong, the Western Capital — the origin of the name, one of the five Liao capitals. The Huayan Monastery, whose sutra hall dates from 1038, and the Shanhua Monastery are Liao works, the most important old buildings in Datong today.'],
'大同|金': ['1122 年金军攻取西京大同,仍以此为西京。金代重修华严寺大雄宝殿(1140 年),是现存辽金木构中最大的佛殿之一;城中的九龙壁虽是明代的,但辽金以来大同一直是山西北部的中心城市。',
 'The Jin took the Western Capital in 1122 and kept it as such. In 1140 the Jin rebuilt the great hall of the Huayan Monastery, among the largest surviving Liao-Jin timber halls; and although the Nine-Dragon Screen is Ming, from Liao and Jin times onward Datong was the chief city of northern Shanxi.'],
'大同|蒙古帝国': ['1211 年成吉思汗伐金,1214 年前后蒙古军攻下西京大同,这里成为蒙古进取中原的前沿。此后大同一带被划为汉地世侯的地盘,城市在战火后逐渐恢复。',
 'Genghis Khan attacked the Jin in 1211, and around 1214 Mongol forces took the Western Capital; Datong became a forward base for the Mongol advance into north China. The region was then given to Chinese hereditary commanders, and the city slowly recovered from the fighting.'],
'大同|元': ['元代设大同路,属中书省。这里是从大都去往漠北、西域的要道之一,驿站繁忙;云冈石窟在元代仍有僧人住持,寺院多有修葺。',
 'Under the Yuan this was Datong circuit, directly under the central secretariat. It lay on one of the main roads from the capital to Mongolia and the western regions, and its post stations were busy; the Yungang caves still had resident monks and their temples were repaired.'],
'大同|明': ['明代大同是「九边」重镇之一,设大同镇,城墙在洪武年间包砖加固,朱元璋十三子代王封在这里,代王府前的九龙壁(1392 年)保存至今。1449 年土木堡之变后大同压力剧增,1550 年俺答汗先犯大同、再东破古北口直逼北京。今天看到的大同城墙轮廓就是明代的。',
 'Under the Ming Datong was one of the Nine Frontier Garrisons; the walls were faced with brick in the Hongwu reign, Zhu Yuanzhang\'s thirteenth son was enfeoffed here as Prince of Dai, and the Nine-Dragon Screen of 1392 that stood before his palace survives. Pressure on Datong rose sharply after the Tumu disaster of 1449, and in 1550 Altan Khan struck Datong first, then broke through Gubeikou to the east and reached Beijing. The outline of the walls seen today is Ming.'],
'大同|清': ['清代大同府是山西北部的商路节点,晋商往来蒙古的驼队多经此地,城里的煤在这时已开始大量开采外运。1900 年前后大同一带曾发生教案与义和团活动。',
 'Under the Qing Datong prefecture was a node on the trade routes of northern Shanxi; the Shanxi merchants\' camel caravans to Mongolia passed through, and coal from the surrounding hills was already being mined and shipped out in quantity. Around 1900 the area saw anti-missionary incidents and Boxer activity.'],
'大同|民国': ['1914 年京绥铁路通到大同,煤矿随之大规模开发。1937 年 9 月日军占领大同,此后八年大同煤矿在日本控制下开采,留下万人坑遗址。',
 'The Beijing-Suiyuan railway reached Datong in 1914 and coal mining expanded on a large scale. Japanese forces occupied the city in September 1937 and worked the mines under their control for eight years, leaving the mass graves of the mine\'s dead.'],
'大同|共和国': ['大同长期是中国最大的煤炭基地之一,有「煤都」之称。2001 年云冈石窟列入世界遗产;2008 年起大同大规模重建古城墙与古城,争议很大——支持者说恢复了辽金明的格局,反对者说是新造古董。',
 'Datong was long one of China\'s largest coal bases, the coal capital. The Yungang grottoes were listed as World Heritage in 2001; from 2008 the city rebuilt its walls and old town on a large scale, a much-argued project — supporters say it restored the Liao-Jin-Ming layout, critics call it new-made antiquity.'],
'太原|春秋': ['前 497 年前后,晋国的赵简子让家臣董安于在汾河西岸筑晋阳城,作为赵氏的根据地——这是太原建城的开始,城址在今太原西南的晋源一带。晋阳城墙用夯土,宫室的柱础是青铜的,后来赵氏被围时曾拆下来铸兵器。',
 'Around 497 BC Zhao Jianzi of Jin had his retainer Dong Anyu build the walled city of Jinyang on the west bank of the Fen — the beginning of Taiyuan, on a site in the Jinyuan district southwest of today\'s city. Its walls were rammed earth, and its palace columns stood on bronze bases, which the Zhao later stripped for weapons when besieged.'],
'太原|战国': ['前 455—前 453 年,智伯联合韩、魏围攻晋阳,决晋水灌城,城中「悬釜而炊」;赵襄子暗中说动韩魏反戈,三家灭智氏,由此「三家分晋」——战国由此开始。晋阳是赵国最早的都城,后来才迁中牟、邯郸。',
 'In 455-453 BC Zhi Bo with Han and Wei besieged Jinyang and diverted the Jin river to flood it — the defenders hung their pots to cook above the water; Zhao Xiangzi secretly won Han and Wei over, the three destroyed the Zhi, and the partition of Jin followed — the start of the Warring States. Jinyang was Zhao\'s first capital before the move to Zhongmou and Handan.'],
'太原|秦': ['前 247 年秦攻取赵国的太原地区,设太原郡,郡治晋阳——「太原」作为地名从此固定下来。秦统一后太原郡是北边的重要屯戍区,与雁门、代郡一起对着匈奴。',
 'In 247 BC Qin took the Taiyuan region from Zhao and set up Taiyuan commandery with its seat at Jinyang — the name Taiyuan has stuck ever since. After unification the commandery was an important garrison area of the north, facing the Xiongnu together with Yanmen and Dai.'],
'太原|西汉': ['汉初这里是代国的地盘,前 196 年刘邦封儿子刘恒为代王,传统上说他都于晋阳(一说中都),十几年后刘恒被迎立为帝,就是汉文帝。西汉在太原郡设并州刺史部,晋阳成了并州的中心。',
 'In the early Han this was the kingdom of Dai; in 196 BC Liu Bang enfeoffed his son Liu Heng here, traditionally said to have ruled from Jinyang, and a dozen years later Liu Heng was called to the throne as Emperor Wen. The Western Han placed the Bing provincial inspectorate in Taiyuan commandery, and Jinyang became the centre of Bing province.'],
'太原|东汉': ['东汉并州刺史治晋阳。48 年南匈奴归附,被安置在并州北部,太原以北成了匈奴与汉人杂居的地方;东汉末年并州刺史丁原带吕布南下,董卓之乱由此牵动。',
 'Under the Eastern Han the inspector of Bing province sat at Jinyang. In 48 the Southern Xiongnu submitted and were settled in northern Bing, and the country north of Taiyuan became mixed Xiongnu and Han; at the end of the dynasty the provincial inspector Ding Yuan brought Lü Bu south, and the turmoil around Dong Zhuo followed.'],
'太原|三国': ['曹魏时并州治晋阳。曹操把内附的南匈奴分成五部安置在并州,左部就在太原附近——一百年后灭西晋的匈奴刘渊,就是从这些部落里起来的。',
 'Under Wei the province of Bing was governed from Jinyang. Cao Cao split the submitted Southern Xiongnu into five divisions and settled them in Bing, the left division near Taiyuan — the Xiongnu leader Liu Yuan who brought down the Western Jin a century later rose from these very tribes.'],
'太原|西晋': ['304 年匈奴刘渊在离石起兵建汉,并州陷入战乱;306 年起并州刺史刘琨据守晋阳十年,孤城抗敌,「闻鸡起舞」的主人公就是他。316 年刘琨兵败,晋阳落入石勒之手。',
 'In 304 the Xiongnu leader Liu Yuan rose at Lishi and founded Han, and Bing province fell into war; from 306 the governor Liu Kun held Jinyang for ten years, an isolated city against the enemy — he is the man of the story who rose at cockcrow to practise the sword. In 316 he was defeated and Jinyang fell to Shi Le.'],
'太原|南北朝': ['东魏、北齐时高欢父子以晋阳为大本营,称「霸府」,北齐时它是与邺城并列的别都,晋阳宫规模宏大;天龙山石窟主要开凿于北齐,晋祠的前身在此时已有记载。577 年北周灭北齐,晋阳城陷。',
 'Under the Eastern Wei and Northern Qi, Gao Huan and his sons made Jinyang their headquarters, the seat of real power, and under the Qi it was a second capital alongside Ye with a great palace; the Tianlongshan grottoes were mostly cut under the Northern Qi, and the forerunner of the Jinci shrine is recorded by then. In 577 the Northern Zhou destroyed the Qi and Jinyang fell.'],
'太原|隋': ['隋代设太原郡,晋阳是北方重镇。617 年李渊任太原留守,就在这里起兵,率军南下取长安,次年建唐——所以唐朝把太原叫「龙兴之地」。',
 'Under the Sui this was Taiyuan commandery, and Jinyang was a key northern stronghold. In 617 Li Yuan, garrison commander of Taiyuan, raised his army here and marched south to take Chang\'an, founding the Tang the following year — which is why the Tang called Taiyuan the place where the dragon rose.'],
'太原|唐': ['唐朝以晋阳为北都,与长安、洛阳并称三都;晋阳有西城、东城、中城三城跨汾河而建,是唐代北方最大的城市之一。武则天、狄仁杰都是太原人;晋祠在唐代已是名胜,李白有诗写「晋祠流水如碧玉」。',
 'The Tang made Jinyang the Northern Capital, one of three with Chang\'an and Luoyang; it had a western, an eastern and a middle city spanning the Fen, among the largest cities of the north. Empress Wu and Di Renjie were both natives of Taiyuan; the Jinci shrine was already famous, and Li Bai wrote of its water running clear as jade.'],
'太原|五代十国': ['五代的开国者接连从晋阳起家:后唐李存勖、后晋石敬瑭、后汉刘知远都以太原为根据地南下称帝;951 年刘崇在晋阳建北汉,靠契丹支持苦撑二十八年。979 年宋太宗灭北汉,下令火烧、水灌晋阳古城,一座一千四百多年的城由此毁灭。',
 'One founder after another rose from Jinyang in the Five Dynasties: Li Cunxu of the Later Tang, Shi Jingtang of the Later Jin and Liu Zhiyuan of the Later Han all used Taiyuan as their base to march south and take the throne; in 951 Liu Chong founded the Northern Han here and held out for twenty-eight years on Khitan support. In 979 the Song emperor Taizong destroyed the Northern Han and had the ancient city of Jinyang burned and flooded — a town of fourteen centuries wiped out.'],
'太原|金': ['1125 年金军南下,太原被围九个月,守将王禀死守到 1126 年城破——太原一失,开封门户洞开。金代太原是河东北路的治所,晋祠圣母殿前的献殿(1168 年)是金代建筑,殿前的鱼沼飞梁则是北宋之物。',
 'In 1125 the Jin came south and besieged Taiyuan for nine months; the commander Wang Bing held out until the city fell in 1126, and with Taiyuan gone the road to Kaifeng lay open. Under the Jin Taiyuan was the seat of the northern Hedong circuit, and the offering hall of 1168 in front of the Hall of the Holy Mother at Jinci is a Jin building; the flying bridge before it is Northern Song.'],
'太原|蒙古帝国': ['1218 年前后木华黎率蒙古军攻取太原,此后太原属蒙古汉地。城市在金末战乱中残破,蒙古时期由汉人世侯管理,逐渐恢复。',
 'Around 1218 Muqali\'s Mongol army took Taiyuan, and the city passed into the Mongol-held Chinese lands. Damaged in the wars of the late Jin, it was run by Chinese hereditary commanders under the Mongols and slowly recovered.'],
'太原|元': ['元代设冀宁路,治太原,属中书省;马可·波罗从大都西行时经过「太原府」,记下这里出产葡萄酒和丝。城里的纯阳宫、崇善寺前身等在元代已有。',
 'Under the Yuan this was Jining circuit, seated at Taiyuan under the central secretariat; Marco Polo passed through Taiyuan on his way west from the capital and noted its wine and silk. Temples such as the Chunyang palace and the forerunner of the Chongshan Monastery were already here.'],
'太原|明': ['1370 年朱元璋封三子朱棡为晋王,晋王府在城中,太原城扩建为周长二十四里的大城,是九边太原镇的所在。崇善寺(1381 年)是晋王为母亲马皇后所建;今天太原老城的街道格局大体是明代定下的。',
 'In 1370 Zhu Yuanzhang made his third son Zhu Gang Prince of Jin; his palace stood in the city, which was enlarged into a great walled town of twenty-four li round, seat of the Taiyuan garrison of the Nine Frontiers. The Chongshan Monastery of 1381 was built by the prince for his mother, Empress Ma; the street plan of the old town largely dates from the Ming.'],
'太原|清': ['清代太原是山西巡抚驻地,晋商的票号总号多在祁县、平遥、太谷,但太原是全省行政中心。1900 年义和团运动中山西巡抚毓贤在太原杀害传教士,成为八国联军索赔的重要事由。',
 'Under the Qing Taiyuan was the seat of the governor of Shanxi; the head offices of the great Shanxi banks were in Qixian, Pingyao and Taigu, but Taiyuan was the province\'s administrative centre. In 1900 the governor Yuxian had missionaries killed here during the Boxer movement, one of the main grounds for the indemnities demanded by the foreign powers.'],
'太原|民国': ['1911 年太原新军响应武昌起义,阎锡山由此掌握山西,一直统治到 1949 年,前后三十八年,山西一度以修铁路、办工业出名。1937 年太原会战后 11 月太原陷落;1949 年 4 月太原战役是解放战争中打得最久的城市攻坚战之一。',
 'In 1911 the new army at Taiyuan answered the Wuchang rising, and Yan Xishan took control of Shanxi, ruling it until 1949 — thirty-eight years in which the province was known for its railways and industry. After the Battle of Taiyuan the city fell in November 1937; the siege of April 1949 was one of the longest city battles of the civil war.'],
'太原|共和国': ['太原是「一五」时期重点建设的重工业城市,太钢、太重都在这里。晋祠圣母殿(北宋 1023—1032 年建)是中国现存最早的木构大殿之一;晋阳古城遗址近年持续发掘,把 979 年被毁的城一点点找回来。',
 'Taiyuan was one of the heavy-industry cities built up in the First Five-Year Plan, home to the Taiyuan steel and heavy machinery works. The Hall of the Holy Mother at Jinci, built 1023-1032 under the Northern Song, is among the earliest surviving large timber halls in China; excavation of the ancient Jinyang site goes on, slowly recovering the city destroyed in 979.'],
'长沙|秦': ['秦统一后设长沙郡,「长沙」作为郡名从此出现,郡治临湘就在今长沙城区。这里是秦朝南方的边郡,再往南就是南岭与百越之地。',
 'After unification the Qin set up Changsha commandery — the first appearance of the name — with its seat at Linxiang, in today\'s city. It was a southern frontier commandery; beyond it lay the Nanling range and the lands of the Yue.'],
'长沙|西汉': ['前 202 年刘邦封吴芮为长沙王,长沙国是汉初异姓诸侯王里唯一传了几代的;贾谊被贬为长沙王太傅,在这里写下《吊屈原赋》。1972—74 年发掘的马王堆汉墓就是长沙国丞相轪侯利苍一家的墓,墓中辛追夫人的遗体两千一百年不腐,还出土了帛书与素纱襌衣。',
 'In 202 BC Liu Bang made Wu Rui king of Changsha, the only kingdom of the early Han\'s non-imperial kings to last several generations; Jia Yi, demoted to tutor of the king, wrote his lament for Qu Yuan here. The Mawangdui tombs excavated in 1972-74 belonged to the family of Li Cang, chancellor of Changsha and Marquis of Dai: the body of Lady Xin Zhui was still preserved after twenty-one centuries, and silk manuscripts and a gauze robe of a few dozen grams came out of the tomb.'],
'长沙|东汉': ['东汉时长沙王国改为长沙郡,是荆州南部的大郡。相传医圣张仲景曾任长沙太守,坐堂行医的说法即出于此;东汉末孙坚任长沙太守,从这里起兵北上讨董卓。',
 'Under the Eastern Han the kingdom became Changsha commandery, a large one in southern Jing province. Tradition makes the physician Zhang Zhongjing its governor, seeing patients in the yamen hall — the origin of the phrase for a doctor in his consulting room; at the end of the dynasty Sun Jian, governor of Changsha, marched north from here against Dong Zhuo.'],
'长沙|三国': ['三国时长沙属孙吴,是吴国荆州的重要郡。1996 年长沙走马楼出土十余万枚孙吴简牍,是吴国长沙郡的官府档案,记录了赋税、户籍、军粮,数量超过此前出土的全部三国简牍。',
 'In the Three Kingdoms Changsha belonged to Wu, an important commandery of its Jing province. In 1996 more than a hundred thousand Wu bamboo slips were dug up at Zoumalou in the city centre — the archives of Wu\'s Changsha commandery, recording taxes, households and army grain, more than all Three Kingdoms slips found before.'],
'长沙|西晋': ['西晋统一后长沙郡属荆州,是南方比较安定的地区;晋武帝的儿子司马乂曾封长沙王,是八王之乱中的一位。永嘉之乱后北方人口南来,湘江流域也开始接纳移民。',
 'After the Western Jin unification Changsha commandery belonged to Jing province, a relatively settled part of the south; Emperor Wu\'s son Sima Ai held the title Prince of Changsha and was one of the eight princes whose wars wrecked the dynasty. After the Yongjia disorders northerners came south, and the Xiang valley too began taking in migrants.'],
'长沙|东晋·十六国': ['东晋名将陶侃因平定叛乱被封为长沙郡公,他节俭勤政,「陶侃运甓」的故事就是这时候的。湘州(治临湘)西晋 307 年初置、旋废,412 年东晋复置——长沙由此成为一级政区的中心。',
 'The Eastern Jin general Tao Kan was made Duke of Changsha for putting down a rebellion; frugal and hard-working, he is the man of the story who carried bricks in and out every day to keep fit. Xiang province, seated at Linxiang, had been created briefly by the Western Jin in 307; the Eastern Jin re-established it in 412, and Changsha became the centre of a top-level province.'],
'长沙|南北朝': ['南朝时湘州治所在长沙,宋齐梁陈都在这里驻重臣;梁武帝时长沙寺庙渐多,岳麓山的道林寺相传创于此时。侯景之乱中湘州是南朝残存力量的据点之一。',
 'Under the Southern Dynasties Xiang province was governed from Changsha, and Song, Qi, Liang and Chen each posted senior men here; temples multiplied under Emperor Wu of Liang, and the Daolin Temple on Yuelu hill is traditionally dated to then. During the Hou Jing rebellion Xiang province was one of the strongholds of what remained of the southern court.'],
'长沙|隋': ['589 年隋灭陈后改湘州为潭州——因城南湘江中的昭潭得名,「潭州」这个名字一直用到元代。隋代长沙是通往岭南的必经之地。',
 'After destroying Chen in 589 the Sui renamed Xiang province Tan prefecture, after the Zhao pool in the Xiang river south of the city — a name that lasted into the Yuan. Under the Sui Changsha lay on the road every traveller to Lingnan had to take.'],
'长沙|唐': ['唐代潭州属江南西道,湘江边的长沙窑(铜官窑)烧出釉下彩瓷器,通过扬州、广州大量外销,西亚、东非都出土过它的碎片。769 年杜甫漂泊到潭州,次年春在这里写下「正是江南好风景,落花时节又逢君」,同年冬在湘江舟中去世。',
 'Under the Tang, Tan prefecture belonged to the Jiangnan West circuit; the Changsha kilns at Tongguan on the Xiang fired underglaze-painted wares that were exported in quantity through Yangzhou and Guangzhou — sherds have turned up in West Asia and East Africa. In 769 Du Fu drifted to Tanzhou; the next spring he wrote here his poem on meeting an old friend among the falling blossoms, and that winter he died on a boat on the Xiang.'],
'长沙|五代十国': ['907 年马殷据潭州建楚国,史称马楚,是十国里唯一以湖南为根基的政权;马殷鼓励种茶、行商,把茶叶卖到北方换战马。951 年马楚在内乱中被南唐所灭。',
 'In 907 Ma Yin set up the state of Chu at Tanzhou — Ma\'s Chu — the only one of the Ten Kingdoms based in Hunan; he encouraged tea-growing and trade, selling tea north in exchange for war horses. In 951 the state, torn by family strife, was destroyed by the Southern Tang.'],
'长沙|北宋': ['976 年潭州太守朱洞在岳麓山下创办岳麓书院,1015 年宋真宗赐额,成为「天下四大书院」之一;北宋潭州是荆湖南路的治所,湘江上的商船与米船往来不绝。',
 'In 976 the prefect Zhu Dong founded the Yuelu Academy at the foot of Yuelu hill; Emperor Zhenzong gave it its name-board in 1015 and it became one of the four great academies of the empire. Under the Northern Song Tanzhou was the seat of the Jinghu South circuit, and the Xiang was busy with merchant boats and rice barges.'],
'长沙|南宋': ['1167 年朱熹到潭州与张栻在岳麓书院会讲,听讲的人多到「饮马池水立涸」,是理学史上的名场面。1275 年元军围潭州,知州李芾率军民死守三个月,1276 年初城破时全家殉难,史称长沙保卫战。',
 'In 1167 Zhu Xi came to Tanzhou to debate with Zhang Shi at the Yuelu Academy, before crowds so large that the horse-pond was said to have run dry — a famous scene in the history of Neo-Confucianism. In 1275 the Yuan besieged Tanzhou; the prefect Li Fu held out for three months and died with his family when the city fell early in 1276.'],
'长沙|蒙古帝国': ['1276 年初元军攻破潭州,湖南全境归入蒙古人的版图。城市在围城中残破,此后逐步恢复,岳麓书院不久也重开。',
 'Yuan forces took Tanzhou early in 1276, and all of Hunan passed into the Mongol realm. The city was badly damaged in the siege, recovered step by step, and the Yuelu Academy soon reopened.'],
'长沙|元': ['元代先为潭州路,1329 年改名天临路。这里是湖广行省的重要城市,湘江水运把湖南的米运往长江下游。',
 'Under the Yuan this was Tanzhou circuit, renamed Tianlin circuit in 1329, an important city of the Huguang province; the Xiang carried Hunan\'s rice down to the lower Yangtze.'],
'长沙|明': ['1372 年改设长沙府,「长沙」重新成为正式地名;朱元璋第八子潭王朱梓封在长沙,后来吉王(明英宗之子朱见浚,1477 年就藩)接着用这座王府,占了城中很大一块。明代长沙府是湖广的粮仓,「湖广熟,天下足」的说法在这时流传开。',
 'In 1372 the Ming set up Changsha prefecture and the name Changsha became official again; Zhu Yuanzhang\'s eighth son was enfeoffed here as Prince of Tan, and later the Prince of Ji — a son of the Zhengtong emperor, installed in 1477 — used the same palace, which took up a large part of the town. Ming Changsha was the granary of Huguang, and the saying that when Huguang has a good harvest the realm is fed spread in these years.'],
'长沙|清': ['1664 年湖广分省,长沙成为湖南巡抚驻地,湖南从此作为一省存在。1852 年太平军围攻长沙八十一天未克,西王萧朝贵在城下阵亡;此后曾国藩在湖南练湘军,长沙是湘军的大后方。岳麓书院在清末改为湖南高等学堂。',
 'In 1664 Huguang was split and Changsha became the seat of the governor of Hunan — the province has existed ever since. In 1852 the Taiping besieged the city for eighty-one days without taking it, and their Western King Xiao Chaogui was killed beneath the walls; Zeng Guofan then raised the Hunan Army in the province, with Changsha as its base. At the end of the dynasty the Yuelu Academy became the Hunan Higher School.'],
'长沙|民国': ['1938 年 11 月国民政府因误传日军逼近而放火焚城,「文夕大火」烧掉了长沙大半座城;1939—1944 年间四次长沙会战在城郊反复拉锯。毛泽东青年时期在长沙求学、办《湘江评论》,橘子洲头的诗写的就是这里。',
 'In November 1938 the Nationalist government, on a false report that the Japanese were near, set the city on fire — the Wenxi fire burned most of Changsha; the four Battles of Changsha of 1939-1944 were fought back and forth around its outskirts. Mao Zedong studied here as a young man and edited the Xiang River Review; his poem on Orange Isle is about this stretch of river.'],
'长沙|共和国': ['1972 年马王堆汉墓的发现震动世界,辛追夫人与文物现藏湖南博物院;长沙是湖南省会,岳麓书院至今仍是湖南大学的一部分,门口「惟楚有材,于斯为盛」的对联是清代的。',
 'The discovery of the Mawangdui tombs in 1972 made news around the world; Lady Xin Zhui and the finds are in the Hunan Museum. Changsha is the capital of Hunan, and the Yuelu Academy remains part of Hunan University, the Qing couplet at its gate still claiming that the talent of Chu flourishes here.'],
'新加坡|三佛齐': ['三佛齐时代的新加坡岛还谈不上城市:马来编年史里叫它「淡马锡」,是海峡里的一个小据点。考古在福康宁山一带发现了 14 世纪的聚落与中国瓷片,说明三佛齐衰落前后这里已有人经营港口贸易,但规模远不能与巨港、马六甲相比。',
 'In Srivijaya\'s day Singapore was hardly a town: the Malay chronicles call it Temasek, a small post in the straits. Excavations around Fort Canning hill have turned up a fourteenth-century settlement with Chinese porcelain, showing that around the time Srivijaya declined people here were already trading through the port — on nothing like the scale of Palembang or Malacca.'],
'新加坡|马六甲及诸苏丹国': ['马来编年史说马六甲的建立者拜里米苏拉先在淡马锡称王、后被逐才北上建马六甲(约 1400 年);此后新加坡岛属马六甲、再属柔佛苏丹国,岛上只有小村与渔民,直到 1819 年莱佛士登陆时全岛不过一千人上下。',
 'The Malay chronicles say Malacca\'s founder Parameswara first ruled at Temasek and, driven out, went north to found Malacca around 1400; after that the island belonged to Malacca and then to the Johor sultanate, holding only villages and fishermen — when Raffles landed in 1819 there were perhaps a thousand people on it.'],
'新加坡|荷兰共和国': ['荷兰东印度公司 1641 年从葡萄牙人手里夺得马六甲,此后一百多年控制着海峡的贸易,新加坡岛在它的势力范围之内但没有据点;1824 年英荷条约(此时已是荷兰王国)把海峡以南划给荷兰、以北给英国,新加坡从此明确归英。',
 'The Dutch East India Company took Malacca from the Portuguese in 1641 and controlled the trade of the straits for over a century; Singapore lay within its sphere but held no Dutch post. The Anglo-Dutch treaty of 1824 — by then with the Kingdom of the Netherlands — gave the Dutch what lay south of the straits and the British what lay north, and Singapore was British from then on.'],
'吉隆坡|三佛齐': ['三佛齐的时代吉隆坡还不存在——这里是巴生河上游的雨林,只有零星的原住民聚落。三佛齐的势力主要在海峡两岸的港口,马来半岛内陆很少受到直接管理。',
 'In Srivijaya\'s time Kuala Lumpur did not exist — this was rainforest on the upper Klang river with only scattered indigenous settlements. Srivijaya\'s power lay in the ports along the straits, and the interior of the peninsula was seldom directly governed.'],
'吉隆坡|马六甲及诸苏丹国': ['马六甲和后来的柔佛、雪兰莪苏丹国统治马来半岛西岸时,吉隆坡所在的巴生河谷仍是内陆的锡矿区边缘,没有城镇;雪兰莪的中心在海边的瓜拉雪兰莪。吉隆坡要到 1857 年华人锡矿工人溯河而上才建立。',
 'When Malacca and later the Johor and Selangor sultanates ruled the west coast of the peninsula, the Klang valley where Kuala Lumpur now stands was still the edge of an inland tin district with no town; Selangor\'s centre was Kuala Selangor on the coast. Kuala Lumpur was only founded in 1857, when Chinese tin miners came up the river.'],
'吉隆坡|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1857 年一批华人矿工在巴生河与鹅唛河交汇处登岸采锡,吉隆坡由此建镇,名字的意思就是「泥泞的河口」;甲必丹叶亚来在 1870 年代把它从战乱中重建起来。1880 年英国人把雪兰莪首府迁来,1896 年成为马来联邦首府,苏丹阿都沙末大厦(1897)就是这时的殖民政府大楼。',
 'In 1857 a party of Chinese miners landed at the meeting of the Klang and Gombak rivers to dig tin, and the town began — the name means muddy river-mouth; the Kapitan Yap Ah Loy rebuilt it after civil war in the 1870s. The British moved the Selangor capital here in 1880 and made it capital of the Federated Malay States in 1896; the Sultan Abdul Samad Building of 1897 was the colonial government offices.'],
'吉隆坡|现代东南亚': ['1957 年 8 月 31 日马来亚在吉隆坡默迪卡体育场宣布独立;1963 年马来西亚成立后它是首都。1998 年建成的双子塔一度是世界最高的楼;联邦政府 1999 年起陆续迁往新建的布城,吉隆坡仍是首都与最大城市。',
 'On 31 August 1957 Malaya declared independence at the Merdeka Stadium in Kuala Lumpur, and it became the capital of Malaysia when the federation formed in 1963. The Petronas Towers of 1998 were for a time the tallest buildings in the world; from 1999 the federal government moved in stages to the new city of Putrajaya, but Kuala Lumpur remains the capital and the largest city.'],
'胡志明市|扶南': ['扶南是湄公河三角洲最早的国家,今天的胡志明市一带在它的东部边缘;主要港口喔㕭在今越南西南部,出土过罗马金币与印度饰物。这时的西贡地区是沼泽与河汊,几乎没有定居的城镇。',
 'Funan was the earliest state of the Mekong delta, and the area of today\'s Ho Chi Minh City lay on its eastern edge; its main port, Oc Eo in the south-west of Vietnam, has yielded Roman coins and Indian ornaments. The Saigon area then was marsh and creeks with hardly a settled town.'],
'胡志明市|高棉·吴哥': ['吴哥王朝时期这一带属高棉,是它东部的边地,高棉人叫这里「普利安哥」(Prey Nokor,意为「林中之城」)——越南语的「西贡」一名可能就与此有关。这里长期只是高棉的一个小港与渔村,要到 17 世纪越南人南下才成为城镇。',
 'Under Angkor this was Khmer land, its eastern frontier; the Khmer called it Prey Nokor, city in the forest, from which the Vietnamese name Saigon may derive. For a long time it was only a small Khmer port and fishing village, becoming a town only when the Vietnamese pushed south in the seventeenth century.'],
'胡志明市|欧洲殖民东南亚': ['1859 年法军攻占西贡,1862 年阮朝割让南圻东三省、1867 年法国占了全部南圻,西贡成为法属交趾支那的首府,1887 年后是整个法属印度支那的经济中心;圣母大教堂(1880)、中央邮局(1891)与大剧院都是这时建的,「东方巴黎」的名声由此而来。',
 'French forces took Saigon in 1859, the Nguyen court ceded the three eastern provinces of the south in 1862 and France seized the rest in 1867; Saigon became the capital of French Cochinchina and after 1887 the economic centre of all French Indochina. The cathedral of 1880, the central post office of 1891 and the opera house date from then, and the name Paris of the East comes from this period.'],
'胡志明市|现代东南亚': ['1955—1975 年西贡是越南共和国的首都;1975 年 4 月 30 日北越坦克撞开独立宫大门,战争结束,次年改名胡志明市。今天它是越南最大的城市与经济中心,统一宫仍按 1975 年那天的样子保留着。',
 'From 1955 to 1975 Saigon was the capital of the Republic of Vietnam; on 30 April 1975 North Vietnamese tanks crashed through the gates of the Independence Palace and the war ended, and the city was renamed for Ho Chi Minh the next year. It is now Vietnam\'s largest city and economic centre, and the palace is kept as it was on that day.'],
'塔什干|粟特': ['粟特人的时代塔什干叫「石国」(赭时),是粟特城邦中最靠北的一个,守着从河中通往草原的商路;唐代文献里石国以善舞闻名,「胡腾舞」「柘枝舞」都与这里有关。751 年怛罗斯之战的起因之一,就是唐将高仙芝攻破石国、俘其国王。',
 'In Sogdian times Tashkent was Chach, the northernmost of the Sogdian city-states, guarding the road from Transoxiana out to the steppe; Tang sources knew it for its dancers — the leaping hu dance and the zhezhi dance are both linked to it. One cause of the battle of Talas in 751 was the Tang general Gao Xianzhi\'s sack of Chach and capture of its king.'],
'迪拜|阿拉伯哈里发': ['哈里发国时期的迪拜一带只有海边的渔村与珍珠采集点,阿拉伯商船从这里沿海岸去印度与东非。真正有「迪拜」这个名字的记录,传为 11 世纪安达卢斯地理学家巴克里的书里,那时它还只是个小地方。',
 'In the age of the caliphs the Dubai coast held only fishing villages and pearling grounds, from which Arab ships followed the shore to India and East Africa. The first record of the name Dubai is traditionally placed in the eleventh-century geography of al-Bakri of Andalusia, when it was still a small place.'],
'迪拜|现代中东': ['1833 年马克图姆家族带着八百人迁到迪拜湾定居,靠珍珠与转口贸易起家;1966 年发现石油,1971 年迪拜与其他五个酋长国组成阿联酋,次年又加入一个。此后它靠港口、航空与地产成为海湾的商业中心,2010 年建成的哈利法塔是世界最高建筑。',
 'In 1833 the Maktoum family settled on Dubai creek with some eight hundred followers and built the town on pearls and entrepôt trade; oil was found in 1966, and in 1971 Dubai joined five other emirates to form the United Arab Emirates, and a seventh joined the next year. It has since become the commercial hub of the Gulf on ports, aviation and property, and the Burj Khalifa of 2010 is the tallest building in the world.'],
'米兰|罗马共和国': ['米兰是凯尔特人因苏布雷部落的城,前 222 年被罗马攻取,拉丁名「梅迪奥拉努姆」一般解为「平原中央」;前 89 年获拉丁公民权,前 49 年凯撒给了它罗马公民权。共和国末期它已是波河平原北部的重要市镇。',
 'Milan was a town of the Celtic Insubres, taken by Rome in 222 BC; its Latin name Mediolanum is usually taken to mean the place in the middle of the plain. It received Latin rights in 89 BC and Roman citizenship from Caesar in 49 BC, and by the end of the Republic was an important town of the northern Po plain.'],
'米兰|中世纪西欧': ['中世纪的米兰是意大利北部最强的城市公社之一:1162 年被红胡子腓特烈夷平,1176 年伦巴第同盟在莱尼亚诺打败皇帝,米兰是同盟的核心。14 世纪起维斯孔蒂家族、后来的斯福尔扎家族做米兰公爵,1386 年动工的大教堂与达·芬奇的《最后的晚餐》(1498)都出自这两个家族的时代。',
 'Medieval Milan was among the strongest city communes of northern Italy: razed by Frederick Barbarossa in 1162, it was the heart of the Lombard League that beat the emperor at Legnano in 1176. From the fourteenth century the Visconti and then the Sforza ruled as dukes; the cathedral begun in 1386 and Leonardo\'s Last Supper of 1498 both belong to their age.'],
'米兰|法兰西': ['1796 年拿破仑率军进入米兰,1805 年他在米兰大教堂加冕为意大利国王,米兰是拿破仑「意大利王国」的首都直到 1814 年;斯卡拉歌剧院(1778)在这时成为欧洲一流的舞台。此前的 1499—1525 年,法国国王也曾几度占有米兰公国。',
 'Napoleon marched into Milan in 1796 and in 1805 was crowned king of Italy in its cathedral; the city was the capital of his Kingdom of Italy until 1814, and La Scala, opened in 1778, became one of Europe\'s leading opera houses in these years. Earlier, between 1499 and 1525, the kings of France had several times held the duchy of Milan.'],
'巴塞罗那|罗马共和国': ['前 218 年罗马军队在附近的恩波里翁登陆对付迦太基,加泰罗尼亚海岸从此进入罗马世界;巴塞罗那本身要到帝国初、奥古斯都时代(约前 15 年)才作为退伍军人殖民地「巴尔基诺」建城,城址就在今天的哥特区。',
 'In 218 BC a Roman army landed at nearby Emporion to fight Carthage, and the Catalan coast entered the Roman world; Barcelona itself was founded only at the start of the empire, under Augustus around 15 BC, as the veterans\' colony of Barcino, on the site of today\'s Gothic quarter.'],
'巴塞罗那|罗马帝国': ['罗马帝国时期的巴尔基诺是一座不大的殖民城,有城墙、广场与神庙——奥古斯都神庙的四根柱子至今立在哥特区一间院子里,4 世纪的城墙也还能看到一段。它当时远不如塔拉戈纳重要,后者才是行省首府。',
 'Under the empire Barcino was a modest colonial town with walls, forum and temples — four columns of the temple of Augustus still stand in a courtyard of the Gothic quarter, and a stretch of the fourth-century wall survives. It mattered far less than Tarragona, the provincial capital.'],
'巴塞罗那|西班牙·葡萄牙帝国': ['1469 年阿拉贡的费迪南与卡斯蒂利亚的伊莎贝拉联姻,两个王国从此共主,巴塞罗那所在的加泰罗尼亚仍保留自己的法制与议会;1493 年哥伦布首航归来在此觐见两位国王。此后西班牙的重心与美洲贸易都在塞维利亚,巴塞罗那相对沉寂,1714 年 9 月 11 日在王位继承战争中被腓力五世攻陷,加泰罗尼亚的自治制度随之被废,这一天成了今天的加泰罗尼亚民族日。',
 'The marriage of Ferdinand of Aragon and Isabella of Castile in 1469 put the two crowns under one couple, while Catalonia and Barcelona kept their own laws and parliament; in 1493 Columbus was received here by the two monarchs on returning from his first voyage. Thereafter Spain\'s centre and the American trade lay in Seville and Barcelona was comparatively quiet; on 11 September 1714 it fell to Philip V in the War of the Spanish Succession and Catalonia\'s self-government was abolished — the date is now Catalonia\'s national day.'],
'内罗毕|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1899 年英国修建蒙巴萨到乌干达的铁路,在一片马赛人放牧的沼泽地上设了一个补给站,内罗毕由此而生,名字来自马赛语「凉水」;1905 年成为英属东非的首府,白人移民占据了周围的高地农场,凯伦·布里克森的《走出非洲》写的就是城郊的咖啡园。',
 'In 1899 the British, building the railway from Mombasa to Uganda, set up a supply depot on a marsh where the Maasai grazed cattle, and Nairobi began — the name is Maasai for cool water. It became the capital of British East Africa in 1905, white settlers took the highland farms around it, and Karen Blixen\'s Out of Africa is about a coffee farm on its outskirts.'],
'内罗毕|现代非洲': ['1963 年肯尼亚独立,内罗毕是首都;1973 年建成的肯雅塔国际会议中心多年是城市的地标。它是联合国环境规划署与人居署的总部所在——联合国四大总部城市里唯一在发展中国家的一个;城边的内罗毕国家公园里,长颈鹿背后就是市区的高楼。',
 'Kenya became independent in 1963 with Nairobi as its capital; the Kenyatta International Convention Centre of 1973 was long the city\'s landmark. It is the seat of the UN environment and human settlements programmes — the only one of the UN\'s four headquarters cities in the developing world; in the national park on its edge, giraffes graze with the city\'s towers behind them.'],
'约翰内斯堡|欧洲殖民非洲': ['1886 年在威特沃特斯兰德发现世界上最大的金矿脉,矿工蜂拥而至,约翰内斯堡十年之内从荒地长成南非最大的城市;它当时属布尔人的德兰士瓦共和国,英布战争(1899—1902)后归英国。金矿的劳动力大量来自被圈进保留地的非洲人,种族隔离的雏形从矿区宿舍开始。',
 'In 1886 the world\'s richest gold reef was found on the Witwatersrand, miners poured in, and within ten years Johannesburg grew from empty veld into the largest city in South Africa; it lay in the Boers\' Transvaal republic and passed to Britain after the Boer War of 1899-1902. The mines drew their labour from Africans confined to reserves, and the pattern of segregation began in the mine compounds.'],
'约翰内斯堡|现代非洲': ['1948 年起南非推行种族隔离,约翰内斯堡西南的索韦托是黑人被强制迁入的城区,1976 年索韦托学生起义震动世界;曼德拉曾住在这里的奥兰多西区,那栋房子现在是博物馆。1994 年种族隔离结束,约翰内斯堡仍是南非最大的城市与经济中心,宪法法院就建在旧监狱的地基上。',
 'From 1948 South Africa enforced apartheid, and Soweto, south-west of Johannesburg, was the township into which black residents were moved; the Soweto student uprising of 1976 shook the world. Mandela lived in Orlando West there, and the house is now a museum. Apartheid ended in 1994; Johannesburg remains the country\'s largest city and economic centre, and the Constitutional Court stands on the foundations of the old prison.'],
'纽约|荷兰共和国': ['1624 年荷兰西印度公司在曼哈顿南端建新阿姆斯特丹,1626 年据说用价值 60 荷兰盾的货物从原住民手里「买」下全岛;城北的一道木栅栏就是今天华尔街的由来。1664 年英国舰队兵临城下,总督斯泰弗森特不战而降,城市改名纽约。',
 'In 1624 the Dutch West India Company founded New Amsterdam at the southern tip of Manhattan, and in 1626 is said to have bought the island from its native inhabitants for goods worth sixty guilders; the wooden palisade on the town\'s northern edge is where Wall Street gets its name. In 1664 an English fleet appeared and the governor Stuyvesant surrendered without a fight; the city became New York.'],
'旧金山|美国': ['1848 年萨特磨坊发现金子,次年数万「四九年淘金者」涌到,旧金山从几百人的小镇一年之内变成两三万人的城市;1906 年大地震与随后的大火毁掉了城市的四分之三。金门大桥 1937 年通车,1945 年联合国宪章在这里签署。',
 'Gold was found at Sutter\'s mill in 1848, tens of thousands of forty-niners arrived the next year, and San Francisco went from a village of a few hundred to a city of twenty or thirty thousand within a year; the earthquake and fire of 1906 destroyed three-quarters of it. The Golden Gate Bridge opened in 1937, and the United Nations Charter was signed here in 1945.'],
'芝加哥|美国': ['芝加哥建在密歇根湖与密西西比水系之间的地峡上,1837 年建市,靠运河与铁路成了美国内陆的枢纽,谷物、牲畜、木材都在这里集散。1871 年大火烧掉市中心,重建后到 1880 年代建筑师开始用钢框架盖楼,1885 年的家庭保险大楼被视为第一座摩天楼——今天城市的天际线从那时开始。',
 'Chicago stands on the portage between Lake Michigan and the Mississippi system; incorporated in 1837, it became the hub of the American interior through canal and railway, where grain, cattle and timber changed hands. After the great fire of 1871 gutted the centre the city was rebuilt, and by the 1880s architects were building in steel frame; the Home Insurance Building of 1885 is counted the first skyscraper — the city\'s skyline begins there.'],
'西雅图|美国': ['1851 年移民在艾略特湾登陆建镇,以当地杜瓦米什部落首领西雅图的名字命名;1897 年克朗代克淘金潮把它变成通往阿拉斯加的门户。波音公司 1916 年在这里创立,1962 年世博会留下了太空针塔,今天亚马逊在城里、微软在东郊的雷德蒙德。',
 'Settlers landed on Elliott Bay in 1851 and named the town after Chief Seattle of the Duwamish; the Klondike gold rush of 1897 made it the gateway to Alaska. Boeing was founded here in 1916, the 1962 world\'s fair left the Space Needle, and today Amazon is in the city and Microsoft in Redmond on its eastern edge.'],
'华盛顿|美国': ['1790 年国会决定在波托马克河畔建一座不属于任何州的首都,由法国工程师朗方规划,1800 年政府迁入;1814 年英军攻入并烧毁了白宫与国会大厦。国会大厦的穹顶大体是在南北战争期间建成的,林肯坚持工程不停,以示联邦不会解体。',
 'In 1790 Congress decided to build a capital belonging to no state on the Potomac, laid out by the French engineer L\'Enfant, and the government moved in in 1800; in 1814 British troops entered and burned the White House and the Capitol. The Capitol dome was largely built during the Civil War — Lincoln insisted the work go on as a sign that the Union would hold.'],
'波士顿|美国': ['波士顿是美国革命的起点:1770 年波士顿惨案、1773 年倾茶事件都发生在这里,1775 年 4 月列克星敦的第一枪就在城外打响。法尼尔厅(1742)因革命者在此集会被称为「自由的摇篮」;哈佛(1636)与麻省理工在查尔斯河对岸,这里至今是美国的大学之城。',
 'Boston is where the American Revolution began: the Boston Massacre of 1770 and the Tea Party of 1773 happened here, and the first shots at Lexington in April 1775 were fired just outside the town. Faneuil Hall of 1742 is called the cradle of liberty for the meetings held there; Harvard, founded in 1636, and MIT stand across the Charles, and it remains America\'s university city.'],
'迈阿密|西葡殖民美洲': ['1513 年庞塞·德莱昂到达佛罗里达,西班牙人此后名义上统治这里近三百年,但迈阿密一带只有特克斯塔原住民与几个传教点,西班牙的据点在北边的圣奥古斯丁。1819 年西班牙把佛罗里达让给了美国。',
 'Ponce de León reached Florida in 1513, and Spain nominally ruled it for nearly three centuries, but the Miami area held only the Tequesta people and a few mission posts — the Spanish stronghold was St Augustine to the north. In 1819 Spain ceded Florida to the United States.'],
'迈阿密|美国': ['1896 年铁路修到这里,迈阿密才正式建市,当时不到四百人;1920 年代地产热与 1930 年代南滩的装饰艺术旅馆把它变成度假胜地。1959 年古巴革命后大批古巴人迁来,迈阿密成了拉丁美洲与美国之间的门户城市。',
 'The railway arrived in 1896 and Miami was incorporated with fewer than four hundred people; the land boom of the 1920s and the Art Deco hotels of South Beach in the 1930s made it a resort. After the Cuban revolution of 1959 Cubans came in great numbers, and Miami became the gateway between Latin America and the United States.'],
'多伦多|大英帝国·英国': ['1793 年英国人在安大略湖北岸建约克镇,作为上加拿大的首府,1812 年战争中被美军攻占焚烧;1834 年改名多伦多。19 世纪它是英属加拿大的商业中心之一,1867 年加拿大联邦成立后是安大略省的省会,今天是加拿大最大的城市。',
 'In 1793 the British founded the town of York on the north shore of Lake Ontario as the capital of Upper Canada; American troops took and burned it in the War of 1812, and in 1834 it was renamed Toronto. It became one of the commercial centres of British Canada, the capital of Ontario after Confederation in 1867, and today Canada\'s largest city.'],
'蒙特利尔|大英帝国·英国': ['蒙特利尔 1642 年由法国人建立,1760 年英军攻占后归英国;此后一百多年它是英属北美最大的城市与毛皮贸易中心,1825 年拉钦运河、1859 年维多利亚大桥使它成为圣劳伦斯河上的港口枢纽。城市讲法语的多数与讲英语的商界并存至今。',
 'Montreal was founded by the French in 1642 and taken by British troops in 1760; for the next century and more it was the largest city of British North America and the centre of the fur trade, and the Lachine canal of 1825 and the Victoria bridge of 1859 made it the port hub of the St Lawrence. Its French-speaking majority and English-speaking business world have lived side by side ever since.'],
'温哥华|大英帝国·英国': ['1792 年英国海军军官乔治·温哥华勘测了这一带海岸,城市以他命名;1886 年建市,次年加拿大太平洋铁路延到这里,温哥华成为英属加拿大面向太平洋的门户。华工修铁路后留下的社区形成了北美最大的老唐人街之一。',
 'The British naval officer George Vancouver charted this coast in 1792, and the city takes his name; it was incorporated in 1886, the Canadian Pacific Railway was extended to it the next year, and it became British Canada\'s gateway to the Pacific. The Chinese labourers who built the railway stayed on, forming one of the largest historic Chinatowns in North America.'],
'悉尼|大英帝国·英国': ['1788 年 1 月 26 日,菲利普船长率第一舰队十一艘船在悉尼湾登陆,建立英国的流放犯殖民地——这一天后来成了澳大利亚国庆日;最初几年殖民地几乎饿死,靠原住民的土地与后来的羊毛业才站稳。海德公园兵营(1819)是流放犯住过的房子,至今还在。',
 'On 26 January 1788 Captain Phillip landed the eleven ships of the First Fleet at Sydney Cove and founded a British convict colony — the date later became Australia Day; in its first years the settlement came close to starving, and it found its footing on the land of the Aboriginal people and later on wool. The Hyde Park Barracks of 1819, where convicts slept, still stand.'],
'悉尼|澳新与太平洋岛国': ['1901 年澳大利亚联邦成立时首都之争悬而未决,悉尼与墨尔本相持不下,最后另建堪培拉;悉尼仍是最大城市。1932 年海港大桥、1973 年歌剧院先后建成,2000 年奥运会在这里举行。',
 'When the Australian federation formed in 1901 the capital was disputed between Sydney and Melbourne, and Canberra was built as a compromise; Sydney remained the largest city. The Harbour Bridge opened in 1932 and the Opera House in 1973, and the city hosted the Olympic Games in 2000.'],
'墨尔本|澳大利亚原住民': ['墨尔本所在的雅拉河口是库林各族的土地,乌伦杰里人在这里生活了几万年;他们按季节在河口与内陆之间迁徙,雅拉河边的集会地至今在市中心。1835 年巴特曼声称与长老签约「买」下这片地,殖民地政府很快宣布无效——原住民的土地被视为无主。',
 'The mouth of the Yarra where Melbourne stands is the country of the Kulin nations, and the Wurundjeri people have lived here for tens of thousands of years, moving with the seasons between river-mouth and inland; their meeting ground by the Yarra lies in the city centre today. In 1835 John Batman claimed to have bought the land by treaty with the elders, and the colonial government soon voided it — Aboriginal land was treated as belonging to no one.'],
'墨尔本|大英帝国·英国': ['1835 年从塔斯马尼亚来的移民在雅拉河边建镇,1837 年以英国首相墨尔本子爵命名;1851 年维多利亚发现金矿后城市暴富,1880 年为万国博览会建了皇家展览馆,那时的墨尔本是大英帝国里仅次于伦敦的富城之一。',
 'Settlers from Tasmania founded a town on the Yarra in 1835, named in 1837 after the British prime minister Lord Melbourne; the Victorian gold rush from 1851 made it rich, and the Royal Exhibition Building went up for the world\'s fair of 1880, when Melbourne was one of the wealthiest cities in the empire after London.'],
'墨尔本|欧洲殖民大洋洲': ['殖民时期的墨尔本是维多利亚殖民地首府,金矿带来的移民里有大量华人,今天的唐人街 1850 年代就已成形;1854 年尤里卡栅栏事件的矿工起义就在附近的巴拉瑞特,被视为澳大利亚民主的起点之一。',
 'Melbourne was the capital of the colony of Victoria; among the migrants the gold brought were many Chinese, and today\'s Chinatown had formed by the 1850s. The Eureka Stockade rising of 1854 took place at nearby Ballarat and is counted among the beginnings of Australian democracy.'],
'墨尔本|澳新与太平洋岛国': ['1901—1927 年墨尔本是澳大利亚联邦的临时首都,联邦议会就在皇家展览馆开幕,后来搬到堪培拉;1956 年它办了南半球第一届奥运会。今天它与悉尼争「第一大城」多年不分高下。',
 'From 1901 to 1927 Melbourne was the temporary capital of the Australian federation — parliament opened in the Royal Exhibition Building before moving to Canberra; in 1956 it held the first Olympic Games in the southern hemisphere. It has contested first place with Sydney for years without settling it.'],
'奥克兰|毛利': ['奥克兰的地峡是毛利人的「塔马基」,两岸都是港湾、又有火山锥可筑要塞,是全新西兰人口最密、争夺最烈的地方之一;一树山(芒格基基)上的台地就是当年毛利要塞「帕」的遗迹。19 世纪初火枪战争让这里人口锐减。',
 'The Auckland isthmus was Tamaki to the Māori — harbours on both coasts and volcanic cones for forts made it one of the most populous and fought-over places in New Zealand; the terraces on One Tree Hill, Maungakiekie, are the remains of a great pā. The Musket Wars of the early nineteenth century emptied it of most of its people.'],
'奥克兰|大英帝国·英国': ['1840 年怀唐伊条约签署后,总督霍布森选定这处地峡建城,以印度总督奥克兰勋爵命名,1841—1865 年是新西兰的首都;此后首都迁往惠灵顿,奥克兰靠港口与移民一直是最大城市。',
 'After the Treaty of Waitangi in 1840 Governor Hobson chose the isthmus for his town and named it after Lord Auckland, then governor-general of India; it was New Zealand\'s capital from 1841 to 1865. The capital then moved to Wellington, but Auckland stayed the largest city on its port and its migrants.'],
'奥克兰|欧洲殖民大洋洲': ['殖民时期的奥克兰是新西兰北岛的商业中心,1860 年代怀卡托战争就是从这里南下的,战后没收的毛利土地大量落到移民手里;20 世纪后半叶大量太平洋岛民迁来,奥克兰成了世界上波利尼西亚人最多的城市。',
 'Colonial Auckland was the commercial centre of the North Island; the Waikato war of the 1860s was launched south from here, and much Māori land confiscated afterwards went to settlers. In the later twentieth century Pacific islanders came in great numbers, and Auckland became the city with the largest Polynesian population in the world.'],
'太原|北宋': ['979 年晋阳被毁后,982 年潘美在汾河东岸的唐明镇另筑太原城,就是今天太原老城的位置;北宋以它为河东路治所,面对北面的辽与西北的西夏,是重要的边防重镇。晋祠圣母殿(1023—1032 年建)与殿前的鱼沼飞梁都是这一时期的木构,至今还在。',
 'After Jinyang was destroyed in 979, Pan Mei built a new Taiyuan in 982 at Tangming on the east bank of the Fen — the site of today\'s old town; the Northern Song made it the seat of the Hedong circuit, a key frontier stronghold facing the Liao to the north and the Western Xia to the north-west. The Hall of the Holy Mother at Jinci, built 1023-1032, and the flying bridge in front of it are timber structures of this period and still stand.'],
/* v208:版图修正后新出现的 13 行 */
'西安|东晋·十六国': ['西晋亡后长安先后做过前赵(319—329)、前秦、后秦的都城。前秦苻坚在这里重用王猛,一度统一北方,383 年淝水之战大败后国家崩解;后秦时鸠摩罗什被迎到长安(401 年),在逍遥园译出《金刚经》《法华经》等,是中国佛经翻译史上的一座高峰。',
 'After the Western Jin fell, Chang\'an served in turn as capital of the Former Zhao (319-329), the Former Qin and the Later Qin. Fu Jian of the Former Qin ruled here with his minister Wang Meng and briefly united the north, then saw the state collapse after the defeat at Fei River in 383; under the Later Qin the monk Kumarajiva was brought to Chang\'an in 401 and translated the Diamond and Lotus sutras among others — a peak in the history of Chinese scripture translation.'],
'洛阳|东晋·十六国': ['311 年匈奴汉赵攻破洛阳、掳走晋怀帝,是为永嘉之乱,城市残破、贵族大批南逃;此后一百多年洛阳在前赵、后赵、前燕、前秦、后秦之间几度易手,始终没有恢复都城的地位。这时的洛阳是十六国争夺的中原要冲,而不是文化中心。',
 'In 311 the Xiongnu state of Han-Zhao stormed Luoyang and carried off Emperor Huai — the disaster of the Yongjia era; the city was wrecked and the great families fled south. For a century and more it changed hands among the Former Zhao, Later Zhao, Former Yan, Former Qin and Later Qin without ever regaining its standing as a capital — a contested crossroads of the Sixteen Kingdoms, not a centre of culture.'],
'北京|东晋·十六国': ['十六国时北京一带称蓟城,是幽州的治所。350 年鲜卑慕容氏的前燕把都城从龙城迁到蓟、352 年在这里称帝,几年后又迁到邺;后来蓟城先后属前秦、后燕。这是燕国之后蓟城第一次做帝都,虽然只有几年。',
 'In the Sixteen Kingdoms the Beijing area was Ji, seat of You province. In 350 the Xianbei Murong clan\'s Former Yan moved its capital from Longcheng to Ji and proclaimed an emperor here in 352, moving on to Ye a few years later; the town then passed to the Former Qin and the Later Yan. It was the first time since the state of Yan that Ji served as a capital — an imperial one this time, though only for a few years.'],
'开封|东晋·十六国': ['这一时期开封一带称浚仪,属陈留郡,是十六国在中原争夺的地区之一——先属汉赵、后赵,再属前燕、前秦,后来落到东晋与后燕之间反复拉锯。它离邺城和洛阳都不远,常年在战线上,没有留下什么建设。',
 'In these years the Kaifeng area was Junyi county in Chenliu commandery, one of the central-plain districts the Sixteen Kingdoms fought over — held first by Han-Zhao and the Later Zhao, then the Former Yan and Former Qin, later swinging between the Eastern Jin and the Later Yan. Close to both Ye and Luoyang, it sat on the front line for decades and saw little building.'],
'大同|东晋·十六国': ['这时的平城是拓跋鲜卑代国的地盘:代国 338 年由拓跋什翼犍立国,376 年被前秦所灭,386 年拓跋珪复国、改称魏,398 年就把都城定在了平城。所以对大同来说,十六国的一百年正是从鲜卑牧地变成北魏都城的前夜。',
 'Pingcheng in these years belonged to the Tuoba Xianbei state of Dai: founded by Tuoba Shiyijian in 338, destroyed by the Former Qin in 376, revived by Tuoba Gui in 386 under the name Wei — and in 398 Wei made Pingcheng its capital. For Datong the century of the Sixteen Kingdoms was the eve of its turn from Xianbei pasture into the capital of the Northern Wei.'],
'太原|东晋·十六国': ['316 年刘琨兵败,晋阳落入石勒之手,此后属后赵、前燕、前秦。淝水之战后前秦崩解,386 年鲜卑慕容永在长子建西燕,晋阳一带是它的地盘,394 年被后燕所灭,晋阳归后燕,396 年北魏拓跋珪攻取。一百年里换了六七个主人。',
 'After Liu Kun\'s defeat in 316 Jinyang fell to Shi Le and passed to the Later Zhao, Former Yan and Former Qin. When the Former Qin collapsed after Fei River, the Xianbei leader Murong Yong set up the Western Yan at Changzi in 386 with the Jinyang area in its lands; the Later Yan destroyed it in 394 and took Jinyang, and Tuoba Gui of the Northern Wei seized it in 396 — six or seven masters in a hundred years.'],
'孟买|百乘王朝': ['百乘王朝的西海岸门户是孟买北边的索帕拉(今纳拉索帕拉),阿育王时代就有石刻;罗马商人在《厄立特里亚海航行记》里把它记作重要港口。今天孟买市区的坎赫里石窟,最早的洞窟就是百乘时期开凿的。',
 'The Satavahanas\' gateway on the west coast was Sopara, just north of Mumbai, which already had an Ashokan inscription; the Roman Periplus of the Erythraean Sea lists it as a major port. The Kanheri caves inside today\'s Mumbai were first cut in the Satavahana period.'],
'孟买|中世纪诸王朝': ['中世纪的孟买是七座小岛,先后属卡拉丘里、拉什特拉库塔与西拉哈拉等王朝;象岛石窟的湿婆三面像约刻于 6 世纪。这时孟买还不是城市,岛上是渔村与寺庙,真正的城要到 17 世纪英国人手里才长出来。',
 'Medieval Mumbai was seven small islands, held in turn by the Kalachuris, the Rashtrakutas and the Shilaharas; the three-faced Shiva of the Elephanta caves was carved around the sixth century. There was no city yet, only fishing villages and temples on the islands — the town only grew under the English in the seventeenth century.'],
'孟买|伐卡塔卡与德干诸国': ['这几百年孟买一带属于西萨特拉普——塞人后裔建的政权,握着阿拉伯海的港口,和内陆的伐卡塔卡各据一头。它铸的银币上一面是国王侧面像、一面写着名号,而且是印度最早在钱上标年份的政权之一,考古断代到今天还在用这批币。约 409 年笈多王旃陀罗笈多二世南下把它灭掉,西海岸的港口从此归了北方。',
 'For these centuries the country around Mumbai belonged to the Western Kshatrapas, a dynasty descended from Saka governors that held the Arabian Sea ports while the Vakatakas held the interior. Their silver coins carry a royal portrait on one face and titles on the other, and they were among the first in India to strike dates onto coinage — archaeologists still date sites by them. Around 409 Chandragupta II of the Guptas came south and destroyed them, and the west-coast harbours passed to the north.'],
'加尔各答|笈多王朝': ['笈多时期孟加拉是帝国的东部,恒河三角洲上有稠密的村落与港口(如坦拉里普蒂),法显 5 世纪初就是从坦拉里普蒂搭船去斯里兰卡的。加尔各答所在的胡格利河边那时只有村落,城市要到 1690 年英国人设商馆才开始。',
 'Under the Guptas Bengal was the eastern part of the empire, its delta thick with villages and ports such as Tamralipti — from which the pilgrim Faxian sailed for Sri Lanka early in the fifth century. The Hooghly bank where Calcutta stands held only villages then; the city began with the English trading post of 1690.'],
'巴特那|德里苏丹国': ['苏丹国时期华氏城早已衰落成小镇,比哈尔在 13 世纪初被巴赫蒂亚尔·哈尔吉攻占,那烂陀等佛教大寺也在这一波中被毁;此后比哈尔在德里苏丹与孟加拉苏丹之间反复易手。今天的巴特那城,是 1541 年舍尔沙重新建的。',
 'By the time of the sultanate Pataliputra had long shrunk to a small town; Bihar was overrun by Bakhtiyar Khalji early in the thirteenth century, and the great Buddhist monasteries such as Nalanda were destroyed in that wave; the province then swung between the Delhi and Bengal sultans. The present town of Patna was refounded by Sher Shah in 1541.'],
'巴特那|巽伽与恒河诸国': ['前 185 年那场弑君就发生在这里:孔雀王朝的末代君主在华氏城外阅兵,他的总司令普沙密多罗当场动手,自己做了王。新王朝仍以华氏城为都,却再也守不住前朝那么大的地盘。这一时期的华氏城出土过大量陶塑小像,不是王室的东西,是寻常人家摆在屋里的,做得随手却生动——朝廷换了,城里的日子照过。',
 'The killing that ended the Mauryas happened here in 185 BC: the last Mauryan king was reviewing his troops outside Pataliputra when his own commander-in-chief, Pushyamitra, struck him down and took the throne. The new dynasty kept Pataliputra as its capital but never again held anything like the old empire. Quantities of small terracotta figures survive from the city in this period — not royal objects but things ordinary households kept indoors, roughly made and full of life. The court changed; the city went on living.'],
'喀布尔|莫卧儿帝国': ['1504 年巴布尔从中亚败退到喀布尔,以此为根据地经营二十年,1526 年从这里南下攻入印度建立莫卧儿帝国;他至死念着喀布尔,遗嘱把自己葬回来——巴布尔花园就是他的墓园。此后喀布尔一直是莫卧儿的西北重镇,直到 1738 年被纳迪尔沙夺走。',
 'In 1504 Babur, driven out of Central Asia, took Kabul and made it his base for twenty years; in 1526 he marched south from here into India and founded the Mughal empire. He never stopped missing Kabul and asked to be buried there — the Gardens of Babur are his tomb. Kabul remained the Mughals\' north-western stronghold until Nader Shah took it in 1738.'],
'拉萨|元': ['元朝把吐蕃划归宣政院管辖,由萨迦派的僧人代管地方政教,是西藏第一次被纳入一个以中原为中心的王朝的行政体系。萨迦派的八思巴受封帝师,奉忽必烈之命造了一套拼写蒙古语的新字,史称八思巴文,元朝的官印与钱币上都用它,元亡后即废弃。这一时期拉萨不是政治中心——萨迦寺才是,拉萨的分量要到 17 世纪五世达赖建布达拉宫才重新回来。',
 'The Yuan placed Tibet under the Bureau of Buddhist and Tibetan Affairs, with monks of the Sakya school administering both religion and government locally — the first time Tibet was brought into the administrative system of a dynasty centred on China. The Sakya lama Phagpa was made imperial preceptor and, on Kublai\'s orders, devised a new script for writing Mongolian, used on Yuan seals and coinage and abandoned when the dynasty fell. Lhasa was not the political centre in this period — Sakya monastery was; its weight returned only in the seventeenth century when the fifth Dalai Lama built the Potala.'],
'拉萨|蒙古帝国': ['1240 年阔端派兵进入吐蕃,1247 年他与萨迦派的领袖萨迦班智达在凉州(今甘肃武威)会面。议定的事情很具体:各地要呈上土地与户口的册子、按数缴纳贡赋、沿路设置驿站;寺院的事交给萨迦派管,官府的事由蒙古派人。萨迦班智达为此写信回藏地,劝各方接受这些条件。西藏纳入蒙古治下,比元朝建立早了二十多年。',
 'In 1240 Koden sent troops into Tibet, and in 1247 he met Sakya Pandita, head of the Sakya school, at Liangzhou — today\'s Wuwei in Gansu. What they settled was specific: registers of land and households were to be handed over, tribute paid by the count, post stations set up along the roads; monastery affairs went to the Sakya school, while civil administration got officials appointed by the Mongols. Sakya Pandita wrote back to Tibet urging the lords and clergy to accept these terms. Tibet came under Mongol rule more than twenty years before the Yuan dynasty was founded.'],
'布拉格|奥地利·哈布斯堡': ['1526 年波希米亚国王战死于对奥斯曼的战场,王位由哈布斯堡家族继承,布拉格从此归维也纳。鲁道夫二世 1583 年把皇帝的宫廷搬到这里住了三十年,请来第谷·布拉赫与开普勒在城里观星——开普勒行星运动定律的观测数据就是在这段日子里攒下的。1618 年新教贵族把皇帝派来的两名钦差总督连同他们的秘书一起从城堡窗户扔了出去,三十年战争由此开打;战后布拉格降为一座省城,直到 1918 年捷克斯洛伐克独立。',
 'When the king of Bohemia fell fighting the Ottomans in 1526 the crown passed to the Habsburgs, and Prague answered to Vienna from then on. Rudolf II moved the imperial court here in 1583 and kept it for thirty years, bringing Tycho Brahe and Kepler to observe the sky from the city — the data behind Kepler\'s laws of planetary motion was gathered in those years. In 1618 Protestant nobles threw the emperor\'s two regents and their secretary out of a castle window and the Thirty Years War began; afterwards Prague sank to a provincial capital until Czechoslovak independence in 1918.'],
'科尔多瓦|中世纪西欧': ['1236 年卡斯蒂利亚国王费尔南多三世取科尔多瓦,此城归入基督教一侧,大清真寺改作主教座堂。改法很特别:没有拆。三百年后的 1523 年起,人们在森林般的马蹄形拱柱中间挖开一块、插进一座教堂中殿(哥特起手,最后以文艺复兴的样子收尾)——查理五世后来见了说,你们毁掉了世上独一无二的东西,盖起了到处都有的东西。今天它仍是这个样子,两种建筑套在一起。',
 'Ferdinand III of Castile took Córdoba in 1236 and the city passed to the Christian side, its great mosque becoming the cathedral. The conversion was unusual: they did not demolish it. Three centuries later, from 1523, an opening was cut in the forest of horseshoe arches and a nave inserted — begun Gothic and finished in Renaissance dress — Charles V, seeing it later, is said to have told them they had destroyed something unique in the world to build what could be found anywhere. It stands that way still, one building inside the other.'],
'里斯本|中世纪西欧': ['1147 年葡萄牙国王阿方索一世借道路过的北方十字军之力围下里斯本,穆斯林统治在此结束;1255 年前后王室把都城从科英布拉迁来,此后再没搬过。它靠着特茹河口这个天然良港,先做与北欧的鳕鱼和羊毛生意,后来才成为大航海的起点——恩里克王子推动的西非航行,船就是从这条河上出去的。',
 'In 1147 Afonso I of Portugal took Lisbon with the help of northern crusaders who happened to be passing, ending Muslim rule there; around 1255 the court moved the capital here from Coimbra and never moved it again. On its natural harbour at the mouth of the Tagus it first traded cod and wool with northern Europe, and only later became the starting point of the age of discovery — the ships Henry the Navigator sent down the African coast went out from this river.'],
'巴塞罗那|中世纪西欧': ['巴塞罗那伯爵领 1137 年与阿拉贡王国联姻合并,此后两百多年间,加泰罗尼亚的船队做遍地中海,一度控制西西里、撒丁与雅典公国。《海洋法典》(Llibre del Consolat de Mar)规定海难、货损、船员工资怎么办,是中世纪地中海通用的一部商法;它的文本源头是巴塞罗那 13 世纪的《海事习惯》,最早的汇编则出自瓦伦西亚,14 世纪的定本在巴塞罗那。哥特区那些窄巷与教堂,基本就是这几百年盖的。',
 'The county of Barcelona merged with the crown of Aragon by marriage in 1137, and for the next two centuries Catalan fleets traded across the Mediterranean, at times holding Sicily, Sardinia and the duchy of Athens. The Book of the Consulate of the Sea set out what to do about shipwreck, damaged cargo and sailors\' wages and was the commercial law used across the medieval Mediterranean; its textual root is the thirteenth-century Customs of the Sea of Barcelona, the earliest compilation came out of Valencia, and the settled fourteenth-century version was Barcelona\'s. The narrow lanes and churches of the Gothic Quarter are largely the work of these centuries.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|阿拉伯哈里发': ['711 年,一支阿拉伯军队由十七岁的将领穆罕默德·本·卡西姆率领攻入信德,与征服伊比利亚同一年;印度河下游从此并入哈里发国的版图,是伊斯兰教进入南亚最早的一步。而摩亨佐达罗此时早已是一座没人知道来历的土丘——它在公元前 19 世纪就被弃置,地面上只剩后来贵霜时代立起的那座佛塔;要到 1922 年考古队循着佛塔往下挖,才知道底下压着一座城。阿拉伯人骑马从这里走过时,看见的是塔,不是城。',
 'In 711 an Arab army under a seventeen-year-old commander, Muhammad bin Qasim, took Sind — the same year as the conquest of Iberia — and the lower Indus was brought into the caliphate, the earliest step of Islam into South Asia. Mohenjo-daro by then was a mound whose origin no one knew: abandoned in the nineteenth century BC, all that showed above ground was the Buddhist stupa raised on it in Kushan times, and only in 1922 did archaeologists dig down from that stupa and find a city beneath. The Arabs who rode past saw a tower, not a city.'],
'摩亨佐达罗|印度-希腊诸王': ['这一行讲的是这片地方,不是这座城——摩亨佐达罗此时已经埋在土里一千多年了。信德是希腊人诸王国最先丢掉的一块:塞人从北边南下,先占了这里,再一路往东挤。后来这一带在钱币上出现的名字,已经不是希腊名号,而是塞人首领的名字用希腊字母拼出来的样子。',
 'This row is about the place, not the city — Mohenjo-daro had already lain buried for well over a thousand years. Sindh was the first piece the Greek kings lost: the Sakas came down from the north, took it, and pushed on east from there. The names that turn up on coins here afterwards are no longer Greek titles but the names of Saka chiefs, spelled out in Greek letters.'],
'拉合尔|德里苏丹国': ['拉合尔是德里苏丹国的西北门户,守着从中亚下来的路。这个位置的代价是首当其冲:1241 年蒙古人破城屠掠,此后一个多世纪里蒙古军队一次次来袭,苏丹国把主力常年摆在这一线。城里的很多建筑是后来莫卧儿时期盖的——拉合尔真正的黄金时代要等到阿克巴与贾汗吉尔,他们把这里当作第二个都城。',
 'Lahore was the north-western gate of the Delhi Sultanate, holding the road down from Central Asia. The price of that position was taking the first blow: the Mongols sacked it in 1241 and came back again and again for over a century, and the sultanate kept its main armies on this line. Most of the buildings there now are Mughal — Lahore\'s own golden age waited for Akbar and Jahangir, who treated it as a second capital.'],
'拉合尔|吠陀时代': ['吠陀时代没有留下城,只留下诗,而诗里反复出现的是河。旁遮普的意思就是「五条河」,《梨俱吠陀》里唱的七条河大多在这一带;拉合尔紧挨着的拉维河,吠陀里叫帕鲁湿尼,著名的「十王之战」就打在这条河边。这个时代没有印度河文明那样的砖城可看——它留下的东西不在墙里,在一代代背下来的诗句里。',
 'The Vedic age left no cities, only hymns, and what the hymns keep returning to is rivers. Punjab means "five rivers", and most of the seven rivers sung in the Rigveda run through this country; the Ravi, right beside Lahore, is the Parushni of the hymns, and the famous Battle of the Ten Kings was fought on its banks. This age left no brick cities of the kind the Indus civilization built — what it left is not in walls but in verses carried in memory from one generation to the next.'],
'拉合尔|印度-希腊诸王': ['米南德一世的都城舍羯罗就在拉合尔北边约一百公里(今锡亚尔科特)。佛教经典《弥兰陀王问经》把场景设在这座城里:希腊国王一遍遍追问那先比丘「既然没有一个不变的我,那到底是谁在轮回」,僧人指着国王自己的马车反问——车辕不是车,车轮不是车,拆开来哪一件都不是车,那车又是什么?这场对话被记下来,两千年后还在被读。',
 'Menander I\'s capital of Sagala stood about a hundred kilometres north of Lahore, at today\'s Sialkot. The Buddhist text known as the Milinda Panha sets its scene in that city: the Greek king presses the monk Nagasena again and again — if there is no unchanging self, then who exactly is it that is reborn? The monk points at the king\'s own chariot and asks back: the pole is not the chariot, nor is a wheel; take it apart and no single piece is the chariot — so what is? The conversation was written down, and is still read two thousand years later.'],
'加尔各答|德里苏丹国': ['孟加拉 1204 年被德里苏丹国的将领攻下,并入版图,不到一百四十年后又自立为孟加拉苏丹国。而加尔各答这座城此时还不存在——恒河三角洲这一带当时是几个村子和水道,英国东印度公司要到 1690 年才在这里设商站,这座城的历史从那时算起。所以这一行讲的是这片地方,不是这座城。',
 'Bengal was taken by a general of the Delhi Sultanate in 1204 and annexed, and broke away as the independent Sultanate of Bengal less than a hundred and forty years later. Calcutta itself did not yet exist: this part of the Ganges delta was a few villages and waterways, and the English East India Company set up a trading post here only in 1690, which is where the city\'s own history begins. This row is about the place, not the city.'],
'杭州|战国': ['战国时这一带先属越、越亡于楚后属楚,是钱塘江口的边缘地区,不是任何一国的重心。真正让杭州成为大城的是隋代开通的大运河——它成了运河的南端起点,此后一路长到南宋的都城临安。战国时候的杭州,大约只是江边的几处聚落与盐场。',
 'In the Warring States period this area belonged first to Yue and then, after Yue fell to Chu, to Chu — an edge of the map at the mouth of the Qiantang, central to no one. What made Hangzhou a great city was the Grand Canal cut under the Sui, which made it the southern terminus; from there it grew into Lin\'an, the capital of the Southern Song. In the Warring States it was probably a few settlements and salt pans by the river.'],
'奥斯陆|北欧诸王国': ['奥斯陆传为哈拉尔·哈德拉达约 1049 年在峡湾尽头建镇,考古证据把聚落的起点还要往前推到约 1000 年;1299 年哈康五世把王座迁到这里,在城边修了阿克斯胡斯城堡守海口——那座石堡至今还在。黑死病之后挪威的都城地位随国力一起沉了下去,1537 年后国家由哥本哈根治理,奥斯陆成了一座省城。1624 年一场大火把木头城烧光,丹麦国王克里斯蒂安四世在城堡旁边按棋盘格重建,并把城改名「克里斯蒂安尼亚」,这个名字一直用到 1925 年才改回奥斯陆。',
 'Oslo is traditionally dated to Harald Hardrada\'s market town of about 1049, though archaeology pushes the settlement back towards 1000; in 1299 Håkon V moved his seat here and built Akershus fortress by the water to guard the approach — the stone castle is still there. After the Black Death the town sank along with the kingdom, and from 1537 the country was run from Copenhagen and Oslo became a provincial capital. A fire destroyed the wooden town in 1624, and King Christian IV of Denmark rebuilt it on a grid beside the fortress and renamed it Christiania, a name it kept until 1925.'],
'哥本哈根|北欧诸王国': ['哥本哈根本是「商人的港」,1417 年成为丹麦王室驻地,此后一直是这个联合王国的中心:卡尔马联盟的国王、丹麦-挪威的国王都住在这里。1479 年建大学,1660 年国王在此宣布绝对君主制。城靠海峡吃饭——厄勒海峡的过路税就在门口收。1728 年和 1795 年两场大火各烧掉城里一大片,1801 年英国舰队在城外海面击败丹麦横在城前的一排浮动炮台,1807 年又炮击全城三天,为的是逼丹麦交出舰队;今天彩色的新港一带,多是那之后重建的。',
 'Copenhagen began as a merchants\'s harbour and became the seat of the Danish crown in 1417, the centre of the double kingdom ever after: the kings of the Kalmar Union and of Denmark-Norway alike lived here. Its university was founded in 1479, and in 1660 the king proclaimed absolute monarchy in the city. It lived off the strait — the Sound Dues were collected at its doorstep. Great fires in 1728 and 1795 each destroyed a large part of the town, a British fleet beat the line of floating batteries moored outside the harbour in 1801, and in 1807 the city was bombarded for three days to force the surrender of the Danish navy; much of the colourful Nyhavn frontage seen today was rebuilt after that.'],
'斯德哥尔摩|北欧诸王国': ['斯德哥尔摩建在梅拉伦湖入海的一串岛上,13 世纪中叶筑城守住湖口,汉萨同盟的德国商人很早就在城里占了很大比重。卡尔马联盟时期它是瑞典这一支的中心,也是联盟内部矛盾最集中的地方:1520 年丹麦国王在大广场处死八十多名瑞典贵族、主教与市民,史称「斯德哥尔摩惨案」,三年后古斯塔夫·瓦萨领着瑞典脱离联盟,此后这里事实上就是首都(法律上正式确立要到 1634 年)。老城的窄巷与广场,格局大体就是那时候的。',
 'Stockholm was built on the string of islands where Lake Mälaren meets the sea, fortified in the mid-thirteenth century to hold the entrance to the lake, and German merchants of the Hanseatic League made up a large share of its people early on. Under the Kalmar Union it was the centre of the Swedish side and the focus of the union\'s quarrels: in 1520 the Danish king had more than eighty Swedish nobles, bishops and burghers executed in the main square, and three years later Gustav Vasa led Sweden out of the union and the city was the capital in practice from then on, though only formally so from 1634. The lanes and squares of the old town still follow that plan.'],
'迪拜|海湾诸邦': ['迪拜是这排小港里起步很晚的一个:1833 年马克图姆·本·布蒂带着阿勒布法拉萨部落八百来人从阿布扎比迁到迪拜溪边定居,今天的迪拜王室就是这一支。城分两边,德拉与布尔迪拜隔着一条溪,靠摆渡往来,今天那种叫 abra 的小木船还在开。1894 年和 1901 年两次免税措施把波斯与印度商人吸引过来,溪边的金市与香料市就是那时起的家底。采珠季一到,城里的男人多半出海,一走三四个月;1930 年代珍珠卖不动之后,这里靠转口和走私撑了二十来年,石油要到 1966 年才发现。',
 'Dubai was a late starter among these ports: in 1833 Maktoum bin Butti brought some eight hundred people of the Al Bu Falasah from Abu Dhabi to settle by the creek, and the ruling family of Dubai today is that line. The town lay on two sides of the water, Deira facing Bur Dubai, crossed by ferry — the little wooden abras still run. Tax exemptions in 1894 and 1901 drew Persian and Indian merchants over, and the gold and spice markets by the creek date from then. When the pearling season came most of the men of the town went to sea for three or four months; after the pearl trade died in the 1930s the place lived on entrepôt trade and smuggling for twenty-odd years, and oil was not found until 1966.'],
'非斯|摩洛哥诸王朝': ['非斯有两座老城:八九世纪之交建起的非斯巴利,与马林人 1276 年另建的非斯杰迪德,王宫和政府搬进了新城。马林诸王在这里盖了一批学院,阿塔林学院(1323—1325)与布伊纳尼亚学院(1350—1355)的雪松木雕和彩釉拼砖今天还在。1492 年格拉纳达陷落后,大批安达卢斯的穆斯林与犹太人迁来,把技艺和曲调一并带进城里,犹太区「梅拉」就在新城边上。皮革染坊那些圆形的石头染缸,几百年来没怎么变过。',
 'Fez has two old cities: Fes el-Bali, begun around the turn of the ninth century, and Fes el-Jdid, which the Marinids laid out in 1276 and into which the palace and government moved. The Marinid kings built a series of colleges here, and the carved cedar and glazed tilework of the Attarine (1323–1325) and the Bou Inania (1350–1355) are still there. After Granada fell in 1492 large numbers of Muslims and Jews came from al-Andalus, bringing their crafts and their music with them, and the Jewish quarter, the mellah, sits beside the new city. The round stone vats of the tanneries have changed little in centuries.'],
'喀布尔|阿富汗': ['喀布尔在兴都库什山南麓的河谷里,海拔一千八百米上下,冬天会下雪。1776 年帖木儿沙把都城从坎大哈迁到这里,此后一直是首都;夏天在喀布尔、冬天去白沙瓦,是杜兰尼诸王的老规矩。老城里的巴布尔花园还是莫卧儿开国者的墓园,「鸡街」曾是外国人必逛的巷子。1979 年之后这座城被反复争夺,1990 年代军阀混战几乎把西城打成瓦砾;21 世纪重建,人口从几十万涨到四百多万,一多半住在山坡上后盖的房子里。',
 'Kabul sits in a valley on the southern side of the Hindu Kush, some eighteen hundred metres up, and gets snow in winter. Timur Shah moved the capital here from Kandahar in 1776 and it has been the capital ever since; summers in Kabul and winters in Peshawar was the old habit of the Durrani kings. The Gardens of Babur in the old city are still the tomb of the Mughal founder, and Chicken Street was once the lane every foreigner visited. After 1979 the city was fought over again and again, and warlord fighting in the 1990s reduced much of the west of it to rubble; it was rebuilt in this century and grew from a few hundred thousand people to over four million, more than half of them in houses built later up the hillsides.'],
'喀布尔|孔雀王朝': ['亚历山大死后,他的部将塞琉古想收回印度方面的领土,结果和旃陀罗笈多媾和:把喀布尔河谷一带割给孔雀,换来五百头战象。这批象后来被塞琉古牵到小亚细亚打了一场决定性的会战。阿育王的敕令刻到这一带时,用的不是印度文字——今天阿富汗南边的坎大哈出土过一块,一面希腊文、一面阿拉米文,因为这里的人本来就不说印度话。',
 'After Alexander died, his general Seleucus tried to recover the Indian territories and instead came to terms with Chandragupta: the Kabul valley and its neighbours went to the Mauryas, and five hundred war elephants went to Seleucus. He marched those elephants to Asia Minor and won a decisive battle with them. When Ashoka\'s edicts reached this country they were not cut in an Indian script — one found at Kandahar in southern Afghanistan is in Greek on one side and Aramaic on the other, because the people here did not speak an Indian language to begin with.'],
'喀布尔|印度-希腊诸王': ['这些国王留下的东西,大半是从喀布尔一带的地里挖出来的钱币。1830 年代,马松在喀布尔的集市上成批收购古币,前后近七万枚。这些钱上不写年份,学者是靠别的办法把国王排出来的:同一个名字正面用希腊文、背面用佉卢文,两面对读就认出了人;哪一枚被改铸盖在哪一枚上面,就定出了谁先谁后。三十多位国王,大部分在任何一本史书里都没有名字——他们是从零钱里被重新认出来的。',
 'Most of what these kings left has come out of the ground around Kabul in the form of coins. In the 1830s Charles Masson bought old coins by the sackful in the Kabul bazaars — nearly seventy thousand of them. The coins carry no dates, so the kings were worked out by other means: the same name appears in Greek on one face and in Kharoshthi on the other, and reading the two together identified the man; which coin was overstruck on which fixed the order. More than thirty kings, most of whose names appear in no written history at all, were recovered from small change.'],
'维也纳|中世纪西欧': ['维也纳在 12 世纪成为巴本堡家族奥地利公国的都城,1278 年后归哈布斯堡家族;圣斯蒂芬大教堂 1137 年始建,西立面罗马式的巨人门是 13 世纪扩建时的,至今还在。1365 年维也纳大学创办,是德语世界最早的大学之一;1485—1490 年匈牙利国王马加什曾占领此城。',
 'Vienna became the seat of the Babenberg dukes of Austria in the twelfth century and passed to the Habsburgs after 1278; St Stephen\'s Cathedral was begun in 1137, and the Romanesque Giant\'s Door on its west front, from the thirteenth-century enlargement, still stands. The University of Vienna, founded in 1365, is among the oldest in the German-speaking world; the Hungarian king Matthias held the city from 1485 to 1490.'],
'里约热内卢|拉丁美洲诸国': ['1822 年巴西独立后里约是帝国首都,1889 年共和后仍是首都,直到 1960 年迁往新建的巴西利亚。救世基督像 1931 年立在科科瓦多山顶,科帕卡巴纳与狂欢节让它成为拉美最有名的城市之一;2016 年在这里办了南美洲第一届奥运会。',
 'After Brazilian independence in 1822 Rio was the imperial capital, and it stayed the capital under the republic from 1889 until the move to the new city of Brasília in 1960. Christ the Redeemer was raised on Corcovado in 1931, and Copacabana and the carnival made it one of the most famous cities in Latin America; in 2016 it held the first Olympic Games in South America.'],
/* v211:现代欧洲诸国 */
'罗马|现代欧洲诸国': ['1870 年意大利军队攻入罗马,次年定为意大利王国首都,教皇退守梵蒂冈,直到 1929 年《拉特兰条约》梵蒂冈才成为独立的城国。1922 年墨索里尼「向罗马进军」上台;1957 年六国在卡比托利欧山签《罗马条约》,今天的欧盟从这里起步;1960 年罗马办了奥运会。',
 'Italian troops entered Rome in 1870 and it became the capital of the kingdom the next year, the pope withdrawing into the Vatican until the Lateran Treaty of 1929 made it an independent city-state. Mussolini\'s March on Rome brought him to power in 1922; in 1957 six states signed the Treaty of Rome on the Capitoline hill, the starting point of today\'s European Union; and the city held the Olympic Games in 1960.'],
'维也纳|现代欧洲诸国': ['1918 年帝国解体后维也纳成了一个小共和国的大首都;1938 年德国吞并奥地利,二战后被四国分区占领到 1955 年。此后它靠中立地位成为联合国的第三个总部所在地(1979 年起),欧佩克、国际原子能机构都设在这里;环城大道两侧的歌剧院与博物馆是 19 世纪帝国留下的。',
 'After the empire broke up in 1918 Vienna was the oversized capital of a small republic; Germany annexed Austria in 1938, and after the war the city was divided among four occupying powers until 1955. Neutrality then made it the third seat of the United Nations from 1979, with OPEC and the atomic energy agency based here; the opera house and museums along the Ringstrasse are what the nineteenth-century empire left behind.'],
'雅典|现代欧洲诸国': ['1834 年独立不久的希腊把首都从纳夫普利翁迁到雅典,那时它只是个几千人的小镇,卫城脚下的新城是按新古典样式规划出来的。1896 年第一届现代奥运会在这里的大理石体育场举行,2004 年又办了一次;1967—1974 年的军政府与 2010 年代的债务危机都以雅典为中心。',
 'In 1834 the newly independent Greek state moved its capital from Nafplio to Athens, then a town of a few thousand, and a new neoclassical city was laid out below the Acropolis. The first modern Olympic Games were held in the marble stadium here in 1896, and the city hosted them again in 2004; the military junta of 1967-1974 and the debt crisis of the 2010s both had Athens at their centre.'],
'马德里|现代欧洲诸国': ['19 世纪的西班牙政变频繁,马德里作为首都换过多次政体;1936—1939 年内战中它被围困两年多,是抵抗佛朗哥最久的城市之一,战后成为独裁政权的首都直到 1975 年。1975 年后西班牙迅速转向民主,1986 年入欧共体;马德里的普拉多美术馆(1819 年开馆)藏着委拉斯开兹与戈雅。',
 'Nineteenth-century Spain went through coup after coup, and Madrid as capital saw one regime after another; in the civil war of 1936-1939 it was besieged for over two years, among the last cities to hold out against Franco, and then served as the seat of his dictatorship until 1975. After 1975 Spain moved quickly to democracy and joined the European Community in 1986; the Prado, opened in 1819, holds Velázquez and Goya.'],
'科尔多瓦|现代欧洲诸国': ['近代的科尔多瓦是安达卢西亚的一座内陆省城,失去了中世纪的光彩;19 世纪起大清真寺—主教座堂开始被当作古迹保护,1984 年列入世界遗产,老城随后整体列入。1992 年塞维利亚世博会那年,高铁把它与马德里连了起来。',
 'Modern Córdoba was an inland provincial town of Andalusia, its medieval glory gone; from the nineteenth century the Mosque-Cathedral was treated as a monument to be preserved, listed as World Heritage in 1984 with the old town added later. In 1992, the year of the Seville world\'s fair, the high-speed railway linked it to Madrid.'],
'里斯本|现代欧洲诸国': ['1910 年葡萄牙革命废除君主制,里斯本成为共和国首都;1926 年政变后萨拉查建立独裁,「新国家」体制维持到 1974 年 4 月 25 日的康乃馨革命——军人起义几乎没有流血,士兵枪管上插着康乃馨。里斯本 1998 年办了世博会,老城电车与法多歌声是它的名片。',
 'The revolution of 1910 abolished the Portuguese monarchy and made Lisbon a republican capital; after the coup of 1926 Salazar built a dictatorship, the New State, which lasted until the Carnation Revolution of 25 April 1974 — a military rising almost without bloodshed, soldiers carrying carnations in their gun barrels. Lisbon held the world\'s fair in 1998, and its old trams and fado singing are its calling cards.'],
'巴塞罗那|现代欧洲诸国': ['19 世纪工业化让巴塞罗那成为西班牙的工业之都,1859 年塞尔达规划的扩展区(Eixample)是棋盘格新城,高迪的圣家堂 1882 年在这里动工至今未完;1936—1939 年内战中它是共和国最后的首都之一。1992 年奥运会把海岸线整个翻新,今天它是加泰罗尼亚自治区的首府。',
 'Industrialisation made Barcelona the manufacturing capital of Spain in the nineteenth century; Cerdà\'s grid-planned Eixample was laid out from 1859, and Gaudí\'s Sagrada Família, begun here in 1882, is still unfinished; in the civil war of 1936-1939 it was one of the Republic\'s last capitals. The Olympic Games of 1992 remade the whole waterfront, and today it is the capital of the autonomous community of Catalonia.'],
'布拉格|现代欧洲诸国': ['1918 年捷克斯洛伐克在布拉格宣告独立,两次大战之间它是中欧最富、最民主的国家之一;1948 年共产党掌权,1968 年「布拉格之春」的改革被苏军坦克终止。1989 年的天鹅绒革命几乎不流血地更换了政权,剧作家哈维尔当选总统;1993 年捷克与斯洛伐克和平分手,布拉格是捷克首都。',
 'Czechoslovakia declared its independence in Prague in 1918 and between the wars was among the richest and most democratic states in Central Europe; the communists took power in 1948, and the reforms of the Prague Spring of 1968 were ended by Soviet tanks. The Velvet Revolution of 1989 changed the regime almost without bloodshed and made the playwright Havel president; in 1993 the Czechs and Slovaks parted peacefully, and Prague is the Czech capital.'],
'华沙|现代欧洲诸国': ['1795 年波兰亡国后华沙先后属普鲁士、拿破仑的华沙公国和俄国治下的波兰王国,1830 与 1863 年两次起义都从这里爆发;1918 年波兰复国,华沙重做首都。1939 年被德军攻占,1944 年起义失败后全城被系统炸毁,战后照着老图纸重建了老城,1980 年因此列入世界遗产;1989 年圆桌会议后波兰第一个走出苏联阵营。',
 'After Poland was wiped off the map in 1795 Warsaw belonged in turn to Prussia, to Napoleon\'s Duchy of Warsaw and to the Russian-ruled Kingdom of Poland, and the risings of 1830 and 1863 both began here; in 1918 Poland was reborn with Warsaw as its capital. Taken by the Germans in 1939 and systematically demolished after the failed rising of 1944, the old town was rebuilt after the war from the old plans and listed as World Heritage in 1980; after the round-table talks of 1989 Poland was the first to leave the Soviet bloc.'],
'斯德哥尔摩|现代欧洲诸国': ['瑞典自 1814 年后再没打过仗,是欧洲维持中立最久的国家之一(2024 年才加入北约);斯德哥尔摩在 19 世纪末工业化,1901 年起每年十二月在这里颁发诺贝尔奖(和平奖在奥斯陆),市政厅的蓝厅是颁奖晚宴的地方。1912 年这里办了奥运会。',
 'Sweden has fought no war since 1814, one of the longest neutralities in Europe (it joined NATO only in 2024); Stockholm industrialised at the end of the nineteenth century, and since 1901 the Nobel prizes have been presented here every December, the peace prize in Oslo, with the banquet in the Blue Hall of the city hall. The city held the Olympic Games in 1912.'],
'阿姆斯特丹|现代欧洲诸国': ['1815 年后阿姆斯特丹是荷兰王国的首都,但政府和王室都在海牙——这个安排至今没变。19 世纪它靠殖民贸易与运河翻新恢复繁荣,20 世纪成了自行车与运河游船的城市;1940—1945 年被德军占领,安妮·弗兰克一家藏身的房子就在王子运河边,今天是全城最多人排队的博物馆之一。',
 'After 1815 Amsterdam was the capital of the Kingdom of the Netherlands, though the government and the royal court sat in The Hague — an arrangement unchanged to this day. It recovered its prosperity in the nineteenth century on colonial trade and renewed canals and became in the twentieth the city of bicycles and canal boats; occupied by the Germans in 1940-1945, it holds on the Prinsengracht the house where Anne Frank\'s family hid, now among the most queued-for museums in town.'],
'威尼斯|现代欧洲诸国': ['1797 年拿破仑终结了千年共和国,威尼斯几经易手后 1866 年并入意大利王国;19 世纪起铁路桥把它连上大陆,它慢慢从港口变成博物馆式的城市。1932 年起办电影节,双年展始于 1895 年;潟湖的海水一年比一年高,2020 年起活动堤坝「摩西」开始拦潮。',
 'Napoleon ended the thousand-year republic in 1797, and after changing hands several times Venice joined the Kingdom of Italy in 1866; a railway causeway tied it to the mainland in the nineteenth century, and it slowly turned from a port into a museum city. The film festival dates from 1932 and the Biennale from 1895; the lagoon rises a little more each year, and from 2020 the movable MOSE barrier began holding back the high tides.'],
'佛罗伦萨|现代欧洲诸国': ['1865—1871 年佛罗伦萨做过意大利王国的临时首都,城墙因此被拆、老市场被改成共和广场;此后它靠乌菲兹与老城成为文艺复兴的博物馆之城。1944 年德军撤退时炸毁了阿诺河上除老桥之外的全部桥梁;1966 年大洪水淹了城,世界各地的志愿者赶来抢救文物,被称为「泥浆天使」。',
 'From 1865 to 1871 Florence was the temporary capital of the Kingdom of Italy, and its walls were pulled down and the old market rebuilt as the Piazza della Repubblica; it then lived on the Uffizi and the old town as the museum city of the Renaissance. Retreating German troops in 1944 blew up every bridge over the Arno except the Ponte Vecchio; the great flood of 1966 drowned the city, and volunteers from around the world who came to rescue its books and paintings were called the mud angels.'],
'米兰|现代欧洲诸国': ['1859 年米兰脱离奥地利、加入撒丁王国,两年后进入意大利王国,此后一直是意大利的工商业首都;斯卡拉歌剧院、1906 年世博会、1920 年代的公司总部与后来的时装周都在这里。1943 年盟军轰炸损毁了斯卡拉与大教堂周边,战后重建;米兰大教堂拖了近六百年,1965 年才最后完工。',
 'In 1859 Milan left Austria for the Kingdom of Sardinia and two years later entered the Kingdom of Italy, and it has been the country\'s commercial and industrial capital ever since — La Scala, the world\'s fair of 1906, the company headquarters of the 1920s and later the fashion weeks all belong here. Allied bombing in 1943 damaged La Scala and the area around the cathedral, rebuilt after the war; the cathedral itself, six centuries in the making, was finally completed in 1965.'],
/* v212:维京·北欧 */
'奥斯陆|维京·北欧': ['维京时代还没有奥斯陆城——挪威国王哈拉尔三世(哈德拉达)约 1049 年在峡湾尽头建镇,他就是 1066 年死在斯坦福桥的那位;奥斯陆峡湾一带早就是船的世界,从墓丘挖出的奥塞贝格、戈克斯塔德、图讷三条 9—10 世纪长船收藏在城西比格迪半岛的维京时代博物馆(改建中,计划 2027 年重开)。',
 'There was no town of Oslo yet in the Viking Age — King Harald III, Hardrada, founded it at the head of the fjord around 1049, the same king who died at Stamford Bridge in 1066; the Oslo fjord was already a world of ships, and the three longships of the ninth and tenth centuries dug from mounds at Oseberg, Gokstad and Tune are kept in the Museum of the Viking Age on the Bygdøy peninsula (being rebuilt, due to reopen in 2027).'],
'哥本哈根|维京·北欧': ['哥本哈根这时只是厄勒海峡边的一处渔村与港口,城要到 1167 年主教阿布萨隆筑堡才算开始;但它周围就是维京丹麦的核心——西边罗斯基勒是丹麦王的驻地,峡湾里打捞出的五条 11 世纪沉船现在陈列在罗斯基勒的维京船博物馆,而日德兰的耶灵石碑上刻着哈拉尔「蓝牙」让丹麦人改信基督教的话。',
 'Copenhagen was then only a fishing village and harbour on the Øresund; the town proper began when Bishop Absalon built a fort in 1167. But all around it was the heart of Viking Denmark — Roskilde to the west was the seat of the Danish kings, five eleventh-century ships raised from its fjord are shown in the Viking Ship Museum there, and the Jelling stones in Jutland carry Harald Bluetooth\'s boast of making the Danes Christian.'],
'斯德哥尔摩|维京·北欧': ['斯德哥尔摩要到 1252 年才建城,但它西边梅拉伦湖里的比尔卡岛是维京时代瑞典最大的贸易城镇(约 750—975 年),阿拉伯银币、拜占庭丝绸都在那里出土;瑞典维京人主要向东走,顺俄罗斯的河流去做买卖,乌普兰一带立着全瑞典最多的卢恩石碑,不少刻着「他死在东方」。',
 'Stockholm was founded only in 1252, but Birka, an island in Lake Mälaren just west of it, was the largest trading town of Viking-age Sweden (about 750-975), where Arab silver and Byzantine silk have been dug up; the Swedish Vikings mostly went east, trading down the rivers of Russia, and the countryside of Uppland has more rune stones than anywhere else in Sweden, many of them recording a man who died in the east.'],
'奥斯陆|现代欧洲诸国': ['1814 年挪威从丹麦转归瑞典、有了自己的宪法,1905 年全民公投后和平独立,奥斯陆(1925 年前叫克里斯蒂安尼亚)成为独立王国的首都;1940—1945 年被德军占领。1969 年北海发现石油,挪威成了欧洲最富的国家之一,主权基金全球最大;诺贝尔和平奖按遗嘱在奥斯陆颁发,1994 年冬奥会在城北一百八十公里的利勒哈默尔举行。',
 'In 1814 Norway passed from Denmark to Sweden and got its own constitution, and after a referendum in 1905 it became independent peacefully, with Oslo — called Christiania until 1925 — as capital of the new kingdom; German forces occupied it in 1940-1945. Oil was found in the North Sea in 1969 and Norway became one of the richest countries in Europe, with the largest sovereign wealth fund in the world; the Nobel Peace Prize is awarded in Oslo as the will requires, and the 1994 Winter Olympics were held at Lillehammer, a hundred and eighty kilometres to the north.'],
'哥本哈根|现代欧洲诸国': ['1801 年英国舰队在城外海面击败丹麦舰队,1807 年又炮击哥本哈根、烧掉了城市的大片;1849 年丹麦颁布宪法成为君主立宪国,1864 年输给普鲁士丢了南部的石勒苏益格与荷尔斯泰因。1940—1945 年被德军占领,1943 年市民用渔船把七千多名犹太人送到瑞典;2000 年厄勒海峡大桥通车,哥本哈根与瑞典的马尔默连成一片,今天它常被称为欧洲的自行车之都。',
 'A British fleet beat the Danish ships off Copenhagen in 1801 and bombarded the city itself in 1807, burning much of it; in 1849 Denmark adopted a constitution and became a constitutional monarchy, and in 1864 it lost Schleswig and Holstein in the south to Prussia. Occupied by Germany in 1940-1945, its citizens ferried more than seven thousand Jews to Sweden in fishing boats in 1943; the Øresund bridge opened in 2000 and joined Copenhagen to Malmö in Sweden, and today it is often called the bicycle capital of Europe.'],
/* v213:斯里兰卡 */
'科伦坡|斯里兰卡诸王国': ['僧伽罗诸王国的都城都在内陆,科伦坡在中世纪只是西海岸的一处港口,阿拉伯商人从 8 世纪起在这里常住做肉桂和宝石买卖,「科伦坡」这个名字在 14 世纪的阿拉伯旅行家伊本·白图泰笔下已经出现;沿海的科特王国 15 世纪以科伦坡东南的科特为都,1505 年葡萄牙人第一次登陆就是在这附近。',
 'The capitals of the Sinhalese kingdoms all lay inland; in the middle ages Colombo was a port on the west coast where Arab merchants had lived since the eighth century trading cinnamon and gems, and the name appears in the fourteenth-century traveller Ibn Battuta. The coastal kingdom of Kotte ruled from Kotte, just south-east of Colombo, in the fifteenth century, and the Portuguese first landed near here in 1505.'],
'科伦坡|英属印度': ['1796 年英国从荷兰手里接过科伦坡,1802 年锡兰成为单独的直辖殖民地(不归印度总督管),首府就设在这里;英国人在城里留下堡区的官署与银行,在山区先种咖啡、后改种茶,把泰米尔劳工从南印度运来——锡兰红茶的名声由此而来。荷兰时期的沃尔文达尔教堂(1757)至今还在。',
 'The British took Colombo from the Dutch in 1796, and when Ceylon became a crown colony of its own in 1802 — separate from British India — the capital was placed here; they left the offices and banks of the Fort district, planted coffee and then tea in the hills and brought Tamil labourers from south India to work the estates — the origin of Ceylon tea\'s fame. The Dutch-period Wolvendaal Church of 1757 still stands.'],
'科伦坡|印度·南亚诸国': ['1948 年锡兰独立,科伦坡是首都,独立纪念堂 1953 年建成;1972 年改国名斯里兰卡,1980 年代起议会迁到城郊的斯里贾亚瓦德纳普拉科特,科伦坡仍是最大城市与商业中心。1983—2009 年僧伽罗人与泰米尔人之间的内战打了二十六年,科伦坡多次遭袭;2004 年印度洋海啸重创全岛海岸。',
 'Ceylon became independent in 1948 with Colombo as capital, and Independence Memorial Hall was finished in 1953; the country took the name Sri Lanka in 1972, and from the 1980s parliament moved to Sri Jayawardenepura Kotte on the outskirts, Colombo remaining the largest city and commercial centre. The civil war between Sinhalese and Tamils ran for twenty-six years, 1983-2009, and Colombo was attacked many times; the Indian Ocean tsunami of 2004 devastated the island\'s coasts.'],
/* v214:蒙古国 / 朝鲜 */
'乌兰巴托|蒙古国': ['库伦 1911 年成为博克多汗的都城,1924 年改名乌兰巴托——「红色英雄」;苏联时期按莫斯科的样子盖起了广场、剧院和板楼,1930 年代城里的甘丹寺是少数没被拆掉的大寺,1944 年为了给来访的美国副总统看而重新开放。1990 年的绝食示威就在市中心的苏赫巴托尔广场;今天全国近一半人住在这座城,冬天煤烟让它成为世界上空气最差的首都之一。',
 'Urga became the Bogd Khan\'s capital in 1911 and was renamed Ulaanbaatar, Red Hero, in 1924; under Soviet influence it acquired a square, a theatre and apartment blocks on the Moscow pattern, and Gandan, one of the few great monasteries spared in the 1930s, was reopened in 1944 to be shown to a visiting American vice-president. The hunger strikes of 1990 took place in Sükhbaatar Square in the centre; nearly half the country lives in the city today, and coal smoke in winter makes it one of the worst-polluted capitals in the world.'],
'乌兰巴托|辽': ['回鹘的城 840 年破在西边的鄂尔浑河谷,而土拉河这一带并没有因此空下来。辽在漠北设西北路招讨司,1004 年在回鹘可敦城的旧地置镇州,派兵长驻,管着周围的部落。一个以农耕区为财源的政权,肯在草原深处养一支不换防的驻军,是因为它同时要当草原的主人——辽的两个身份,在这里同时看得见。',
 'The Uyghur city fell in 840 over in the Orkhon valley to the west, but the Tuul country did not empty out. The Liao set up a northwestern command in the Mongolian steppe and in 1004 established Zhenzhou on the site of the old Uyghur Khatun City, keeping a permanent garrison there to hold the surrounding tribes. A state drawing its revenue from farmland was willing to keep a garrison that never rotated home this deep in the grass because it meant to be master of the steppe as well — both halves of the Liao are visible in one place here.'],
'乌兰巴托|北元·蒙古诸部': ['喇嘛教在这几十年里传遍蒙古各部(「达赖喇嘛」这个称号的来历写在这条色带自己的卡片里),这一带的土谢图汗家族也改了信仰。1639 年,就在这条色带结束之后四年,他们家一个五岁的孩子被认定为活佛,信众围着他的帐篷扎下营地——那片营地后来长成了乌兰巴托。',
 'Lamaism spread through the Mongol tribes in these decades (where the title "Dalai Lama" came from is told on this band\'s own card), and the Tüsheet Khan family of this country converted with the rest. In 1639, four years after this band ends, a five-year-old boy of that family was recognised as a living Buddha, and his followers pitched camp around his tent — that camp is what eventually grew into Ulaanbaatar.'],
'哈拉和林|蒙古国': ['蒙古国建立后哈拉和林只是鄂尔浑河谷的一处遗址和额尔德尼召寺旁的小镇;1930 年代寺院被毁大半,1990 年后恢复为寺院与博物馆。2004 年鄂尔浑河谷整体列入世界遗产,近年蒙古国政府提出把首都迁回哈拉和林的计划,是否真做尚未定。',
 'After the Mongolian state was founded Karakorum was only a ruin in the Orkhon valley and a small town beside the Erdene Zuu monastery; most of the monastery was destroyed in the 1930s and it was restored as a monastery and museum after 1990. The Orkhon valley as a whole was listed as World Heritage in 2004, and the government has recently floated a plan to move the capital back to Karakorum — whether it happens is undecided.'],
'哈拉和林|辽': ['840 年回鹘的城破,1235 年蒙古人在这里筑城,中间隔着四百年——这四百年河谷并非无人。辽的可敦城在东边几百里的土拉河边,驻军管着这一带的部落。1124 年前后辽被金打垮时,宗室耶律大石正是带着人马北走可敦城,在那里聚起兵马再一路西行,几年后在中亚建起西辽——一个王朝灭亡之后,它在草原上留的那颗钉子,成了它续命的地方。',
 'The Uyghur city fell in 840; the Mongols built here in 1235. The four hundred years between were not empty. The Liao\'s Khatun City stood a few hundred li east on the Tuul, its garrison holding the tribes of this country. When the Jin broke the Liao around 1124, it was to Khatun City that the imperial kinsman Yelu Dashi rode north, gathered men there and went on west, founding the Western Liao in Central Asia a few years later — the nail a dynasty had driven into the steppe turned out to be where it went on living.'],
'哈拉和林|北元·蒙古诸部': ['元亡之后,北元的大汗不再定都。城残破在那里,而朝廷回到了帐篷里——忽必烈那几代人用了几十年学会住城、修宫殿、设官府,被赶回草原之后,他的后代又把这些一样样放下了。1585 年阿巴岱汗在旧城旁边动土,是这一带两百年里唯一一次大兴土木,而他修的是寺院,不是城。',
 'After the Yuan fell, the Northern Yuan khans kept no capital. The city lay in ruins and the court went back into tents — Khubilai\'s generation had spent decades learning to live in cities, build palaces and staff offices, and once driven back to the grass his descendants set all of it down again, piece by piece. When Abtai Khan broke ground beside the ruins in 1585 it was the only major construction here in two centuries, and what he built was a monastery, not a city.'],
'平壤|朝鲜': ['平壤在朝鲜战争中几乎被夷平,战后按苏联式规划重建:宽阔的马路、大广场、纪念碑,1982 年建起 170 米高的主体思想塔和平壤凯旋门,105 层的柳京饭店 1987 年动工至今没有营业。城里的居民是挑选过的,外地人进城要许可证;大同江边的大同门(1635 年重建)和高句丽古墓群是它留下的古迹,2004 年后者列入世界遗产。',
 'Pyongyang was all but levelled in the Korean War and rebuilt on Soviet lines — broad avenues, great squares and monuments; the 170-metre Juche Tower and the city\'s own Arch of Triumph went up in 1982, and the 105-storey Ryugyong Hotel, begun in 1987, has never opened. Residence in the city is by selection and people from elsewhere need a permit to enter; the Taedong Gate (rebuilt 1635) by the river and the Goguryeo tombs, listed as World Heritage in 2004, are its old monuments.'],
};
